window.NovaManualData = {"built":"2026-10-14T11:57:48.778Z","recentDays":7,"suite":null,"apps":[{"id":"agent","name":"Nova Agent","colour":"#FF5FA8","glyph":"✦","where":"Online for everyone, on the studio's server","links":[["Open Nova Agent","https://nova.novacane.co.uk/agent/"]],"repo":"na","shared":"","tagline":"Your planner, your Nova Agent and the studio's hands in Acuity, on the studio's VPS.","intro":"<p>Talk to it, give it a goal, and it plans your days to the second. It also works Acuity&#39;s admin pages for Novacane Studios.</p>\n<p>Nova Agent is the studio&#39;s one app. Everything that used to be a separate Nova app is a panel of it: <strong>Nova Portal</strong> (the staff app: enquiries, website chats, bookings, alerts, Ask NovaBot, sign-in, your planet and the team; Nova Portal is part of it now), <strong>Nova Calendar</strong>, <strong>Nova Notes</strong>, <strong>Nova Index</strong>, <strong>Nova Observatory</strong>, <strong>Nova Lossless audio</strong> and <strong>Admin</strong>. The panels only ever open inside Nova Agent. Nova Agent has one address, for everyone:  (every address in the suite: Nova Manual → All addresses, or Nova Portal → Settings → Addresses). It runs on the studio&#39;s server, so it works with every laptop off.</p>\n<p><code>/agent/</code> (<code>/agent/calendar</code>, <code>/agent/portal</code>, <code>/agent/notes</code>, <code>/agent/index</code>...) opens Nova Agent with that panel. Nova Bot (the website chat) keeps the main address.</p>\n<p>Nova Agent, Nova Missions, Nova Quests, Nova Calendar and the Nova Visualizer run on the VPS (<code>nova-agent.service</code>, the same server as Nova Bot), day and night, with every laptop off. The online Nova Agent reaches them over a link Nova Agent opens to Nova Bot (<code>src/relay.ts</code>, a WebSocket with <code>AGENT_NOVA_KEY</code>), for signed-in staff only. If that link is ever down, the online page says so and the other panels keep working. Run on a computer of its own, its pages open the online Nova Agent, so there&#39;s one address; set <code>NOVA_LOCAL_UI=1</code> in <code>.env</code> to keep using the pages there (when the internet is down).</p>\n<p>Open  and you get one screen that fits without scrolling: <strong>Nova Missions</strong> on the left, <strong>Nova Agent</strong> in the middle, <strong>Nova Quests</strong> (today&#39;s plan) on the right, and the <strong>panels</strong> along the bottom.</p>\n<p>Behind Nova Agent sits a planner: tell it a goal and it becomes a <strong>Mission</strong> of <strong>Nova Quests</strong>, fitted around your sleep, your calendar and your travel, with reminders and check-ins as you go. And behind that sits the job it started with: a careful, self-healing browser helper that does what <a href=\"https://acuityscheduling.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Acuity Scheduling</a>&#39;s API can&#39;t, for <a href=\"https://github.com/tuniveza/nova-bot\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Nova Bot</a>.</p>\n<p>All the pictures here come from a separate sample copy with made-up quests and people.</p>","guide":[{"id":"at-a-glance-0","title":"At a glance","html":"<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Nova Agent</strong></td><td>Claude, with tools for quests, missions, Nova Calendar, Acuity (read-only) and its own status</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nova Missions and Nova Quests</strong></td><td>Goals broken into quests, planned hour by hour (to the second), re-planned on every change</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Reminders</strong></td><td>Pop-ups, check-ins, a morning plan and evening wrap-up, chimes, system notifications and your phone</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nova Calendar</strong></td><td>Built in, saving to Nova Agent, so Nova Agent and the calendar always agree</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Panels</strong></td><td>Nova Portal, Nova Calendar, Nova Notes, Nova Index, Nova Observatory and Nova Lossless audio, inside Nova Agent or in their own window</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Online</strong></td><td>The same Nova Portal, Nova Index, Nova Calendar and Nova Notes at Nova Bot&#39;s address (<code>/portal/</code> and so on), for the phones</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nova Index</strong></td><td>Reads what Nova Agent remembers before it replies, and learns after</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Acuity helper</strong></td><td>Changes session types, prices and paid status for Nova Bot, safely, healing itself when pages change</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nova Visualizer</strong></td><td>Every step the Acuity helper takes, live</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","text":"Nova Agent Claude, with tools for quests, missions, Nova Calendar, Acuity (read-only) and its own status Nova Missions and Nova Quests Goals broken into quests, planned hour by hour (to the second), re-planned on every change Reminders Pop-ups, check-ins, a morning plan and evening wrap-up, chimes, system notifications and your phone Nova Calendar Built in, saving to Nova Agent, so Nova Agent and the calendar always agree Panels Nova Portal, Nova Calendar, Nova Notes, Nova Index, Nova Observatory and Nova Lossless audio, inside Nova Agent or in their own window Online The same Nova Portal, Nova Index, Nova Calendar and Nova Notes at Nova Bot's address ( /portal/ and so on), for the phones Nova Index Reads what Nova Agent remembers before it replies, and learns after Acuity helper Changes session types, prices and paid status for Nova Bot, safely, healing itself when pages change Nova Visualizer Every step the Acuity helper takes, live"},{"id":"the-panels-1","title":"The panels","html":"<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Panel</th><th>What it is</th><th>On the VPS (Nova Agent)</th><th>Online (Nova Bot)</th><th>Code</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Nova Agent</strong></td><td>Talk to Nova Agent; Nova Missions and Nova Quests</td><td><code>/</code></td><td></td><td><code>src/</code>, <code>web/agent/</code></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nova Portal</strong></td><td>The staff app: enquiries, website chats, bookings, quests, alerts, Ask NovaBot, push to the phones, and sign-in, your planet, the team and invites</td><td><code>/portal/</code></td><td><code>/portal/</code></td><td><code>web/portal/</code></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nova Calendar</strong></td><td>Note cards and day cards; Nova Agent plans into it</td><td><code>/calendar/</code></td><td><code>/calendar/</code></td><td><code>web/calendar/</code></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nova Notes</strong></td><td>Nova Notes and documents, Google Docs export</td><td><code>/notes/</code></td><td><code>/notes/</code></td><td><code>web/notes/</code></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nova Index</strong></td><td>Everything Nova Agent remembers: browse, edit, approve</td><td><code>/app/memory/</code></td><td><code>/app/memory/</code></td><td><code>web/index/</code></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nova Observatory</strong></td><td>Every project on this computer, measured and mapped</td><td><code>/observatory/</code></td><td></td><td><code>web/observatory/</code>, <code>scripts/observatory/</code></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nova Lossless audio</strong></td><td>Raw PCM between two devices, anywhere</td><td></td><td>its own address for now</td><td><code>web/lossless/</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>What they share (themes, sounds, the badge, the Nova Manual) is in <code>web/shared/</code>. Each panel&#39;s guide is in <code>docs/apps//</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Signing in.</strong> Nova Portal uses Nova Bot&#39;s staff API. Sign in on the Nova Portal panel and Nova Agent signs in to Nova Bot as you (an app sign-in; the token stays in <code>data/signin.json</code> and never reaches the browser); after that the panels work with your own permissions, and Nova Agent works for you. Only Nova Agent&#39;s own pages can use it.</p>\n<p><strong>Online.</strong> Nova Bot&#39;s worker copies the panels in at build time (its <code>scripts/sync-apps.mjs</code>, from this repo&#39;s <code>web/</code>) and serves them for phones, laptops and everywhere else. Nova Portal&#39;s old address (<code>/app/</code>) opens Nova Portal; its API (<code>/app/api/</code>), Nova Index (<code>/app/memory/</code>) and the push helper that phones which installed Nova Portal still use (<code>/app/sw.js</code>) keep their addresses.</p>","text":"Panel What it is On the VPS (Nova Agent) Online (Nova Bot) Code Nova Agent Talk to Nova Agent; Nova Missions and Nova Quests / src/ , web/agent/ Nova Portal The staff app: enquiries, website chats, bookings, quests, alerts, Ask NovaBot, push to the phones, and sign-in, your planet, the team and invites /portal/ /portal/ web/portal/ Nova Calendar Note cards and day cards; Nova Agent plans into it /calendar/ /calendar/ web/calendar/ Nova Notes Nova Notes and documents, Google Docs export /notes/ /notes/ web/notes/ Nova Index Everything Nova Agent remembers: browse, edit, approve /app/memory/ /app/memory/ web/index/ Nova Observatory Every project on this computer, measured and mapped /observatory/ web/observatory/ , scripts/observatory/ Nova Lossless audio Raw PCM between two devices, anywhere its own address for now web/lossless/ What they share (themes, sounds, the badge, the Nova Manual) is in web/shared/ . Each panel's guide is in docs/apps// . Signing in. Nova Portal uses Nova Bot's staff API. Sign in on the Nova Portal panel and Nova Agent signs in to Nova Bot as you (an app sign-in; the token stays in data/signin.json and never reaches the browser); after that the panels work with your own permissions, and Nova Agent works for you. Only Nova Agent's own pages can use it. Online. Nova Bot's worker copies the panels in at build time (its scripts/sync-apps.mjs , from this repo's web/ ) and serves them for phones, laptops and everywhere else. Nova Portal's old address ( /app/ ) opens Nova Portal; its API ( /app/api/ ), Nova Index ( /app/memory/ ) and the push helper that phones which installed Nova Portal still use ( /app/sw.js ) keep their addresses."},{"id":"what-it-does-2","title":"What it does","html":"<h4>Nova Agent, in the middle</h4>\n<p>Nova Agent (<code>src/chat.ts</code>) is Claude with tools. Ask it what to do next (&quot;What should I do now?&quot; gives one clear recommendation), plan a mission, block out an evening (&quot;I&#39;m out tonight from 7 to 11&quot;), push your day back (&quot;I&#39;m running late&quot;), add or change Nova Calendar note cards and day cards (&quot;make 31 October a Halloween day card&quot;), look at the studio&#39;s Acuity bookings, check the Acuity login, research anything on the web (with links to where it came from), look at any public webpage (it opens it in a browser of its own, never the Acuity one, and sees a screenshot and the page&#39;s contents), or ask how Nova Agent is doing. Whatever it changes shows up as a little chip under its reply, and the plan beside it redraws straight away.</p>\n<p>On a wide screen the three columns sit side by side above Nova Agent, all on one screen; on a phone or a very short window they stack (Nova Agent first) and the page scrolls.</p>\n<h4>Nova Missions and Nova Quests</h4>\n<p>Today: the now card, then Ahead, Done, Coming up, Pulses and Needs a slot. Coming up: the next few days at a glance. Nova Missions: each one&#39;s progress ring and its quests.</p>\n<p>Tell Nova Agent any goal, in the studio or anywhere in your life (&quot;release the EP by 1 December&quot;, &quot;I&#39;ve fallen behind on my 52-release challenge and have two months left: I need a content strategy, a release strategy and the quickest way to film and edit it all&quot;) and it becomes a <strong>Mission</strong>. Claude (<code>src/quests/planner.ts</code>) writes:</p>\n<ul><li>a <strong>strategy</strong>, in the sections the goal needs (release, content, production, filming and editing, a typical week, how to catch up), with the maths done;</li><li><strong>tracks</strong> (workstreams such as Music, Content, Release, Gear), each with its own colour and progress bar;</li><li>dated <strong>milestones</strong>, which also appear in Nova Calendar as ◆ cards;</li><li><strong>Nova Quests</strong>, each with a length, a priority, a deadline, what it waits for, where it happens and the travel to get there. Work that repeats per item (every song&#39;s finish → mix → film → edit → post) is described once as a <strong>series</strong> and written out here with exact spacing;</li><li>the <strong>assumptions</strong> it made and the <strong>questions</strong> that would sharpen it. Answer them in the mission&#39;s <strong>Refine</strong> tab (or just tell Nova Agent) and the work that&#39;s left is planned again;</li><li><strong>research</strong>: when current facts would make the plan better (how a platform works now, distributor lead times, prices, opening hours), it searches the web and reads pages while it plans. What it used is listed under &quot;Researched on the web&quot; in the mission&#39;s Plan tab, each with a link, and only pages it really read are kept.</li></ul>\n<p>Tap a mission to open its plan: <strong>Plan</strong> (tracks and strategy), <strong>Roadmap</strong> (milestones by month, tick them off), <strong>Nova Quests</strong> (by week, filtered by track) and <strong>Refine</strong>.</p>\n<p>As you type to Nova Agent, a <strong>cue</strong> above the box shows what the message will become (Nova Mission, Quest, repeating quest, pulse, blocked time, quest update, mission detail, calendar card, studio bookings or a question) and what it picked out (deadline, time, length, how often, how many, platforms).</p>\n<p>Then a planner with no AI in it (<code>src/quests/scheduler.ts</code>) fits every quest into your days:</p>\n<ul><li>around your <strong>rhythm</strong>: get up, a start-up time, wind-down and bedtime, a buffer between quests, a proper break after long ones, a cap on quest hours per day, and <strong>days off</strong> with no quests at all (the ⚙ button; say &quot;I can&#39;t work Sundays&quot; and the planner sets it);</li><li>around Nova Calendar entries and any <strong>blocked time</strong>;</li><li>most urgent first (the least slack between when it may start and its deadline, weighted by priority), never before the quests it depends on, in the part of the day it suits;</li><li>as far ahead as the furthest deadline needs (up to a year), not just the rhythm&#39;s &quot;plan ahead&quot; days;</li><li>with <strong>travel time</strong> in front of anything somewhere else, and a &quot;leave by&quot; reminder;</li><li>flagging anything that can&#39;t make its deadline as <strong>at risk</strong>, and anything that can&#39;t be placed at all under <strong>Needs a slot</strong>, with the reason.</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Any length, from a second to forever</strong> (<code>src/quests/lengths.ts</code>):</p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Kind</th><th>Example</th><th>How it&#39;s planned</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Seconds</td><td>&quot;Text Dana back&quot;, 30 s</td><td>Placed to the second; quick ones go back to back</td></tr><tr><td>Hours</td><td>&quot;Comp the vocal takes&quot;, 1 h 15 min</td><td>One slot</td></tr><tr><td>Long work</td><td>&quot;Mix the EP&quot;, 8 h</td><td>Split into sessions of up to 3 hours (&quot;part 2 of 3&quot;), in order</td></tr><tr><td>Ongoing</td><td>&quot;Practise scales&quot;, 20 min a day</td><td>A session every day, weekday, week or any interval, until you end it or its deadline passes</td></tr><tr><td>Pulse</td><td>&quot;Drink some water&quot;, every 2 min</td><td>Repeats faster than every 5 minutes run on their own exact timer (down to every second), only while you&#39;re awake, without taking slots in the plan</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><strong>Pace limits</strong> (in the rhythm) are the safety switch: on, quests start a few minutes from now, on 5-minute marks, with buffers and breaks; off, they can start right now, to the second, back to back.</p>\n<p>It <strong>re-plans on every change</strong>: finish early and the rest moves up, press Not now and it finds a new slot, and a quest left unanswered an hour after its end is moved and you&#39;re told where. Nova Missions can be paused, resumed or removed, and a mission finishes itself when its last quest is done.</p>\n<h4>Reminders, check-ins and chimes</h4>\n<p>Checked every 10 seconds (<code>src/quests/reminders.ts</code>):</p>\n<ul><li>a <strong>reminder</strong> before each quest (or before you need to leave), with Start and In 15 min;</li><li>a <strong>check-in</strong> when it should be finished: Done, +15 min or Move it;</li><li>a <strong>morning plan</strong> and an <strong>evening wrap-up</strong>;</li><li>each <strong>pulse</strong> as one ticking card that counts its beats, instead of a pile of pop-ups.</li></ul>\n<p>Each kind has its own bright <strong>chime</strong>, made live in the browser. Press 🔔 for <strong>system notifications</strong>, which arrive even with Nova Agent in the background and bring it back when clicked. With the rhythm&#39;s phone setting on, they also go to the <strong>your phone</strong>, where Nova Agent, Quest and Mission alerts each have their own label, check-ins stay on screen until they&#39;re answered, and a pulse replaces its last notification.</p>\n<h4>Nova Quests on the phones</h4>\n<p>Nova Agent sends its plan (missions, quests, pulses, and Nova Calendar&#39;s note and day cards) to Nova Bot&#39;s worker whenever it changes, and every minute so &quot;now&quot; keeps moving (<code>src/quests/portalsync.ts</code>). Nova Portal&#39;s Nova Quests and Nova Calendar tabs show it on the staff phones, and taps made there (Done, Start, Not now, Skip, pause a mission) come back with each job check and are carried out within about a second.</p>\n<h4>Nova Calendar, built in</h4>\n<p>Nova Calendar is a panel (<code>web/calendar/</code>) served at <code>/calendar/</code>. Inside Nova Agent it saves to <code>data/calendar.json</code> instead of only the browser, so Nova Agent, the planner and the calendar always see the same note cards and day cards. Every planned quest and blocked time shows up in it as a note card (✦ for a quest, ∞ for a repeat, ⚠ when at risk, ✓ when done), and its theme colours the whole of Nova Agent. The <strong>Nova Calendar</strong> tab fits it to the plan column with no scrolling.</p>\n<h4>The Nova Agent, inside or in a window</h4>\n<p>The ✦ Nova Agent launcher, with the &quot;Open apps&quot; switch. Nova Calendar opened inside Nova Agent from the rail.</p>\n<p>The rail down the left (and the ✦ Nova Agent launcher) holds every Nova app: Nova Portal, Nova Notes, Nova Calendar, Nova Bot, the visualizer, Nova Index, Admin, all links and features, Nova Observatory and the code. One switch decides where they open:</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Inside Nova Agent</strong>: the app takes the middle of the screen, with &quot;← Nova Agent&quot;, reload and &quot;↗ open in its own window&quot; above it. Nova Agent serves Nova Calendar, Nova Notes (<code>/notes/</code>), Nova Observatory (<code>/observatory/</code>) and Nova Index (<code>/app/memory/</code>) itself, from the folders next to it, so they open inside in any browser.</li><li><strong>New window</strong>: each app in its own tab or window.</li></ul>\n<p>Admin and the links page always get their own window: they refuse to be shown inside other pages, which keeps their sign-in safe, and Nova Agent says so once.</p>\n<h4>Sound effects</h4>\n<p>Novacane&#39;s soft glass tones, warm under-tones and breaths of air for every tap, tab, switch, open, close, send, done and delete, made live with the Web Audio API (no sound files). Ambient, not beeps: everything swells in, chords bloom together rather than running up like a game, and a tap is a low felt touch. They&#39;re in D lydian, the same key as the ambient music, so the two always sound right together; they&#39;re placed across left and right and washed in a little reverb and echo, and kept quiet: calm, relaxing and lush, never loud or chatty. Every sound swells in slowly, with a warm, soft top end and plenty of space; never more than three notes at once; the small sounds (taps, tabs, menus) keep well apart and the same one doesn&#39;t come straight back.</p>\n<p><strong>Quiet extras</strong>, barely there and with their own switch (Nova Portal → Options → Quiet extras, or on a phone the gear → Quiet extras): a breath of air as you scroll (quieter the slower you go, a few times a second at most), the softest touch per key when typing in a box, tones that rise and fall as you drag a slider, a sound when you pick up and put down something you drag (Nova Calendar&#39;s note cards, with a tiny tick at each step), and an extra-faint shimmer as the mouse arrives on a tile. They&#39;re off to begin with (calm first) and only heard while sound effects are on. Nova Agent chimes when it answers, and a short &quot;hello&quot; (D–A–C♯–F♯) plays when sounds are switched on. The 🔊 switch at the top left turns them off (on a phone: the gear → Sound), and the choice is remembered on that device. It&#39;s the same <code>web/shared/sfx.js</code> in every panel.</p>\n<p><strong>Every panel sounds like itself</strong>, all in the same key: Nova Notes is paper and pencil, Nova Calendar soft clock ticks and chimes, Nova Portal deep and roomy like its planet, Nova Index droplets that echo away, Nova Observatory the wide night sky, Nova Lossless audio a soft electric piano, Nova Visualizer glass glints, Nova Quests a warm kalimba and Nova Missions a low, steady swell. A button that opens a panel sounds like that panel. Different kinds of things have their own sounds (switches, tick boxes, menus, lists, links, tabs…), each button has its own notes, and no sound plays exactly the same way twice running, so they never get too familiar. When sounds come thick and fast they get softer by themselves, and come back after a pause.</p>\n<h4>The panels bar and motion</h4>\n<p>It shows and hides itself (<strong>Auto</strong>, the default), with the title panel: see &quot;Auto show and hide&quot; below. Over an open panel or on the home, it moves as one piece and only slides. On a tablet or a phone on its side the bar is one row, each group as wide as its places and their names need (<code>--tg-cols</code>, set by <code>phone.js</code>), so no name is squeezed or cut.</p>\n<p>Each panel&#39;s icon is from one line-art set, in its own colour (Nova Notes amber, Nova Calendar moon-violet, Nova Index teal…) blended with the theme&#39;s accent, so the icons change with the theme and still keep their own mood. The bar shows and hides itself (Auto, the default), or is <strong>Always shown</strong> or <strong>Always hidden</strong>: see &quot;Auto show and hide&quot; below (<code>web/agent/assets/bar.js</code> and <code>bar.css</code>).</p>\n<p>Along the bottom on a computer: every panel in its four groups (Apps, Tasks, Tools, Helpers), edge to edge. It&#39;s the same bar whatever is open; with a panel open it only gets smaller. Motion is light (only scale and opacity move): buttons and tiles press in softly, the open panel&#39;s tile breathes, and panels fade in as they open (<code>web/shared/inside.js</code>, and Nova Calendar&#39;s <code>embed.js</code>). It all stops when the device asks for less motion or Nova Portal&#39;s Options → Animations is off.</p>\n<h4>One look, the top bar, and the status line</h4>\n<p><strong>One theme for everything:</strong> in the Panels window (the gear at the top; on a phone the phone&#39;s gear → Theme &amp; look) pick a theme (Novacane, Solar Flare, Pulsar, Aurora, Eclipse, Quasar or Mono) and every app, task, tool and helper wears it, whatever its own theme setting; &quot;Each panel&#39;s own&quot; goes back to each panel&#39;s own. <strong>Colour everything from my planet</strong> tints it all with the colours of your planet in Nova Portal (Nova Bot sends them with who you are). Saved on the device; every open panel follows at once (<code>web/shared/look.js</code>, loaded first in every panel). With both on, the planet keeps its look (its dark backgrounds and soft light) and the colour you picked takes the buttons, glows and highlights, so every colour choice clearly shows: Pulsar gives cyan, Aurora green and violet, Eclipse gold. With &quot;Each panel&#39;s own&quot;, the planet colours everything as before.</p>\n<p><strong>One title panel everywhere:</strong> Nova Agent&#39;s header on the home and the title panel over every open panel (an app, a plan, a tool or a helper) are the same bar (<code>web/shared/topbar.css</code>, class <code>nv-topbar</code>): the same height (52px on a computer, 48px on a phone), the full width, the same look, the same controls in the same places. Left: ← back (with a panel open), sound, music, Live. Middle: Nova Agent&#39;s mark, or the panel&#39;s icon and name (tap it to switch panels). Right: the Nova Manual, the planet (sign in and out, your Nova Portal account), Install, Reload (with a panel open) and the gear. Compact but easy to hit: every control is at least 40px on a computer and 44px on a phone (plain round buttons without their own borders), with plain, readable words (13px and up; no small spaced-out word above the name). One Install control (the chip: it also does the browser&#39;s one-tap install when it&#39;s offered). On a phone Live is its coloured dot and Install its icon. There&#39;s never a second bar. The panel sits in its own box under it (<code>#viewer-body</code>). <code>scripts/check-bars.mjs</code> fails a title panel that differs from the home&#39;s header in height or width, or a control smaller than 40/44px.</p>\n<p><strong>Auto show and hide (the default):</strong> the title panel and the navigation panel (with its status row) slide out of the way while you work, and the panel (or the home) grows into all the room they leave; they&#39;re back the moment you want them. Back at once, with no wait: the mouse at the very top or bottom edge of the screen, a tap or a swipe at the edge (a thin strip there; on a touch screen a small handle at the bottom), Tab into a bar, or scrolling up inside a panel. Away: when the mouse has been away from a bar for 1.5 s, or on a phone or touch screen after scrolling down a good way on purpose; never while the mouse is on it, the keyboard is in it, or a window, menu or the sign-in card is open. The bars only slide (transform and opacity: in 0.1 s, away in 0.09 s; at once when the device asks for less motion), and the content changes size once per move, never during a slide: a bar going away gives up its row after its slide, a bar coming back slides in over the edge of the content first and then takes its row (<code>web/agent/assets/bar.js</code>, <code>bar.css</code>). Panels report their mouse, scrolling and swipes to Nova Agent, so it works over any panel. <strong>Always shown</strong> and <strong>Always hidden</strong> are the other choices, for each bar: the Panels window (the PANELS button) or the gear (Bar, Top bar); remembered on the device. Measured by <code>node scripts/check-autohide.mjs </code>: at computer and phone sizes, on the home and over a panel, both bars go after 1.5 s, the content then fills the window minus the bars still showing, each bar is back within a frame plus 120 ms with the content kept still while it slides and no slow frame, the keyboard in a bar keeps it, Always shown never moves and Always hidden starts away. <code>node scripts/check-fit.mjs … --bars away</code> checks every panel again in the bigger room.</p>\n<p><strong>One screen:</strong> inside Nova Agent a panel&#39;s page never scrolls, and neither does its `<code>: the panel fills the space between the bars, and only a box inside it scrolls when it has more than fits (Portal&#39;s open section, a list, a column, a card). Where there&#39;s room things sit side by side: Portal&#39;s Today (numbers left, today&#39;s calendar and new enquiries right), Quests&#39; groups and days as columns, Lossless&#39;s four cards in a row, the Visualizer&#39;s three columns; Calendar&#39;s month shares the screen with the day&#39;s plan on phones; the Fixer&#39;s open tab scrolls under its numbers and tabs. Panels and Portal&#39;s sections show at once when they open (no fade in). </code>scripts/check-fit.mjs<code> fails a page or a </code>` that scrolls inside Nova Agent.</p>\n<p><strong>The status line</strong> is the bottom row of the navigation bar, inside its frame, below the icons (the panels strip on a computer, the bar on a phone), on the home and with any panel open: the version and build, the latest change in a few still words (for the group or panel you point at, or the one that&#39;s open), when you came on and were last off, what you&#39;ve done lately (tap it for the list), the date (&quot;Mon 12 Oct&quot;) and a 12-hour clock (<code>web/agent/assets/status.js</code>; the words come from <code>web/shared/status-data.js</code>, made by <code>npm run status</code>, which <code>npm run manual</code> runs too). Every part shows; when the bar is narrower than the line it wraps onto a second row. Always hidden hides it everywhere; each part (the date too) can be switched off in the Panels window.</p>\n<p><strong>The icons</strong> are little glowing scenes of space, each on its own small Novacane nebula (its own colour mixed with the theme&#39;s): the Novacane sigil in an orbiting orb (Nova Agent), a ringed planet and its moon (Nova Portal), the moon over its phases (Nova Calendar), a quill writing a constellation (Nova Notes), a glowing star cluster (Nova Index), a comet streaking to a star flag (Nova Quests), a rocket (Nova Missions), a pulsar (Nova Lossless audio), a spiral galaxy (Nova Visualizer), a domed observatory under the moon (Nova Observatory) and a star atlas (Nova Manual). The panels bar itself is a strip of night sky: nebula light in the theme&#39;s colours, faint stars, the sigil softly in the corner, a glowing edge and shimmering group names; its tiles sit right on the sky (no boxes), with a soft glow behind the one you point at and a line of light under the open one. The same glowing edge and nebula light are on the top bar, the columns, an open panel&#39;s frame, the pop-up windows and the status line, and every button, tab and box (in the panels too) glows the same way when you&#39;re on it (<code>glow.css</code>). On a computer the top bar, the panels bar and the status line are only as wide as what&#39;s in them. <strong>Centred text:</strong> all text in Nova Agent and its panels is centred (Panels window → Centre all text switches it off); what you write in a Nova Notes document, and code, keep their own alignment. It comes and goes with a quick spring, its tiles popping in one after another. The gear (settings) is on computers too: it opens the Panels window.</p>\n<h4>The latest polish</h4>\n<ul><li>The panels bar is smaller, with each group&#39;s name centred between two fine lines of light.</li><li>The status line is plain words with small icons: the version, what&#39;s new (&quot;Nova Calendar: note cards back&quot;), &quot;Here since …&quot;, &quot;Last left …&quot;, what you did last (&quot;Opened Nova Notes · 2 min ago&quot;: tap for the list) and the day and time.</li><li>The two settings buttons look different: sliders at the top for Look &amp; layout (theme, bars, text), and the sun and moon over the horizon on Nova Quests for your daily rhythm.</li><li>Nova Quests fits more on one screen: the next thing is a full card, the rest slim one-line rows (time and title) that open on a tap.</li><li>Scrollbars everywhere are slim, rounded and glowing in the theme&#39;s colours, with soft sounds when you take hold of one, as you drag it (a tone that follows where you are) and let go.</li><li>The sky behind Nova Agent is a deep nebula with a faint band of the galaxy and far galaxies, and it takes on the colour of the app that&#39;s open, slowly.</li><li>The columns&#39; titles are centred, and so is the conversation (every message in the middle).</li></ul>\n<h4>Every window size</h4>\n<p>Nova Agent fits whatever size its window is: computer windows down to 481px tall keep the computer layout, getting tighter as they get shorter (a slimmer header, Nova Agent&#39;s suggestions in one row you swipe, smaller bars); narrower computer windows get slimmer side columns and smaller buttons; tablets and windows between phone and computer size get the bar in one centred row; and phones keep their own layout. In Auto, the mouse anywhere in the lower part of the window (its bottom 14%) brings the panels bar up. Inside Nova Agent, Nova Notes never runs off the screen: its toolbar wraps, and the page starts as tall as the window.</p>\n<h4>Today in music (the front page)</h4>\n<p>Under the welcome, until you start talking to Nova Agent: small cards, a line or two each. The <strong>Top 10 worldwide</strong> (live: the songs most played on Apple Music across 12 countries, via Nova Bot&#39;s /music-world, kept 6 hours), <strong>popular genres</strong>, <strong>budget gear</strong> (what each does, rough price), the <strong>music industry</strong> (IFPI Global Music Report 2026: $31.7bn in 2025, up 6.4%), a musician&#39;s <strong>quote of the day</strong> with their picture (from Wikipedia; &quot;attributed&quot; when its origin isn&#39;t certain) and a <strong>song of the day</strong> (named and described, with a link to its lyrics: lyrics themselves are copyrighted). A tap on a card opens a short list. Data: <code>web/agent/assets/music-data.js</code>.</p>\n<h4>Phones and tablets</h4>\n<p>Nova Agent knows when it&#39;s on a phone or a tablet from the device itself (iPads included), not just the window&#39;s size (<code>look.js</code> puts is-touch / is-phone / is-tablet on every page). There it&#39;s made for fingers and kept light: bigger tap targets, no zoom when you tap into a box, nothing that needs a mouse, no frosted-glass blur or drifting sky. On a tablet showing the computer layout the bars hide and show with your swipes and a handle brings them back. The conversation&#39;s pages turn with a sideways swipe (<code>web/agent/assets/touch.css</code>).</p>\n<h4>Install or remove the apps (and help)</h4>\n<p>An <strong>App</strong> button (the phone with an arrow, in the top bar of Nova Agent and of the Nova Portal app, on Nova Portal&#39;s sign-in screen, in the phone&#39;s gear menu and in the Panels window) opens one sheet: Nova Agent and Nova Portal, each with <strong>Install</strong> and <strong>Remove</strong>, and the steps for exactly this device (it reads iPhone or iPad and its iOS version, Android phone or tablet and its version, and the browser). Android and computers get a real one-tap install when the browser offers it; iPhone and iPad can&#39;t be installed by a website, so it shows Safari&#39;s two taps. <strong>Remove</strong> wipes the app from the device (notifications off, signed out, saved data and offline files gone; shared notes and everything online stay safe), then shows the one step that deletes its icon. <strong>Something not working?</strong> covers the in-between problems: installed but can&#39;t find it, no install option, opens in the browser, no notifications, an old name or picture, signing in again, two copies, stuck or out of date, or a phone too old (<code>web/shared/install.js</code>, <code>install.css</code>).</p>\n<h4>Updates arrive by themselves</h4>\n<p>Phones don&#39;t reload an app from the home screen: they wake the copy still in memory. So Nova Agent and the Nova Portal app ask Nova Bot which version is live (<code>/app-version</code>, new with every deploy) whenever they&#39;re opened or come back to the front, and every 10 minutes while on screen; when it&#39;s new they refresh themselves (waiting while you type or have a window open), then say &quot;Updated ✦&quot; (<code>web/shared/update.js</code>). A new name or icon still needs the app re-added on iPhone and iPad (Apple never updates those); Android updates them by itself within about a day.</p>\n<h4>Ambient music</h4>\n<p>Quiet, never-ending Novacane ambient music: slow warm pads, a soft bass, star-like bells, now and then a short soft electric-piano phrase, and a faint ocean of air, all made live (no sound files, nothing downloaded) by <code>web/shared/ambient.js</code>. It&#39;s off until you switch it on with the ♫ switch at the top left (on a phone: the gear → Music; in Nova Portal: its music button). There&#39;s one player for the whole app, in Nova Agent&#39;s main page, so it carries on while panels open and close, and every switch shows the same state. On or off is remembered on the device: when it was on, it starts again on your first tap (browsers only allow sound after a tap). The volume is Nova Portal&#39;s Options → Ambient music volume.</p>\n<p>Coming next: music with bass and melody, seven moods.</p>\n<h4>Nova Index: it remembers</h4>\n<p>Before each reply and each mission plan, Nova Agent asks Nova Index (the suite&#39;s shared memory, on Nova Bot&#39;s worker) for the few facts that matter: the studio&#39;s, and those of the person Nova Agent works for (found by itself: see below). The read is quick (a short timeout and a 30-second cache) and never holds a reply up for long. After each conversation, the exchange is handed back to be learned from, in the background (<code>src/memory.ts</code>). It reads studio and staff memory only, never customers&#39;.</p>\n<p>Nova Index itself opens inside Nova Agent from the rail, through Nova Agent&#39;s own key: you can browse and edit the studio&#39;s and staff memory there, while approvals of customers&#39; facts stay behind a Nova Portal sign-in. Without <code>AGENT_NOVA_KEY</code>, memory is simply switched off.</p>\n<h4>The Acuity helper</h4>\n<p>The job Nova Agent was built for. It drives Acuity&#39;s admin pages in a real Chromium, the way a person would, for the jobs Acuity&#39;s API can&#39;t do.</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Jobs from Nova Bot</strong> (<code>src/jobs.ts</code>): it waits on the worker for jobs and picks each one up within about a second. Today that&#39;s <code>change</code> jobs (staff asked in Nova Portal to change a booking&#39;s session type, price or paid status); it does them in Acuity, checks the result and reports back to staff phones. Customer bookings go through Acuity&#39;s own booking page, so the deposit is always paid first; <code>book</code> jobs are still understood here.</li><li><strong>Logs itself in</strong> and saves the session; logs back in when it expires.</li><li><strong>Self-healing element finder</strong> (<code>src/heal/</code>): every task says <em>what</em> it wants (&quot;the Cancel Appointment button&quot;), never <em>how</em> to find it. <code>resolve()</code> tries the selector memory first (instant and free), then asks Claude, checks the answer against the page, and remembers it.</li><li><strong>Appointment actions</strong> (<code>src/acuity/</code>) from the command line: list, search, book, cancel, edit and reschedule.</li><li><strong>Safety first</strong>: a dry-run mode that stops before every final click, a second layer that refuses any change-making request, exact-match rules for cancel and edit, and a read-only healthcheck every morning. See Safety.</li></ul>\n<h4>The visualizer</h4>\n<p>Anatomy, live steps, what the browser sees and the selector memory.  Where the agent last found each element, and how often.</p>\n<p><code>/visualizer</code> shows the Acuity helper at work: its anatomy, every step in plain English, what the browser sees, and its memory. Its buttons only ever run read-only tasks (check the login, the next 7 or last 30 days, a read-only tour, the healthcheck), and <strong>Wipe memory</strong> lets you watch it heal again. These screenshots are of an idle visualizer: at work it shows real Acuity pages and client names, which is why Nova Agent only ever listens on <code>127.0.0.1</code>.</p>\n<h4>An app for your launcher</h4>\n<p>Open  (on a phone: Share → Add to Home Screen) and press <strong>Install app</strong>: Nova Agent opens in its own window, with shortcuts to Today, a new mission, Nova Calendar and the visualizer. Its service worker shows reminders as system notifications; nothing is cached, because Nova Agent is its own server on the same machine.</p>","text":"Nova Agent, in the middle Nova Agent ( src/chat.ts ) is Claude with tools. Ask it what to do next (\"What should I do now?\" gives one clear recommendation), plan a mission, block out an evening (\"I'm out tonight from 7 to 11\"), push your day back (\"I'm running late\"), add or change Nova Calendar note cards and day cards (\"make 31 October a Halloween day card\"), look at the studio's Acuity bookings, check the Acuity login, research anything on the web (with links to where it came from), look at any public webpage (it opens it in a browser of its own, never the Acuity one, and sees a screenshot and the page's contents), or ask how Nova Agent is doing. Whatever it changes shows up as a little chip under its reply, and the plan beside it redraws straight away. On a wide screen the three columns sit side by side above Nova Agent, all on one screen; on a phone or a very short window they stack (Nova Agent first) and the page scrolls. Nova Missions and Nova Quests Today: the now card, then Ahead, Done, Coming up, Pulses and Needs a slot. Coming up: the next few days at a glance. Nova Missions: each one's progress ring and its quests. Tell Nova Agent any goal, in the studio or anywhere in your life (\"release the EP by 1 December\", \"I've fallen behind on my 52-release challenge and have two months left: I need a content strategy, a release strategy and the quickest way to film and edit it all\") and it becomes a Mission . Claude ( src/quests/planner.ts ) writes: a strategy , in the sections the goal needs (release, content, production, filming and editing, a typical week, how to catch up), with the maths done; tracks (workstreams such as Music, Content, Release, Gear), each with its own colour and progress bar; dated milestones , which also appear in Nova Calendar as ◆ cards; Nova Quests , each with a length, a priority, a deadline, what it waits for, where it happens and the travel to get there. Work that repeats per item (every song's finish → mix → film → edit → post) is described once as a series and written out here with exact spacing; the assumptions it made and the questions that would sharpen it. Answer them in the mission's Refine tab (or just tell Nova Agent) and the work that's left is planned again; research : when current facts would make the plan better (how a platform works now, distributor lead times, prices, opening hours), it searches the web and reads pages while it plans. What it used is listed under \"Researched on the web\" in the mission's Plan tab, each with a link, and only pages it really read are kept. Tap a mission to open its plan: Plan (tracks and strategy), Roadmap (milestones by month, tick them off), Nova Quests (by week, filtered by track) and Refine . As you type to Nova Agent, a cue above the box shows what the message will become (Nova Mission, Quest, repeating quest, pulse, blocked time, quest update, mission detail, calendar card, studio bookings or a question) and what it picked out (deadline, time, length, how often, how many, platforms). Then a planner with no AI in it ( src/quests/scheduler.ts ) fits every quest into your days: around your rhythm : get up, a start-up time, wind-down and bedtime, a buffer between quests, a proper break after long ones, a cap on quest hours per day, and days off with no quests at all (the ⚙ button; say \"I can't work Sundays\" and the planner sets it); around Nova Calendar entries and any blocked time ; most urgent first (the least slack between when it may start and its deadline, weighted by priority), never before the quests it depends on, in the part of the day it suits; as far ahead as the furthest deadline needs (up to a year), not just the rhythm's \"plan ahead\" days; with travel time in front of anything somewhere else, and a \"leave by\" reminder; flagging anything that can't make its deadline as at risk , and anything that can't be placed at all under Needs a slot , with the reason. Any length, from a second to forever ( src/quests/lengths.ts ): Kind Example How it's planned Seconds \"Text Dana back\", 30 s Placed to the second"},{"id":"safety-3","title":"Safety","html":"<ul><li><strong>Dry run</strong> (<code>DRY_RUN=true</code>): book, cancel and edit stop before the final click. As a second layer, the browser refuses any request that could change something in Acuity. Acuity&#39;s cancel is a plain GET, so this also blocks anything carrying Acuity&#39;s <code>__csrf_magic</code> change token.</li><li><strong>The healthcheck</strong> always runs with that second layer on, even when live.</li><li><strong>Cancel and edit</strong> need an exact date and time match (and the client&#39;s name if given). If more than one appointment matches, the agent refuses.</li><li><strong>Nova Agent is read-only in Acuity</strong>: it can look at bookings and check the login, never book, move or cancel.</li><li><strong>The page&#39;s buttons</strong> only work from the page itself (a custom header other websites can&#39;t send), and Nova Agent only listens on this computer.</li><li><strong>Alerts</strong> (login problems, failed healthchecks) go to the console, <code>data/alerts.log</code>, and staff phones through the worker when <code>AGENT_NOVA_KEY</code> is set. Repeats are held back for six hours.</li></ul>","text":"Dry run ( DRY_RUN=true ): book, cancel and edit stop before the final click. As a second layer, the browser refuses any request that could change something in Acuity. Acuity's cancel is a plain GET, so this also blocks anything carrying Acuity's __csrf_magic change token. The healthcheck always runs with that second layer on, even when live. Cancel and edit need an exact date and time match (and the client's name if given). If more than one appointment matches, the agent refuses. Nova Agent is read-only in Acuity : it can look at bookings and check the login, never book, move or cancel. The page's buttons only work from the page itself (a custom header other websites can't send), and Nova Agent only listens on this computer. Alerts (login problems, failed healthchecks) go to the console, data/alerts.log , and staff phones through the worker when AGENT_NOVA_KEY is set. Repeats are held back for six hours."},{"id":"works-with-4","title":"Works with","html":"<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Project</th><th>What it is</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong><a href=\"https://github.com/tuniveza/nova-agent\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">nova-agent</a></strong></td><td>This repo: the studio&#39;s one app, with every panel</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://github.com/tuniveza/nova-bot\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">nova-bot</a></td><td>NovaBot on the website, and Nova Agent&#39;s back end online (sign-in, push, bookings, memory, jobs)</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://github.com/tuniveza/nova-club\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">nova-club</a></td><td>Members&#39; Android app that shows the studio&#39;s busy times</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","text":"Project What it is nova-agent This repo: the studio's one app, with every panel nova-bot NovaBot on the website, and Nova Agent's back end online (sign-in, push, bookings, memory, jobs) nova-club Members' Android app that shows the studio's busy times"}],"built":[{"id":"how-it-works-0","title":"How it works","html":"<pre><code>flowchart LR\n    You[You, on any phone or computer] --&gt; UI[Nova Agent page&lt;br/&gt;Agent · plan · suite]\n    UI --&gt; Chat[Agent&lt;br/&gt;src/chat.ts] --&gt; Claude[Claude]\n    Chat --&gt; Q[(Quests and calendar&lt;br/&gt;data/)]\n    UI --&gt; Q\n    Chat &lt;--&gt;|reads before, learns after| NI[Index&lt;br/&gt;on Nova Bot&#39;s worker]\n    Q --&gt;|plan, reminders| Phone[your phone]\n    S[Staff in Portal] --&gt; NB[Nova Bot Worker]\n    NB --&gt;|queues jobs| J[(agent_jobs)]\n    NA[Acuity helper] --&gt;|&quot;any jobs?&quot; long-poll| J\n    NA --&gt; R[resolve&amp;#40;&amp;#41;] --&gt;|1st| M[(Selector memory)]\n    R --&gt;|if memory fails| Claude\n    NA --&gt; B[Playwright Chromium] --&gt; A[Acuity admin pages]\n    NA --&gt;|result| NB</code></pre>\n<ul><li><strong>No open ports.</strong> Nova Agent only listens on <code>127.0.0.1</code> and only calls out to the worker, so it runs on any always-on computer.</li><li><strong>Limits.</strong> <code>BOOKINGS_PER_VISITOR_PER_DAY</code> (default 2) is sent to the worker each time Nova Agent checks in.</li><li><strong>Nova Notes on Acuity&#39;s real pages</strong> (addresses, buttons, forms, and the safety finding that cancelling is a plain GET) are in docs/acuity-ui-notes.md. Read it before changing cancel, book or edit.</li></ul>","text":"flowchart LR You[You, on any phone or computer] --> UI[Nova Agent page<br/>Nova Agent · plan · suite] UI --> Chat[Nova Agent<br/>src/chat.ts] --> Claude[Claude] Chat --> Q[(Nova Quests and calendar<br/>data/)] UI --> Q Chat <-->|reads before, learns after| NI[Nova Index<br/>on Nova Bot's worker] Q -->|plan, reminders| Phone[your phone] S[Staff in Nova Portal] --> NB[Nova Bot Worker] NB -->|queues jobs| J[(agent_jobs)] NA[Acuity helper] -->|\"any jobs?\" long-poll| J NA --> R[resolve&#40;&#41;] -->|1st| M[(Selector memory)] R -->|if memory fails| Claude NA --> B[Playwright Chromium] --> A[Acuity admin pages] NA -->|result| NB No open ports. Nova Agent only listens on 127.0.0.1 and only calls out to the worker, so it runs on any always-on computer. Limits. BOOKINGS_PER_VISITOR_PER_DAY (default 2) is sent to the worker each time Nova Agent checks in. Nova Notes on Acuity's real pages (addresses, buttons, forms, and the safety finding that cancelling is a plain GET) are in docs/acuity-ui-notes.md. Read it before changing cancel, book or edit."},{"id":"run-it-locally-1","title":"Run it locally","html":"<p>You need Node 22 or newer. Acuity is only needed for the Acuity helper, and only with an account you&#39;re allowed to automate.</p>\n<pre><code>git clone --recurse-submodules https://github.com/tuniveza/nova-agent.git\ncd nova-agent             # (already cloned? git submodule update --init  brings in calendar/)\nnpm install\nnpx playwright install chromium\ncp .env.example .env      # then fill it in\nnpm run visualizer        # http://localhost:4545/agent/\nnpm run login             # for the Acuity helper: log in once in a visible browser window\nnpm start                 # should say &quot;Logged in to Acuity&quot;</code></pre>\n<p>Nova Agent and mission planning need <code>ANTHROPIC_API_KEY</code> in <code>.env</code> (Claude also powers the self-healing element finder). Jobs, phone alerts, the phones&#39; Nova Quests sync and Nova Index memory need <code>AGENT_NOVA_KEY</code>; without it they&#39;re simply off. To bring the calendar up to date with its own repo: <code>git submodule update --remote calendar</code>.</p>\n<p>Nova Observatory, Nova Notes and Nova Index open inside Nova Agent when their repos sit next to this one (<code>../no</code>, <code>../nn</code>, <code>../ni</code>).</p>\n<p><code>DRY_RUN=true</code> is the default in <code>.env.example</code>, so book, cancel and edit stop before the final click until you decide otherwise.</p>\n<h4>A second copy with sample data</h4>\n<p><code>NOVA_DATA_DIR</code> points Nova Agent at another data folder, so a preview or a screenshots copy never touches the real quests, calendar or Acuity session:</p>\n<pre><code>NOVA_DATA_DIR=/tmp/nova-sample AGENT_NOVA_KEY= DRY_RUN=true VISUALIZER_PORT=4547 npm run visualizer</code></pre>\n<p>With <code>AGENT_NOVA_KEY</code> empty it won&#39;t collect jobs, read memory or send phone alerts.</p>\n<h4>Commands</h4>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Command</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>npm run visualizer</code></td><td>Nova Agent itself: Nova Agent and plan at http://localhost:4545, reminders, the phones&#39; Nova Quests sync, the daily healthcheck and job collection (<code>npm run service</code> is the same)</td></tr><tr><td><code>npm start</code></td><td>Checks the Acuity login; logs in automatically if the session expired</td></tr><tr><td><code>npm run login</code></td><td>Opens a visible browser so you can log in to Acuity by hand</td></tr><tr><td><code>npm run list</code></td><td>Appointments for the next 7 days</td></tr><tr><td><code>npm run list -- 2026-09-01 2026-09-30</code></td><td>Appointments between two dates</td></tr><tr><td><code>npm run search -- name=Kai</code></td><td>Search; also <code>type=</code>, <code>email=</code>, <code>phone=</code>, <code>from=</code>, <code>to=</code> (default: today to 60 days ahead)</td></tr><tr><td><code>npm run book -- &quot;type=...&quot; date=... time=... first=... last=... email=...</code></td><td>Book (stops before the final click if <code>DRY_RUN=true</code>)</td></tr><tr><td><code>npm run cancel -- date=... time=... &quot;name=...&quot; [notify=no]</code></td><td>Cancel (same safety)</td></tr><tr><td><code>npm run edit -- date=... time=... &quot;name=...&quot; [phone= email= first= last= type= notes= newdate= newtime=]</code></td><td>Edit and/or reschedule (same safety)</td></tr><tr><td><code>npm run healthcheck</code></td><td>Read-only check that every Acuity page and button can still be found</td></tr><tr><td><code>npm run typecheck</code></td><td>Checks the code for type errors</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h4>Running it all the time</h4>\n<p><code>deploy/agent-nova.service</code> is a systemd <strong>user</strong> service that runs Nova Agent (the page, reminders, the daily healthcheck and job collection), starts when you log in, and restarts if it crashes. Edit its <code>WorkingDirectory</code> to where you cloned the repo, then:</p>\n<pre><code>cp deploy/agent-nova.service ~/.config/systemd/user/\nsystemctl --user daemon-reload\nsystemctl --user enable --now agent-nova\njournalctl --user -u agent-nova -f      # its log\nsystemctl --user restart agent-nova     # after changing .env or code\nloginctl enable-linger $USER            # keep it running when logged out</code></pre>\n<p>On a server with no screen, <code>npm run login</code> won&#39;t work; with <code>ACUITY_EMAIL</code> and <code>ACUITY_PASSWORD</code> set, the agent logs itself in instead. View it through an SSH tunnel: <code>ssh -L 4545:localhost:4545 your-server</code>.</p>","text":"You need Node 22 or newer. Acuity is only needed for the Acuity helper, and only with an account you're allowed to automate. git clone --recurse-submodules https://github.com/tuniveza/nova-agent.git cd nova-agent # (already cloned? git submodule update --init brings in calendar/) npm install npx playwright install chromium cp .env.example .env # then fill it in npm run visualizer # http://localhost:4545/agent/ npm run login # for the Acuity helper: log in once in a visible browser window npm start # should say \"Logged in to Acuity\" Nova Agent and mission planning need ANTHROPIC_API_KEY in .env (Claude also powers the self-healing element finder). Jobs, phone alerts, the phones' Nova Quests sync and Nova Index memory need AGENT_NOVA_KEY ; without it they're simply off. To bring the calendar up to date with its own repo: git submodule update --remote calendar . Nova Observatory, Nova Notes and Nova Index open inside Nova Agent when their repos sit next to this one ( ../no , ../nn , ../ni ). DRY_RUN=true is the default in .env.example , so book, cancel and edit stop before the final click until you decide otherwise. A second copy with sample data NOVA_DATA_DIR points Nova Agent at another data folder, so a preview or a screenshots copy never touches the real quests, calendar or Acuity session: NOVA_DATA_DIR=/tmp/nova-sample AGENT_NOVA_KEY= DRY_RUN=true VISUALIZER_PORT=4547 npm run visualizer With AGENT_NOVA_KEY empty it won't collect jobs, read memory or send phone alerts. Commands Command What it does npm run visualizer Nova Agent itself: Nova Agent and plan at http://localhost:4545, reminders, the phones' Nova Quests sync, the daily healthcheck and job collection ( npm run service is the same) npm start Checks the Acuity login; logs in automatically if the session expired npm run login Opens a visible browser so you can log in to Acuity by hand npm run list Appointments for the next 7 days npm run list -- 2026-09-01 2026-09-30 Appointments between two dates npm run search -- name=Kai Search; also type= , email= , phone= , from= , to= (default: today to 60 days ahead) npm run book -- \"type=...\" date=... time=... first=... last=... email=... Book (stops before the final click if DRY_RUN=true ) npm run cancel -- date=... time=... \"name=...\" [notify=no] Cancel (same safety) npm run edit -- date=... time=... \"name=...\" [phone= email= first= last= type= notes= newdate= newtime=] Edit and/or reschedule (same safety) npm run healthcheck Read-only check that every Acuity page and button can still be found npm run typecheck Checks the code for type errors Running it all the time deploy/agent-nova.service is a systemd user service that runs Nova Agent (the page, reminders, the daily healthcheck and job collection), starts when you log in, and restarts if it crashes. Edit its WorkingDirectory to where you cloned the repo, then: cp deploy/agent-nova.service ~/.config/systemd/user/ systemctl --user daemon-reload systemctl --user enable --now agent-nova journalctl --user -u agent-nova -f # its log systemctl --user restart agent-nova # after changing .env or code loginctl enable-linger $USER # keep it running when logged out On a server with no screen, npm run login won't work; with ACUITY_EMAIL and ACUITY_PASSWORD set, the agent logs itself in instead. View it through an SSH tunnel: ssh -L 4545:localhost:4545 your-server ."},{"id":"configuration-2","title":"Configuration","html":"<p>All settings come from <code>.env</code> (copy <code>.env.example</code>); variables already set in the shell win. Names only here; never commit <code>.env</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Default</th><th>What it&#39;s for</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>ANTHROPIC_API_KEY</code></td><td>–</td><td>Nova Agent, mission planning and the AI element finder</td></tr><tr><td><code>NOVA_MODEL</code></td><td><code>claude-opus-5-5</code></td><td>The Claude model name</td></tr><tr><td><code>NOVA_WORKER_URL</code></td><td>Novacane&#39;s worker</td><td>Nova Bot&#39;s worker: jobs, alerts, the phones&#39; Nova Quests sync and Nova Index</td></tr><tr><td><code>AGENT_NOVA_KEY</code></td><td>–</td><td>Must match the worker&#39;s <code>AGENT_NOVA_KEY</code> secret; blank = no jobs, phone alerts, Nova Quests sync or memory</td></tr><tr><td><code>NOVA_STAFF_ID</code></td><td><em>(found by itself)</em></td><td>Only to force who Nova Agent works for. Without it, Nova Agent picks the studio&#39;s first Nova Portal admin, and anyone can switch it to themselves with <strong>Connect as me</strong> on the Nova Agent badge (kept in <code>data/staff.json</code>)</td></tr><tr><td><code>NOVA_DATA_DIR</code></td><td><code>data/</code></td><td>Where everything is kept; point a second copy somewhere else</td></tr><tr><td><code>ACUITY_EMAIL</code>, <code>ACUITY_PASSWORD</code></td><td>–</td><td>Automatic re-login</td></tr><tr><td><code>ACUITY_ADMIN_URL</code></td><td>Acuity&#39;s appointments page</td><td>The page used to check the login</td></tr><tr><td><code>ACUITY_TIMEZONE</code></td><td><code>Europe/London</code></td><td>The business&#39;s timezone; &quot;today&quot; is worked out in it</td></tr><tr><td><code>JOBS_EVERY_SECONDS</code></td><td><code>10</code></td><td>How long to wait before asking again if the worker answers at once</td></tr><tr><td><code>ACTION_PAUSE_MS</code></td><td><code>150</code></td><td>Longest human-like pause before each click or typed box (0 = flat out)</td></tr><tr><td><code>BOOKINGS_PER_VISITOR_PER_DAY</code></td><td><code>2</code></td><td>A number, or <code>unlimited</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>HEALTHCHECK_CRON</code></td><td><code>0 6 * * *</code></td><td>When the read-only healthcheck runs (UK time)</td></tr><tr><td><code>VISUALIZER_PORT</code></td><td><code>4545</code></td><td>Nova Agent&#39;s page</td></tr><tr><td><code>HEADLESS</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td>Show the browser or not</td></tr><tr><td><code>DRY_RUN</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td>Stop before every final click (the status pill says <strong>Rehearsal</strong>)</td></tr><tr><td><code>NOTIFY_CLIENTS</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td>Tick Acuity&#39;s &quot;Send email to client&quot; when cancelling</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>Your rhythm (wake, sleep, buffers, breaks, the daily cap, reminders, check-ins, briefings, phone alerts and pace limits) is set on the page with ⚙, or by asking Nova Agent.</p>\n<p>Everything Nova Agent writes at run time goes in <code>data/</code> (or <code>NOVA_DATA_DIR</code>), which git ignores: quests and missions (<code>quests.json</code>), the calendar (<code>calendar.json</code>), the saved Acuity session (<code>session.json</code>, which works like a password), the selector memory, the healthcheck result, screenshots, daily logs (<code>logs/.jsonl</code>, which include client names) and <code>alerts.log</code>.</p>","text":"All settings come from .env (copy .env.example ); variables already set in the shell win. Names only here; never commit .env . Name Default What it's for ANTHROPIC_API_KEY – Nova Agent, mission planning and the AI element finder NOVA_MODEL claude-opus-5-5 The Claude model name NOVA_WORKER_URL Novacane's worker Nova Bot's worker: jobs, alerts, the phones' Nova Quests sync and Nova Index AGENT_NOVA_KEY – Must match the worker's AGENT_NOVA_KEY secret; blank = no jobs, phone alerts, Nova Quests sync or memory NOVA_STAFF_ID (found by itself) Only to force who Nova Agent works for. Without it, Nova Agent picks the studio's first Nova Portal admin, and anyone can switch it to themselves with Connect as me on the Nova Agent badge (kept in data/staff.json ) NOVA_DATA_DIR data/ Where everything is kept; point a second copy somewhere else ACUITY_EMAIL , ACUITY_PASSWORD – Automatic re-login ACUITY_ADMIN_URL Acuity's appointments page The page used to check the login ACUITY_TIMEZONE Europe/London The business's timezone; \"today\" is worked out in it JOBS_EVERY_SECONDS 10 How long to wait before asking again if the worker answers at once ACTION_PAUSE_MS 150 Longest human-like pause before each click or typed box (0 = flat out) BOOKINGS_PER_VISITOR_PER_DAY 2 A number, or unlimited HEALTHCHECK_CRON 0 6 * * * When the read-only healthcheck runs (UK time) VISUALIZER_PORT 4545 Nova Agent's page HEADLESS true Show the browser or not DRY_RUN true Stop before every final click (the status pill says Rehearsal ) NOTIFY_CLIENTS true Tick Acuity's \"Send email to client\" when cancelling Your rhythm (wake, sleep, buffers, breaks, the daily cap, reminders, check-ins, briefings, phone alerts and pace limits) is set on the page with ⚙, or by asking Nova Agent. Everything Nova Agent writes at run time goes in data/ (or NOVA_DATA_DIR ), which git ignores: quests and missions ( quests.json ), the calendar ( calendar.json ), the saved Acuity session ( session.json , which works like a password), the selector memory, the healthcheck result, screenshots, daily logs ( logs/.jsonl , which include client names) and alerts.log ."},{"id":"tests-3","title":"Tests","html":"<p><code>npm test</code> runs the Quest reminders on a simulated clock (Vitest fake timers, a pretend Nova Bot worker and a throwaway data folder: <code>test/harness.ts</code>): a reminder every 30 minutes for 4 hours pings exactly 8 times, a ping the worker turns away is retried, Nova Agent being off across a session gives one late &quot;Missed&quot; ping, no session is moved past without a delivery record, taps from the phones count once, and the BST/GMT clock changes. It also checks that edits save or say why (100 rapid edits included), that saves from Nova Calendar merge with changes made elsewhere, and that a mission re-plan keeps quests changed by hand.</p>\n<p><code>npx tsx test/scheduler.test.ts</code> checks the Quest planner (sleep, deadlines, priorities, dependencies, travel, buffers, breaks, the daily cap, blocked time and at-risk flags), and <code>npx tsx test/planner.test.ts</code> checks mission plans (series written out with exact spacing, quests months ahead, one-day windows not being crowded out, and days off). <code>npm run typecheck</code> checks the types, and <code>npm run healthcheck</code> is a read-only check against the real Acuity pages. The worker side of the job queue is covered by Nova Bot&#39;s tests (<code>test/agent-nova.spec.js</code>).</p>\n<p>To try each Acuity action by hand, make a test booking in Acuity under a made-up name with your own email, then run (with <code>DRY_RUN=true</code> first to rehearse):</p>\n<pre><code>npm run edit -- date=2026-10-31 time=17:00 &quot;name=Dana Hollis&quot; phone=07700900789 &quot;notes=Test note from Nova Agent&quot;\nnpm run edit -- date=2026-10-31 time=17:00 &quot;name=Dana Hollis&quot; newdate=2026-11-04 newtime=14:00\nnpm run book -- &quot;type=Voiceover Recording with Engineer - 1 hour&quot; date=2026-11-05 time=15:00 first=Agent last=Test email=you@example.com\nnpm run cancel -- date=2026-11-05 time=15:00 &quot;name=Agent Test&quot;\nnpm run cancel -- date=2026-11-04 time=14:00 &quot;name=Dana Hollis&quot;</code></pre>\n<p>Each one ends with ✓ or ✗. The visualizer&#39;s <strong>Read-only tour</strong> shows the AI element finder at work: the first run heals each element and saves it, the second comes straight from memory.</p>","text":"npm test runs the Quest reminders on a simulated clock (Vitest fake timers, a pretend Nova Bot worker and a throwaway data folder: test/harness.ts ): a reminder every 30 minutes for 4 hours pings exactly 8 times, a ping the worker turns away is retried, Nova Agent being off across a session gives one late \"Missed\" ping, no session is moved past without a delivery record, taps from the phones count once, and the BST/GMT clock changes. It also checks that edits save or say why (100 rapid edits included), that saves from Nova Calendar merge with changes made elsewhere, and that a mission re-plan keeps quests changed by hand. npx tsx test/scheduler.test.ts checks the Quest planner (sleep, deadlines, priorities, dependencies, travel, buffers, breaks, the daily cap, blocked time and at-risk flags), and npx tsx test/planner.test.ts checks mission plans (series written out with exact spacing, quests months ahead, one-day windows not being crowded out, and days off). npm run typecheck checks the types, and npm run healthcheck is a read-only check against the real Acuity pages. The worker side of the job queue is covered by Nova Bot's tests ( test/agent-nova.spec.js ). To try each Acuity action by hand, make a test booking in Acuity under a made-up name with your own email, then run (with DRY_RUN=true first to rehearse): npm run edit -- date=2026-10-31 time=17:00 \"name=Dana Hollis\" phone=07700900789 \"notes=Test note from Nova Agent\" npm run edit -- date=2026-10-31 time=17:00 \"name=Dana Hollis\" newdate=2026-11-04 newtime=14:00 npm run book -- \"type=Voiceover Recording with Engineer - 1 hour\" date=2026-11-05 time=15:00 first=Nova Agent last=Test email=you@example.com npm run cancel -- date=2026-11-05 time=15:00 \"name=Nova Agent Test\" npm run cancel -- date=2026-11-04 time=14:00 \"name=Dana Hollis\" Each one ends with ✓ or ✗. The visualizer's Read-only tour shows the AI element finder at work: the first run heals each element and saves it, the second comes straight from memory."},{"id":"project-layout-4","title":"Project layout","html":"<pre><code>src/visualizer/server.ts  Nova Agent&#39;s server: the pages, the plan&#39;s API, the suite apps, reminders\nsrc/visualizer/chat.html  the main page: Nova Agent rail, Agent, Today, Missions, Calendar\nsrc/visualizer/page.html  the visualizer\nsrc/visualizer/app/       the installable app: manifest, service worker, icons, sfx.js (sound effects)\nsrc/visualizer/calendar-sync.js  makes Calendar save to Nova Agent\nsrc/chat.ts               Agent: Claude with quest, calendar, Acuity (read-only), web and status tools\nsrc/web.ts                web research and seeing webpages (public pages only, in a browser of its own)\nsrc/memory.ts             Index: what the suite remembers, read before replies, learned after\nsrc/config.ts             every setting, read once from .env\nsrc/quests/store.ts       Missions, Quests, blocked time and your rhythm (quests.json)\nsrc/quests/scheduler.ts   the planner: places every quest at a time, to the second (no AI)\nsrc/quests/lengths.ts     lengths from a second to forever: sessions, repeats, plain words\nsrc/quests/pulses.ts      repeats faster than every 5 minutes, each on its own timer\nsrc/quests/planner.ts     turning a goal into a Mission and its Quests (Claude)\nsrc/quests/plan.ts        re-planning, and mirroring quests into Calendar\nsrc/quests/reminders.ts   reminders, check-ins, the morning plan and evening wrap-up\nsrc/quests/deliveries.ts  every phone ping: sent once, checked, retried, logged (data/nova.db)\nsrc/quests/portalsync.ts     the plan to the phones (Portal), and their taps back\nsrc/quests/actions.ts     everything Agent and the page can do with them\nsrc/calendar/store.ts     Calendar&#39;s data (calendar.json, with a revision per save)\nsrc/calendar/page.ts      saves from the calendar page, merged with changes made elsewhere\nsrc/index.ts              command-line entry point for the Acuity helper\nsrc/browser.ts            Chromium, the saved session and the change-blocking safety layer\nsrc/tasks.ts              the tasks (check login, list, search, book, cancel, edit)\nsrc/jobs.ts               collecting jobs from Nova Bot&#39;s worker and reporting results\nsrc/healthcheck.ts        the daily read-only healthcheck\nsrc/alerts.ts             alerts to the console, alerts.log and staff phones\nsrc/llm.ts                the Claude client (JSON answers, with web research for mission plans)\nsrc/heal/                 resolve() and the selector memory\nsrc/acuity/               Acuity pages: login, list, book, cancel, edit, targets, types\nsrc/trace.ts              every step, for the console, logs and visualizer\ntest/harness.ts           the simulated clock for `npm test`\ntest/*.spec.ts            reminders, deliveries, taps from the phones, clock changes\ntest/scheduler.test.ts    planner checks\ntest/planner.test.ts      mission plans: series written out, quests far ahead\ntest/web.test.ts          research only cites pages it read; public webpages only\nweb/agent/                Nova Agent&#39;s own page (chat.html), the visualizer and the installable app\nweb/portal/               the Portal panel (Portal is part of it; old-app-address/ is what\n                          phones that installed Portal from its old address, /app/ still use)\nweb/calendar/ web/notes/ web/index/ web/observatory/ web/lossless/   the other panels\nweb/shared/               themes, sounds, the badge and the Manual (manual-data.js: npm run manual)\nsrc/signin.ts             signing in to Nova Bot as a person, for Portal\nscripts/                  the manual builder; scripts/observatory/ scans and captures your projects\ndocs/apps/&lt;panel&gt;/        each panel&#39;s guide and pictures\ndeploy/agent-nova.service systemd user service\ndocs/acuity-ui-notes.md   what Acuity&#39;s real admin pages look like\ndocs/media/               README images</code></pre>","text":"src/visualizer/server.ts Nova Agent's server: the pages, the plan's API, the suite apps, reminders src/visualizer/chat.html the main page: Nova Agent rail, Nova Agent, Today, Nova Missions, Nova Calendar src/visualizer/page.html the visualizer src/visualizer/app/ the installable app: manifest, service worker, icons, sfx.js (sound effects) src/visualizer/calendar-sync.js makes Nova Calendar save to Nova Agent src/chat.ts Nova Agent: Claude with quest, calendar, Acuity (read-only), web and status tools src/web.ts web research and seeing webpages (public pages only, in a browser of its own) src/memory.ts Nova Index: what the suite remembers, read before replies, learned after src/config.ts every setting, read once from .env src/quests/store.ts Nova Missions, Nova Quests, blocked time and your rhythm (quests.json) src/quests/scheduler.ts the planner: places every quest at a time, to the second (no AI) src/quests/lengths.ts lengths from a second to forever: sessions, repeats, plain words src/quests/pulses.ts repeats faster than every 5 minutes, each on its own timer src/quests/planner.ts turning a goal into a Mission and its Nova Quests (Claude) src/quests/plan.ts re-planning, and mirroring quests into Nova Calendar src/quests/reminders.ts reminders, check-ins, the morning plan and evening wrap-up src/quests/deliveries.ts every phone ping: sent once, checked, retried, logged (data/nova.db) src/quests/portalsync.ts the plan to the phones (Nova Portal), and their taps back src/quests/actions.ts everything Nova Agent and the page can do with them src/calendar/store.ts Nova Calendar's data (calendar.json, with a revision per save) src/calendar/page.ts saves from the calendar page, merged with changes made elsewhere src/index.ts command-line entry point for the Acuity helper src/browser.ts Chromium, the saved session and the change-blocking safety layer src/tasks.ts the tasks (check login, list, search, book, cancel, edit) src/jobs.ts collecting jobs from Nova Bot's worker and reporting results src/healthcheck.ts the daily read-only healthcheck src/alerts.ts alerts to the console, alerts.log and staff phones src/llm.ts the Claude client (JSON answers, with web research for mission plans) src/heal/ resolve() and the selector memory src/acuity/ Acuity pages: login, list, book, cancel, edit, targets, types src/trace.ts every step, for the console, logs and visualizer test/harness.ts the simulated clock for `npm test` test/*.spec.ts reminders, deliveries, taps from the phones, clock changes test/scheduler.test.ts planner checks test/planner.test.ts mission plans: series written out, quests far ahead test/web.test.ts research only cites pages it read; public webpages only web/agent/ Nova Agent's own page (chat.html), the visualizer and the installable app web/portal/ the Nova Portal panel (Nova Portal is part of it; old-app-address/ is what phones that installed Nova Portal from its old address, /app/ still use) web/calendar/ web/notes/ web/index/ web/observatory/ web/lossless/ the other panels web/shared/ themes, sounds, the badge and the Nova Manual (manual-data.js: npm run manual) src/signin.ts signing in to Nova Bot as a person, for Nova Portal scripts/ the manual builder; scripts/observatory/ scans and captures your projects docs/apps/<panel>/ each panel's guide and pictures deploy/agent-nova.service systemd user service docs/acuity-ui-notes.md what Acuity's real admin pages look like docs/media/ README images"}],"news":[],"history":{"total":243,"first":"2026-10-06T15:47:46+01:00","commits":[{"hash":"97eddb3","date":"2026-10-14T12:48:01+01:00","subject":"Fixer looks: a problem seen only signed out is looked at signed out in the fix's copy too (no sample sign-in), so its before and after show the same screen","body":""},{"hash":"d1b4525","date":"2026-10-14T12:29:05+01:00","subject":"Fixer: the looks check. Every hour and after each update it opens Nova Agent and every panel inside it, signed in (Nova Bot's looks account, which can only look) and signed out, at six sizes, and finds big empty gaps, blank panels, low headers, bars covering a panel, extra title panels, scrolling or cut-off pages, cut-off text, errors and slow panels; each a problem with pictures, and a fix for one is looked at again where it was seen, before and after side by side (still waits for Approve). Check looks now in Health, a switch in Settings, and a note when Claude Code isn't signed in. The sweep's layout checks run again (esbuild's __name helper in the page)","body":""},{"hash":"8481f78","date":"2026-10-14T12:26:02+01:00","subject":"One title panel everywhere: the home's header and every panel's title panel are the same bar","body":"The same height (52px on a computer, 48px on a phone), the same full width and the same controls in\nthe same places (left: back, sound, music, Live; middle: the mark or the panel's icon and name;\nright: the Manual, the planet, Install, Reload, the gear). Compact but easier to hit: every control\nis 40px on a computer and 44px on a phone, plain round buttons without their own borders. Easier to\nread: Live and the buttons' words are plain 13px, the name has no small spaced-out word above it,\nand the planet's role word is larger. One Install control in the bar (the chip, which also does\nthe browser's one-tap install). check-bars now fails unequal heights or widths and any control\nsmaller than 40/44px."},{"hash":"40aa7ec","date":"2026-10-14T11:28:43+01:00","subject":"Fix the big gap: a kept-loaded panel frame always goes in the panel's box","body":"After more than six panels had been opened on a computer, the page's first frame was let go and\nnew frames were put beside the panel's box instead of in it, so every panel sat in a short second\nrow under an empty box, running on behind the navigation panel. New scripts/check-gaps.mjs opens\nevery panel twice round and fails a frame outside the box, a panel not filling it, one behind the\nnavigation panel, a scrolled panel page or an empty band at the top."},{"hash":"97ab53f","date":"2026-10-14T07:02:26+01:00","subject":"check-bars: no taps on the panel (the bars no longer come and go with touches, and a tap could open something)","body":""},{"hash":"da25c93","date":"2026-10-14T06:59:46+01:00","subject":"bars test: the groups now sit in the bar's row holder","body":""},{"hash":"b4a697d","date":"2026-10-14T06:53:56+01:00","subject":"Phone bar on a short phone: one row of every place (group names kept) that slides sideways inside the bar, the open place brought into view; two rows on taller phones. Portal's sliding row on a phone has room for each count","body":""},{"hash":"86a3899","date":"2026-10-14T06:36:14+01:00","subject":"Portal on a phone inside Nova Agent: every section on its row, which slides sideways inside itself (More is gone there too)","body":""},{"hash":"b17b42d","date":"2026-10-14T06:26:55+01:00","subject":"check-bars: finds the panel's frame when its address doesn't say the panel, and touches a quiet spot of the panel (not a button that would open or close something)","body":""},{"hash":"3350456","date":"2026-10-14T06:14:02+01:00","subject":"Portal's lanes share lines when there's room (Plans, You and the settings icons beside Today; Admin beside Studio's second half): about half the height at 1280x800. The home's welcome sizes itself in two layouts instead of a dozen when nothing changed, and rounds its size down, so it no longer ends a hair too big and scrolls","body":""},{"hash":"0f35d15","date":"2026-10-14T06:05:13+01:00","subject":"Fixer on a wide screen: all seven parts at once, no tabs (Needs you down the left; Health, Fixer quests and Suggested along the top; Done, Activity and Settings below; each scrolls inside itself); the numbers and Check now in one row; phones keep the tabs","body":""},{"hash":"c3dc189","date":"2026-10-14T06:03:27+01:00","subject":"No menus hiding things: every place stays on the phone's bar (two rows: Apps on top, Plans, Tools and Helpers below, each group as wide as its places; More is gone), and Quests' options sit on screen in a row under its bar (the ⋯ menu is gone; it wraps on a computer and slides sideways inside itself on a phone)","body":""},{"hash":"7d684d4","date":"2026-10-14T05:56:03+01:00","subject":"Index on a wide screen: Browse, Live and Approve all at once (numbers along the top, Browse left, Live and Approve right, each scrolling inside itself; no tabs needed); Live keeps updating while it's on screen; narrower, the tabs are back","body":""},{"hash":"0e275ec","date":"2026-10-14T05:47:48+01:00","subject":"One screen everywhere: inside Nova Agent no panel's page (or its <main>) scrolls; only a box inside it does. Portal's open section scrolls inside itself under compact lanes, Today side by side (numbers | today's calendar + new enquiries); Quests' groups and days as columns; Lossless's four cards in a row; the Visualizer's columns (two by two or stacked on phones, each scrolling inside); the Fixer's open tab under its numbers and tabs; Index's open view; Observatory's decks; Calendar's week, day and list scroll inside their own box and the month shares the screen with the day's plan on phones and tablets. Panels and Portal's sections show at once (no fade in). check-fit.mjs fails a page or a <main> that scrolls inside Nova Agent","body":""},{"hash":"159528a","date":"2026-10-14T05:38:57+01:00","subject":"Calendar inside Nova Agent no longer reloads itself after its own save: on a change it looks at Nova Agent's copy first and only reloads for a real change from elsewhere (no 1-second blink every time)","body":""},{"hash":"670b20d","date":"2026-10-14T05:29:41+01:00","subject":"Nova Agent's link comes back within seconds after a deploy: an attempt that hasn't opened in 12 s (not 45) starts again, checked every 4 s (not 15), and retries are at most 10 s apart (not 30), so Nova isn't \"off\" for a minute each time Nova Bot restarts","body":""},{"hash":"4c9b060","date":"2026-10-14T05:16:02+01:00","subject":"perf-live: measures a returning visit (after Nova's files have settled on the device) and the page that stays when Nova Agent reloads itself","body":""},{"hash":"fe359a5","date":"2026-10-14T05:15:55+01:00","subject":"Faster Nova: the panels' files are fetched quietly a few seconds after the service worker first starts, so even a first visit's first panel opens fast","body":""},{"hash":"fbc3aa2","date":"2026-10-14T05:01:06+01:00","subject":"Faster Nova: a page says which deploy it's from (X-Nova-Build), so the service worker uses the files it keeps at once instead of asking for the list first (the list only when a deploy is new); navigation preload, so a page never waits for the service worker to wake","body":""},{"hash":"32e5538","date":"2026-10-14T04:43:35+01:00","subject":"Faster Nova: the service worker keeps Nova's own files on the device by fingerprint (/nova-build.json from each deploy: used straight from the device while unchanged, only changed files fetched after a deploy, the other panels' files fetched quietly after Nova Agent opens, Google's fonts kept); the last panels opened stay loaded on a computer too (six; Lossless audio still closes for real); the Manual's \"new\" dot reads manual-news.js (a few bytes) instead of the whole 540 KB manual; scripts/perf-live.mjs measures the live site","body":""},{"hash":"7828f7e","date":"2026-10-14T04:39:28+01:00","subject":"One slim title panel with a panel open: Nova Agent's header becomes that panel's title panel (← back, its icon and name, Reload, with sound, music, Live, the planet, Install, Panels and the gear right there; 48px on a computer, 44px on a phone) instead of a second bar under it; the status line is the bottom row inside the navigation bar's frame, below the icons, on the home and every panel, every part showing (wraps onto a second row when narrow)","body":""},{"hash":"a341eb4","date":"2026-10-14T04:09:13+01:00","subject":"Bars always shown: the panels bar and the top bar stay in the page on every panel (no hiding, sliding or waiting); the old Auto is gone and a device that had it gets Always shown; Always hidden is still a choice","body":""},{"hash":"c663224","date":"2026-10-14T03:56:51+01:00","subject":"The bar in one row (tablet, short or zoomed-in window, phone on its side): every place the same width whichever group it's in, each group just as wide as its places, groups centred together; names never overlap (too long: …)","body":""},{"hash":"e55c220","date":"2026-10-14T03:30:02+01:00","subject":"Plans is Quests and Missions: today's plan is no longer a place of its own on the bar, in More or in the Panels window (Quests opens on Today); old links to it, and a phone that was on it, open Quests. Quests in the bars screenshots","body":""},{"hash":"8e178e2","date":"2026-10-14T03:25:49+01:00","subject":"Quests opens in Today (hour by hour) unless changed: Options → Opens in Today, Focus, List or Board (remembered on the device; ?view= still picks one); switching views no longer changes where it opens","body":""},{"hash":"b14adcc","date":"2026-10-14T03:12:29+01:00","subject":"One top bar for Nova Agent and every open panel (web/shared/topbar.css: the same capsule, height, corners, mark and name, in the same place and width), on phones too; the panels bar floats over an open panel and only slides (0.18 s in, 0.15 s away), so the panel never resizes or jumps: no room taken and given back, no trail, no tile ripple, nothing measured per move, no endless frame polling; scrolling down hides it with a mouse too; typing on the home no longer shifts the page; the one-row bar (tablet, phone on its side) shares its width by places and name lengths, so nothing is squeezed or cut. scripts/check-bars.mjs measures it","body":""},{"hash":"2ae52a2","date":"2026-10-14T03:05:10+01:00","subject":"Quests: the fit layer too, and in the fit check","body":""},{"hash":"3a49323","date":"2026-10-14T02:54:08+01:00","subject":"Fit on screen in every panel: /shared/fit.js + fit.css keep menus, pop-ups, tooltips, non-modal dialogs and anything marked data-fit (or handed over with NovaFit.keep) inside the screen — nudged back in just far enough, capped and scrolling inside only when bigger than the screen, checked again on resize, turning round, a phone's keyboard and growing content; Agent's activity list and the planet card hooked in. scripts/check-fit-all.sh runs the whole fit check (throwaway server, 360×640, 768×1024, 1440×900, the Manual) and check-fit.mjs now also proves the fit layer is on every page and works after the window shrinks","body":""},{"hash":"a96223c","date":"2026-10-14T02:52:57+01:00","subject":"Calendar: one modern line-icon set (2px, round), icons that say what they are (booking = ticked calendar, quest = target, note card, ghost/flame/party/suitcase/flower for day kinds), birthdays and anniversaries win over food, tooltips and names on every icon button. Observatory: everything at once on computers and standing tablets (decks left on their side, star map right, filling the window; the map closes in on the stars and keeps names readable), phones one row shorter","body":""},{"hash":"b2822b3","date":"2026-10-14T02:48:29+01:00","subject":"Quests: a panel of its own (/quests/). Quick add in everyday words with a preview of what was understood; Focus (one thing now), List (Now, Overdue, Today, Coming up, Any time, Done), Board (by how it's going, drag between columns) and Today (hour by hour); steps, tags, drag to reorder (and Alt+arrows), delete with Undo, Calm, little celebrations, search and #tag filters, keyboard shortcuts. Quests keep steps, tags and their own order (POST /actions/quests/order). In Nova Agent's Plans and on the phone's bar; today's plan beside Agent stays (Today)","body":""},{"hash":"76c86ec","date":"2026-10-14T02:42:59+01:00","subject":"Index gets smarter: search that forgives typos with Did you mean, filters (kind, when it changed, pinned), Ask Index with sources, pinned and recent files, related files, look-alike and old-file hints, Ctrl+K and arrow keys, Open the chat on Approve (logic in web/index/smart.js)","body":""},{"hash":"dc26b62","date":"2026-10-14T02:40:34+01:00","subject":"Fixer: scripted checks (no AI) with every hourly check and on their own (Health → Run the quick checks): every address, Nova Agent's pages and data, the status page's parts, bookings, the server's services, timed jobs, backup, memory, load and mail queue, SPF/DKIM/DMARC, the database, the Manual's links; grouped pass/fail with why; server fails are told, never prepared; the sweep also covers Board and Console. Online link: a watcher restarts a stuck attempt, and a hello/here check redoes a link Nova Bot lost","body":""},{"hash":"c27179b","date":"2026-10-14T02:12:02+01:00","subject":"Computer says the VPS inside: 'Your VPS', 'On the VPS', 'Move Nova Agent to the VPS'; Console names Nova Agent instead of the studio computer; Manual's Computer section describes the VPS (no Cloudflare)","body":""},{"hash":"8b1676e","date":"2026-10-14T01:23:54+01:00","subject":"All addresses: every web address in the suite in one list (Manual → All addresses; Portal → Settings → Addresses, and Apps and links), each with a plain line, Copy and Open; admins also see the ones other services use. Every link people see is https://nova.novacane.co.uk now (no studio-computer addresses in Portal, the Manual or the READMEs). scripts/check-addresses.mjs checks each one answers live","body":""},{"hash":"01bcb95","date":"2026-10-14T01:17:34+01:00","subject":"Campaigns sent by the studio's own mail server: Resend gone from Agent, Portal, the Fixer's rules and the docs","body":"Portal shows a campaign going out (Sending · n of m) and own-server results (sent, unsubscribed,\ndidn't go); Agent's campaign summaries say the same."},{"hash":"2b2f304","date":"2026-10-14T01:12:16+01:00","subject":"Computer shows Nova's own computer (the VPS) only: where Nova Agent runs and how to move it, mail sender, backups kept, Restart Nova Agent; Console's computer/deploy without the old host","body":""},{"hash":"a98c163","date":"2026-10-13T23:51:38+01:00","subject":"Nova Agent on the server: NOVA_ON_SERVER mode, only one Nova Agent runs (link says where; PC stands down on 4002 and stays off by marker), Console + Shell is the server's shell (ssh tunnel), Fixer restarts nova-agent.service and checks Claude Code's sign-in, watchdog becomes a self-watch","body":""},{"hash":"4dbdd3f","date":"2026-10-13T23:06:54+01:00","subject":"Watchdog: every 5 minutes the PC reads Nova Bot's status page; after 2 misses in a row a calm desktop (and optional ntfy) notification, once, and again when it's back","body":""},{"hash":"a23c9e9","date":"2026-10-13T22:54:11+01:00","subject":"Nova's own address in Nova Agent: nova.novacane.co.uk (the PC's link, links, the Manual); Computer talks about Nova's own computer","body":""},{"hash":"d9f82f5","date":"2026-10-13T22:49:12+01:00","subject":"Fixer: put fixes live with vps/deploy-live.sh, wherever Nova Bot is live (a plain wrangler deploy would undo the switch-over)","body":""},{"hash":"3c6c6b5","date":"2026-10-13T22:43:26+01:00","subject":"Desk is called Computer now: Portal → Admin → Computer, Console's computer command (desk still works, and it says which side is live), view=computer, the status words","body":""},{"hash":"fa3ffaf","date":"2026-10-13T22:31:52+01:00","subject":"Switch-over: Desk's Live now card (which side is live, switch and switch-back commands, warnings); Portal gets a new notification address quietly when the server's key changes, or asks once, calmly","body":""},{"hash":"3887fe6","date":"2026-10-13T20:22:49+01:00","subject":"check-console.mjs reads everything printed in the tab that's showing","body":""},{"hash":"ce41c59","date":"2026-10-13T20:18:34+01:00","subject":"Console: terminal check (on this computer: + Shell runs, + VPS reaches odysi; online: shut, with an Open Console on this computer button)","body":""},{"hash":"073c34b","date":"2026-10-13T20:17:09+01:00","subject":"Console tests: every command runs (answers stood in for), help covers every command, did-you-mean and other words","body":""},{"hash":"5c20f4d","date":"2026-10-13T20:16:33+01:00","subject":"WIP Console: centred and readable (a centred column, bigger text, headings, coloured lined-up help with examples, stacked on phones), commands to tap, an Open on this computer button online","body":""},{"hash":"eac261c","date":"2026-10-13T20:11:53+01:00","subject":"WIP Console: opens on the studio computer itself (/console/?here=1) for its terminals, the VPS set by default, the PC's person keeps their admin role until Nova Bot answers","body":""},{"hash":"d17994d","date":"2026-10-13T20:11:00+01:00","subject":"WIP Console: grouped help with examples, today, version, desk, deploy status, backup, search, ask, Portal shortcuts, aliases, did-you-mean","body":""},{"hash":"cbde021","date":"2026-10-13T19:44:41+01:00","subject":"Portal → Admin → Desk: Nova Bot on Cloudflare and on the VPS side by side (online, how busy, jobs, PC link, problems), back up and restart for admins","body":""},{"hash":"234cf9b","date":"2026-10-13T18:44:58+01:00","subject":"Allow node-pty's build step (Console's terminals)","body":""},{"hash":"3e3efd6","date":"2026-10-13T18:34:14+01:00","subject":"WIP Console: tests (commands, approvals typed back, terminals only on this computer for admins, VPS address, tokens), state and log through the link","body":""},{"hash":"98548ec","date":"2026-10-13T18:32:05+01:00","subject":"check-board.mjs: BOARD_URL picks the throwaway server","body":""},{"hash":"fc66d31","date":"2026-10-13T18:29:57+01:00","subject":"WIP Console in Nova Agent's Tools (icon, phone bar, status words, Manual list), fit check and click-through check","body":""},{"hash":"fa34c0a","date":"2026-10-13T11:35:33+01:00","subject":"WIP Board welcome: everything fits above the banner, labels that fit, video and sound cards say what they are; a check script for the welcome board and big files","body":""},{"hash":"9d7ab79","date":"2026-10-13T11:33:36+01:00","subject":"WIP Console: terminals on the PC (admins, this computer only), the VPS's address, the log; xterm.js vendored","body":""},{"hash":"ecc8f34","date":"2026-10-13T11:33:29+01:00","subject":"WIP Board page: the Welcome banner (clear it, keep it and start a new one, keep as is), media with a calm loading shimmer and Try again, hint labels, uploads with progress and the new limits","body":""},{"hash":"3f91d85","date":"2026-10-13T11:32:17+01:00","subject":"WIP Board: the Welcome board, given once to each person (a showcase of every kind of card)","body":""},{"hash":"640482f","date":"2026-10-13T11:31:12+01:00","subject":"WIP Board welcome media: a looping nebula and planet video, a still of it, a calm chime (made here, nothing borrowed)","body":""},{"hash":"c56bba4","date":"2026-10-13T11:30:51+01:00","subject":"Console: xterm.js and node-pty","body":""},{"hash":"d3b256b","date":"2026-10-13T11:28:41+01:00","subject":"WIP Board files: saved as they arrive (500 MB here, 95 MB online), parts on request (Range) so videos start at once, a copy in Google Drive for online, webm/mov/ogg too","body":""},{"hash":"bf5c68c","date":"2026-10-13T11:14:28+01:00","subject":"Board's click-through check (scripts/check-board.mjs)","body":""},{"hash":"412e437","date":"2026-10-13T11:02:10+01:00","subject":"Board: a table in Nova Agent's Apps for notes, the calendar, Agent's answers, question cards, stickies, links, pictures and files, moved with the mouse and pinned in place","body":""},{"hash":"e2f0ff6","date":"2026-10-13T11:00:12+01:00","subject":"WIP Board: tests (ownership, saving, cards, files, links, relay), one save at a time per board","body":""},{"hash":"41bbcd0","date":"2026-10-13T10:58:22+01:00","subject":"WIP Board: new cards find a free spot, hidden boxes stay hidden, the open board remembered, Board in the fit check","body":""},{"hash":"cf1ca77","date":"2026-10-13T10:45:15+01:00","subject":"WIP Board in Nova Agent's Apps (its icon and the phone bar); Notes opens one note from ?note=","body":""},{"hash":"ffccbbc","date":"2026-10-13T10:44:34+01:00","subject":"WIP Board: the table, cards, dragging, pinning, dropping, the drawer and saving","body":""},{"hash":"3bb5c49","date":"2026-10-13T10:38:45+01:00","subject":"WIP Board: boards, files and link previews kept on the PC, their addresses and relay rules","body":""},{"hash":"7ca9608","date":"2026-10-13T10:25:23+01:00","subject":"Fixer: Nova Agent: the tests fail","body":"I gave one slow music check more time to finish: 5 minutes instead of 2. The check listens to 160 seconds of the background music to make sure it moves between pieces with crossfades. Nothing else changed: the check is the same and so is the app.\nPrepared by the Fixer with Claude Code; waits for an admin's approval."},{"hash":"130a4d8","date":"2026-10-13T00:43:35+01:00","subject":"Fixer: Nova Agent: the audio took too long and was stopped","body":"The nightly sound check wasn't failing because anything was too loud. Every level it measured was within the calm limits. It failed because it plays about 67 minutes of music one piece at a time and ran past the Fixer's 20-minute limit. I changed it to share that work across a few hidden browsers at once (up to 4, depending on how many processors the machine has), so it does the same measuring in a fraction of the time.\nPrepared by the Fixer with Claude Code; waits for an admin's approval."},{"hash":"321c19c","date":"2026-10-12T21:33:21+01:00","subject":"Google round two on the PC and in the panels: Tasks sync, Files in Drive, Agent's Drive/Docs/Tasks/YouTube tools, YouTube in Social, Meet in Calendar, today's calendar in Portal and what_now, Keep in Google Docs and Open a Google Doc in Notes, Google Contacts search in one-to-one emails","body":""},{"hash":"e6c2d32","date":"2026-10-12T20:21:21+01:00","subject":"Sizing: Portal's tabs never squash or cut off (the side menu only from 1024px; tab lanes below that whatever's chosen), Chats on narrow phones, Notes never left short of its frame, and a resize check","body":""},{"hash":"1d69ce2","date":"2026-10-12T20:19:55+01:00","subject":"Portal's Admin address is view=manage: ad blockers block any address with \"view=ad…\" (old admin links and remembered places are turned into the new one)","body":""},{"hash":"93a17ce","date":"2026-10-12T19:28:07+01:00","subject":"Portal → Conversations: answer a website chat yourself (Take over, a reply box, Hand back), live both ways","body":""},{"hash":"731432a","date":"2026-10-12T19:16:25+01:00","subject":"Fixer: one problem wherever it's seen, fixes closed when their problem's gone, no alarms for Nova Bot blips, the sweep only looks","body":"- The same file/script/console problem on several panels or widths is one issue (and one fix) saying where it was seen; older per-place issues carry on as the grouped one\n- A queued, ready, failed or blocked fix whose problem has gone is closed\n- Nova Bot not answering / 502-504 / dropped connections are checked again (3 tries over ~2 minutes) before they count, and never get a fix prepared\n- The sweep's browser marks its requests (x-nova-fixer-sweep) and Nova Agent's server turns away its writes, so it can't make shared notes, calendar items or quests"},{"hash":"2303434","date":"2026-10-12T18:52:49+01:00","subject":"Google: Portal → Admin → Google (set up one step at a time, what's kept in step), copies to Drive and nightly backups, Money's sheet, Notes to Docs in one tap, Agent's read-only Google tools","body":""},{"hash":"e5f30f8","date":"2026-10-12T18:38:42+01:00","subject":"Status line on every panel: a slim strip along the bottom of the open panel (its news, the date and time), and the date everywhere","body":""},{"hash":"bee5413","date":"2026-10-12T18:29:13+01:00","subject":"Music: a calm late-night studio band (moving bass, melodies that come back and get answered, soulful chords, soft swung drums) in seven pieces","body":"Glow, Warm keys, Tape beat, Late night, Night trio, Whisper garage and Afro glow, each a groove\n(68-86 bpm) in sections (intro, A, B, breakdowns). Peaks stay at or under -27.6 dBFS at the\ndefault volume; scripts/music-previews.mjs renders WAVs and measures each piece."},{"hash":"4371d4d","date":"2026-10-12T18:09:33+01:00","subject":"Portal → Test stuff: what looks like tests or copies, with why, Delete (into a bin) and Not a test","body":"Admins only. Nova Bot's list (enquiries, chats, bookings, clients, Index, notes, drafts) and the\nstudio PC's (quests, missions, calendar notes, Fixer jobs, files), each with reasons in words, what\ngoes with it, Open; deleting goes through each thing's own delete with a copy in a 30-day bin.\nAgent can only read the list."},{"hash":"9c3a973","date":"2026-10-12T17:07:23+01:00","subject":"Fixer: undo “Nova Agent at 1280px: a file didn't load: /music-world/img …”","body":""},{"hash":"10212be","date":"2026-10-12T16:31:50+01:00","subject":"Money: invoices, payments and expenses in Portal, receipts on the PC","body":"Portal → Money (Studio, after Clients): invoices that are emailed to a client only after an\nadmin's Approve, payments (part paid, paid), reminders that wait for an Approve, expenses with\nreceipts kept on the studio PC (src/receipts.ts, relayed for staff online), the UK tax year's\ntotals, the accountant's CSV and invoice settings. Today gets an \"Invoices overdue\" tile.\nAgent gets money_summary, list_invoices, draft_invoice, edit_invoice_draft and log_expense\n(unconfirmed); nothing that sends, approves, pays or changes settings."},{"hash":"06f8a94","date":"2026-10-12T16:21:15+01:00","subject":"Social (Quest 4): Portal → Social, pictures and videos kept on the studio computer, Agent's social tools","body":"- Portal → Social (Studio group, after Campaigns): write a post (counts for Instagram's limits,\n  Facebook/Instagram, pictures made JPEGs, videos, a UK time), waiting cards with Approve (twice),\n  Edit and Reject, posts to put up by hand while Meta isn't connected (copy, download, \"I posted\n  it\"), what's coming up by day, results, followers, comments with replies to approve, ideas and\n  trends (opens Agent with the question ready) and a link to Meta's Ads Manager\n- src/social-media.ts: the files on this computer (random ids, checked by their first bytes,\n  ranges for videos), behind a small store so the VPS can take over; their addresses relayed\n  for signed-in staff (and Nova Bot, for Meta)\n- Agent: social_context, create_social_draft, edit_social_draft, list_social_posts,\n  social_results, list_social_comments, draft_comment_reply; nothing approves or posts"},{"hash":"e5e3f8f","date":"2026-10-12T16:14:34+01:00","subject":"Portal inbox: sort enquiries like tickets, Spam, saved replies, chats marked","body":"- Enquiries: New / Open / Waiting on them / Done / Spam chips with counts, search,\n  one-press moves, who's on it, labels, the spam reason, Not spam.\n- Saved replies: add, change, remove; a picker in the reply box fills it ({name}\n  becomes their first name), and Send still sends.\n- Conversations: Needs a person / Done marks and filters.\n- Agent: enquiry_set_state (sorts only) and saved_replies_list.\n- The reply box's To line wraps a long address."},{"hash":"e8fb4a9","date":"2026-10-12T16:05:44+01:00","subject":"One-to-one emails: Agent drafts personal emails, an admin approves them in Portal → Campaigns","body":"Agent gets draft_outreach_email, edit_outreach_email and list_outreach_emails (no send or\napprove tool). Portal's Campaigns view gets a One-to-one emails part: write one, waiting cards\nwith Approve (pressed twice) / Edit / Reject / Send me a test, sent and rejected ones, and a\nbox to record someone who replied \"no thanks\". The Campaigns badge counts both."},{"hash":"07c2d29","date":"2026-10-12T15:17:48+01:00","subject":"Fixer: Nova Agent at 1280px: a file didn't load: /music-world/img (404)","body":"Album covers on Nova Agent's \"Today in music\" (the Top 10, Popular genres and Song of the day) now still show up when Apple has moved or removed the exact picture. Nova Agent sends the song's name along with each cover, and if the saved picture is gone, Nova Bot looks the song up on Apple's public music search and shows its current cover. Nova Bot also now stops waiting for a slow cover after a few seconds. Before, it could wait with no limit.\nPrepared by the Fixer with Claude Code; waits for an admin's approval."},{"hash":"a0ad31b","date":"2026-10-12T01:39:49+01:00","subject":"Fixer: Nova Agent at 390px: a file didn't load: /music-world/photo/Nina_Simo…","body":"The musician photo beside the quote on Nova Agent's music front page (and the other small pictures there) could show up as a failed file, an error 502. Nova Bot now stops waiting on Wikipedia after 8 seconds and answers \"no photo\". If Nova Agent can't reach Nova Bot at all, it now gives that same quiet \"no photo\" for these pictures instead of an error. One step was blocked: my first try at the Nova Bot edit was a small script, and it needed approval that nobody here could give. I made the same change with the normal file editor instead. New tests check both cases and pass, and the type check …\nPrepared by the Fixer with Claude Code; waits for an admin's approval."},{"hash":"2a78169","date":"2026-10-11T13:51:24+01:00","subject":"Fixer: Index at 390px: a file didn't load: /staff/tuniveza/planet.svg (404)","body":"When Nova Bot can't be reached, Nova Agent now draws the signed-in person's planet badge itself instead of answering \"file not found\". It uses the planet drawing code Portal already has, and it doesn't keep that drawing, so the real saved planet comes back as soon as Nova Bot is reachable again.\nPrepared by the Fixer with Claude Code; waits for an admin's approval."},{"hash":"59b8b8a","date":"2026-10-11T12:32:24+01:00","subject":"Fit check covers the Fixer; its screenshot box keeps its ✕ inside","body":""},{"hash":"1f748b5","date":"2026-10-11T12:11:55+01:00","subject":"Everything fits: nothing hangs off the screen in any panel; what doesn't fit scrolls inside its own box","body":"scripts/check-fit.mjs opens Nova Agent's home and every panel (on its own and inside Nova Agent) at\n7 sizes (incl. a phone with its keyboard up) with long sample content, opens every sheet, dialog and\npop-up, and reports anything past the screen or its clipping box. Fixes what it found:\n- Portal: the side-menu tab row started off its left edge (tabs unreachable); Booking tools' picked\n  day was wider than the screen; a chat's Enquiry pill was clamped away; Options buttons squashed\n  their icon; a busy day's dots spilled out; long words wrap in views\n- Calendar: long words break inside cards; day cards no longer squashed; narrow short events clamp\n  their title to their height; What to show scrolls inside on short screens\n- Notes: menus and pop-ups scroll inside (and stay on screen) on short screens; snippets wrap\n- Nova Agent: chat action chips, mission summaries and file titles wrap; Ho"},{"hash":"a756a95","date":"2026-10-11T11:50:32+01:00","subject":"The Fixer: hourly checks, fixer quests and suggestions, fixes prepared by Claude Code that wait for an admin's Approve","body":"- src/fixer: checks (tests, typecheck, a sweep of every panel at 390 and 1280, health; audio daily),\n  issues by fingerprint, one job at a time with a daily cap and time limit, each in its own worktree,\n  Claude Code headless and restricted, approval cards with before/after pictures\n- Nothing merges or deploys without Approve: only approve() mints the approval land() needs;\n  undoing a change that made things worse is the only thing it does by itself\n- Admin-only routes (PC page, or online admins through the relay); FIXER_DRY=1 makes it inert\n- web/fixer: the Fixer app; its tile in Tools and the Panels window; a Manual chapter"},{"hash":"ccda75f","date":"2026-10-11T11:23:11+01:00","subject":"P0-4: chats, quests, missions and reminders tied to each person","body":"- Who's asking (src/person.ts): online, the staff member Nova Bot's relay\n  passes (marked on the request object itself, so it can't be forged); on\n  the PC, the person Nova Agent works for. Anything with no owner is theirs.\n- The Agent's system prompt names the person and their role; what its tools\n  make (missions, quests, blocked times, rhythm) is theirs; Index memory is\n  theirs.\n- Each person has their own Agent conversation (data/chats/<staff id>.json);\n  the PC person's old browser history is brought over once.\n- Missions, quests and blocks have an `owner`. Quests panels, Missions and\n  the Agent's tools show your own; admins and the PC can switch to\n  everyone's. Staff change only their own (and quests tied to a shared note).\n- Each person is planned in their own time: their own blocks, music time and\n  (optional) rhythm; one person's quests never take another's time.\n- Reminders"},{"hash":"2d565ef","date":"2026-10-11T11:06:39+01:00","subject":"Tidy: risk and priority colours follow the theme; the PC answers /app-version","body":"- The main window's at-risk, warning and priority colours use the theme's warn/bad colours\n  instead of fixed orange and red.\n- The studio PC answers /app-version (the newest change in web/), so the page's update check no\n  longer logs a 404 there, and an open Nova Agent refreshes itself after an update on the PC too."},{"hash":"b6a81f5","date":"2026-10-11T05:13:18+01:00","subject":"Merge branch 'calm-audio'","body":""},{"hash":"ba952f1","date":"2026-10-11T05:04:14+01:00","subject":"Panels window: a short row of tiles sits in the middle (with text centred)","body":""},{"hash":"df3406f","date":"2026-10-11T04:55:16+01:00","subject":"Status line's list centred; no broken-picture icons in Today in music","body":""},{"hash":"bb1c08b","date":"2026-10-11T04:49:41+01:00","subject":"Centred text in Notes' list and Nova Agent's dialogs; days off wear the theme","body":"A note's name and its Shared / Local badge sit in the middle of its row; the daily rhythm's tick\nboxes, days off and buttons, and a mission's deadline row and buttons, gather in the middle. The\ndays-off chips use the theme's highlight instead of a fixed red."},{"hash":"7de0a7e","date":"2026-10-11T04:45:11+01:00","subject":"Centred text in Index's header, Lossless meters and Observatory's header; themed tick boxes","body":"Index's name sits under its kicker, Lossless' meter names sit with their levels, Observatory's\nname, buttons and line sit in the middle. The Panels window's tick boxes wear the theme instead of\nthe browser's blue."},{"hash":"37afbb8","date":"2026-10-11T04:28:58+01:00","subject":"Comments say Agent where they still said Chat","body":""},{"hash":"6bb3462","date":"2026-10-11T04:28:58+01:00","subject":"Centred text reaches the last left-aligned corners","body":"The Manual (apps down the side, On this page, search, cards, results, next/previous), the Portal\nbadge's name and role, the Panels window's group headings (a line either side), Calendar's chosen\nday, Notes' menu bar and status bar, and Visualizer's header, buttons and part names. All follow\nCentre all text, so Left still works. Also: Visualizer is just \"Visualizer\" (not \"Nova\nVisualizer\"), Nova Bot spelt the usual way, and the Manual and badge say \"Nova Agent\" and\n\"panel\" rather than \"Nova app\"."},{"hash":"ce1ff1c","date":"2026-10-11T04:25:36+01:00","subject":"Dates and times written the British way, in London time, whatever the browser's language","body":"Calendar's mid-size day labels read \"19 Oct\" and \"19/10\" (not \"10month 19day\" and \"10 19\");\nthe status line's clock no longer follows the browser's language (\"So 5:04 am\"); Visualizer's\nstep times and every other date label say en-GB, Europe/London."},{"hash":"7e770a8","date":"2026-10-11T04:01:04+01:00","subject":"Portal room to breathe + a Menu option; apps open full screen; Nova Agent's icon choice","body":"- Portal: more space between tabs, rows and groups, group labels clear of their tabs; buttons\n  and chips get more room around their words (centred by eye) and between each other.\n- Portal → Options → Menu: Tabs on top (default) or Side menu (the original vertical menu);\n  the tab bar now lives in tabbar.css, switched off for the side menu.\n- Opening an app: Nova Agent's bars are simply away (no slide or trail to watch); they come\n  back at the edge as before, and Always shown keeps them.\n- The duplicate Nova Agent title over the conversation is for screen readers only now; the\n  top banner's icon can be the classic mark or the chat bubble (Panels window)."},{"hash":"2b4fffb","date":"2026-10-11T03:48:56+01:00","subject":"Calm audio: six new generative music pieces with seeds, gentle ASMR-like extra sounds","body":"Music (shared/ambient.js): Glow (the original, kept) now takes turns with Warm keys,\nSlow drone, Tape chords, Distant air, Low strings and Night rain, crossfading slowly\n(never the same piece twice running). A seed (six-letter code) drives the piece order,\nkey and mode (always next to D lydian, so the sound effects fit), pace, chords,\nvoicings, filters, reverb size, echo and textures: a new seed each session, or keep\none / type one back in (Portal > Options > Sound). Pauses while the app is hidden,\ntinted subtly by the theme's colour, a safety curve at the end so it can never clip.\nSounds (shared/sfx.js), with the Quiet extras switch (off by default): a velvety\nwhisper only during sustained scrolling or scrollbar dragging, soft fabric on sheets,\na brush that slides the way a tab moved, a felt touch under switches, a shimmer on\ntheme changes, a warm unfolding when a panel opens; each vari"},{"hash":"6c61f18","date":"2026-10-11T03:27:25+01:00","subject":"Merge branch 'shell-motion'","body":""},{"hash":"5349f15","date":"2026-10-11T03:26:05+01:00","subject":"Nova Agent: quicker, calmer bar show/hide, sheets that fade, and a theme trail as the bar moves","body":"- Bottom bar (computer): comes after resting the mouse at the bottom edge for 120 ms (passing\n  through no longer pops it over the panel), stays while the mouse is on or near it, goes after\n  a calm 600 ms well above it; same for the top bar. Never while hovered, keyboard-focused, or a\n  window/sheet/activity list is open; Tab into a bar brings it.\n- One motion everywhere: in 0.24 s with a soft settle, away 0.2 s; tile ripple capped.\n- The panel takes/gives back the bars' room in one step (no per-frame resize); the status line\n  fades and gives up its row once, after the bar has gone.\n- Phone: scroll caused by the bar itself is ignored, so no show/hide loop at the page end.\n- Trail: soft echoes and a glow in the theme's colours follow the bar (about 0.4 s); halo on arrival.\n- Windows and sheets fade/lift in and out; the handle fades in. Reduced motion: none of it."},{"hash":"91d1fad","date":"2026-10-11T03:25:54+01:00","subject":"Plain app names again (only Nova Agent and Nova Bot keep Nova); titles on one surface; Portal's tabs wrap on tablets too","body":"Undoes the 'Nova <App>' renaming line by line (the ✦ marks, the tab bar and the scrollbars\nstay). Inside Nova Agent a shared rule kept Portal's tabs on one sliding row under 981px:\nfrom 761px they now wrap too, so every tab is on screen."},{"hash":"43e7562","date":"2026-10-11T03:18:54+01:00","subject":"Titles sit centred at the top of each open app (icon + name in the theme's gradient), Back and Reload tucked in the corners; Portal's tabs wrap so all stay on screen","body":""},{"hash":"beb626e","date":"2026-10-11T03:05:16+01:00","subject":"Merge branch 'tools-manual'","body":"# Conflicts:\n#\tweb/agent/page.html\n#\tweb/shared/manual.js"},{"hash":"e46ce40","date":"2026-10-11T03:04:28+01:00","subject":"Tools in the Nova Agent family: Lossless audio, the Visualizer and Observatory","body":"- web/shared/tools.css: the tools' shared look, all theme tokens (deep sky, glass cards with the\n  soft gradient edge, display-font headings, mono small-caps labels, boxes, menus, sliders,\n  switches, chips, meters, tables, fold-outs, empty and loading states)\n- Lossless audio: off its own light/grey palette onto themes.css + tools.css; cards for Room,\n  Live, Sound devices and The connection (two columns when wide, one on a phone); every id,\n  button and line of help kept\n- Visualizer: the same; glass header with the live light, the four numbers as tiles, each part\n  of the agent coloured from the theme; the hidden screenshot no longer draws a stray line\n- Observatory: \"All links\" and the sound switch are the shared glass pills (no inline style),\n  the empty note spans the page, Star map's heading sits over its line, no empty map frame,\n  the search box gets its own row on phones, hard-"},{"hash":"d6d2213","date":"2026-10-11T02:57:49+01:00","subject":"Nova first in every app name (the bottom bars keep their short labels)","body":"Nova Portal, Nova Agent, Nova Calendar, Nova Notes, Nova Index, Nova Quests, Nova Missions,\nNova Lossless, Nova Visualizer, Nova Observatory, Nova Manual: titles, headers, the Panels\nwindow, the status line, the Manual, manifests, messages and alerts. Also: the Nova mark's CSS on\nthe panel icons (chat.html), Portal's tab labels and tabbar.js, and the scrollbars link in each page."},{"hash":"d805620","date":"2026-10-11T02:22:08+01:00","subject":"Merge branch 'themes-buttons'","body":""},{"hash":"95b9569","date":"2026-10-11T02:21:20+01:00","subject":"Themes: a colour spectrum with a Custom colour; one button look for every panel","body":"A spectrum of themes for all of Nova Agent (web/shared/spectrum.js): Crimson, Rose,\nCoral, Amber, Lime, Jade, Teal, Glacier, Indigo, Violet and Orchid join the old ones,\neach a hand-tuned set (deep sky, luminous accent, matching gradients and glows) whose\ntext reads at WCAG AA or better. Custom makes a whole theme from one hue and a\nvividness (OKLCH, so every hue is as readable as every other), remembered on the device\n(\"nova-look-custom\"). The pickers in the Panels window and Portal's and Index's Options\nshow every theme as an orb in rainbow order, then Custom with its two sliders; choosing\none, or moving a slider, recolours Nova Agent and every open panel straight away (look.js\nover storage events). Cosmic stays the default and looks the same; every old theme, id\nand the \"Each panel's own\" choice still work, and Portal's own theme can be any of them.\nOne button system (web/shared/butto"},{"hash":"4e34046","date":"2026-10-11T02:08:35+01:00","subject":"Notes: the page always fits the screen, and only its writing scrolls","body":"The page (sheet) used to be a 1056px-tall card that scrolled whole inside the\nwriting area, and a wide table pushed it sideways, so the page slid off screen.\nNow the page fills the space under the bars and stays put; the note scrolls\ninside it. Wide tables and code slide sideways in their own box, pictures stay\ninside. Find and replace sits over the page's corner. On phones the window\nfollows the visible screen (dvh, and js/fit.js with visualViewport, including\nNova Agent's around the frame) so the bars stay on top when the keyboard is up\nand the caret stays in view; the window itself never scrolls.\nscripts/check-notes-fit.mjs checks it at phone, tablet and desktop sizes, on\nits own and inside Nova Agent, with the side panels open."},{"hash":"fe3085e","date":"2026-10-11T01:44:30+01:00","subject":"Tests: say which Acuity setting they mean (a real .env on the studio PC may set ACUITY_SOURCE)","body":""},{"hash":"3a2016a","date":"2026-10-11T01:43:33+01:00","subject":"Merge branch 'index-cleanup'","body":""},{"hash":"483e1ac","date":"2026-10-11T01:42:17+01:00","subject":"Plans: one Quests view with Calendar's reminders, a shorter phone bar, saved tests for two fixes","body":"- The bar's \"Tasks\" group is now \"Plans\" (same Quests and Missions; the Panels window and the\n  status line's area name too)\n- Quests: every quest says where it came from (its mission, \"Notes · <note>\", or Agent; blocked\n  time says Agent), in the timeline, the up-next card and the Coming up, Pulses and Needs a slot\n  lists\n- Quests: a quiet \"Also coming up\" list of Calendar's note cards with reminders in the next 7\n  days (UK time, repeating ones each time); tapping one opens Calendar on that day\n  (/calendar/?day=YYYY-MM-DD, new and additive in cal.js)\n- Phones held upright (600px and under): Portal, Agent, Calendar, Notes and Quests on the bar\n  plus More, a sheet with Missions, Index, Lossless, Visualizer, Observatory and Manual (same\n  icons, same opening; More lights up when one of them is open; Escape or Close puts it away).\n  Wider screens keep the whole bar\n- Tests: Calendar's k"},{"hash":"b41ad38","date":"2026-10-11T01:42:03+01:00","subject":"P0-5 Index cleanup: Tidy up for admins, permission-aware editing, a confirm per fact","body":"- Options > Tidy up (admins only): Check now shows what would be removed (counts, examples,\n  reasons, which copy stays); a second press, Remove them, sends exactly that report's ids.\n  The 30-day bin lists removed entries with Put back, and who ran each cleanup.\n- Files a person may not change (studio-wide memory for non-admins) open read-only with a\n  calm note; deleting a fact asks in its own line first; save toasts say why lines were left\n  out; deleting a file says it can come back from the bin. A new file needs its first fact.\n- On the studio PC without a Portal sign-in, the cleanup routes are refused."},{"hash":"2f3b01e","date":"2026-10-11T00:32:37+01:00","subject":"Quest 3 (Nova Agent): email campaigns with an admin's approval, on Resend","body":"- Agent: suggest_campaign (saves nothing), create_campaign_draft, edit_campaign_draft,\n  campaign_results (opened/clicked as percentages in plain words), list_campaigns, all on\n  /nova-agent/campaigns* with AGENT_NOVA_KEY. No send, schedule, approve or test tool.\n- Agent's campaign card: subject, audience and count, send time, a short preview; Approve\n  (pressed twice, checks nothing changed) / Edit / Reject on the person's own Portal sign-in,\n  Open in Portal on the studio computer.\n- Portal → Campaigns (Studio, badge = waiting): sandboxed preview, Approve / Edit / Reject /\n  Send me a test for admins, scheduled and sent with stats, Write one, the fan sign-up link\n  with Copy and opted-in counts."},{"hash":"b1f2881","date":"2026-10-11T00:20:06+01:00","subject":"Quest 2 (Nova Agent): client list in Portal, Agent's client tools, bookings from Acuity's calendar feed","body":"- ACUITY_SOURCE=feed: studio_bookings and the Quests busy-time cache read\n  /nova-agent/bookings-feed (no browser, no API tools, no propose_booking_change)\n- Agent: client_find, client_history, clients_owing, clients_not_booked_since (read-only)\n- Portal → Clients: search, filters, client page, edit form (money in pounds), marketing\n  consent switch with source and date, consent history; admins: Sync now and Import CSV"},{"hash":"ad246c7","date":"2026-10-10T23:46:26+01:00","subject":"Quest 1 (Nova Agent): Acuity API tools, booking proposals for approval, bookings as busy time, music time","body":"- ACUITY_SOURCE=api|browser (default api). With api, Agent reads bookings, free times,\n  blocked times, session types and clients through Nova Bot's /nova-agent/acuity/* routes\n  (src/acuity-api.ts) and can only PROPOSE booking changes (propose_booking_change,\n  booking_actions). No tool or export can approve. check_acuity_login only in browser mode.\n- Bookings (not cancelled) and Acuity blocked times are cached in data/bookings.json (no\n  client details), refreshed every 10 minutes and when /nova-agent/next says bookingsChanged\n  is newer than bookingsSeen; then Quests re-plan. Acuity unreachable: last copy kept, trace says so.\n- Music time: rhythm.music { days, start, minutes } (off by default), planned up to 21 days,\n  moved to the nearest free stretch that day on a clash, busy for quests, \"music-\" note cards\n  in Calendar, one calm notice when a booking moves today's or tomorrow's. A"},{"hash":"387275f","date":"2026-10-10T16:57:24+01:00","subject":"Enquiries: conversation and replies in Portal; Agent drafts replies for approval","body":"- Portal: open an enquiry to see the conversation, Send a reply or add a note, status\n  chips (sending / sent / failed + Retry), Agent's drafts with Edit, Approve & send and\n  Discard, Call / Text links, consent line and a Don't contact toggle. Checks every 5 s\n  while open; only changed messages are redrawn\n- Agent: enquiry_list, enquiry_read, enquiry_draft_reply (no send tool); the draft's card\n  under the reply has Approve & send (the person's Portal sign-in) and Open in Portal\n- Portal times shown in UK time"},{"hash":"46014b9","date":"2026-10-10T16:37:57+01:00","subject":"Front page: each quest card wears its mode's colour (card, edge, glow, title)","body":""}],"work":[{"state":"changed","file":"scripts/check-bars.mjs"},{"state":"changed","file":"scripts/check-fit.mjs"},{"state":"changed","file":"test/bars.spec.ts"},{"state":"changed","file":"web/agent/assets/bar.css"},{"state":"changed","file":"web/agent/assets/bar.js"},{"state":"changed","file":"web/agent/assets/music.js"},{"state":"changed","file":"web/agent/assets/status.css"},{"state":"changed","file":"web/agent/assets/touch.css"},{"state":"changed","file":"web/agent/chat.html"},{"state":"new","file":"scripts/check-autohide.mjs"}],"workCount":10,"workStat":"9 files changed, 390 insertions(+), 425 deletions(-)"}},{"id":"portal","name":"Portal","colour":"#9DB4FF","glyph":"◉","where":"A Nova Agent panel; on the staff phones too","links":[["Open Portal","https://nova.novacane.co.uk/portal/"]],"repo":"na","shared":"","tagline":"The studio's staff app, one sign-in for the whole of Nova Agent, and a planet for everyone.","intro":"<blockquote><strong>A Nova Agent panel.</strong> Its code is in <code>web/portal/</code> in Nova Agent&#39;s repo, and it opens inside Nova Agent at <code>/portal/</code>. Online, Nova Bot serves it at the same address, and it installs on a phone.</blockquote>\n<p><strong>The studio&#39;s staff app, one sign-in for the whole of Nova Agent, and a planet for everyone.</strong> A panel of <a href=\"https://github.com/tuniveza/nova-agent\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Nova Agent</a>, for Novacane Studios.</p>\n<p>Nova Portal is where the staff work: enquiries, website chats, bookings, quests, alerts, Ask NovaBot and push notifications to the staff phones. It&#39;s also where you sign in (once, for Nova Portal, Nova Index and the admin pages), and where every member of the team has a profile with a unique planet, drawn from their id.</p>\n<p>Nova Portal&#39;s old address, <code>/app/</code>, opens Nova Portal (with the same tab: <code>/app/?view=alerts</code> is <code>/portal/?view=alerts</code>). Phones that added Nova Portal to the Home Screen keep working and keep getting notifications; adding Nova Portal to the Home Screen gives the new icon.</p>","guide":[{"id":"the-tabs-0","title":"The tabs","html":"<p>Every section shows at once, so nothing hides behind a click. On a computer or tablet they sit at the top in <strong>lanes</strong>:</p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Lane</th><th>Tabs</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Today · You · Admin</strong></td><td>Share the first lane: Today&#39;s overview, your profile and planet, and (admins) Admin and <strong>Test stuff</strong>.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Studio</strong></td><td>Enquiries, Conversations, Clients, Money, Nova Calendar, Booking tools, Approvals, Campaigns, Social, Website bot.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Plans</strong></td><td>Nova Quests, Alerts and Nova Agent.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Settings</strong> (inside Nova Agent)</td><td>Voice, music, Options and apps.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>Each lane starts with its name in a small chip, all the same width, so the tabs line up; soft lines sit between lanes. A lane too wide for the window splits into two even halves, the second under the first. On a phone the tabs are along the bottom (with More); Options → Menu → <strong>Side menu</strong> puts them down the side instead.</p>\n<p>The address follows the tab, so a reload or a link lands in the same place: <code>/portal/?view=enquiries</code> (or <code>chats</code>, <code>calendar</code>, <code>quests</code>, <code>alerts</code>, <code>bot</code>), <code>/portal/?view=me</code>, <code>/portal/?view=crew</code>, <code>/portal/?id=</code>. With no <code>?view=</code>, Nova Portal opens on the starting tab from Options; a Nova Agent notification (<code>#nova</code>) opens Alerts.</p>\n<p>Sign in with Nova Portal.  Enquiries: email, call, send a booking link, read the chat, mark done.  The smart calendar: the week at a glance, and days that glow as they fill.    A day: how full it is, a clash, a tight changeover, and free slots.  Nova Quests from Nova Agent: what&#39;s on now and today&#39;s plan.  Nova Missions: progress, deadlines and anything at risk.    Alerts: every booking is checked with Acuity itself.  The Nova Agent sheet: every app, one tap away.  🔒 All links, each checked as you open it.    What&#39;s changed and everything the suite can do.  Options: theme, text, motion, sound and the starting tab.  Ask NovaBot in staff mode: a booking link, deposit first.</p>\n<p>Tap a free slot, and NovaBot · bookings opens with the request already written.</p>","text":"Every section shows at once, so nothing hides behind a click. On a computer or tablet they sit at the top in lanes : Lane Tabs Today · You · Admin Share the first lane: Today's overview, your profile and planet, and (admins) Admin and Test stuff . Studio Enquiries, Conversations, Clients, Money, Nova Calendar, Booking tools, Approvals, Campaigns, Social, Website bot. Plans Nova Quests, Alerts and Nova Agent. Settings (inside Nova Agent) Voice, music, Options and apps. Each lane starts with its name in a small chip, all the same width, so the tabs line up; soft lines sit between lanes. A lane too wide for the window splits into two even halves, the second under the first. On a phone the tabs are along the bottom (with More); Options → Menu → Side menu puts them down the side instead. The address follows the tab, so a reload or a link lands in the same place: /portal/?view=enquiries (or chats , calendar , quests , alerts , bot ), /portal/?view=me , /portal/?view=crew , /portal/?id= . With no ?view= , Nova Portal opens on the starting tab from Options; a Nova Agent notification ( #nova ) opens Alerts. Sign in with Nova Portal. Enquiries: email, call, send a booking link, read the chat, mark done. The smart calendar: the week at a glance, and days that glow as they fill. A day: how full it is, a clash, a tight changeover, and free slots. Nova Quests from Nova Agent: what's on now and today's plan. Nova Missions: progress, deadlines and anything at risk. Alerts: every booking is checked with Acuity itself. The Nova Agent sheet: every app, one tap away. 🔒 All links, each checked as you open it. What's changed and everything the suite can do. Options: theme, text, motion, sound and the starting tab. Ask NovaBot in staff mode: a booking link, deposit first. Tap a free slot, and NovaBot · bookings opens with the request already written."},{"id":"signing-in-1","title":"Signing in","html":"<ul><li><strong>Sign in once, everywhere:</strong> email and password give you a secure session that Nova Portal, Nova Index and the admin pages all trust. Signing out (from any of them) ends it everywhere at once.</li><li><strong>Setting up:</strong> the very first admin is created with the <code>ADMIN_PASSWORD</code> secret, to prove it&#39;s you. After that, admins <strong>invite</strong> people with a link (valid for 7 days), and each person chooses their own password. Nobody else ever knows it.</li><li>Signing in here also signs Nova Agent in to Nova Bot as you.</li><li><strong>Nova Club and other native apps</strong> can sign in through the same API and get an app token instead of a cookie.</li></ul>","text":"Sign in once, everywhere: email and password give you a secure session that Nova Portal, Nova Index and the admin pages all trust. Signing out (from any of them) ends it everywhere at once. Setting up: the very first admin is created with the ADMIN_PASSWORD secret, to prove it's you. After that, admins invite people with a link (valid for 7 days), and each person chooses their own password. Nobody else ever knows it. Signing in here also signs Nova Agent in to Nova Bot as you. Nova Club and other native apps can sign in through the same API and get an app token instead of a cookie."},{"id":"you-and-the-crew-2","title":"You, and the crew","html":"<ul><li><strong>Your profile:</strong> your planet, big and animated, with your name, role and &quot;member since&quot;. You can re-roll your planet (or go back to your original), change your name, open your own Nova Index, and sign out.</li><li><strong>The crew (admins):</strong> everyone as a planet, with their role, status and last sign-in. Invite people, change roles, switch accounts off (which signs them out at once), and send fresh invite links.</li><li><strong>Roles:</strong></li><li class=\"sub\"><strong>Admins</strong> see and manage everything, including customers&#39; facts and approvals in Nova Index.</li><li class=\"sub\"><strong>Staff</strong> see the studio&#39;s memory and their own partition.</li><li><strong>The badge, on every Nova Agent panel:</strong> `` shows your planet, your name and your role in the top bar. Tap it for your planet up close and links to your profile and your Nova Index.</li><li><strong>The Nova Manual, on every panel:</strong> `<code> sits beside the badge. It has a **Guide**, **How it&#39;s built**, the **History** and **What&#39;s new** for every panel, with search. Press **?** on any panel, or add </code>#nova-manual` to the address.</li></ul>","text":"Your profile: your planet, big and animated, with your name, role and \"member since\". You can re-roll your planet (or go back to your original), change your name, open your own Nova Index, and sign out. The crew (admins): everyone as a planet, with their role, status and last sign-in. Invite people, change roles, switch accounts off (which signs them out at once), and send fresh invite links. Roles: Admins see and manage everything, including customers' facts and approvals in Nova Index. Staff see the studio's memory and their own partition. The badge, on every Nova Agent panel: `` shows your planet, your name and your role in the top bar. Tap it for your planet up close and links to your profile and your Nova Index. The Nova Manual, on every panel: ` sits beside the badge. It has a **Guide**, **How it's built**, the **History** and **What's new** for every panel, with search. Press **?** on any panel, or add #nova-manual` to the address."},{"id":"the-work-tabs-3","title":"The work tabs","html":"<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Tab</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Enquiries</strong></td><td>Every enquiry NovaBot took, sorted like a ticket inbox: New, Open, Waiting on them, Done and Spam (one press moves it; likely spam lands in Spam by itself, with the reason, and nothing is ever deleted). Who&#39;s on it, a label, search, and the team&#39;s saved replies for routine questions. Email, call, make a booking link with the customer&#39;s details filled in, read the chat it came from. Details: Nova Bot&#39;s README-ENQUIRIES.md.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Chats</strong></td><td>What customers asked NovaBot on the website (kept for 90 days). Mark a chat <strong>Needs a person</strong> (you&#39;re put on it) or <strong>Done</strong>, and filter by either, so follow-ups don&#39;t get lost. Open a chat to answer the visitor yourself: see Live chat.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Clients</strong></td><td>Everyone who has booked or enquired: their sessions, money (deposits, invoiced, owed) and marketing consent with its date and source. Admins can import Acuity&#39;s spreadsheet; Nova Agent can look people up.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Money</strong></td><td>Invoices (sent only after an admin&#39;s Approve), payments and expenses. See Money.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nova Calendar</strong></td><td>Every booking in Acuity&#39;s diary, as a month you can swipe, with Nova Calendar&#39;s cards and planned quests alongside. See the smart calendar.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nova Quests</strong></td><td>Nova Agent&#39;s plan, synced from the VPS: the quest on now, repeating pulses, today, Nova Missions with progress rings, and every quest. Taps (Start, Done, +15 min, Not now, Skip, Pause) go straight back to Nova Agent.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Approvals</strong></td><td>Booking changes Nova Agent proposed. Nothing changes in Acuity until an admin presses Approve.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Campaigns</strong></td><td>Email newsletters to fans and clients who opted in, sent by the studio&#39;s own mail server (a few a minute, each with its own unsubscribe link) once an admin approves them. Below them, <strong>one-to-one emails</strong>: a personal email to one person (a venue, label, brand or other business at its work address; a studio client; someone who wrote in). Nova Agent or anyone in the team writes one; Nova Bot checks the person may be emailed (never anyone who said no; a client only about their own booking unless they said yes to studio news; no personal Gmail-style addresses as &quot;business&quot;) and adds a footer with a &quot;don&#39;t email me again&quot; link (<code>/no-thanks</code>). Nothing is sent until an admin presses Approve (twice), and it goes exactly as approved, once. Someone who replies &quot;no thanks&quot; can be recorded under the list. Nova Bot&#39;s <code>src/outreach.js</code>, migration <code>0028_outreach.sql</code>.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Alerts</strong></td><td>Every notification that reached a phone, newest first, with colour-coded labels, exact times, Call/Email buttons and an auto-delete switch.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Social</strong></td><td>Facebook and Instagram posts. Write one (or let Nova Agent draft it), add pictures and videos, pick a time; an admin approves it and Nova Bot posts it. See Social.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Test stuff</strong></td><td>(Admin) Things that look like tests or copies, with why, and Delete (into a 30-day bin) or Not a test. See Test stuff.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>NovaBot</strong></td><td>Two chats. <strong>Ask Nova</strong> answers questions about the studio&#39;s bookings, enquiries and alerts (Nova Bot&#39;s <code>src/studio-ask.js</code>). <strong>NovaBot · bookings</strong> is NovaBot with the booking tools, talking to you as staff: get a link for a client, find, move, cancel or change a booking. Every change shows a summary and waits for a yes.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","text":"Tab What it does Enquiries Every enquiry NovaBot took, sorted like a ticket inbox: New, Open, Waiting on them, Done and Spam (one press moves it; likely spam lands in Spam by itself, with the reason, and nothing is ever deleted). Who's on it, a label, search, and the team's saved replies for routine questions. Email, call, make a booking link with the customer's details filled in, read the chat it came from. Details: Nova Bot's README-ENQUIRIES.md. Chats What customers asked NovaBot on the website (kept for 90 days). Mark a chat Needs a person (you're put on it) or Done , and filter by either, so follow-ups don't get lost. Open a chat to answer the visitor yourself: see Live chat. Clients Everyone who has booked or enquired: their sessions, money (deposits, invoiced, owed) and marketing consent with its date and source. Admins can import Acuity's spreadsheet; Nova Agent can look people up. Money Invoices (sent only after an admin's Approve), payments and expenses. See Money. Nova Calendar Every booking in Acuity's diary, as a month you can swipe, with Nova Calendar's cards and planned quests alongside. See the smart calendar. Nova Quests Nova Agent's plan, synced from the VPS: the quest on now, repeating pulses, today, Nova Missions with progress rings, and every quest. Taps (Start, Done, +15 min, Not now, Skip, Pause) go straight back to Nova Agent. Approvals Booking changes Nova Agent proposed. Nothing changes in Acuity until an admin presses Approve. Campaigns Email newsletters to fans and clients who opted in, sent by the studio's own mail server (a few a minute, each with its own unsubscribe link) once an admin approves them. Below them, one-to-one emails : a personal email to one person (a venue, label, brand or other business at its work address; a studio client; someone who wrote in). Nova Agent or anyone in the team writes one; Nova Bot checks the person may be emailed (never anyone who said no; a client only about their own booking unless they said yes to studio news; no personal Gmail-style addresses as \"business\") and adds a footer with a \"don't email me again\" link ( /no-thanks ). Nothing is sent until an admin presses Approve (twice), and it goes exactly as approved, once. Someone who replies \"no thanks\" can be recorded under the list. Nova Bot's src/outreach.js , migration 0028_outreach.sql . Alerts Every notification that reached a phone, newest first, with colour-coded labels, exact times, Call/Email buttons and an auto-delete switch. Social Facebook and Instagram posts. Write one (or let Nova Agent draft it), add pictures and videos, pick a time; an admin approves it and Nova Bot posts it. See Social. Test stuff (Admin) Things that look like tests or copies, with why, and Delete (into a 30-day bin) or Not a test. See Test stuff. NovaBot Two chats. Ask Nova answers questions about the studio's bookings, enquiries and alerts (Nova Bot's src/studio-ask.js ). NovaBot · bookings is NovaBot with the booking tools, talking to you as staff: get a link for a client, find, move, cancel or change a booking. Every change shows a summary and waits for a yes."},{"id":"social-4","title":"Social","html":"<p>Facebook and Instagram posts, in Nova Portal → Social (the Studio group, after Campaigns).</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Writing.</strong> Anyone signed in writes a post: the words (with Instagram&#39;s 2,200-character and 30-hashtag counts), Facebook, Instagram or both, up to 10 pictures or videos, and a time (UK). Nova Agent can draft and edit posts too (<code>create_social_draft</code>, <code>edit_social_draft</code>), but it can&#39;t add pictures, approve or post.</li><li><strong>Approval.</strong> Nothing is posted until an admin, signed in to Nova Portal in a browser, presses Approve (twice: it says exactly what will happen). Nova Bot keeps a hash of exactly what was approved; any edit clears the approval.</li><li><strong>Posting.</strong> With Meta connected, Nova Bot posts it through Meta&#39;s Graph API, now or at its time (Instagram videos are checked every minute until Meta has them ready). Without Meta, the approved post waits under <strong>Post these by hand</strong>: copy the words, download the files, post it, then press <strong>I posted it</strong> (with the link, if you like). One platform can be connected and the other not.</li><li><strong>Pictures and videos</strong> are kept on the VPS (Nova Agent&#39;s <code>data/social-media/</code>), which is on day and night, so posts go out with every laptop off. Pictures become JPEGs (what Instagram takes) before they&#39;re added; videos are MP4 or MOV, up to 25 MB from a phone (bigger straight to Nova Agent).</li><li><strong>Results, followers and comments</strong> come from Meta every hour for 30 days. Replies to comments are drafts until an admin approves them. Dealt-with comments are deleted after 90 days.</li><li><strong>Ideas and trends</strong> opens Nova Agent with a question ready to send. <strong>Paid ads</strong> stay in Meta&#39;s Ads Manager: Nova never spends money.</li></ul>\n<p>Connecting Meta (Nova Bot&#39;s secrets, with <code>npx wrangler secret put</code>):</p>\n<ol><li>In <a href=\"https://developers.facebook.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Meta for Developers</a>, make a Business app and add <strong>Facebook Login for Business</strong> and the <strong>Instagram Graph API</strong>. The studio&#39;s Instagram must be a Business or Creator account, linked to its Facebook Page.</li><li>In the Graph API Explorer, get a <strong>user token</strong> for the app with <code>pages_show_list</code>, <code>pages_read_engagement</code>, <code>pages_manage_posts</code>, <code>pages_manage_engagement</code>, <code>read_insights</code>, <code>instagram_basic</code>, <code>instagram_content_publish</code>, <code>instagram_manage_comments</code> and <code>instagram_manage_insights</code>. Exchange it for a <strong>long-lived</strong> one (Access Token Debugger → Extend), then call <code>GET /me/accounts</code> with it: the Page&#39;s <code>access_token</code> there doesn&#39;t expire.</li><li>Set <code>META_PAGE_TOKEN</code> (that Page token), <code>META_PAGE_ID</code> (the Page&#39;s id) and <code>META_IG_USER_ID</code> (<code>GET /?fields=instagram_business_account</code>). Nova Portal → You → How it works → What Nova runs on shows what&#39;s connected.</li></ol>\n<p>When the VPS takes over the files: give Nova Agent another store in <code>src/social-media.ts</code> (the same four functions) and set <code>SOCIAL_MEDIA_BASE</code> (where the VPS serves <code>.</code>) and <code>SOCIAL_MEDIA_KEY</code> on Nova Bot: it fetches files from there instead of the VPS.</p>","text":"Facebook and Instagram posts, in Nova Portal → Social (the Studio group, after Campaigns). Writing. Anyone signed in writes a post: the words (with Instagram's 2,200-character and 30-hashtag counts), Facebook, Instagram or both, up to 10 pictures or videos, and a time (UK). Nova Agent can draft and edit posts too ( create_social_draft , edit_social_draft ), but it can't add pictures, approve or post. Approval. Nothing is posted until an admin, signed in to Nova Portal in a browser, presses Approve (twice: it says exactly what will happen). Nova Bot keeps a hash of exactly what was approved; any edit clears the approval. Posting. With Meta connected, Nova Bot posts it through Meta's Graph API, now or at its time (Instagram videos are checked every minute until Meta has them ready). Without Meta, the approved post waits under Post these by hand : copy the words, download the files, post it, then press I posted it (with the link, if you like). One platform can be connected and the other not. Pictures and videos are kept on the VPS (Nova Agent's data/social-media/ ), which is on day and night, so posts go out with every laptop off. Pictures become JPEGs (what Instagram takes) before they're added; videos are MP4 or MOV, up to 25 MB from a phone (bigger straight to Nova Agent). Results, followers and comments come from Meta every hour for 30 days. Replies to comments are drafts until an admin approves them. Dealt-with comments are deleted after 90 days. Ideas and trends opens Nova Agent with a question ready to send. Paid ads stay in Meta's Ads Manager: Nova never spends money. Connecting Meta (Nova Bot's secrets, with npx wrangler secret put ): In Meta for Developers , make a Business app and add Facebook Login for Business and the Instagram Graph API . The studio's Instagram must be a Business or Creator account, linked to its Facebook Page. In the Graph API Explorer, get a user token for the app with pages_show_list , pages_read_engagement , pages_manage_posts , pages_manage_engagement , read_insights , instagram_basic , instagram_content_publish , instagram_manage_comments and instagram_manage_insights . Exchange it for a long-lived one (Access Token Debugger → Extend), then call GET /me/accounts with it: the Page's access_token there doesn't expire. Set META_PAGE_TOKEN (that Page token), META_PAGE_ID (the Page's id) and META_IG_USER_ID ( GET /?fields=instagram_business_account ). Nova Portal → You → How it works → What Nova runs on shows what's connected. When the VPS takes over the files: give Nova Agent another store in src/social-media.ts (the same four functions) and set SOCIAL_MEDIA_BASE (where the VPS serves . ) and SOCIAL_MEDIA_KEY on Nova Bot: it fetches files from there instead of the VPS."},{"id":"the-smart-calendar-5","title":"The smart calendar","html":"<ul><li><strong>The week at a glance</strong>: sessions, hours booked and how full, session value, the busiest day, the next free hour, and any clashes.</li><li><strong>Glowing days</strong>: each day glows brighter as it fills; a nearly full day says FULL.</li><li><strong>A day in detail</strong>: hours booked, a fill meter, ⚠ clashes, ⏱ tight changeovers (under 15 minutes), and free slots of an hour or more within opening hours.</li><li><strong>One tap from a booking link</strong>: tapping a free slot opens NovaBot · bookings with the request written for you. &quot;✦ Ask Nova&quot; buttons ask about the week or the day.</li></ul>","text":"The week at a glance : sessions, hours booked and how full, session value, the busiest day, the next free hour, and any clashes. Glowing days : each day glows brighter as it fills; a nearly full day says FULL. A day in detail : hours booked, a fill meter, ⚠ clashes, ⏱ tight changeovers (under 15 minutes), and free slots of an hour or more within opening hours. One tap from a booking link : tapping a free slot opens NovaBot · bookings with the request written for you. \"✦ Ask Nova\" buttons ask about the week or the day."},{"id":"features-6","title":"Features","html":"<ul><li><strong>Real-booking checks.</strong> A booking alert asks Acuity about that booking as it comes into view: &quot;✓ Real booking: confirmed in Acuity&quot;, with the deposit paid, or &quot;Cancelled&quot; or &quot;Not found&quot;. Tests are labelled as tests, so nothing fake can pass for a booking.</li><li><strong>Push notifications that work with the app closed</strong> (Nova Bot&#39;s <code>src/push.js</code>, and <code>web/portal/sw.js</code>; phones that installed Nova Portal from <code>/app/</code> keep <code>/app/sw.js</code>). New enquiries, bookings (with every detail from Acuity&#39;s private calendar feed), and alerts from Nova Agent, Quest and Mission. Android gets rich notifications with their own buzz; iPhones get the plain version, so nothing is ever lost.</li><li><strong>Pings.</strong> With Nova Portal open, an alert rings out with a bright ping (a different one for each kind) and drops a banner from the top.</li><li><strong>Staff voice.</strong> Tap the mic and say what to do (&quot;show alerts&quot;, &quot;call Eric&quot;, &quot;new enquiries&quot;, &quot;ask NovaBot what the prices are&quot;); Whisper on Workers AI writes it down. Hands-free mode listens while the app is open for anything that starts with &quot;Nova&quot;.</li><li><strong>Nova Quests from Nova Agent</strong> (<code>src/agent-nova.js</code>): Nova Agent sends its plan here every time it changes, and picks up taps within about a second.</li><li><strong>Ambient music</strong> (<code>web/shared/ambient.js</code>, moved from <code>web/portal/</code>): Novacane&#39;s quiet, never-ending late-night studio music, made live with the Web Audio API (no audio files): a small band on a gentle pulse with soulful 7th/9th chords, a warm moving bass line, a melody of short motifs that come back and get answered, and very soft swung lo-fi drums, in sections (intro, A, B, breakdowns). Seven pieces take turns (Glow, Warm keys, Tape beat, Late night, Night trio, Whisper garage, Afro glow); a seed picks keys, tempos, progressions and motifs. Previews and measurements: <code>node scripts/music-previews.mjs</code>. Inside Nova Agent, Nova Portal&#39;s music button works the one player in Nova Agent&#39;s main page, so the music carries on across panels.</li><li><strong>Sound effects</strong> (<code>web/shared/sfx.js</code>): Novacane&#39;s glass bells, warm under-tones and soft breaths of air for taps, tabs, switches, sends and deletes, all in the music&#39;s key, and a two-note chime when NovaBot answers.</li><li><strong>Six themes</strong>: Cosmic, Ember, Aurora, Ocean, Gold and Mono, shared with the admin pages.</li><li><strong>Options</strong> (<code>web/portal/options.js</code>): theme, text alignment and size, how times show on alerts, animations, the drifting starfield, sound effects, pings, music volume and the starting tab (any work tab, or You). Saved on the device.</li><li><strong>The suite sheet</strong> (<code>web/portal/suite.js</code>): tap the Nova Portal brand to see every Nova app, 🔒 <strong>All links</strong> (every live and testing address, each checked on the spot), <strong>What&#39;s changed</strong> (every change by day and app: what, why and what&#39;s better), <strong>everything the suite can do</strong>, and the theme picker.</li></ul>\n<p>Switching themes in Options.  Browsing the suite sheet.</p>\n<p>One screen, six themes.</p>\n<p>On a desktop, the tabs become a side rail and lists go two-up.</p>\n<p>Ask Nova (questions about the studio&#39;s own diary)</p>\n<p><strong>Behind the scenes:</strong> Acuity&#39;s API can&#39;t change a booking&#39;s session type, price or paid status, so those changes are queued for <a href=\"https://github.com/tuniveza/nova-agent\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Nova Agent</a>, the browser helper on the VPS, which does them in Acuity&#39;s admin pages and reports back (<code>src/agent-nova.js</code>). Every day at 06:00 UK time the Worker checks it can still reach Acuity&#39;s API and alerts staff phones if not (<code>src/health.js</code>).</p>","text":"Real-booking checks. A booking alert asks Acuity about that booking as it comes into view: \"✓ Real booking: confirmed in Acuity\", with the deposit paid, or \"Cancelled\" or \"Not found\". Tests are labelled as tests, so nothing fake can pass for a booking. Push notifications that work with the app closed (Nova Bot's src/push.js , and web/portal/sw.js ; phones that installed Nova Portal from /app/ keep /app/sw.js ). New enquiries, bookings (with every detail from Acuity's private calendar feed), and alerts from Nova Agent, Quest and Mission. Android gets rich notifications with their own buzz; iPhones get the plain version, so nothing is ever lost. Pings. With Nova Portal open, an alert rings out with a bright ping (a different one for each kind) and drops a banner from the top. Staff voice. Tap the mic and say what to do (\"show alerts\", \"call Eric\", \"new enquiries\", \"ask NovaBot what the prices are\"); Whisper on Workers AI writes it down. Hands-free mode listens while the app is open for anything that starts with \"Nova\". Nova Quests from Nova Agent ( src/agent-nova.js ): Nova Agent sends its plan here every time it changes, and picks up taps within about a second. Ambient music ( web/shared/ambient.js , moved from web/portal/ ): Novacane's quiet, never-ending late-night studio music, made live with the Web Audio API (no audio files): a small band on a gentle pulse with soulful 7th/9th chords, a warm moving bass line, a melody of short motifs that come back and get answered, and very soft swung lo-fi drums, in sections (intro, A, B, breakdowns). Seven pieces take turns (Glow, Warm keys, Tape beat, Late night, Night trio, Whisper garage, Afro glow); a seed picks keys, tempos, progressions and motifs. Previews and measurements: node scripts/music-previews.mjs . Inside Nova Agent, Nova Portal's music button works the one player in Nova Agent's main page, so the music carries on across panels. Sound effects ( web/shared/sfx.js ): Novacane's glass bells, warm under-tones and soft breaths of air for taps, tabs, switches, sends and deletes, all in the music's key, and a two-note chime when NovaBot answers. Six themes : Cosmic, Ember, Aurora, Ocean, Gold and Mono, shared with the admin pages. Options ( web/portal/options.js ): theme, text alignment and size, how times show on alerts, animations, the drifting starfield, sound effects, pings, music volume and the starting tab (any work tab, or You). Saved on the device. The suite sheet ( web/portal/suite.js ): tap the Nova Portal brand to see every Nova app, 🔒 All links (every live and testing address, each checked on the spot), What's changed (every change by day and app: what, why and what's better), everything the suite can do , and the theme picker. Switching themes in Options. Browsing the suite sheet. One screen, six themes. On a desktop, the tabs become a side rail and lists go two-up. Ask Nova (questions about the studio's own diary) Behind the scenes: Acuity's API can't change a booking's session type, price or paid status, so those changes are queued for Nova Agent , the browser helper on the VPS, which does them in Acuity's admin pages and reports back ( src/agent-nova.js ). Every day at 06:00 UK time the Worker checks it can still reach Acuity's API and alerts staff phones if not ( src/health.js )."},{"id":"the-planets-7","title":"The planets","html":"<p><code>planet/</code> is a pure, deterministic generator: <code>generatePlanet(seed, theme, overrides?)</code> then <code>renderPlanetSVG(planet, { size, animate })</code>. The same seed and theme always give the same planet, so nothing is stored but the seed.</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Kinds:</strong> banded gas giants, cratered rocky worlds, ocean worlds with continents, molten worlds with glowing cracks, ice worlds, and ringed giants.</li><li><strong>Details:</strong> each has a palette drawn from the theme&#39;s ramps, an atmosphere glow, clouds or bands, and maybe rings (split properly in front of and behind the planet), up to three moons, an aurora or a storm.</li><li><strong>A real sphere:</strong> surface detail is projected onto it, with limb darkening, a terminator shadow and a specular highlight. Small badges simplify themselves, and the 512px hero animates.</li><li><strong>Speed:</strong> 1,000 planets generate and render in about half a second.</li><li><strong>Themes hold all the art direction:</strong> palettes, surfaces, glow, rings, moons, naming and the starfield. The Nova look lives in <code>planet/themes/nova.js</code>. When the studio&#39;s own lore is ready, it becomes a new theme file, with no change to the generator. A test proves it with a &quot;lore&quot; theme.</li><li><strong>Porting:</strong> <code>planet/README.md</code> documents the exact random number generator and draw order, so a Kotlin port (for Nova Club) draws identical planets.</li></ul>","text":"planet/ is a pure, deterministic generator: generatePlanet(seed, theme, overrides?) then renderPlanetSVG(planet, { size, animate }) . The same seed and theme always give the same planet, so nothing is stored but the seed. Kinds: banded gas giants, cratered rocky worlds, ocean worlds with continents, molten worlds with glowing cracks, ice worlds, and ringed giants. Details: each has a palette drawn from the theme's ramps, an atmosphere glow, clouds or bands, and maybe rings (split properly in front of and behind the planet), up to three moons, an aurora or a storm. A real sphere: surface detail is projected onto it, with limb darkening, a terminator shadow and a specular highlight. Small badges simplify themselves, and the 512px hero animates. Speed: 1,000 planets generate and render in about half a second. Themes hold all the art direction: palettes, surfaces, glow, rings, moons, naming and the starfield. The Nova look lives in planet/themes/nova.js . When the studio's own lore is ready, it becomes a new theme file, with no change to the generator. A test proves it with a \"lore\" theme. Porting: planet/README.md documents the exact random number generator and draw order, so a Kotlin port (for Nova Club) draws identical planets."},{"id":"money-8","title":"Money","html":"<p>Nova Portal → <strong>Money</strong> (in Studio, after Clients) keeps the studio&#39;s invoices, the payments against them, and its expenses. The badge counts invoices and reminders waiting for an admin, plus overdue invoices; Today has an <strong>Invoices overdue</strong> tile.</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Four tiles:</strong> money in this month (payments), money out (confirmed expenses), what clients owe, and what&#39;s overdue.</li><li><strong>Write an invoice:</strong> pick a client from the list (their name and email fill in) or type them in. Add lines (what it&#39;s for, how many, the price of one), with VAT, the issue and due days, and a note. The totals add up as you type, in whole pence. It&#39;s saved <strong>waiting for approval</strong>; Nova Agent can write one too.</li><li><strong>Approve (admins, signed in to Nova Portal in a browser):</strong> pressed twice (&quot;Email it to … now?&quot;). Nova Bot then emails the client a link to their invoice&#39;s own page, <code>/invoice/</code>. There they can see it, print it or save it as a PDF, and pay: by card through Stripe&#39;s own page (when Stripe is set up; the payment comes back by itself), or by bank transfer with the studio&#39;s bank details. Admins can also Reject (with why), Send me a test, and Void. Anyone can Edit it until it&#39;s sent.</li><li><strong>Payments:</strong> Record a payment (amount, day, bank transfer / card / cash / other, a note). The invoice becomes part paid or paid, and the client&#39;s money on the client list follows: invoiced and owed go up when it&#39;s sent, owed comes down with each payment. An admin can take a payment back that was a mistake; a Stripe one is refunded in Stripe.</li><li><strong>Reminders:</strong> Ask for a reminder on an unpaid invoice. It waits under <strong>Reminders to approve</strong> until an admin approves it, then goes to the client with the link.</li><li><strong>Expenses:</strong> amount, what for (a list of categories), who it was paid to, the day, a note and a receipt. The receipt is a photo or a PDF, kept on the VPS (<code>data/receipts/</code>), so you can add one any time. Expenses Nova Agent notes come in <strong>Not confirmed</strong> and count in no total until someone presses Confirm.</li><li><strong>Tax year:</strong> in, out and the difference for this UK tax year (6 April to 5 April), where the money went by category, the accountant&#39;s spreadsheets (CSV: invoices, payments, expenses; admins), and <strong>Invoice settings</strong> for admins: studio name, address, reply email, VAT number, bank details, VAT on new invoices and days to pay.</li></ul>\n<p>Nova Agent&#39;s money tools: <code>money_summary</code>, <code>list_invoices</code>, <code>draft_invoice</code>, <code>edit_invoice_draft</code>, <code>log_expense</code>. It has nothing that sends, approves, reminds, voids, records a payment or changes settings.</p>\n<p>Setting it up: invoices are emailed through the studio&#39;s own mail server (<code>MAIL_API_URL</code>, <code>MAIL_KEY</code>) from <code>INVOICE_FROM</code> (or the enquiry replies&#39; from address). Card payments use the Stripe keys Nova Bot already has (<code>STRIPE_SECRET_KEY</code>, <code>STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET</code>); the same webhook records invoice payments. The tables come from Nova Bot&#39;s <code>migrations/0029_money.sql</code>.</p>","text":"Nova Portal → Money (in Studio, after Clients) keeps the studio's invoices, the payments against them, and its expenses. The badge counts invoices and reminders waiting for an admin, plus overdue invoices; Today has an Invoices overdue tile. Four tiles: money in this month (payments), money out (confirmed expenses), what clients owe, and what's overdue. Write an invoice: pick a client from the list (their name and email fill in) or type them in. Add lines (what it's for, how many, the price of one), with VAT, the issue and due days, and a note. The totals add up as you type, in whole pence. It's saved waiting for approval ; Nova Agent can write one too. Approve (admins, signed in to Nova Portal in a browser): pressed twice (\"Email it to … now?\"). Nova Bot then emails the client a link to their invoice's own page, /invoice/ . There they can see it, print it or save it as a PDF, and pay: by card through Stripe's own page (when Stripe is set up; the payment comes back by itself), or by bank transfer with the studio's bank details. Admins can also Reject (with why), Send me a test, and Void. Anyone can Edit it until it's sent. Payments: Record a payment (amount, day, bank transfer / card / cash / other, a note). The invoice becomes part paid or paid, and the client's money on the client list follows: invoiced and owed go up when it's sent, owed comes down with each payment. An admin can take a payment back that was a mistake; a Stripe one is refunded in Stripe. Reminders: Ask for a reminder on an unpaid invoice. It waits under Reminders to approve until an admin approves it, then goes to the client with the link. Expenses: amount, what for (a list of categories), who it was paid to, the day, a note and a receipt. The receipt is a photo or a PDF, kept on the VPS ( data/receipts/ ), so you can add one any time. Expenses Nova Agent notes come in Not confirmed and count in no total until someone presses Confirm. Tax year: in, out and the difference for this UK tax year (6 April to 5 April), where the money went by category, the accountant's spreadsheets (CSV: invoices, payments, expenses; admins), and Invoice settings for admins: studio name, address, reply email, VAT number, bank details, VAT on new invoices and days to pay. Nova Agent's money tools: money_summary , list_invoices , draft_invoice , edit_invoice_draft , log_expense . It has nothing that sends, approves, reminds, voids, records a payment or changes settings. Setting it up: invoices are emailed through the studio's own mail server ( MAIL_API_URL , MAIL_KEY ) from INVOICE_FROM (or the enquiry replies' from address). Card payments use the Stripe keys Nova Bot already has ( STRIPE_SECRET_KEY , STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET ); the same webhook records invoice payments. The tables come from Nova Bot's migrations/0029_money.sql ."},{"id":"test-stuff-9","title":"Test stuff","html":"<p>Nova Portal → <strong>Test stuff</strong> (in Admin; admins only) lists things that look like tests or copies, so they can be cleared in a few taps. Today shows a quiet line (&quot;3 things look like tests · look&quot;) when there are any, and the tab has a count of the likely ones.</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Where it looks:</strong> on Nova Bot, enquiries, website chats, chat bookings (and their booking jobs), clients, Nova Index pages, shared notes, and drafts that haven&#39;t gone anywhere (social posts, one-to-one emails, invoices, expenses). On the VPS (Nova Agent), quests, missions, calendar notes, Fixer jobs and Nova Agent&#39;s files. If Nova Agent can&#39;t be reached, Nova Bot&#39;s list still shows, and it says Nova Agent&#39;s part isn&#39;t checked.</li><li><strong>Why it thinks so,</strong> in words on each card: a staff member&#39;s own email or a TV and film phone number (07700 900…) used as a customer; test, rude or joke words, or a name from the studio&#39;s own tests (the list is <code>src/tidy-words.js</code> in Nova Bot and <code>src/tidy-words.ts</code> here: change both); keyboard mashing; the same first message in several chats minutes apart; Claude&#39;s test chats; chat bookings that never reached Acuity; Nova Index pages whose chat is gone; the same facts, note, draft or file twice (the newest stays); copies of a quest (the one in progress stays); quests seconds long, made and finished within minutes (reminder tests); Fixer fixes for a problem that&#39;s gone or was fixed another way. One strong reason, or two weaker ones, makes it <strong>Likely a test</strong>; one weaker one makes it <strong>Maybe</strong>. A real client (sessions, money, consent, invoices) is never listed unless a strong sign says so, and then only as Maybe, and it can&#39;t be deleted here.</li><li><strong>Each card:</strong> what it is and where, when it was made and by whom, the reasons, what goes with it (a test chat&#39;s bookings, enquiry and Nova Index pages: <strong>Delete these too</strong> is ticked), and <strong>Delete</strong>, <strong>Not a test</strong> and <strong>Open</strong>.</li><li><strong>Delete all likely:</strong> pressed twice; the second press says how many. Esc cancels.</li><li><strong>Safe:</strong> everything deleted can be put back for 30 days (<strong>Put back</strong> right after, or under <strong>Recently deleted</strong>). Nova Index pages go through Nova Index&#39;s own bin; shared notes and expenses are deleted the way their apps do it, so every copy follows; quests, calendar notes and files go through their own delete, so the calendar&#39;s sync tells Nova Bot too. A Fixer job is only cleared (the Fixer&#39;s Reject), so it can&#39;t come back. <strong>Not a test</strong> is remembered (under <strong>Marked as real</strong>, with Undo). Every delete and put-back is logged with ids and kinds only.</li><li><strong>Accessible:</strong> every button is at least 44 px tall and works from the keyboard; after a delete the focus moves to the next card; what happened is read out; reasons and confidence are words, not colours.</li></ul>\n<p>Nova Agent can read the list (<code>test_stuff_list</code>) but has nothing that deletes. Nova Bot&#39;s side is <code>src/tidy.js</code> (tables from <code>migrations/0031_tidy.sql</code>: <code>tidy_bin</code>, <code>tidy_real</code>, <code>tidy_log</code>); Nova Agent&#39;s side is <code>src/tidy.ts</code> (its bin and &quot;Not a test&quot; list are in <code>data/tidy.json</code>), at <code>/tidy-api/state</code> and <code>/actions/tidy/*</code>, relayed online for admins only.</p>","text":"Nova Portal → Test stuff (in Admin; admins only) lists things that look like tests or copies, so they can be cleared in a few taps. Today shows a quiet line (\"3 things look like tests · look\") when there are any, and the tab has a count of the likely ones. Where it looks: on Nova Bot, enquiries, website chats, chat bookings (and their booking jobs), clients, Nova Index pages, shared notes, and drafts that haven't gone anywhere (social posts, one-to-one emails, invoices, expenses). On the VPS (Nova Agent), quests, missions, calendar notes, Fixer jobs and Nova Agent's files. If Nova Agent can't be reached, Nova Bot's list still shows, and it says Nova Agent's part isn't checked. Why it thinks so, in words on each card: a staff member's own email or a TV and film phone number (07700 900…) used as a customer; test, rude or joke words, or a name from the studio's own tests (the list is src/tidy-words.js in Nova Bot and src/tidy-words.ts here: change both); keyboard mashing; the same first message in several chats minutes apart; Claude's test chats; chat bookings that never reached Acuity; Nova Index pages whose chat is gone; the same facts, note, draft or file twice (the newest stays); copies of a quest (the one in progress stays); quests seconds long, made and finished within minutes (reminder tests); Fixer fixes for a problem that's gone or was fixed another way. One strong reason, or two weaker ones, makes it Likely a test ; one weaker one makes it Maybe . A real client (sessions, money, consent, invoices) is never listed unless a strong sign says so, and then only as Maybe, and it can't be deleted here. Each card: what it is and where, when it was made and by whom, the reasons, what goes with it (a test chat's bookings, enquiry and Nova Index pages: Delete these too is ticked), and Delete , Not a test and Open . Delete all likely: pressed twice; the second press says how many. Esc cancels. Safe: everything deleted can be put back for 30 days ( Put back right after, or under Recently deleted ). Nova Index pages go through Nova Index's own bin; shared notes and expenses are deleted the way their apps do it, so every copy follows; quests, calendar notes and files go through their own delete, so the calendar's sync tells Nova Bot too. A Fixer job is only cleared (the Fixer's Reject), so it can't come back. Not a test is remembered (under Marked as real , with Undo). Every delete and put-back is logged with ids and kinds only. Accessible: every button is at least 44 px tall and works from the keyboard; after a delete the focus moves to the next card; what happened is read out; reasons and confidence are words, not colours. Nova Agent can read the list ( test_stuff_list ) but has nothing that deletes. Nova Bot's side is src/tidy.js (tables from migrations/0031_tidy.sql : tidy_bin , tidy_real , tidy_log ); Nova Agent's side is src/tidy.ts (its bin and \"Not a test\" list are in data/tidy.json ), at /tidy-api/state and /actions/tidy/* , relayed online for admins only."},{"id":"google-10","title":"Google","html":"<p>Nova Portal → <strong>Google</strong> (in Admin; admins only) connects the studio&#39;s Google account and keeps it in step with Nova Agent. Everyone else just sees the results (events in Nova Calendar, replies in Enquiries, the Money sheet, Docs from Nova Notes).</p>\n<p><strong>Setting it up (about 5 minutes, once):</strong> the page shows one step at a time: a sentence, a button that opens the right Google page, and <strong>Copy</strong> buttons for exactly what to paste.</p>\n<ol><li><strong>Switch on Google&#39;s features</strong>: Nova Calendar, Gmail, Drive, People (Contacts), Sheets, Docs, Tasks and YouTube, in a Google Cloud project called Nova Agent.</li><li><strong>Google&#39;s permission screen</strong>: app name Nova Agent, audience External.</li><li><strong>Publish it</strong> (otherwise Google stops the connection every 7 days).</li><li><strong>Make the key</strong>: a Web application, with  as its web address and  to come back to.</li><li><strong>Paste the key</strong> (Client ID and Client secret: the secret is kept encrypted on Nova Bot).</li><li><strong>Connect Google</strong>: Google&#39;s page opens in a small window; pick the studio&#39;s account and tick every box. (&quot;This app isn&#39;t verified&quot;: press Advanced, then Go to Nova Agent. That&#39;s expected.)</li></ol>\n<p>A connection made before a feature existed shows <strong>Connect again to switch on: …</strong>; pressing it adds the new permissions.</p>\n<p><strong>What&#39;s kept in step</strong> (each has a switch, how it last went in plain words, and <strong>Sync now</strong>):</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Nova Calendar, both ways.</strong> Nova&#39;s Nova Calendar events and day cards go into a &quot;Novacane Studio&quot; calendar in Google (made on the first sync); events from the studio&#39;s own Google Nova Calendar come into Nova&#39;s Nova Calendar, and so count as busy time for quests. A change or a deletion on either side is made on the other (the later change wins). Every 5 minutes.</li><li class=\"sub\"><strong>Bookings in Google Nova Calendar:</strong> copies of Acuity&#39;s bookings (60 days ahead). Bookings are only ever made, moved or cancelled in Acuity: nothing books from Google.</li><li class=\"sub\"><strong>Nova Quests and music time in Google Nova Calendar</strong> (off unless switched on): Nova Agent&#39;s plan too.</li><li><strong>Send approved emails from Gmail.</strong> Enquiry replies, one-to-one emails, invoices and their reminders go from the studio&#39;s Gmail once an admin has approved them (so they&#39;re in its Sent folder), each joining its own thread. On the VPS the studio&#39;s own mail server sends them first and Gmail is the backup; with Gmail off or saying no, the mail server sends them. Campaigns always go through the mail server (with their own unsubscribe links).</li><li><strong>Customers&#39; replies into Enquiries.</strong> Every hour, replies to those emails (and emails from people with open enquiries) land in the right enquiry as their reply, without the quoted email under it, and the enquiry goes back to Open; a reply about a one-to-one email or an invoice starts a new enquiry. Gmail is only read, never changed.</li><li><strong>Clients in Google Contacts,</strong> both ways, under a &quot;Novacane clients&quot; label. A contact given the label in Google becomes a client (with no marketing consent: that stays Nova&#39;s alone, with its date and source, and is never sent to Google). Nobody is made twice: the same email links the two. Hourly.</li><li><strong>Pictures, videos and receipts in Google Drive,</strong> in a &quot;Nova Agent&quot; folder. Each social post picture or video and each receipt saved on the VPS gets a copy there, so posts go out (and Nova Portal shows receipts) even if Nova Agent can&#39;t be reached. Nova Agent only sees the files it made itself.</li><li><strong>Nightly backups:</strong> all of Nova Index (the last 14 nights kept) and Nova Agent&#39;s files, about 3am.</li><li><strong>Money in Google Sheets:</strong> one live sheet (Invoices, Payments, Expenses) for the accountant, brought up to date hourly and when someone presses <strong>Open in Google Sheets</strong> in Money → Tax year.</li><li><strong>Gmail as Enquiries&#39; inbox.</strong> Every 15 minutes, new customer emails to the studio&#39;s Gmail (its Primary inbox) come into Enquiries like the website&#39;s form; newsletters, notifications, mailing lists and other automatic mail stay out, and likely spam goes to Enquiries&#39; Spam folder. With the Gmail permission each gets a <strong>Nova</strong> label in Gmail, and one marked <strong>Done</strong> is archived in Gmail (back in the inbox if it&#39;s opened again). Nothing is sent from here.</li><li><strong>Google Meet links.</strong> Tick <strong>Google Meet link</strong> on an event in Nova Calendar and Google makes the link at the next sync (it then shows on the event, on Today and in Nova Agent&#39;s what_now); online-session bookings get one too.</li><li><strong>Nova Quests in Google Tasks.</strong> Nova Agent&#39;s own person&#39;s quests (not repeating ones) are kept in a <strong>Nova quests</strong> list every 10 minutes; ticking one off in Google Tasks marks it done in Nova.</li><li><strong>Nova Notes kept in Google Docs.</strong> A shared note ticked <strong>Keep in Google Docs</strong> (Nova Notes → File) stays in step with its Doc both ways every 15 minutes; when both changed, the newer wins and the other is kept as a copy. <strong>Open a Google Doc</strong> (Nova Notes → File) brings a Doc from the studio&#39;s Drive into Nova Notes; one Nova didn&#39;t make only comes in (Google lets Nova change only its own Docs).</li><li><strong>Files and invoices in Drive.</strong> Nova Agent&#39;s files are kept in &quot;Nova Agent/Files&quot; as they&#39;re saved, and each sent invoice is a Doc in &quot;Nova Agent/Invoices&quot; (download it as a PDF from Drive), updated when it&#39;s paid or cancelled.</li><li><strong>YouTube.</strong> The channel&#39;s subscribers (Social → at a glance) and each video&#39;s views, likes and comments, and YouTube as a place to post in Social: one video per post, its first line the title, uploaded only after an admin&#39;s Approve. Google keeps uploads from a new Google Cloud project private until YouTube has checked it: make each one public in YouTube Studio till then.</li><li><strong>Today:</strong> Nova Portal → Today shows today&#39;s calendar (Nova&#39;s events and Google Nova Calendar&#39;s, with Meet links).</li><li><strong>Google Contacts search:</strong> Campaigns&#39; one-to-one email form has <strong>Find in Google Contacts</strong>, which fills in the name and email.</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Within the free Workers plan:</strong> each part works in small steps (a few Google calls and database trips a run), saves where it got to and carries on at the next free minute (&quot;… the rest next run&quot;). Google busy or briefly down holds that part 5, 10, 20… minutes (2 hours at most). Google turning the connection down shows <strong>Connect again</strong> here and pings the admins once a day. <strong>Sync now</strong> starts in the background and this page shows how it went.</p>\n<p><strong>Later:</strong> Google reviews (Business Profile) need Google to approve the studio for its Business Profile API first (Google&#39;s access request form, project nova-agent).</p>\n<p>Nova Notes&#39; <strong>Send to Google Docs</strong> is one tap once Google is connected: the note becomes a Google Doc in the Nova Agent folder and opens (not connected: the old dialog).</p>\n<p>Nova Agent can look but not touch: <code>google_calendar_busy</code>, <code>gmail_search</code> (who, subject, when and a snippet), <code>google_contacts_find</code>, <code>google_drive_search</code>, <code>google_doc_read</code>, <code>google_tasks_list</code> and <code>youtube_stats</code>, and what_now includes today&#39;s calendar. There&#39;s no tool that sends, books, posts, uploads or changes anything in Google; a YouTube video is a Social draft that an admin approves.</p>\n<p>Built in Nova Bot&#39;s <code>src/google/</code> (<code>calendar.js</code>, <code>gmail.js</code>, <code>contacts.js</code>, <code>drive.js</code>, <code>sheets.js</code>; <code>index.js</code> runs one part a minute at most on the cron, within the free Workers plan&#39;s limit of 50 calls a run; links between Nova&#39;s things and Google&#39;s are in <code>google_links</code>, <code>migrations/0032_google.sql</code>), and here in <code>src/google.ts</code> (copies to Drive, the nightly file backup), <code>src/google-agent.ts</code> and <code>web/portal/google.js</code>.</p>","text":"Nova Portal → Google (in Admin; admins only) connects the studio's Google account and keeps it in step with Nova Agent. Everyone else just sees the results (events in Nova Calendar, replies in Enquiries, the Money sheet, Docs from Nova Notes). Setting it up (about 5 minutes, once): the page shows one step at a time: a sentence, a button that opens the right Google page, and Copy buttons for exactly what to paste. Switch on Google's features : Nova Calendar, Gmail, Drive, People (Contacts), Sheets, Docs, Tasks and YouTube, in a Google Cloud project called Nova Agent. Google's permission screen : app name Nova Agent, audience External. Publish it (otherwise Google stops the connection every 7 days). Make the key : a Web application, with as its web address and to come back to. Paste the key (Client ID and Client secret: the secret is kept encrypted on Nova Bot). Connect Google : Google's page opens in a small window; pick the studio's account and tick every box. (\"This app isn't verified\": press Advanced, then Go to Nova Agent. That's expected.) A connection made before a feature existed shows Connect again to switch on: … ; pressing it adds the new permissions. What's kept in step (each has a switch, how it last went in plain words, and Sync now ): Nova Calendar, both ways. Nova's Nova Calendar events and day cards go into a \"Novacane Studio\" calendar in Google (made on the first sync); events from the studio's own Google Nova Calendar come into Nova's Nova Calendar, and so count as busy time for quests. A change or a deletion on either side is made on the other (the later change wins). Every 5 minutes. Bookings in Google Nova Calendar: copies of Acuity's bookings (60 days ahead). Bookings are only ever made, moved or cancelled in Acuity: nothing books from Google. Nova Quests and music time in Google Nova Calendar (off unless switched on): Nova Agent's plan too. Send approved emails from Gmail. Enquiry replies, one-to-one emails, invoices and their reminders go from the studio's Gmail once an admin has approved them (so they're in its Sent folder), each joining its own thread. On the VPS the studio's own mail server sends them first and Gmail is the backup; with Gmail off or saying no, the mail server sends them. Campaigns always go through the mail server (with their own unsubscribe links). Customers' replies into Enquiries. Every hour, replies to those emails (and emails from people with open enquiries) land in the right enquiry as their reply, without the quoted email under it, and the enquiry goes back to Open; a reply about a one-to-one email or an invoice starts a new enquiry. Gmail is only read, never changed. Clients in Google Contacts, both ways, under a \"Novacane clients\" label. A contact given the label in Google becomes a client (with no marketing consent: that stays Nova's alone, with its date and source, and is never sent to Google). Nobody is made twice: the same email links the two. Hourly. Pictures, videos and receipts in Google Drive, in a \"Nova Agent\" folder. Each social post picture or video and each receipt saved on the VPS gets a copy there, so posts go out (and Nova Portal shows receipts) even if Nova Agent can't be reached. Nova Agent only sees the files it made itself. Nightly backups: all of Nova Index (the last 14 nights kept) and Nova Agent's files, about 3am. Money in Google Sheets: one live sheet (Invoices, Payments, Expenses) for the accountant, brought up to date hourly and when someone presses Open in Google Sheets in Money → Tax year. Gmail as Enquiries' inbox. Every 15 minutes, new customer emails to the studio's Gmail (its Primary inbox) come into Enquiries like the website's form; newsletters, notifications, mailing lists and other automatic mail stay out, and likely spam goes to Enquiries' Spam folder. With the Gmail permission each gets a Nova label in Gmail, and one marked Done is archived in Gmail (back in the inbox if it's opened again). Nothing is sent from here. Google Meet links. Tick Google Meet link on an event in Nova Calendar and Google makes the "},{"id":"computer-11","title":"Computer","html":"<p>Nova Portal → <strong>Computer</strong> (in Admin; admins only; <code>?view=computer</code>) is the studio&#39;s VPS: the server where Nova Bot and Nova Agent both run, day and night, with the laptop off. At the top, <strong>Live now</strong> says Nova&#39;s address, where Nova Agent runs (on the VPS), the one command to move it back to a laptop (<code>vps/agent-switch-back.sh</code>, run in Nova Bot&#39;s folder; it asks first) and any warnings. Under it: the VPS&#39;s memory, disk and services (Nova Bot, Nova Agent, mail, backups, timed jobs), the last backup, each job&#39;s last run and recent problems, with <strong>Back up now</strong>, <strong>Restart Nova Bot</strong>, <strong>Restart Nova Agent</strong> and <strong>Restart web front</strong> (Restart asks twice). Console&#39;s <code>computer</code> command shows the same. It was called Desk once (inside it still is: <code>desk.js</code>, <code>/app/api/desk</code>).</p>","text":"Nova Portal → Computer (in Admin; admins only; ?view=computer ) is the studio's VPS: the server where Nova Bot and Nova Agent both run, day and night, with the laptop off. At the top, Live now says Nova's address, where Nova Agent runs (on the VPS), the one command to move it back to a laptop ( vps/agent-switch-back.sh , run in Nova Bot's folder; it asks first) and any warnings. Under it: the VPS's memory, disk and services (Nova Bot, Nova Agent, mail, backups, timed jobs), the last backup, each job's last run and recent problems, with Back up now , Restart Nova Bot , Restart Nova Agent and Restart web front (Restart asks twice). Console's computer command shows the same. It was called Desk once (inside it still is: desk.js , /app/api/desk )."},{"id":"live-chat-12","title":"Live chat","html":"<p>Someone from the studio can answer a website chat themselves, in Nova Portal → <strong>Conversations</strong>.</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Open a chat.</strong> Under it: who has it, <strong>Take over</strong> (or <strong>Hand back to NovaBot</strong>), and a reply box. Enter sends, Shift+Enter makes a new line.</li><li><strong>Take over</strong> (or just reply): NovaBot stops answering that chat and the visitor sees &quot;Sam from the studio has joined the chat.&quot; Your messages show in their chat with your first name. <strong>Hand back</strong> gives it back to NovaBot, which reads what you said.</li><li><strong>Live both ways:</strong> the visitor&#39;s chat checks for your messages every few seconds while it&#39;s open (a quick look, nothing held open); an open chat in Nova Portal checks for theirs every 4 seconds (10 while NovaBot has it). The list shows <strong>Live · Sam</strong> on chats someone has.</li><li><strong>Phones:</strong> a visitor asking for a person (&quot;can I talk to someone?&quot;) marks the chat <strong>Needs a person</strong> and pings the team quietly (once per half hour per chat); a visitor writing in a chat you have pings you (once every two minutes at most). The ping opens that chat.</li><li><strong>Rules:</strong> these are replies to someone who started the conversation (a service, not marketing), so they need no approval. Only a person signed in to Nova Portal can write as the studio: NovaBot&#39;s AI never does, and Nova Agent has no tool for it.</li></ul>\n<p>Nova Bot&#39;s side is <code>src/livechat.js</code> (<code>POST /chat/live</code> for the website&#39;s chat; <code>POST /app/api/conversations/live</code> for Nova Portal), with <code>migrations/0033_live_chat.sql</code> (a <code>sender</code> column on <code>chat_messages</code>, and <code>chat_live</code>).</p>","text":"Someone from the studio can answer a website chat themselves, in Nova Portal → Conversations . Open a chat. Under it: who has it, Take over (or Hand back to NovaBot ), and a reply box. Enter sends, Shift+Enter makes a new line. Take over (or just reply): NovaBot stops answering that chat and the visitor sees \"Sam from the studio has joined the chat.\" Your messages show in their chat with your first name. Hand back gives it back to NovaBot, which reads what you said. Live both ways: the visitor's chat checks for your messages every few seconds while it's open (a quick look, nothing held open); an open chat in Nova Portal checks for theirs every 4 seconds (10 while NovaBot has it). The list shows Live · Sam on chats someone has. Phones: a visitor asking for a person (\"can I talk to someone?\") marks the chat Needs a person and pings the team quietly (once per half hour per chat); a visitor writing in a chat you have pings you (once every two minutes at most). The ping opens that chat. Rules: these are replies to someone who started the conversation (a service, not marketing), so they need no approval. Only a person signed in to Nova Portal can write as the studio: NovaBot's AI never does, and Nova Agent has no tool for it. Nova Bot's side is src/livechat.js ( POST /chat/live for the website's chat; POST /app/api/conversations/live for Nova Portal), with migrations/0033_live_chat.sql (a sender column on chat_messages , and chat_live )."},{"id":"portal-on-your-phone-its-own-app-13","title":"Nova Portal on your phone (its own app)","html":"<p>Nova Portal can be its own app on a phone&#39;s home screen, separate from Nova Agent: its own icon and name, opening straight into Nova Portal, full screen, with its own notifications. On the phone open <strong>/portal/?app=1</strong> (in Safari on an iPhone, Chrome on Android), sign in, then <strong>Share → Add to Home Screen</strong> (iPhone) or <strong>⋮ → Add to Home screen / Install app</strong> (Android). Opened from that icon, Nova Portal stays Nova Portal (even when it reloads); anywhere else (a normal browser tab) Nova Portal opens inside Nova Agent as before. Tapping a notification on a phone with the Nova Portal app opens Nova Portal, on the right tab (<code>web/shared/inside.js</code> decides; Nova Bot lets Nova Portal&#39;s pages through; <code>sw.js</code> routes taps).</p>","text":"Nova Portal can be its own app on a phone's home screen, separate from Nova Agent: its own icon and name, opening straight into Nova Portal, full screen, with its own notifications. On the phone open /portal/?app=1 (in Safari on an iPhone, Chrome on Android), sign in, then Share → Add to Home Screen (iPhone) or ⋮ → Add to Home screen / Install app (Android). Opened from that icon, Nova Portal stays Nova Portal (even when it reloads); anywhere else (a normal browser tab) Nova Portal opens inside Nova Agent as before. Tapping a notification on a phone with the Nova Portal app opens Nova Portal, on the right tab ( web/shared/inside.js decides; Nova Bot lets Nova Portal's pages through; sw.js routes taps)."}],"built":[{"id":"the-api-on-nova-bot-s-worker-0","title":"The API (on Nova Bot's worker)","html":"<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>POST /auth/login</code></td><td><code>{ email, password, client? }</code> → session cookie, or an app token with <code>client: &quot;app&quot;</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>POST /auth/logout</code></td><td>ends this session everywhere</td></tr><tr><td><code>GET /auth/me</code> · <code>GET /auth/status</code></td><td>who&#39;s signed in · <code>{ setupNeeded, signedIn, staff }</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>POST /auth/setup</code></td><td>the first admin (with the <code>ADMIN_PASSWORD</code> secret)</td></tr><tr><td><code>GET /auth/invite?token=</code> · <code>POST /auth/invite/accept</code></td><td>accepting an invite</td></tr><tr><td><code>GET /staff</code> · <code>POST /staff</code> · <code>POST /staff/:id/invite</code></td><td>the crew, inviting, a fresh link (admins)</td></tr><tr><td><code>GET /staff/:id</code> · <code>PATCH /staff/:id</code></td><td>a profile; changing name, planet, role or status</td></tr><tr><td><code>GET /staff/:id/planet.svg</code></td><td>the planet badge (<code>?size=</code>, <code>?animate=1</code>)</td></tr><tr><td><code>GET /staff/:id/index</code></td><td>that person&#39;s Nova Index partition and the studio&#39;s shared facts</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<ul><li><strong>Passwords:</strong> PBKDF2-SHA256, salted, 100,000 rounds.</li><li><strong>Sessions:</strong> a random token in an httpOnly, Secure cookie. Only its hash is stored, and signing out deletes it.</li><li><strong>Brute force:</strong> sign-in, setup and invite attempts are rate limited.</li><li><strong>Cross-site changes:</strong> changes must come from the site itself.</li></ul>\n<p>The code is in <a href=\"https://github.com/tuniveza/nova-bot\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">nova-bot</a> under <code>src/portal/</code>.</p>","text":"POST /auth/login { email, password, client? } → session cookie, or an app token with client: \"app\" POST /auth/logout ends this session everywhere GET /auth/me · GET /auth/status who's signed in · { setupNeeded, signedIn, staff } POST /auth/setup the first admin (with the ADMIN_PASSWORD secret) GET /auth/invite?token= · POST /auth/invite/accept accepting an invite GET /staff · POST /staff · POST /staff/:id/invite the crew, inviting, a fresh link (admins) GET /staff/:id · PATCH /staff/:id a profile; changing name, planet, role or status GET /staff/:id/planet.svg the planet badge ( ?size= , ?animate=1 ) GET /staff/:id/index that person's Nova Index partition and the studio's shared facts Passwords: PBKDF2-SHA256, salted, 100,000 rounds. Sessions: a random token in an httpOnly, Secure cookie. Only its hash is stored, and signing out deletes it. Brute force: sign-in, setup and invite attempts are rate limited. Cross-site changes: changes must come from the site itself. The code is in nova-bot under src/portal/ ."}],"news":[],"history":{"total":91,"first":"2026-10-07T01:34:16+01:00","commits":[{"hash":"3e5e306","date":"2026-10-14T06:14:02+01:00","subject":"Manual and READMEs: Nova Agent runs on the VPS (day and night, every laptop off), not on the studio PC; Quests' options and the Fixer's wide view described","body":""},{"hash":"3350456","date":"2026-10-14T06:14:02+01:00","subject":"Portal's lanes share lines when there's room (Plans, You and the settings icons beside Today; Admin beside Studio's second half): about half the height at 1280x800. The home's welcome sizes itself in two layouts instead of a dozen when nothing changed, and rounds its size down, so it no longer ends a hair too big and scrolls","body":""},{"hash":"4ea5810","date":"2026-10-14T05:58:10+01:00","subject":"Computer intro says the VPS, not Nova's own computer","body":""},{"hash":"0e275ec","date":"2026-10-14T05:47:48+01:00","subject":"One screen everywhere: inside Nova Agent no panel's page (or its <main>) scrolls; only a box inside it does. Portal's open section scrolls inside itself under compact lanes, Today side by side (numbers | today's calendar + new enquiries); Quests' groups and days as columns; Lossless's four cards in a row; the Visualizer's columns (two by two or stacked on phones, each scrolling inside); the Fixer's open tab under its numbers and tabs; Index's open view; Observatory's decks; Calendar's week, day and list scroll inside their own box and the month shares the screen with the day's plan on phones and tablets. Panels and Portal's sections show at once (no fade in). check-fit.mjs fails a page or a <main> that scrolls inside Nova Agent","body":""},{"hash":"3a49323","date":"2026-10-14T02:54:08+01:00","subject":"Fit on screen in every panel: /shared/fit.js + fit.css keep menus, pop-ups, tooltips, non-modal dialogs and anything marked data-fit (or handed over with NovaFit.keep) inside the screen — nudged back in just far enough, capped and scrolling inside only when bigger than the screen, checked again on resize, turning round, a phone's keyboard and growing content; Agent's activity list and the planet card hooked in. scripts/check-fit-all.sh runs the whole fit check (throwaway server, 360×640, 768×1024, 1440×900, the Manual) and check-fit.mjs now also proves the fit layer is on every page and works after the window shrinks","body":""},{"hash":"c27179b","date":"2026-10-14T02:12:02+01:00","subject":"Computer says the VPS inside: 'Your VPS', 'On the VPS', 'Move Nova Agent to the VPS'; Console names Nova Agent instead of the studio computer; Manual's Computer section describes the VPS (no Cloudflare)","body":""},{"hash":"8b1676e","date":"2026-10-14T01:23:54+01:00","subject":"All addresses: every web address in the suite in one list (Manual → All addresses; Portal → Settings → Addresses, and Apps and links), each with a plain line, Copy and Open; admins also see the ones other services use. Every link people see is https://nova.novacane.co.uk now (no studio-computer addresses in Portal, the Manual or the READMEs). scripts/check-addresses.mjs checks each one answers live","body":""},{"hash":"01bcb95","date":"2026-10-14T01:17:34+01:00","subject":"Campaigns sent by the studio's own mail server: Resend gone from Agent, Portal, the Fixer's rules and the docs","body":"Portal shows a campaign going out (Sending · n of m) and own-server results (sent, unsubscribed,\ndidn't go); Agent's campaign summaries say the same."},{"hash":"2b2f304","date":"2026-10-14T01:12:16+01:00","subject":"Computer shows Nova's own computer (the VPS) only: where Nova Agent runs and how to move it, mail sender, backups kept, Restart Nova Agent; Console's computer/deploy without the old host","body":""},{"hash":"a23c9e9","date":"2026-10-13T22:54:11+01:00","subject":"Nova's own address in Nova Agent: nova.novacane.co.uk (the PC's link, links, the Manual); Computer talks about Nova's own computer","body":""},{"hash":"188bc07","date":"2026-10-13T22:44:31+01:00","subject":"Portal's README: Computer (Live now, the switch commands, the VPS side by side); Manual rebuilt","body":""},{"hash":"3c6c6b5","date":"2026-10-13T22:43:26+01:00","subject":"Desk is called Computer now: Portal → Admin → Computer, Console's computer command (desk still works, and it says which side is live), view=computer, the status words","body":""},{"hash":"fa3ffaf","date":"2026-10-13T22:31:52+01:00","subject":"Switch-over: Desk's Live now card (which side is live, switch and switch-back commands, warnings); Portal gets a new notification address quietly when the server's key changes, or asks once, calmly","body":""},{"hash":"cbde021","date":"2026-10-13T19:44:41+01:00","subject":"Portal → Admin → Desk: Nova Bot on Cloudflare and on the VPS side by side (online, how busy, jobs, PC link, problems), back up and restart for admins","body":""},{"hash":"ac41738","date":"2026-10-12T22:00:11+01:00","subject":"Docs and Manual: Google round two (inbox, Meet, Tasks, Docs, Files, YouTube, Today, limits)","body":""},{"hash":"321c19c","date":"2026-10-12T21:33:21+01:00","subject":"Google round two on the PC and in the panels: Tasks sync, Files in Drive, Agent's Drive/Docs/Tasks/YouTube tools, YouTube in Social, Meet in Calendar, today's calendar in Portal and what_now, Keep in Google Docs and Open a Google Doc in Notes, Google Contacts search in one-to-one emails","body":""},{"hash":"ec79681","date":"2026-10-12T21:05:43+01:00","subject":"WIP Portal Google: sync progress, Connect again banner","body":""},{"hash":"e6c2d32","date":"2026-10-12T20:21:21+01:00","subject":"Sizing: Portal's tabs never squash or cut off (the side menu only from 1024px; tab lanes below that whatever's chosen), Chats on narrow phones, Notes never left short of its frame, and a resize check","body":""},{"hash":"1d69ce2","date":"2026-10-12T20:19:55+01:00","subject":"Portal's Admin address is view=manage: ad blockers block any address with \"view=ad…\" (old admin links and remembered places are turned into the new one)","body":""},{"hash":"b29d53e","date":"2026-10-12T19:36:52+01:00","subject":"Portal → Google: Connect opens Google in its own window with a one-time pass (never inside Portal's frame), looks again when it closes","body":""},{"hash":"93a17ce","date":"2026-10-12T19:28:07+01:00","subject":"Portal → Conversations: answer a website chat yourself (Take over, a reply box, Hand back), live both ways","body":""},{"hash":"4d6e5b8","date":"2026-10-12T19:19:14+01:00","subject":"Google: the Connect step shows the key's boxes when no key is saved yet, instead of a switched-off button","body":""},{"hash":"10334b3","date":"2026-10-12T19:17:54+01:00","subject":"Manual: Social, Money, the sorted inbox, one-to-one emails, Test stuff, the tab lanes, planet + chosen colour, Notes' Welcome guide, and Google (once connected)","body":""},{"hash":"2303434","date":"2026-10-12T18:52:49+01:00","subject":"Google: Portal → Admin → Google (set up one step at a time, what's kept in step), copies to Drive and nightly backups, Money's sheet, Notes to Docs in one tap, Agent's read-only Google tools","body":""},{"hash":"bee5413","date":"2026-10-12T18:29:13+01:00","subject":"Music: a calm late-night studio band (moving bass, melodies that come back and get answered, soulful chords, soft swung drums) in seven pieces","body":"Glow, Warm keys, Tape beat, Late night, Night trio, Whisper garage and Afro glow, each a groove\n(68-86 bpm) in sections (intro, A, B, breakdowns). Peaks stay at or under -27.6 dBFS at the\ndefault volume; scripts/music-previews.mjs renders WAVs and measures each piece."},{"hash":"4371d4d","date":"2026-10-12T18:09:33+01:00","subject":"Portal → Test stuff: what looks like tests or copies, with why, Delete (into a bin) and Not a test","body":"Admins only. Nova Bot's list (enquiries, chats, bookings, clients, Index, notes, drafts) and the\nstudio PC's (quests, missions, calendar notes, Fixer jobs, files), each with reasons in words, what\ngoes with it, Open; deleting goes through each thing's own delete with a copy in a 30-day bin.\nAgent can only read the list."},{"hash":"f7803be","date":"2026-10-12T17:43:35+01:00","subject":"Portal tabs: lanes (Today, You and Admin share the first; a lane each for Studio, Plans and Settings) with name chips and soft lines between","body":""},{"hash":"0f8f196","date":"2026-10-12T17:28:07+01:00","subject":"Portal tabs: compact, one line per group (its name in a column on the left)","body":""},{"hash":"10212be","date":"2026-10-12T16:31:50+01:00","subject":"Money: invoices, payments and expenses in Portal, receipts on the PC","body":"Portal → Money (Studio, after Clients): invoices that are emailed to a client only after an\nadmin's Approve, payments (part paid, paid), reminders that wait for an Approve, expenses with\nreceipts kept on the studio PC (src/receipts.ts, relayed for staff online), the UK tax year's\ntotals, the accountant's CSV and invoice settings. Today gets an \"Invoices overdue\" tile.\nAgent gets money_summary, list_invoices, draft_invoice, edit_invoice_draft and log_expense\n(unconfirmed); nothing that sends, approves, pays or changes settings."},{"hash":"06f8a94","date":"2026-10-12T16:21:15+01:00","subject":"Social (Quest 4): Portal → Social, pictures and videos kept on the studio computer, Agent's social tools","body":"- Portal → Social (Studio group, after Campaigns): write a post (counts for Instagram's limits,\n  Facebook/Instagram, pictures made JPEGs, videos, a UK time), waiting cards with Approve (twice),\n  Edit and Reject, posts to put up by hand while Meta isn't connected (copy, download, \"I posted\n  it\"), what's coming up by day, results, followers, comments with replies to approve, ideas and\n  trends (opens Agent with the question ready) and a link to Meta's Ads Manager\n- src/social-media.ts: the files on this computer (random ids, checked by their first bytes,\n  ranges for videos), behind a small store so the VPS can take over; their addresses relayed\n  for signed-in staff (and Nova Bot, for Meta)\n- Agent: social_context, create_social_draft, edit_social_draft, list_social_posts,\n  social_results, list_social_comments, draft_comment_reply; nothing approves or posts"},{"hash":"e5e3f8f","date":"2026-10-12T16:14:34+01:00","subject":"Portal inbox: sort enquiries like tickets, Spam, saved replies, chats marked","body":"- Enquiries: New / Open / Waiting on them / Done / Spam chips with counts, search,\n  one-press moves, who's on it, labels, the spam reason, Not spam.\n- Saved replies: add, change, remove; a picker in the reply box fills it ({name}\n  becomes their first name), and Send still sends.\n- Conversations: Needs a person / Done marks and filters.\n- Agent: enquiry_set_state (sorts only) and saved_replies_list.\n- The reply box's To line wraps a long address."},{"hash":"e8fb4a9","date":"2026-10-12T16:05:44+01:00","subject":"One-to-one emails: Agent drafts personal emails, an admin approves them in Portal → Campaigns","body":"Agent gets draft_outreach_email, edit_outreach_email and list_outreach_emails (no send or\napprove tool). Portal's Campaigns view gets a One-to-one emails part: write one, waiting cards\nwith Approve (pressed twice) / Edit / Reject / Send me a test, sent and rejected ones, and a\nbox to record someone who replied \"no thanks\". The Campaigns badge counts both."},{"hash":"e5274cd","date":"2026-10-11T13:50:26+01:00","subject":"Portal tabs: every section at once, whole groups per line","body":"All of Portal's sections show together (no clicking a group to see its tabs).\nSmall groups (Today, Plans, You, Admin, settings) share the first line with thin\ndividers; Studio has its own line and splits evenly when it must wrap; a group\nthat doesn't fit the first line goes after Studio. Phone bar and side menu unchanged."},{"hash":"1f748b5","date":"2026-10-11T12:11:55+01:00","subject":"Everything fits: nothing hangs off the screen in any panel; what doesn't fit scrolls inside its own box","body":"scripts/check-fit.mjs opens Nova Agent's home and every panel (on its own and inside Nova Agent) at\n7 sizes (incl. a phone with its keyboard up) with long sample content, opens every sheet, dialog and\npop-up, and reports anything past the screen or its clipping box. Fixes what it found:\n- Portal: the side-menu tab row started off its left edge (tabs unreachable); Booking tools' picked\n  day was wider than the screen; a chat's Enquiry pill was clamped away; Options buttons squashed\n  their icon; a busy day's dots spilled out; long words wrap in views\n- Calendar: long words break inside cards; day cards no longer squashed; narrow short events clamp\n  their title to their height; What to show scrolls inside on short screens\n- Notes: menus and pop-ups scroll inside (and stay on screen) on short screens; snippets wrap\n- Nova Agent: chat action chips, mission summaries and file titles wrap; Ho"},{"hash":"194fcc2","date":"2026-10-11T11:45:52+01:00","subject":"Portal tabs: two tidy rows (group pills + settings icons, then the open group's tabs)","body":"Row 1 has a medium-large pill per group with its counts and the settings icons;\nrow 2 shows only the open group's tabs (none for one-tab groups). Same look\ninside Nova Agent on a tablet. Phone bar and side menu unchanged."},{"hash":"ccda75f","date":"2026-10-11T11:23:11+01:00","subject":"P0-4: chats, quests, missions and reminders tied to each person","body":"- Who's asking (src/person.ts): online, the staff member Nova Bot's relay\n  passes (marked on the request object itself, so it can't be forged); on\n  the PC, the person Nova Agent works for. Anything with no owner is theirs.\n- The Agent's system prompt names the person and their role; what its tools\n  make (missions, quests, blocked times, rhythm) is theirs; Index memory is\n  theirs.\n- Each person has their own Agent conversation (data/chats/<staff id>.json);\n  the PC person's old browser history is brought over once.\n- Missions, quests and blocks have an `owner`. Quests panels, Missions and\n  the Agent's tools show your own; admins and the PC can switch to\n  everyone's. Staff change only their own (and quests tied to a shared note).\n- Each person is planned in their own time: their own blocks, music time and\n  (optional) rhythm; one person's quests never take another's time.\n- Reminders"},{"hash":"b6a81f5","date":"2026-10-11T05:13:18+01:00","subject":"Merge branch 'calm-audio'","body":""},{"hash":"e466354","date":"2026-10-11T04:35:45+01:00","subject":"Portal centred everywhere, and a tidier phone tab bar","body":"With text centred (the default): headings and their buttons gather in the middle on phones and\ncomputers alike, phone cards stack their title over the time instead of pushing them to the\nedges, the Admin switch and the side menu sit in the middle. Left keeps the classic rows.\nOn a phone, groups whose tabs all live under More no longer leave a row of empty lines, and\nthe chosen tab's glowing line sits under its name instead of through it."},{"hash":"9b6c6e5","date":"2026-10-11T04:28:57+01:00","subject":"Plain names: no more \"every Nova app\" (it's all Nova Agent now)","body":"Portal's sign-in, profile, crew and invite wording, and Index's empty states, speak of Nova Agent\n(and Nova Bot) instead of separate Nova apps."},{"hash":"ce1ff1c","date":"2026-10-11T04:25:36+01:00","subject":"Dates and times written the British way, in London time, whatever the browser's language","body":"Calendar's mid-size day labels read \"19 Oct\" and \"19/10\" (not \"10month 19day\" and \"10 19\");\nthe status line's clock no longer follows the browser's language (\"So 5:04 am\"); Visualizer's\nstep times and every other date label say en-GB, Europe/London."},{"hash":"7e770a8","date":"2026-10-11T04:01:04+01:00","subject":"Portal room to breathe + a Menu option; apps open full screen; Nova Agent's icon choice","body":"- Portal: more space between tabs, rows and groups, group labels clear of their tabs; buttons\n  and chips get more room around their words (centred by eye) and between each other.\n- Portal → Options → Menu: Tabs on top (default) or Side menu (the original vertical menu);\n  the tab bar now lives in tabbar.css, switched off for the side menu.\n- Opening an app: Nova Agent's bars are simply away (no slide or trail to watch); they come\n  back at the edge as before, and Always shown keeps them.\n- The duplicate Nova Agent title over the conversation is for screen readers only now; the\n  top banner's icon can be the classic mark or the chat bubble (Panels window)."},{"hash":"2b4fffb","date":"2026-10-11T03:48:56+01:00","subject":"Calm audio: six new generative music pieces with seeds, gentle ASMR-like extra sounds","body":"Music (shared/ambient.js): Glow (the original, kept) now takes turns with Warm keys,\nSlow drone, Tape chords, Distant air, Low strings and Night rain, crossfading slowly\n(never the same piece twice running). A seed (six-letter code) drives the piece order,\nkey and mode (always next to D lydian, so the sound effects fit), pace, chords,\nvoicings, filters, reverb size, echo and textures: a new seed each session, or keep\none / type one back in (Portal > Options > Sound). Pauses while the app is hidden,\ntinted subtly by the theme's colour, a safety curve at the end so it can never clip.\nSounds (shared/sfx.js), with the Quiet extras switch (off by default): a velvety\nwhisper only during sustained scrolling or scrollbar dragging, soft fabric on sheets,\na brush that slides the way a tab moved, a felt touch under switches, a shimmer on\ntheme changes, a warm unfolding when a panel opens; each vari"},{"hash":"91d1fad","date":"2026-10-11T03:25:54+01:00","subject":"Plain app names again (only Nova Agent and Nova Bot keep Nova); titles on one surface; Portal's tabs wrap on tablets too","body":"Undoes the 'Nova <App>' renaming line by line (the ✦ marks, the tab bar and the scrollbars\nstay). Inside Nova Agent a shared rule kept Portal's tabs on one sliding row under 981px:\nfrom 761px they now wrap too, so every tab is on screen."},{"hash":"43e7562","date":"2026-10-11T03:18:54+01:00","subject":"Titles sit centred at the top of each open app (icon + name in the theme's gradient), Back and Reload tucked in the corners; Portal's tabs wrap so all stay on screen","body":""},{"hash":"d6d2213","date":"2026-10-11T02:57:49+01:00","subject":"Nova first in every app name (the bottom bars keep their short labels)","body":"Nova Portal, Nova Agent, Nova Calendar, Nova Notes, Nova Index, Nova Quests, Nova Missions,\nNova Lossless, Nova Visualizer, Nova Observatory, Nova Manual: titles, headers, the Panels\nwindow, the status line, the Manual, manifests, messages and alerts. Also: the Nova mark's CSS on\nthe panel icons (chat.html), Portal's tab labels and tabbar.js, and the scrollbars link in each page."},{"hash":"14994f8","date":"2026-10-11T02:57:49+01:00","subject":"Portal: the side menu is a tab bar across the top (groups, badges, arrow keys, wheel, soft edges)","body":""},{"hash":"e2b63d9","date":"2026-10-11T02:57:49+01:00","subject":"Icons: the same small Nova sparkle in the corner of every app's icon","body":""},{"hash":"95b9569","date":"2026-10-11T02:21:20+01:00","subject":"Themes: a colour spectrum with a Custom colour; one button look for every panel","body":"A spectrum of themes for all of Nova Agent (web/shared/spectrum.js): Crimson, Rose,\nCoral, Amber, Lime, Jade, Teal, Glacier, Indigo, Violet and Orchid join the old ones,\neach a hand-tuned set (deep sky, luminous accent, matching gradients and glows) whose\ntext reads at WCAG AA or better. Custom makes a whole theme from one hue and a\nvividness (OKLCH, so every hue is as readable as every other), remembered on the device\n(\"nova-look-custom\"). The pickers in the Panels window and Portal's and Index's Options\nshow every theme as an orb in rainbow order, then Custom with its two sliders; choosing\none, or moving a slider, recolours Nova Agent and every open panel straight away (look.js\nover storage events). Cosmic stays the default and looks the same; every old theme, id\nand the \"Each panel's own\" choice still work, and Portal's own theme can be any of them.\nOne button system (web/shared/butto"},{"hash":"50d482d","date":"2026-10-11T00:37:15+01:00","subject":"Campaigns: the preview frame loads Nova Bot's preview page (its own rules let the email's styles show online)","body":""},{"hash":"2f3b01e","date":"2026-10-11T00:32:37+01:00","subject":"Quest 3 (Nova Agent): email campaigns with an admin's approval, on Resend","body":"- Agent: suggest_campaign (saves nothing), create_campaign_draft, edit_campaign_draft,\n  campaign_results (opened/clicked as percentages in plain words), list_campaigns, all on\n  /nova-agent/campaigns* with AGENT_NOVA_KEY. No send, schedule, approve or test tool.\n- Agent's campaign card: subject, audience and count, send time, a short preview; Approve\n  (pressed twice, checks nothing changed) / Edit / Reject on the person's own Portal sign-in,\n  Open in Portal on the studio computer.\n- Portal → Campaigns (Studio, badge = waiting): sandboxed preview, Approve / Edit / Reject /\n  Send me a test for admins, scheduled and sent with stats, Write one, the fan sign-up link\n  with Copy and opted-in counts."},{"hash":"b1f2881","date":"2026-10-11T00:20:06+01:00","subject":"Quest 2 (Nova Agent): client list in Portal, Agent's client tools, bookings from Acuity's calendar feed","body":"- ACUITY_SOURCE=feed: studio_bookings and the Quests busy-time cache read\n  /nova-agent/bookings-feed (no browser, no API tools, no propose_booking_change)\n- Agent: client_find, client_history, clients_owing, clients_not_booked_since (read-only)\n- Portal → Clients: search, filters, client page, edit form (money in pounds), marketing\n  consent switch with source and date, consent history; admins: Sync now and Import CSV"},{"hash":"92cf04a","date":"2026-10-10T23:53:48+01:00","subject":"Approvals: a refused approve, edit or reject keeps its reason on the card","body":""},{"hash":"ad246c7","date":"2026-10-10T23:46:26+01:00","subject":"Quest 1 (Nova Agent): Acuity API tools, booking proposals for approval, bookings as busy time, music time","body":"- ACUITY_SOURCE=api|browser (default api). With api, Agent reads bookings, free times,\n  blocked times, session types and clients through Nova Bot's /nova-agent/acuity/* routes\n  (src/acuity-api.ts) and can only PROPOSE booking changes (propose_booking_change,\n  booking_actions). No tool or export can approve. check_acuity_login only in browser mode.\n- Bookings (not cancelled) and Acuity blocked times are cached in data/bookings.json (no\n  client details), refreshed every 10 minutes and when /nova-agent/next says bookingsChanged\n  is newer than bookingsSeen; then Quests re-plan. Acuity unreachable: last copy kept, trace says so.\n- Music time: rhythm.music { days, start, minutes } (off by default), planned up to 21 days,\n  moved to the nearest free stretch that day on a clash, busy for quests, \"music-\" note cards\n  in Calendar, one calm notice when a booking moves today's or tomorrow's. A"},{"hash":"41e9e80","date":"2026-10-10T22:20:56+01:00","subject":"Portal: WhatsApp on a computer opens straight in WhatsApp Web (one tab), or the WhatsApp app if picked","body":"No more WhatsApp's 'continue to chat' page in between: web.whatsapp.com/send in the same\ntab each time. 'Use the WhatsApp app instead' (remembered on that computer) opens\nwhatsapp://send. Phones still open the WhatsApp app."},{"hash":"21aa776","date":"2026-10-10T19:18:04+01:00","subject":"Portal: WhatsApp, Call and Text on enquiries that work on phone and computer; How it works on You","body":"WhatsApp and Text join Reply and Note in the reply box: they open WhatsApp (app or\nWhatsApp Web) or Messages ready to send, then ask Did it send? and add it to the\nconversation. Call asks how it went. On a computer Call and Text show the number and\nmessage to use on your phone, with Copy buttons. You page: what Nova runs on, with a\ntest email button."},{"hash":"387275f","date":"2026-10-10T16:57:24+01:00","subject":"Enquiries: conversation and replies in Portal; Agent drafts replies for approval","body":"- Portal: open an enquiry to see the conversation, Send a reply or add a note, status\n  chips (sending / sent / failed + Retry), Agent's drafts with Edit, Approve & send and\n  Discard, Call / Text links, consent line and a Don't contact toggle. Checks every 5 s\n  while open; only changed messages are redrawn\n- Agent: enquiry_list, enquiry_read, enquiry_draft_reply (no send tool); the draft's card\n  under the reply has Approve & send (the person's Portal sign-in) and Open in Portal\n- Portal times shown in UK time"},{"hash":"af9fc5a","date":"2026-10-10T16:39:04+01:00","subject":"Portal: each quest card wears its mode's colour (card, edge, glow, title; no motion)","body":""},{"hash":"e739aff","date":"2026-10-10T16:37:30+01:00","subject":"Portal: Booking tools (the bookings month: week at a glance and free slots) one tap away","body":"In the Studio group of the side menu and More, under Calendar, with a small hint; and a link\nunder Today's Studio tiles. It opens /portal/?view=calendar; Calendar still opens the\nCalendar panel. No new animations."},{"hash":"39d9494","date":"2026-10-10T16:28:10+01:00","subject":"Portal: a tapped tab doesn't stay lit on a touch screen (hover only with a real pointer)","body":""},{"hash":"f8426d6","date":"2026-10-10T16:22:55+01:00","subject":"Portal: calm and in groups (no flicker on refresh; Today, Studio, Plans, You, Admin)","body":"Calm:\n- A refresh (the 15 s Quests poll, coming back to the app, a new alert, Today) only\n  changes what changed: cards are matched by id and kept when their data is the same,\n  so nothing blinks, open cards stay open, and scroll and focus stay put\n- Entrance animations play once, when you go to a view (a soft fade); never on a refresh.\n  The staggered card rise, quest shine/sweep/breathe, tag shimmer, risk pulse, mission\n  star spin and progress-ring refill no longer replay or run forever\n- Titles no longer shimmer; the planet changes with a soft fade (no flash, rings or\n  shooting star); forms warm their edge instead of shaking\n- No frosted-glass blur on the header, menu, sheets or chat box (no repaint while scrolling)\n- The calendar draws only what changed (no pop on the picked day, no blink while the\n  bookings load); the \"Checking with Acuity\" panel is filled straight away once know"},{"hash":"9d47515","date":"2026-10-10T16:08:03+01:00","subject":"Portal Admin: a Test booking chip (opens Nova Bot's /admin/test-booking)","body":""},{"hash":"7b816a8","date":"2026-10-10T15:52:31+01:00","subject":"Quests: pick which phones get the reminders; the whole quest wears its mode colour in Notes; Portal shows every quest; full note titles","body":"- A quest can pick its phones (📱 on the front page and in Notes; Agent can too); its pings\n  carry them, and Nova Bot sends them there (or to the studio owner's phones)\n- Notes: a quest's heading and everything under it are tinted in its mode's colour (drawn\n  live, never saved); the side panel's quest cards glow in it too\n- Portal gets every quest (open first, up to 400), shows quests not planned yet under Today,\n  and groups All quests by mode\n- Notes: Your Notes shows each note's whole title (long ones wrap)"},{"hash":"a4976f2","date":"2026-10-10T15:43:29+01:00","subject":"Quests in Notes, tied to Nova Quests; seven modes with colours that follow the theme","body":"- Notes: any heading with QUEST in it (TASK still counts) is a quest: + New quest, change its mode,\n  hand it to Agent, take it off Quests (the text stays). Each one is made in Nova Quests the moment\n  it appears, and kept in step: the heading is its title, the mode goes both ways\n- Nova Quests: every quest has a mode (Waiting, Soon, Working On It, Nearly Finished, Taking longer\n  than expected, Questions, Done), where it's from and what it's tied to; modes set the status\n  they mean (and Done / Start set the mode); Agent can set it; Portal's taps can too\n- Front page and Portal: a coloured mode chip on each quest, tap to change\n- /shared/quest-modes.css|js: the one set of mode colours (tinted toward the theme) and menu"},{"hash":"1f7ea3b","date":"2026-10-10T15:13:08+01:00","subject":"Portal first, Agent second; no 'Chat' left; Agent in Portal's side menu (the same conversation)","body":"- Taskbar and launcher: Portal, Agent, Calendar, Notes, Index\n- Notes' task button says Agent; Portal's website chats are Conversations\n- Portal's side menu (and More on phones) has Agent: inside Nova Agent the panel steps\n  aside for the one Agent conversation (NovaAgent.agent()); on its own it opens /agent/"},{"hash":"7fe9a43","date":"2026-10-10T15:09:12+01:00","subject":"Reminders pick their phones, edits can't be lost, file cards always give a way to the file; emails and passwords from Portal","body":"- Calendar: 'Send to' under Remind me (the owner's phones, or the phones picked)\n- Calendar: a repeating event asks 'Change which?' with the editor still open (Cancel\n  keeps the edit); changing only reminders saves to every time without asking\n- Calendar: each change says which version it was made to, so a device with a slow\n  clock still saves\n- Agent: a file card that can't be drawn becomes a download link (or 'Open your files')\n- Portal: change your email (staff confirm with their password); admins fix anyone's\n  email and set a new password on that person's page"},{"hash":"77924bf","date":"2026-10-10T14:34:17+01:00","subject":"The apps update themselves: they check the live version when opened or brought back, and refresh","body":"Also: the App button's Remove steps on a computer use chrome://apps (the way that always works)."},{"hash":"001fe93","date":"2026-10-10T14:19:00+01:00","subject":"An App button everywhere: install or remove Nova Agent and Portal, with help for this exact device","body":"Install: one tap on Android and computers when the browser offers it; Safari's steps on iPhone and\niPad. Remove: wipes the app from the device (notifications, sign-in, saved data, offline files),\nthen the step that deletes its icon. Help reads the device, OS version and browser and fixes the\nusual in-between problems. In Nova Agent's and the Portal app's top bars, Portal's sign-in\nscreen, the phone's gear menu and the Panels window."},{"hash":"8ddb603","date":"2026-10-10T14:00:01+01:00","subject":"Portal as its own phone app: install link, stays Portal from its home-screen icon, notifications open it","body":"/portal/?app=1 shows Portal on its own (to add to the home screen as Portal, with its icon);\nopened from that icon Portal stays itself, even on reload. In a normal browser tab Portal still\nopens inside Nova Agent. The notification helper opens Portal on phones that have the Portal app\n(each app marks itself on the phone), on the notification's tab."},{"hash":"7099c0b","date":"2026-10-10T13:27:59+01:00","subject":"Portal everywhere: no more Portal (names, code, phone app, Manual)","body":"The staff app is Portal in every word: notifications, the voice command, the old phone app's\nname and icon (installed from /app/), code names (portalsync, window.PortalApp), comments, docs\nand the Manual (old commit notes are told with the new name). Settings saved under the old names\n(theme, options, music, alerts seen, hands-free) carry over once, so nothing resets."},{"hash":"5de742c","date":"2026-10-09T21:42:53+01:00","subject":"Nova Agent: \"Chat\" is now \"Agent\" everywhere you see it","body":"The section title, the panels bar, the phone menu, the status line, the hints, the\ninstall description, Portal's and Calendar's mentions and the manual. Nova Bot's website\nchats (Portal's Chats tab, Index's customer facts) keep their name. Code names stay."},{"hash":"263cf4f","date":"2026-10-09T02:31:27+01:00","subject":"Cosmic icons, one theme for everything, planet colours, smart top bar, status line","body":"Icons: a cosmic set, each with its own colour (mixed with the theme), sky and shape; Talk to\nNova Agent, Quests and Missions have their own. look.js: one theme for every panel (or each its\nown), and colour everything from your planet. Typing hides the panels bar. The top bar: Auto,\nAlways shown or Always hidden. The status line under the bar: Panels button (the top one is\ngone), version and build, what changed lately for the part of the bar you point at, on and off\ntimes, recent activity and a 12-hour clock. Lossless audio's sounds come along."},{"hash":"c228593","date":"2026-10-09T01:24:38+01:00","subject":"Calmer, lusher sounds, and quiet extras with their own switch","body":"Every sound is quieter with a warm top end and more space. New, barely-there extras:\nscrolling, typing, sliders, dragging (Calendar's note cards: pick up, each step, put down)\nand hovering, each kept to its own pace. Their own switch in Portal's Options and the\nphone's gear; only heard while sound effects are on."},{"hash":"48b4b4c","date":"2026-10-09T00:58:39+01:00","subject":"Lush Novacane sounds, and quiet ambient music across all of Nova Agent","body":"Sound effects: glass bells, warm under-tones and breaths of air, in the music's key, with\nstereo, reverb and echo; a hello chime when sounds are switched on. Every old sound kept.\nAmbient music moves to shared/ and becomes one player for the whole app (header switch,\nphone gear → Music, Portal's button), remembered on the device, with a soft electric-piano\nphrase now and then."},{"hash":"a70307d","date":"2026-10-08T17:44:17+01:00","subject":"Admin lives in Portal: no Admin button in Nova Agent","body":"Portal gets an Admin section for admins (Studio pages, Crew, Google, Links),\nshown inside Portal. Nova Agent's bar and launcher lose Admin and All links;\ninviting from the crew page is hidden."},{"hash":"3fbe6c1","date":"2026-10-08T15:30:34+01:00","subject":"Portal on phones: a Today screen, five tabs, full-screen inside Nova Agent, lighter","body":"- Inside Nova Agent on a phone, an open panel gets the whole screen (Nova\n  Agent's header, the panels strip and the floating Manual step aside; the\n  slim bar keeps ← Nova Agent, and the panel's name switches panels), with\n  room for the notch and the home bar.\n- Portal opens on Today: new enquiries, today's chats and bookings, alerts\n  and quests at a glance (each tile opens its section), then the newest\n  enquiries.\n- Phones: five tabs (Today, Enquiries, Chats, Calendar, More); Quests,\n  Alerts, NovaBot and You are under More with their counts. Enquiries fold\n  to one line until tapped; compact alerts and chats; small headings on one\n  line; a smaller planet on You; inputs at 16px (no zoom on typing).\n- Lighter: no frosted glass or moving titles on phones; the ambient music\n  engine loads after the first screen; the Manual (and its 287 KB of\n  content) loads only outside frames, and p"},{"hash":"02e1211","date":"2026-10-08T13:48:41+01:00","subject":"Portal: any password length","body":""},{"hash":"5eb1b0b","date":"2026-10-08T13:43:54+01:00","subject":"Portal: change your password on the You page","body":"Admins choose a new one without the old one; everyone else confirms their\ncurrent password. Other sign-ins end; this one carries on."},{"hash":"ed420d6","date":"2026-10-08T13:33:52+01:00","subject":"Portal is the one sign-in","body":"Signed out, the planet opens Portal's sign-in (in Nova Agent's viewer): no\nsign-in form of its own, and no Sign in with Google anywhere. Google is a\nconnection, not a way in: Portal's You page shows it (connected as whom), with\nSet up / Connect Google for admins (Admin → Google). Notes asks\n/auth/google-status for the studio's Google key."},{"hash":"4fabb4b","date":"2026-10-08T13:26:32+01:00","subject":"Sign in with Google, on the planet and in Portal; Notes uses the studio's Google","body":"- The planet's sign-in card and Portal's sign-in card get a Sign in with\n  Google button once an admin has set Google up (Admin → Google). Google's\n  page opens in a small window (full screen in the installed phone app) and\n  every panel follows when it's done.\n- On the studio PC, Nova Agent starts it (/auth/google): it makes up a\n  verifier, Nova Bot sends back a one-time code to /auth/google/done, and\n  Nova Agent swaps the two for its own sign-in (src/signin.ts).\n- Notes' Save to Google Docs uses the studio's Google key, with nothing to\n  set up; without it, a button opens Admin → Google."},{"hash":"f796db5","date":"2026-10-08T11:47:15+01:00","subject":"Nova Agent lives at /agent/, on the PC and online","body":"/ goes on to /agent/, and /agent/<panel> opens Nova Agent with that panel.\nPanels opened on their own, notifications and the app's shortcuts open\n/agent/?open=<panel>. The installed app starts at /agent/."},{"hash":"00484d5","date":"2026-10-08T11:38:21+01:00","subject":"Nova Agent is the one app: panels open only inside it","body":"- A panel opened on its own (/portal/, /calendar/, /notes/, /app/memory/,\n  /observatory/, /lossless/, /visualizer, /admin...) opens Nova Agent with\n  that panel instead: /?open=<its address>, keeping its query and #hash.\n  The server tells by Sec-Fetch-Dest; inside.js (and Calendar's embed.js)\n  catch browsers that don't say.\n- Nova Agent reads ?open= and opens the panel; a tapped notification opens\n  its panel too (nova-open from the service worker).\n- No more \"Inside / Window\" switch or open-in-a-window button. Visualizer\n  and Admin are panels; Admin is passed on to Nova Bot with this computer's\n  sign-in (Portal first when signed out).\n- One installable app: /sw.js handles phone notifications for the whole\n  app (Portal subscribes through it, keeping an old /app/ or /portal/\n  address if the phone has one, so nothing arrives twice); the old service\n  workers open taps in Nova Agent."},{"hash":"37073d2","date":"2026-10-08T02:15:25+01:00","subject":"One Portal: one staff app at /portal/","body":"Portal is gone as a separate panel. Portal is the one staff app: one header,\none tab bar with Portal's work tabs (Enquiries, Chats, Calendar, Quests,\nAlerts, NovaBot) plus You (your planet and profile; admins reach the crew\nand the admin pages from there). Portal's sign-in, setup and invite cards\nreplace Portal's old sign-in screen.\n- web/portal's scripts and styles move into web/portal (app.js, app.css,\n  ambient.js, options.js, suite.js). portal.js runs the page (who's signed\n  in, the address, the You tab) and starts the work tabs (window.NovaHub);\n  the tabs hand sign-outs back (window.PortalPage). Tabs follow the\n  address: /portal/?view=enquiries|chats|calendar|quests|alerts|bot|me|crew,\n  #nova opens Alerts, no ?view opens the starting tab from Options (which\n  can now be You). Tells the badge when sign-in changes (NovaPortal.changed).\n- portal.css is scoped to Portal's own parts (.pv) with p"},{"hash":"326ecf9","date":"2026-10-08T01:33:59+01:00","subject":"Portal and Index: Portal is the one sign-in","body":"The shared-password box is gone from Portal's and Index's sign-in screens:\nsigned out, there's one button, to Portal, which brings you back to\n/app/ or /app/memory/ (not the old /studio/ and /index/). The guides\nand the Manual say the same."},{"hash":"100fb09","date":"2026-10-08T00:43:48+01:00","subject":"Plain names: everything is Nova Agent, and its panels are Portal, Portal, Calendar…","body":"Undoes the made-up names. \"Studio\" is Portal again and \"Crew\" is Portal again\n(only where the earlier rename had changed them; real uses of the words are\nkept). Every panel and feature drops \"Nova\": Portal, Portal, Calendar, Notes,\nIndex, Observatory, Missions, Quests and the Manual. \"Nova\" stays for Nova\nAgent itself, Nova Bot and Nova Club.\nThe original addresses are back: Portal at /app/, Portal at /portal/ and\nIndex at /app/memory/ (the panels live in web/portal, web/portal, web/index).\nNova Agent's own icons move to /agent/ to make room. /studio/, /crew/ and\n/index/ redirect, for anything that picked them up yesterday."},{"hash":"fef653e","date":"2026-10-07T23:27:20+01:00","subject":"Panels laid out: Studio (was Portal), Crew (was Nova Portal), Index…","body":"- web/studio: Portal's staff app, now Nova Agent's Studio panel\n- web/crew: Nova Portal's app (sign-in, me, crew, invites), now the Crew\n  panel, with the planet avatar generator beside it\n- web/index, web/calendar, web/notes, web/observatory: the panels\n- Each app's README and pictures move to docs/apps/<panel>\n- The manual and badge scripts move to scripts/, and the Observatory's\n  scanning tools to scripts/observatory (npm run observatory:scan,\n  :capture, :build), writing into web/observatory as before\n- Calendar's and Notes' own deploy configs (their separate workers.dev\n  sites) are dropped: they're panels now\nPaths inside the panels are fixed up next."},{"hash":"e91ec2e","date":"2026-10-07T23:23:37+01:00","subject":"Nova Agent takes in Nova Portal (with its history), as web/portal","body":"git-subtree-dir: web/portal\ngit-subtree-mainline: 1ec177bf4bee982fb33f49af61d4e5385a21735e\ngit-subtree-split: 7f3bec195c49d98e0f89c3c6412bbb96cf7fd472"},{"hash":"7f3bec1","date":"2026-10-07T16:31:24+01:00","subject":"The Nova Manual: refreshed with today's changes","body":""},{"hash":"0a62fd3","date":"2026-10-07T16:30:26+01:00","subject":"The Nova Manual: every Nova app's guide, build, history and what's new","body":"<nova-manual> sits beside the Portal badge on every Nova app (or floats\nin the corner where there's no top bar yet). It opens a panel for each\napp in the suite: a Guide, How it's built, its History as a timeline,\nand What's new (the last week, and what's being worked on), with search\nacross all of it. ? opens it anywhere; #nova-manual in the address too.\nscripts/build-manual.mjs makes its pages (app/manual-data.js) from every\napp's README and git history, then shares the badge and the manual with\nNova Notes, Calendar and Observatory. Built like the badge: shadow DOM,\na constructed stylesheet and no inline styles, so it works under Nova\nPortal's strict security rules."},{"hash":"fe6dcd0","date":"2026-10-07T02:01:03+01:00","subject":"Nova Agent's badge: Connect as me, and back to automatic","body":""},{"hash":"dc29ca6","date":"2026-10-07T01:50:03+01:00","subject":"The Nova Portal badge for every Nova app, and Connect","body":"- app/badge.js: <nova-portal-badge>, your planet, name and role with a\n  card (planet up close, profile, Nova Index), themed by each app\n- Connect: other suite sites get a read-only token to show the badge"},{"hash":"d1e6ab3","date":"2026-10-07T01:34:16+01:00","subject":"Nova Portal: one sign-in for the Nova suite, and a planet for everyone","body":"- app/: setup, sign in, invites, profiles with an animated planet, the crew,\n  options; one session for Portal, Nova Index and the admin pages\n- planet/: a pure, deterministic, themeable planet generator (gas giants,\n  rocky, ocean, molten and ice worlds, rings, moons, aurora, storms), with\n  the Nova theme in its own file so the studio's lore can replace it"}],"work":[],"workCount":0,"workStat":""}},{"id":"calendar","name":"Calendar","colour":"#F2D9A0","glyph":"◷","where":"A Nova Agent panel","links":[["Open Calendar","https://nova.novacane.co.uk/calendar/"]],"repo":"na","shared":"","tagline":"The studio's calendar under the real sky: note cards, day cards, the moon and special days, Nova Agent's plan and the studio's bookings, in one place.","intro":"<blockquote><strong>A Nova Agent panel.</strong> Its code is in <code>web/calendar/</code> in Nova Agent&#39;s repo, and it opens inside Nova Agent at <code>/agent/calendar</code>.</blockquote>","guide":[{"id":"what-you-can-do-0","title":"What you can do","html":"<ul><li><strong>See it your way:</strong> Month, Week, Day or List. Arrows (or a swipe) move on, <strong>Today</strong> comes back, and tapping the month&#39;s name jumps to any date. A pink line shows the time now.</li><li><strong>Add a note card:</strong> the <strong>+</strong> button, <strong>+ Note card</strong> under the day, a tap on an empty time (Week and Day), or a second click on a day (Month, on a computer). Typing is quickest: <code>Mix review Friday 2pm 1h @Studio A</code> fills everything in.</li><li><strong>Every note card has its own painted picture</strong> (a planet, a galaxy, a comet…): pick the kind or let it surprise you, press <strong>New artwork</strong> for another, and <strong>Save image</strong> to keep it big.</li><li><strong>Change:</strong> tap a note card to edit it. On a computer, drag it to move it and drag its bottom edge to make it longer; on a phone, hold it for a moment, then drag.</li><li><strong>Repeat:</strong> every day, week, month or year, or a custom rule (every 2 weeks on Mon and Wed, until a date or a number of times). Changing or deleting one of them asks: just this one, this and the ones after, or every one.</li><li><strong>Reminders:</strong> at the start, 10 or 30 minutes, an hour or a day before. They arrive on phones as alerts, even with every laptop off.</li><li><strong>Delete</strong> with <strong>Undo</strong> (a few seconds to change your mind), <strong>duplicate</strong>, pick a <strong>colour</strong>, add <strong>where</strong> and <strong>notes</strong>.</li><li><strong>Day cards:</strong> birthdays, release days, studio sessions, holidays and more (<strong>+ Day card</strong>). Each has a kind with its icon, a <strong>title style</strong> (Nebula, Supernova, Orbit, Constellation, Eclipse, Aurora, Celestial), its own <strong>theme</strong> and a painted header (<strong>New artwork</strong> for another). They show as a banner on the day, wear their theme in the month, and can come back every year.</li><li><strong>The real sky:</strong> the moon&#39;s phases (full moons in gold, with their names), and special days (Easter, Bonfire Night, the solstices and equinoxes, meteor-shower peaks…). Tap <strong>Make it a day card</strong> to keep one. The strip above the month shows its day cards, full moon and special days; tap one to go there.</li><li><strong>Backup</strong> (the layers button): <strong>Export</strong> downloads every note card and day card; <strong>Import</strong> brings a backup back in, including one from the old Nova Calendar.</li><li><strong>What to show</strong> (the layers button): note cards, day cards, the moon and special days, Nova Quests (Nova Agent&#39;s plan: read-only here, change them in Nova Quests) and studio bookings (read-only, from the diary).</li><li><strong>Search</strong> every note card and day card by title, place or notes.</li><li><strong>Icons that say what they are:</strong> one modern line set throughout. A note card shows what it&#39;s about (a mic for a recording, a cake for a birthday, a plane for travel…), a studio booking shows a ticked calendar, a quest a target; each day-card kind has its own (a ghost for Halloween, a flame for Bonfire Night, a party popper for New Year, a suitcase for a trip). Point at one for its name.</li></ul>","text":"See it your way: Month, Week, Day or List. Arrows (or a swipe) move on, Today comes back, and tapping the month's name jumps to any date. A pink line shows the time now. Add a note card: the + button, + Note card under the day, a tap on an empty time (Week and Day), or a second click on a day (Month, on a computer). Typing is quickest: Mix review Friday 2pm 1h @Studio A fills everything in. Every note card has its own painted picture (a planet, a galaxy, a comet…): pick the kind or let it surprise you, press New artwork for another, and Save image to keep it big. Change: tap a note card to edit it. On a computer, drag it to move it and drag its bottom edge to make it longer; on a phone, hold it for a moment, then drag. Repeat: every day, week, month or year, or a custom rule (every 2 weeks on Mon and Wed, until a date or a number of times). Changing or deleting one of them asks: just this one, this and the ones after, or every one. Reminders: at the start, 10 or 30 minutes, an hour or a day before. They arrive on phones as alerts, even with every laptop off. Delete with Undo (a few seconds to change your mind), duplicate , pick a colour , add where and notes . Day cards: birthdays, release days, studio sessions, holidays and more ( + Day card ). Each has a kind with its icon, a title style (Nebula, Supernova, Orbit, Constellation, Eclipse, Aurora, Celestial), its own theme and a painted header ( New artwork for another). They show as a banner on the day, wear their theme in the month, and can come back every year. The real sky: the moon's phases (full moons in gold, with their names), and special days (Easter, Bonfire Night, the solstices and equinoxes, meteor-shower peaks…). Tap Make it a day card to keep one. The strip above the month shows its day cards, full moon and special days; tap one to go there. Backup (the layers button): Export downloads every note card and day card; Import brings a backup back in, including one from the old Nova Calendar. What to show (the layers button): note cards, day cards, the moon and special days, Nova Quests (Nova Agent's plan: read-only here, change them in Nova Quests) and studio bookings (read-only, from the diary). Search every note card and day card by title, place or notes. Icons that say what they are: one modern line set throughout. A note card shows what it's about (a mic for a recording, a cake for a birthday, a plane for travel…), a studio booking shows a ticked calendar, a quest a target; each day-card kind has its own (a ghost for Halloween, a flame for Bonfire Night, a party popper for New Year, a suitcase for a trip). Point at one for its name."},{"id":"works-with-nova-agent-1","title":"Works with Nova Agent","html":"<ul><li>Ask Nova Agent (a note card is what Nova Agent calls an event): &quot;Add a mix review Friday at 2 for an hour at Studio A&quot;, &quot;Move it to 4&quot;, &quot;Make the standup repeat every weekday&quot;, &quot;Remind me 10 minutes before&quot;, &quot;Delete it&quot;.</li><li>Nova Agent&#39;s planner keeps Nova Quests out of your note cards (every time a repeating one happens). All-day note cards are markers, like day cards, not busy time.</li></ul>","text":"Ask Nova Agent (a note card is what Nova Agent calls an event): \"Add a mix review Friday at 2 for an hour at Studio A\", \"Move it to 4\", \"Make the standup repeat every weekday\", \"Remind me 10 minutes before\", \"Delete it\". Nova Agent's planner keeps Nova Quests out of your note cards (every time a repeating one happens). All-day note cards are markers, like day cards, not busy time."},{"id":"where-it-s-kept-2","title":"Where it's kept","html":"<p>The calendar lives on Nova Bot (its D1 database, <code>calendar_items</code>), so it&#39;s the same on every phone and computer and keeps working with every laptop off. Each browser keeps a copy so it opens instantly and works offline; changes made offline save when you&#39;re back. The latest change wins; if another device changed something later, Nova Calendar shows that and says so.</p>\n<p>Nova Agent (on the VPS) keeps its own copy (<code>data/calendar.json</code>, read by its chat and planner) in step with Nova Bot every few seconds (<code>src/calendar/cloud.ts</code> ⇄ <code>POST /nova-agent/calendar</code>).</p>\n<p>Anything an earlier version of Nova Calendar saved in a browser is brought in the first time it opens there (once, never twice).</p>","text":"The calendar lives on Nova Bot (its D1 database, calendar_items ), so it's the same on every phone and computer and keeps working with every laptop off. Each browser keeps a copy so it opens instantly and works offline; changes made offline save when you're back. The latest change wins; if another device changed something later, Nova Calendar shows that and says so. Nova Agent (on the VPS) keeps its own copy ( data/calendar.json , read by its chat and planner) in step with Nova Bot every few seconds ( src/calendar/cloud.ts ⇄ POST /nova-agent/calendar ). Anything an earlier version of Nova Calendar saved in a browser is brought in the first time it opens there (once, never twice)."},{"id":"for-developers-3","title":"For developers","html":"<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>File</th><th>What it is</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>web/calendar/js/cal.js</code></td><td>The views, the editor, drag, keys, backups</td></tr><tr><td><code>web/calendar/js/presets.js</code></td><td>Day card kinds, title styles and line icons</td></tr><tr><td><code>web/calendar/js/sky.js</code></td><td>Moon phases, full moon names, seasonal and cosmic days</td></tr><tr><td><code>web/calendar/js/cosmos.js</code></td><td>The painted pictures (loaded when first needed)</td></tr><tr><td><code>web/calendar/js/themes.js</code></td><td>The themes a day card can wear</td></tr><tr><td><code>web/calendar/js/data.js</code></td><td>Saving to Nova Bot, the offline copy and queue, bringing in old data</td></tr><tr><td><code>web/calendar/js/recur.js</code></td><td>Repeat rules (shared with Nova Agent&#39;s planner and Nova Bot&#39;s reminders)</td></tr><tr><td><code>web/calendar/js/quickadd.js</code></td><td>&quot;Mix review Friday 2pm 1h&quot; → a note card</td></tr><tr><td>Nova Bot <code>src/calendar/items.js</code></td><td><code>GET/PUT/DELETE /app/api/calendar/items</code>, Nova Agent&#39;s sync</td></tr><tr><td>Nova Bot <code>src/calendar/reminders.js</code></td><td>Reminders on phones (every minute)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>Keys: ← → move, <strong>T</strong> today, <strong>N</strong> new, <strong>M W D L</strong> views, <strong>Esc</strong> closes.</p>","text":"File What it is web/calendar/js/cal.js The views, the editor, drag, keys, backups web/calendar/js/presets.js Day card kinds, title styles and line icons web/calendar/js/sky.js Moon phases, full moon names, seasonal and cosmic days web/calendar/js/cosmos.js The painted pictures (loaded when first needed) web/calendar/js/themes.js The themes a day card can wear web/calendar/js/data.js Saving to Nova Bot, the offline copy and queue, bringing in old data web/calendar/js/recur.js Repeat rules (shared with Nova Agent's planner and Nova Bot's reminders) web/calendar/js/quickadd.js \"Mix review Friday 2pm 1h\" → a note card Nova Bot src/calendar/items.js GET/PUT/DELETE /app/api/calendar/items , Nova Agent's sync Nova Bot src/calendar/reminders.js Reminders on phones (every minute) Keys: ← → move, T today, N new, M W D L views, Esc closes."}],"built":[],"news":[],"history":{"total":58,"first":"2026-10-06T15:52:52+01:00","commits":[{"hash":"3e5e306","date":"2026-10-14T06:14:02+01:00","subject":"Manual and READMEs: Nova Agent runs on the VPS (day and night, every laptop off), not on the studio PC; Quests' options and the Fixer's wide view described","body":""},{"hash":"0e275ec","date":"2026-10-14T05:47:48+01:00","subject":"One screen everywhere: inside Nova Agent no panel's page (or its <main>) scrolls; only a box inside it does. Portal's open section scrolls inside itself under compact lanes, Today side by side (numbers | today's calendar + new enquiries); Quests' groups and days as columns; Lossless's four cards in a row; the Visualizer's columns (two by two or stacked on phones, each scrolling inside); the Fixer's open tab under its numbers and tabs; Index's open view; Observatory's decks; Calendar's week, day and list scroll inside their own box and the month shares the screen with the day's plan on phones and tablets. Panels and Portal's sections show at once (no fade in). check-fit.mjs fails a page or a <main> that scrolls inside Nova Agent","body":""},{"hash":"3a49323","date":"2026-10-14T02:54:08+01:00","subject":"Fit on screen in every panel: /shared/fit.js + fit.css keep menus, pop-ups, tooltips, non-modal dialogs and anything marked data-fit (or handed over with NovaFit.keep) inside the screen — nudged back in just far enough, capped and scrolling inside only when bigger than the screen, checked again on resize, turning round, a phone's keyboard and growing content; Agent's activity list and the planet card hooked in. scripts/check-fit-all.sh runs the whole fit check (throwaway server, 360×640, 768×1024, 1440×900, the Manual) and check-fit.mjs now also proves the fit layer is on every page and works after the window shrinks","body":""},{"hash":"a96223c","date":"2026-10-14T02:52:57+01:00","subject":"Calendar: one modern line-icon set (2px, round), icons that say what they are (booking = ticked calendar, quest = target, note card, ghost/flame/party/suitcase/flower for day kinds), birthdays and anniversaries win over food, tooltips and names on every icon button. Observatory: everything at once on computers and standing tablets (decks left on their side, star map right, filling the window; the map closes in on the stars and keeps names readable), phones one row shorter","body":""},{"hash":"321c19c","date":"2026-10-12T21:33:21+01:00","subject":"Google round two on the PC and in the panels: Tasks sync, Files in Drive, Agent's Drive/Docs/Tasks/YouTube tools, YouTube in Social, Meet in Calendar, today's calendar in Portal and what_now, Keep in Google Docs and Open a Google Doc in Notes, Google Contacts search in one-to-one emails","body":""},{"hash":"1f748b5","date":"2026-10-11T12:11:55+01:00","subject":"Everything fits: nothing hangs off the screen in any panel; what doesn't fit scrolls inside its own box","body":"scripts/check-fit.mjs opens Nova Agent's home and every panel (on its own and inside Nova Agent) at\n7 sizes (incl. a phone with its keyboard up) with long sample content, opens every sheet, dialog and\npop-up, and reports anything past the screen or its clipping box. Fixes what it found:\n- Portal: the side-menu tab row started off its left edge (tabs unreachable); Booking tools' picked\n  day was wider than the screen; a chat's Enquiry pill was clamped away; Options buttons squashed\n  their icon; a busy day's dots spilled out; long words wrap in views\n- Calendar: long words break inside cards; day cards no longer squashed; narrow short events clamp\n  their title to their height; What to show scrolls inside on short screens\n- Notes: menus and pop-ups scroll inside (and stay on screen) on short screens; snippets wrap\n- Nova Agent: chat action chips, mission summaries and file titles wrap; Ho"},{"hash":"6bb3462","date":"2026-10-11T04:28:58+01:00","subject":"Centred text reaches the last left-aligned corners","body":"The Manual (apps down the side, On this page, search, cards, results, next/previous), the Portal\nbadge's name and role, the Panels window's group headings (a line either side), Calendar's chosen\nday, Notes' menu bar and status bar, and Visualizer's header, buttons and part names. All follow\nCentre all text, so Left still works. Also: Visualizer is just \"Visualizer\" (not \"Nova\nVisualizer\"), Nova Bot spelt the usual way, and the Manual and badge say \"Nova Agent\" and\n\"panel\" rather than \"Nova app\"."},{"hash":"ce1ff1c","date":"2026-10-11T04:25:36+01:00","subject":"Dates and times written the British way, in London time, whatever the browser's language","body":"Calendar's mid-size day labels read \"19 Oct\" and \"19/10\" (not \"10month 19day\" and \"10 19\");\nthe status line's clock no longer follows the browser's language (\"So 5:04 am\"); Visualizer's\nstep times and every other date label say en-GB, Europe/London."},{"hash":"91d1fad","date":"2026-10-11T03:25:54+01:00","subject":"Plain app names again (only Nova Agent and Nova Bot keep Nova); titles on one surface; Portal's tabs wrap on tablets too","body":"Undoes the 'Nova <App>' renaming line by line (the ✦ marks, the tab bar and the scrollbars\nstay). Inside Nova Agent a shared rule kept Portal's tabs on one sliding row under 981px:\nfrom 761px they now wrap too, so every tab is on screen."},{"hash":"31b1842","date":"2026-10-11T02:58:26+01:00","subject":"Merge branch 'calendar-visuals'","body":""},{"hash":"d6d2213","date":"2026-10-11T02:57:49+01:00","subject":"Nova first in every app name (the bottom bars keep their short labels)","body":"Nova Portal, Nova Agent, Nova Calendar, Nova Notes, Nova Index, Nova Quests, Nova Missions,\nNova Lossless, Nova Visualizer, Nova Observatory, Nova Manual: titles, headers, the Panels\nwindow, the status line, the Manual, manifests, messages and alerts. Also: the Nova mark's CSS on\nthe panel icons (chat.html), Portal's tab labels and tabbar.js, and the scrollbars link in each page."},{"hash":"e2b63d9","date":"2026-10-11T02:57:49+01:00","subject":"Icons: the same small Nova sparkle in the corner of every app's icon","body":""},{"hash":"0b19f1d","date":"2026-10-11T02:57:47+01:00","subject":"Calendar: a calm visual look-over (fits, alignment, theme colours)","body":"- Day cards on \"App theme\" follow every Nova Agent theme (spectrum and Custom), not always Novacane\n- Day card words use the theme's button text colour, readable on light themes\n- Month: day cards no longer spill out of both sides; today keeps its glow on a weekend;\n  phones show a small day's symbols two to a row, so the month fits the screen\n- Phones: the chosen day's buttons sit under its name, clear of the round +\n- Week and day: one-line all-day cards; today's number is the month's glowing disc; narrow\n  overlapping cards show just their wrapped title; the moon never covers a weekday name;\n  the resize bar shows on hover with a mouse; no sideways scroll\n- List: one centred column on wide screens, frosted date headings, quests and bookings show\n  their symbol so every row's times line up, two-line titles, no repeated \"Studio Session\"\n- Bar: \"Note card\" stays on one line and nothing o"},{"hash":"95b9569","date":"2026-10-11T02:21:20+01:00","subject":"Themes: a colour spectrum with a Custom colour; one button look for every panel","body":"A spectrum of themes for all of Nova Agent (web/shared/spectrum.js): Crimson, Rose,\nCoral, Amber, Lime, Jade, Teal, Glacier, Indigo, Violet and Orchid join the old ones,\neach a hand-tuned set (deep sky, luminous accent, matching gradients and glows) whose\ntext reads at WCAG AA or better. Custom makes a whole theme from one hue and a\nvividness (OKLCH, so every hue is as readable as every other), remembered on the device\n(\"nova-look-custom\"). The pickers in the Panels window and Portal's and Index's Options\nshow every theme as an orb in rainbow order, then Custom with its two sliders; choosing\none, or moving a slider, recolours Nova Agent and every open panel straight away (look.js\nover storage events). Cosmic stays the default and looks the same; every old theme, id\nand the \"Each panel's own\" choice still work, and Portal's own theme can be any of them.\nOne button system (web/shared/butto"},{"hash":"483e1ac","date":"2026-10-11T01:42:17+01:00","subject":"Plans: one Quests view with Calendar's reminders, a shorter phone bar, saved tests for two fixes","body":"- The bar's \"Tasks\" group is now \"Plans\" (same Quests and Missions; the Panels window and the\n  status line's area name too)\n- Quests: every quest says where it came from (its mission, \"Notes · <note>\", or Agent; blocked\n  time says Agent), in the timeline, the up-next card and the Coming up, Pulses and Needs a slot\n  lists\n- Quests: a quiet \"Also coming up\" list of Calendar's note cards with reminders in the next 7\n  days (UK time, repeating ones each time); tapping one opens Calendar on that day\n  (/calendar/?day=YYYY-MM-DD, new and additive in cal.js)\n- Phones held upright (600px and under): Portal, Agent, Calendar, Notes and Quests on the bar\n  plus More, a sheet with Missions, Index, Lossless, Visualizer, Observatory and Manual (same\n  icons, same opening; More lights up when one of them is open; Escape or Close puts it away).\n  Wider screens keep the whole bar\n- Tests: Calendar's k"},{"hash":"ad246c7","date":"2026-10-10T23:46:26+01:00","subject":"Quest 1 (Nova Agent): Acuity API tools, booking proposals for approval, bookings as busy time, music time","body":"- ACUITY_SOURCE=api|browser (default api). With api, Agent reads bookings, free times,\n  blocked times, session types and clients through Nova Bot's /nova-agent/acuity/* routes\n  (src/acuity-api.ts) and can only PROPOSE booking changes (propose_booking_change,\n  booking_actions). No tool or export can approve. check_acuity_login only in browser mode.\n- Bookings (not cancelled) and Acuity blocked times are cached in data/bookings.json (no\n  client details), refreshed every 10 minutes and when /nova-agent/next says bookingsChanged\n  is newer than bookingsSeen; then Quests re-plan. Acuity unreachable: last copy kept, trace says so.\n- Music time: rhythm.music { days, start, minutes } (off by default), planned up to 21 days,\n  moved to the nearest free stretch that day on a clash, busy for quests, \"music-\" note cards\n  in Calendar, one calm notice when a booking moves today's or tomorrow's. A"},{"hash":"7fe9a43","date":"2026-10-10T15:09:12+01:00","subject":"Reminders pick their phones, edits can't be lost, file cards always give a way to the file; emails and passwords from Portal","body":"- Calendar: 'Send to' under Remind me (the owner's phones, or the phones picked)\n- Calendar: a repeating event asks 'Change which?' with the editor still open (Cancel\n  keeps the edit); changing only reminders saves to every time without asking\n- Calendar: each change says which version it was made to, so a device with a slow\n  clock still saves\n- Agent: a file card that can't be drawn becomes a download link (or 'Open your files')\n- Portal: change your email (staff confirm with their password); admins fix anyone's\n  email and set a new password on that person's page"},{"hash":"5de742c","date":"2026-10-09T21:42:53+01:00","subject":"Nova Agent: \"Chat\" is now \"Agent\" everywhere you see it","body":"The section title, the panels bar, the phone menu, the status line, the hints, the\ninstall description, Portal's and Calendar's mentions and the manual. Nova Bot's website\nchats (Portal's Chats tab, Index's customer facts) keep their name. Code names stay."},{"hash":"d9eab3f","date":"2026-10-09T18:04:10+01:00","subject":"Calendar: every day measured so nothing is cut off; cards wear the current theme; no \"of\" in day names","body":"Each day steps down only as far as it needs (small line, one-line titles, symbol and title,\nsymbols), then short day numbers, then \"+N\". Special days and the moon become symbols on\nsmall days. The month keeps the screen's height when the chosen day sits below it."},{"hash":"b8f1ce2","date":"2026-10-09T17:35:49+01:00","subject":"Calendar: symbols on phones too","body":""},{"hash":"98b3fab","date":"2026-10-09T17:35:03+01:00","subject":"Calendar: day words and symbols switch at sensible sizes; clear of the moon","body":""},{"hash":"ab63b94","date":"2026-10-09T17:34:13+01:00","subject":"Calendar: size checks read the month's grid (all days alike)","body":""},{"hash":"b12896d","date":"2026-10-09T17:32:46+01:00","subject":"Calendar: small days show cards as symbols, note cards in Nova Agent's glass and glow, the day written out to fit","body":""},{"hash":"69bb593","date":"2026-10-09T17:15:17+01:00","subject":"Calendar: + more under the card","body":""},{"hash":"9fca33a","date":"2026-10-09T17:15:10+01:00","subject":"Calendar: small days show one card on a line and + more","body":""},{"hash":"4fca5a2","date":"2026-10-09T17:14:35+01:00","subject":"Calendar: each day shows what fits it","body":""},{"hash":"bd2a993","date":"2026-10-09T17:14:00+01:00","subject":"Status line: Auto, Always shown or Always hidden, and each part optional; Calendar: fits, spacing, colour, centring (follows Centre all text)","body":""},{"hash":"011089e","date":"2026-10-09T17:02:30+01:00","subject":"Calendar: the time above the title, titles up to three lines","body":""},{"hash":"e2e99aa","date":"2026-10-09T17:01:37+01:00","subject":"Calendar makeover: a cosmic Novacane sky and glassy month, no stripes on Quests and bookings, note cards with their whole title and what they're for","body":""},{"hash":"154133c","date":"2026-10-09T03:08:06+01:00","subject":"Smaller bar, clearer status line, distinct settings icons, compact Quests, glowing scrollbars with sounds, a shifting cosmic sky, centred titles and chat","body":""},{"hash":"1d9cff9","date":"2026-10-09T02:54:25+01:00","subject":"No glass bubbles, one glow everywhere, bars fit their contents, centred text","body":"The panels bar's tiles sit right on the night sky (a glow behind the one you point at, a line of\nlight under the open one, glowing lines between groups). glow.css: the same edge and nebula light\non the header, columns, panel frame, pop-ups and status line, and the same glow on buttons, tabs\nand boxes, in the panels too. On computers the three bars are as wide as their contents. All text\nis centred (a switch in the Panels window turns it off); Notes documents and code keep their own."},{"hash":"263cf4f","date":"2026-10-09T02:31:27+01:00","subject":"Cosmic icons, one theme for everything, planet colours, smart top bar, status line","body":"Icons: a cosmic set, each with its own colour (mixed with the theme), sky and shape; Talk to\nNova Agent, Quests and Missions have their own. look.js: one theme for every panel (or each its\nown), and colour everything from your planet. Typing hides the panels bar. The top bar: Auto,\nAlways shown or Always hidden. The status line under the bar: Panels button (the top one is\ngone), version and build, what changed lately for the part of the bar you point at, on and off\ntimes, recent activity and a 12-hour clock. Lossless audio's sounds come along."},{"hash":"c228593","date":"2026-10-09T01:24:38+01:00","subject":"Calmer, lusher sounds, and quiet extras with their own switch","body":"Every sound is quieter with a warm top end and more space. New, barely-there extras:\nscrolling, typing, sliders, dragging (Calendar's note cards: pick up, each step, put down)\nand hovering, each kept to its own pace. Their own switch in Portal's Options and the\nphone's gear; only heard while sound effects are on."},{"hash":"8ff866a","date":"2026-10-09T01:18:58+01:00","subject":"One panels bar everywhere (no Panels box), softer ambient sounds, light motion","body":"The panels strip loses its Panels box and keeps the same groups and tiles whatever is open;\nwith a panel open it only gets smaller. Sounds swell in and chords bloom together instead of\nrunning up; taps are a low felt touch. Buttons and tiles press in softly, the open panel's\ntile breathes, panels fade in (scale and opacity only; off for reduced motion or calm)."},{"hash":"f276c87","date":"2026-10-08T22:56:34+01:00","subject":"Calendar: note cards again, under the real sky","body":"Every feature the new Calendar had stays; what the old one had comes back.\n- Note cards (stored as kind \"event\"): called note cards everywhere, shown as\n  little tinted cards with their titles in the month (not bars), as cards in\n  week and day, and as rows with their own painted picture. The sheet paints\n  the picture (cosmos.js, back, loaded when first needed): pick its kind,\n  New artwork, Save image (1920×1080).\n- Day cards: their kind and icon, title styles (Nebula … Celestial), their\n  own theme and a painted header (New artwork) are back; a banner on the day,\n  themed in the month. + Day card beside + Note card.\n- The real sky (sky.js, back): moon phases (full moons in gold, with names),\n  the day's moon, seasonal and cosmic days with \"Make it a day card\", and a\n  strip of the month's day cards, full moon and special days. A layer.\n- Backup (in the layers menu): Export, and Import"},{"hash":"3773415","date":"2026-10-08T18:14:42+01:00","subject":"Calendar: a full calendar that works from anywhere","body":"Month, week, day and list views; add (or type it: \"Mix review Friday 2pm 1h\"),\nchange, drag to move and resize, duplicate, delete with Undo; repeats with\n\"just this one / this and following / all\"; reminders on phones; colours,\nplaces, notes; day cards kept; Quests and studio bookings alongside\n(read-only); search. Saved on Nova Bot (works with the PC off), with an\noffline copy and queue in each browser; old browser data brought in once.\nNova Agent keeps data/calendar.json in step with Nova Bot\n(src/calendar/cloud.ts); its planner counts every repeat as busy time and its\nchat can set places, all-day, colours, repeats and reminders."},{"hash":"27a756e","date":"2026-10-08T17:45:50+01:00","subject":"WIP calendar-pro","body":""},{"hash":"932c20c","date":"2026-10-08T16:59:59+01:00","subject":"Panels on phones: fit, lighter, less scrolling","body":"- Notes: one top bar (notes list, the note's name, Google Docs) and the menus;\n  the toolbar is one row you swipe, with the everyday tools (the rest stay in\n  the menus); 16px fields; no glass blur, grain or drifting background.\n- Observatory: a slim title, the numbers as a compact strip, each project as\n  one short row with a small drawn cover (no full-size screenshots on phones);\n  category chips in one row; no star map, no moving sky, no blur.\n- Calendar and Index: no glass blur or endless decorative motion on phones.\n- Lossless audio: snug margins, big buttons, 16px fields.\n- Visualizer: no error when the studio PC is off; fits a phone."},{"hash":"f796db5","date":"2026-10-08T11:47:15+01:00","subject":"Nova Agent lives at /agent/, on the PC and online","body":"/ goes on to /agent/, and /agent/<panel> opens Nova Agent with that panel.\nPanels opened on their own, notifications and the app's shortcuts open\n/agent/?open=<panel>. The installed app starts at /agent/."},{"hash":"00484d5","date":"2026-10-08T11:38:21+01:00","subject":"Nova Agent is the one app: panels open only inside it","body":"- A panel opened on its own (/portal/, /calendar/, /notes/, /app/memory/,\n  /observatory/, /lossless/, /visualizer, /admin...) opens Nova Agent with\n  that panel instead: /?open=<its address>, keeping its query and #hash.\n  The server tells by Sec-Fetch-Dest; inside.js (and Calendar's embed.js)\n  catch browsers that don't say.\n- Nova Agent reads ?open= and opens the panel; a tapped notification opens\n  its panel too (nova-open from the service worker).\n- No more \"Inside / Window\" switch or open-in-a-window button. Visualizer\n  and Admin are panels; Admin is passed on to Nova Bot with this computer's\n  sign-in (Portal first when signed out).\n- One installable app: /sw.js handles phone notifications for the whole\n  app (Portal subscribes through it, keeping an old /app/ or /portal/\n  address if the phone has one, so nothing arrives twice); the old service\n  workers open taps in Nova Agent."},{"hash":"8ac9531","date":"2026-10-08T02:04:26+01:00","subject":"Lossless audio and Observatory as panels everywhere; docs at the real addresses","body":"- Lossless audio is served by Nova Agent at /lossless/ and opens inside it like\n  the other panels. Signalling and the relay setup come from Nova Bot (which now\n  serves it online too), so the other device can be anywhere; invite links point\n  at the online address. /lossless/ice lets Nova Agent's own page ask.\n- Observatory online asks for a Portal sign-in before showing the projects\n  (Nova Bot keeps them for signed-in staff).\n- Calendar's and Notes' guides link to their addresses on Nova Bot, not the old\n  standalone sites."},{"hash":"9e079ef","date":"2026-10-08T00:47:29+01:00","subject":"Notes and Calendar show the current version after an update","body":"Their offline helpers answered from the cache first and refreshed in the\nbackground, so after every change you saw the previous version once (old\nnames, old behaviour). Online they now fetch fresh first and use the cache\nonly when offline. Inside Nova Agent, where nothing needs to work offline,\ntheir helper clears what it kept, unregisters and reloads the page."},{"hash":"100fb09","date":"2026-10-08T00:43:48+01:00","subject":"Plain names: everything is Nova Agent, and its panels are Portal, Portal, Calendar…","body":"Undoes the made-up names. \"Studio\" is Portal again and \"Crew\" is Portal again\n(only where the earlier rename had changed them; real uses of the words are\nkept). Every panel and feature drops \"Nova\": Portal, Portal, Calendar, Notes,\nIndex, Observatory, Missions, Quests and the Manual. \"Nova\" stays for Nova\nAgent itself, Nova Bot and Nova Club.\nThe original addresses are back: Portal at /app/, Portal at /portal/ and\nIndex at /app/memory/ (the panels live in web/portal, web/portal, web/index).\nNova Agent's own icons move to /agent/ to make room. /studio/, /crew/ and\n/index/ redirect, for anything that picked them up yesterday."},{"hash":"9aa754c","date":"2026-10-07T23:40:50+01:00","subject":"README: Nova Agent is the studio's one app, with its panels","body":"The README starts with what Nova Agent is now (every former Nova app as a\npanel, on the studio PC and online for phones), a table of the panels with\ntheir addresses and code, how signing in works on the PC, and the new\nproject layout. Each panel's guide in docs/apps/ loses its old repo's\nbadges, clone and deploy steps and suite tables, says where the panel\nlives, and its pictures point at the right place (every link checked).\nStudio's GIFs move here from Nova Bot. The Nova Manual is rebuilt."},{"hash":"4b86f1f","date":"2026-10-07T23:33:47+01:00","subject":"Portal is Studio, Nova Portal is Crew, and the suite is Nova Agent","body":"- Renamed everywhere in Nova Agent: the code, its page, the panels, the\n  docs and the chat's instructions. On phones, notifications and the\n  installed app say Nova Agent.\n- Nova Agent's launcher lists its panels (Chat, Studio, Crew, Calendar,\n  Notes, Index, Observatory, Lossless audio), which all open inside it from\n  this computer, and Services and admin (Nova Bot, the Visualizer, Admin,\n  All links, the code).\n- On the studio PC, Studio's sign-in is your own account (the shared studio\n  password field is hidden there).\nChecked in a browser on a test copy: every panel opens inside Nova Agent,\nand signed out, Studio and Crew show their sign-in."},{"hash":"d3b02ec","date":"2026-10-07T23:29:25+01:00","subject":"One copy of what the panels share; Studio at /studio/, Crew at /crew/, Index at /index/","body":"- web/shared: the themes, sounds, the Portal badge and the Nova Manual,\n  once, instead of a copy in every app (4-5 copies each before). Nova\n  Agent serves it at /shared/ and no longer fetches the themes from Nova\n  Bot.\n- Studio (was Portal) lives at /studio/, Crew (was Nova Portal) at\n  /crew/ and Index (was at /app/memory/) at /index/; every link between\n  them follows. /app/memory/ redirects. The worker API paths (/app/api,\n  /auth, /staff) are unchanged.\n- Calendar's and Notes' offline helpers no longer list the shared files."},{"hash":"fef653e","date":"2026-10-07T23:27:20+01:00","subject":"Panels laid out: Studio (was Portal), Crew (was Nova Portal), Index…","body":"- web/studio: Portal's staff app, now Nova Agent's Studio panel\n- web/crew: Nova Portal's app (sign-in, me, crew, invites), now the Crew\n  panel, with the planet avatar generator beside it\n- web/index, web/calendar, web/notes, web/observatory: the panels\n- Each app's README and pictures move to docs/apps/<panel>\n- The manual and badge scripts move to scripts/, and the Observatory's\n  scanning tools to scripts/observatory (npm run observatory:scan,\n  :capture, :build), writing into web/observatory as before\n- Calendar's and Notes' own deploy configs (their separate workers.dev\n  sites) are dropped: they're panels now\nPaths inside the panels are fixed up next."},{"hash":"8d2427f","date":"2026-10-07T23:23:35+01:00","subject":"Nova Agent takes in Nova Calendar (with its history), as web/calendar","body":"git-subtree-dir: web/calendar\ngit-subtree-mainline: 851d7a41538174d4f19c4c84b151b36d054e9809\ngit-subtree-split: e57c424622432ebd6c49b6758517f0998c3a40aa"},{"hash":"e57c424","date":"2026-10-07T16:31:15+01:00","subject":"The Nova Manual: refreshed with today's changes","body":""},{"hash":"bef7cda","date":"2026-10-07T16:29:37+01:00","subject":"The Nova Manual, beside the badge","body":"The book button next to the Portal badge opens the Nova Manual: every\nNova app's guide, how it's built, its history and what's new, with\nsearch. js/nova-manual.js and its pages are copies from Nova Portal\n(scripts/build-manual.mjs); the service worker caches them (v7)."},{"hash":"dbe549a","date":"2026-10-07T02:01:05+01:00","subject":"Nova Portal badge: Connect as me in Nova Agent","body":""},{"hash":"8839341","date":"2026-10-07T01:50:07+01:00","subject":"The Nova Portal badge in the top bar (Connect once in Nova Portal)","body":""},{"hash":"361e2e2","date":"2026-10-07T01:34:31+01:00","subject":"README: new screenshots, an add-a-note-card demo, Sound, Links and fit to the window","body":"Fresh screenshots of the month, a day card, the note card and day card\neditors and three themes, all with made-up cards; fit-to-window shots\nat about 900 × 600 and 430 × 600 with ?embed=1; a GIF of adding a note\ncard; and sections on the Sound button, the Links button and how Nova\nAgent builds the calendar in."},{"hash":"07b0820","date":"2026-10-06T23:17:00+01:00","subject":"Fit to the window when shown inside another app","body":"Inside Nova Agent (or with ?embed=1) the calendar fills exactly the space it's\ngiven: a slim header, month rows that share the height, the selected day\nbeside or below with its own scroll, and no footer or legend."},{"hash":"4c636ce","date":"2026-10-06T23:10:50+01:00","subject":"Sound effects, with a Sound button at the top","body":""},{"hash":"755ec37","date":"2026-10-06T21:32:46+01:00","subject":"A locked Links button: every Nova suite address","body":""},{"hash":"9c8e85a","date":"2026-10-06T18:22:19+01:00","subject":"Rename Nova Task to Nova Calendar and make it an installable app","body":"New name throughout (saved data from Nova Task is picked up\nautomatically), a crescent-moon C icon and launch screen, a manifest\nwith New note card / New day card launcher shortcuts, offline support,\nand Cloudflare hosting at https://nova-calendar.novacane-studio.workers.dev"},{"hash":"992a091","date":"2026-10-06T15:52:52+01:00","subject":"Nova Task: a cosmic calendar of note cards and day cards","body":""}],"work":[],"workCount":0,"workStat":""}},{"id":"notes","name":"Notes","colour":"#FF8CC6","glyph":"✎","where":"A Nova Agent panel","links":[["Open Notes","https://nova.novacane.co.uk/notes/"]],"repo":"na","shared":"","tagline":"A note editor that writes from the centre of the universe outwards.","intro":"<blockquote><strong>A Nova Agent panel.</strong> Its code is in <code>web/notes/</code> in Nova Agent&#39;s repo, and it opens inside Nova Agent at <code>/notes/</code>. Online, Nova Bot serves it at the same address.</blockquote>\n<p>Google Docs–style writing in the Novacane cosmic look: centred by default, six colour themes, soft cosmic sounds, import from Word, HTML, Markdown and text, and send it all to Google Docs.</p>\n<h4>✦ <a href=\"https://nova.novacane.co.uk/notes/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Open Nova Notes</a> ✦</h4>\n<p>Works in any modern browser · install it as an app · works offline · also built into Nova Agent</p>","guide":[{"id":"what-it-does-0","title":"What it does","html":"<p><strong>Writes like Google Docs</strong></p>\n<ul><li><strong>Menus and a toolbar</strong> you already know: File, Edit, View, Insert, Format, Tools and Help, with undo, redo, print, zoom, styles, fonts, sizes, colours and highlights.</li><li><strong>Paragraph styles:</strong> Title, Subtitle, Heading 1–3, Normal text, Quote and Code.</li><li><strong>Lists:</strong> bulleted, numbered and <strong>checklists</strong> you tick with a click; indent and outdent.</li><li><strong>Tables</strong> (pick a size, then add or remove rows and columns), <strong>pictures</strong> (upload, paste or drop, then resize and align), <strong>links</strong>, horizontal lines and <strong>page breaks</strong>.</li><li><strong>Find and replace</strong> (match case, whole words), <strong>word count</strong>, a live <strong>outline</strong> of your headings, and <strong>undo that remembers everything</strong>, including the tools the browser forgets.</li><li><strong>Shortcuts as you type:</strong> <code>#</code> heading, <code>-</code> list, <code>1.</code> numbered list, <code>[]</code> checklist, <code>&gt;</code> quote and <code>---</code> for a line. Every Google Docs keyboard shortcut you&#39;d expect is there too (press Ctrl+/).</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Centred by default.</strong> Everything you write (headings, paragraphs, lists and tables) sits in the middle of the page until you choose otherwise. Exports keep it that way.</p>\n<p><strong>In and out</strong></p>\n<ul><li><strong>Import</strong> Word (<code>.docx</code>), web pages (<code>.html</code>), Markdown (<code>.md</code>) and text (<code>.txt</code>): use <em>File → Import</em> or drop files onto the window. Text pasted from Google Docs or the web is cleaned up as it lands.</li><li><strong>Export</strong> to Google Docs, Word (<code>.doc</code>), a web page, Markdown, plain text or PDF (print), or a <code>.json</code> backup of one note or all of them.</li><li><strong>Google Docs</strong>, two ways:</li><li class=\"sub\"><strong>Copy &amp; paste (no set-up):</strong> copies the note with its styling and opens a new Google Doc; press Ctrl+V.</li><li class=\"sub\"><strong>Save to Google Drive (one click once set up):</strong> signs in with Google, creates a real Google Doc, and updates that same Doc each time you save the note again.</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Looks and sounds the part</strong></p>\n<ul><li><strong>Six themes</strong> from Nova Agent: Novacane (magenta), Solar Flare (red-orange), Pulsar (cyan), Aurora (green and violet), Eclipse (gold) and Quasar (ultraviolet).</li><li><strong>Two page styles:</strong> <em>Cosmic</em> (a glowing glass page among twinkling stars) and <em>Paper</em> (white, exactly how the note exports and prints).</li><li><strong>Sound effects:</strong> gentle bells and sparkles as you work (see below).</li><li><strong>Focus mode,</strong> a pageless view, zoom, and a layout that works on phones and tablets.</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Private by default.</strong> Nova Notes are saved in your browser (IndexedDB) as you type. Nothing leaves it unless you export it or send it to Google Docs.</p>","text":"Writes like Google Docs Menus and a toolbar you already know: File, Edit, View, Insert, Format, Tools and Help, with undo, redo, print, zoom, styles, fonts, sizes, colours and highlights. Paragraph styles: Title, Subtitle, Heading 1–3, Normal text, Quote and Code. Lists: bulleted, numbered and checklists you tick with a click; indent and outdent. Tables (pick a size, then add or remove rows and columns), pictures (upload, paste or drop, then resize and align), links , horizontal lines and page breaks . Find and replace (match case, whole words), word count , a live outline of your headings, and undo that remembers everything , including the tools the browser forgets. Shortcuts as you type: # heading, - list, 1. numbered list, [] checklist, > quote and --- for a line. Every Google Docs keyboard shortcut you'd expect is there too (press Ctrl+/). Centred by default. Everything you write (headings, paragraphs, lists and tables) sits in the middle of the page until you choose otherwise. Exports keep it that way. In and out Import Word ( .docx ), web pages ( .html ), Markdown ( .md ) and text ( .txt ): use File → Import or drop files onto the window. Text pasted from Google Docs or the web is cleaned up as it lands. Export to Google Docs, Word ( .doc ), a web page, Markdown, plain text or PDF (print), or a .json backup of one note or all of them. Google Docs , two ways: Copy & paste (no set-up): copies the note with its styling and opens a new Google Doc; press Ctrl+V. Save to Google Drive (one click once set up): signs in with Google, creates a real Google Doc, and updates that same Doc each time you save the note again. Looks and sounds the part Six themes from Nova Agent: Novacane (magenta), Solar Flare (red-orange), Pulsar (cyan), Aurora (green and violet), Eclipse (gold) and Quasar (ultraviolet). Two page styles: Cosmic (a glowing glass page among twinkling stars) and Paper (white, exactly how the note exports and prints). Sound effects: gentle bells and sparkles as you work (see below). Focus mode, a pageless view, zoom, and a layout that works on phones and tablets. Private by default. Nova Notes are saved in your browser (IndexedDB) as you type. Nothing leaves it unless you export it or send it to Google Docs."},{"id":"sound-effects-1","title":"Sound effects","html":"<p>Every press makes a soft cosmic sound: a tap, a menu opening, a dialog closing, an export sending, a note deleting. They&#39;re made live in the browser with the Web Audio API (there are no sound files), tuned to one pentatonic scale so they sound like one family, and kept quiet.</p>\n<ul><li><strong>On or off:</strong> <em>View → Sound effects</em>. It&#39;s ticked while they&#39;re on, and plays a little chime when you switch.</li><li><strong>Remembered</strong> on each device.</li><li><strong>Shared:</strong> the same <code>js/sfx.js</code> makes the sounds in Nova Calendar and Nova Observatory too.</li></ul>","text":"Every press makes a soft cosmic sound: a tap, a menu opening, a dialog closing, an export sending, a note deleting. They're made live in the browser with the Web Audio API (there are no sound files), tuned to one pentatonic scale so they sound like one family, and kept quiet. On or off: View → Sound effects . It's ticked while they're on, and plays a little chime when you switch. Remembered on each device. Shared: the same js/sfx.js makes the sounds in Nova Calendar and Nova Observatory too."},{"id":"inside-nova-agent-2","title":"Inside Nova Agent","html":"<p><a href=\"https://github.com/tuniveza/nova-agent\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Nova Agent</a>, the studio&#39;s helper (it runs on the VPS), serves its own copy of Nova Notes at <strong><code>/notes/</code></strong> ().</p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th></th><th>On the web</th><th>Inside Nova Agent</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Address</td><td>nova.novacane.co.uk/notes/</td><td><code>/notes/</code> on Nova Agent</td></tr><tr><td>Where Local notes are kept</td><td>In that browser</td><td>On the VPS, separate from the web app&#39;s</td></tr><tr><td>Shared notes</td><td>The team&#39;s, kept by Nova Bot</td><td>The same team notes</td></tr><tr><td>Privacy-minded browsers</td><td>May limit what a website saves</td><td>Fine: it&#39;s part of Nova Agent</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","text":"Nova Agent , the studio's helper (it runs on the VPS), serves its own copy of Nova Notes at /notes/ (). On the web Inside Nova Agent Address nova.novacane.co.uk/notes/ /notes/ on Nova Agent Where Local notes are kept In that browser On the VPS, separate from the web app's Shared notes The team's, kept by Nova Bot The same team notes Privacy-minded browsers May limit what a website saves Fine: it's part of Nova Agent"},{"id":"keyboard-shortcuts-3","title":"Keyboard shortcuts","html":"<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Bold / italic / underline</td><td>Ctrl B / I / U</td></tr><tr><td>Strikethrough</td><td>Alt Shift 5</td></tr><tr><td>Normal text / Heading 1–3</td><td>Ctrl Alt 0–3</td></tr><tr><td>Left / centre / right / justify</td><td>Ctrl Shift L / E / R / J</td></tr><tr><td>Numbered / bulleted / checklist</td><td>Ctrl Shift 7 / 8 / 9</td></tr><tr><td>Link</td><td>Ctrl K</td></tr><tr><td>Find and replace</td><td>Ctrl H</td></tr><tr><td>Word count</td><td>Ctrl Shift C</td></tr><tr><td>Page break</td><td>Ctrl Enter</td></tr><tr><td>New note · Import · Print</td><td>Ctrl Alt N · Ctrl O · Ctrl P</td></tr><tr><td>Focus mode</td><td>Ctrl Shift F</td></tr><tr><td>Every shortcut</td><td>Ctrl /</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","text":"Bold / italic / underline Ctrl B / I / U Strikethrough Alt Shift 5 Normal text / Heading 1–3 Ctrl Alt 0–3 Left / centre / right / justify Ctrl Shift L / E / R / J Numbered / bulleted / checklist Ctrl Shift 7 / 8 / 9 Link Ctrl K Find and replace Ctrl H Word count Ctrl Shift C Page break Ctrl Enter New note · Import · Print Ctrl Alt N · Ctrl O · Ctrl P Focus mode Ctrl Shift F Every shortcut Ctrl /"},{"id":"tasks-and-pasting-markdown-4","title":"Tasks, and pasting Markdown","html":"<ul><li><strong>Paste Markdown</strong> (from a chat, a code editor or a .md file) and it becomes real formatting: headings, lists, checklists, quotes, code, bold, links and tables.</li><li><strong>Tasks:</strong> any <strong>heading 3</strong> with the word <strong>TASK</strong> in it shows up in the <strong>Tasks</strong> list at the top of the side panel (a Markdown <code>### TASK …</code> line becomes one). Tap a task to jump to it; with three or more, type to find one. Set how it&#39;s going: <strong>Waiting</strong>, <strong>Soon</strong>, <strong>Working on it</strong>, <strong>Taking longer than expected</strong> or <strong>Done</strong>; the status shows beside the heading in the note and is saved with it (shared notes too). <strong>Chat</strong> hands the task, with what&#39;s written under it, to Nova Agent to talk it through.</li><li>The outline shows every heading in full (long ones wrap); nothing is cut off.</li></ul>","text":"Paste Markdown (from a chat, a code editor or a .md file) and it becomes real formatting: headings, lists, checklists, quotes, code, bold, links and tables. Tasks: any heading 3 with the word TASK in it shows up in the Tasks list at the top of the side panel (a Markdown ### TASK … line becomes one). Tap a task to jump to it; with three or more, type to find one. Set how it's going: Waiting , Soon , Working on it , Taking longer than expected or Done ; the status shows beside the heading in the note and is saved with it (shared notes too). Chat hands the task, with what's written under it, to Nova Agent to talk it through. The outline shows every heading in full (long ones wrap); nothing is cut off."}],"built":[{"id":"how-it-works-0","title":"How it works","html":"<pre><code>flowchart LR\n  subgraph Browser\n    E[editor.js&lt;br/&gt;contenteditable page,&lt;br/&gt;own undo history] --&gt; A[app.js&lt;br/&gt;menus, toolbar,&lt;br/&gt;library, dialogs]\n    A --&gt; S[(store.js&lt;br/&gt;IndexedDB)]\n    A --&gt; C[convert.js&lt;br/&gt;clean · Markdown ·&lt;br/&gt;styled export]\n    X[sfx.js&lt;br/&gt;Web Audio sounds] -.-&gt; A\n  end\n  F[.docx · .html · .md · .txt] -- import --&gt; C\n  C -- copy + docs.new --&gt; G[Google Docs]\n  C -- google.js&lt;br/&gt;Drive API, HTML → Doc --&gt; G\n  C -- download --&gt; D[.doc · .html · .md · .txt · PDF]</code></pre>\n<ul><li><strong><code>editor.js</code></strong>: the writing surface. It handles commands and paragraph styles, lists and checklists, tables, pictures, find and replace, and Markdown-style shortcuts. Undo works from snapshots of the page and selection, so every change can be undone.</li><li><strong><code>convert.js</code></strong>: cleans pasted and imported HTML down to what the editor understands, converts Markdown both ways, and builds the <strong>styled export</strong>: every block is inline-styled in the current theme&#39;s colours, made deep enough to read on white, so Google Docs and Word keep the look and the centring.</li><li><strong><code>google.js</code></strong>: the clipboard route (rich HTML plus plain text) and the Drive route (Google Identity Services token → multipart upload that Drive converts to a Google Doc, then <code>PATCH</code> to update it).</li><li><strong><code>store.js</code></strong>: notes in IndexedDB (falling back to localStorage), settings, backup and restore.</li><li><strong><code>sfx.js</code></strong>: Nova Agent&#39;s sound effects. One listener works out what kind of thing was pressed and plays the matching sound; an element can choose its own with <code>data-sfx</code>.</li><li><strong><code>themes.js</code></strong> and <strong><code>backdrop.js</code></strong>: Nova Agent&#39;s colour themes and the star field, shared with <a href=\"https://github.com/tuniveza/nova-calendar\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Nova Calendar</a>.</li></ul>","text":"flowchart LR subgraph Browser E[editor.js<br/>contenteditable page,<br/>own undo history] --> A[app.js<br/>menus, toolbar,<br/>library, dialogs] A --> S[(store.js<br/>IndexedDB)] A --> C[convert.js<br/>clean · Markdown ·<br/>styled export] X[sfx.js<br/>Web Audio sounds] -.-> A end F[.docx · .html · .md · .txt] -- import --> C C -- copy + docs.new --> G[Google Docs] C -- google.js<br/>Drive API, HTML → Doc --> G C -- download --> D[.doc · .html · .md · .txt · PDF] editor.js : the writing surface. It handles commands and paragraph styles, lists and checklists, tables, pictures, find and replace, and Markdown-style shortcuts. Undo works from snapshots of the page and selection, so every change can be undone. convert.js : cleans pasted and imported HTML down to what the editor understands, converts Markdown both ways, and builds the styled export : every block is inline-styled in the current theme's colours, made deep enough to read on white, so Google Docs and Word keep the look and the centring. google.js : the clipboard route (rich HTML plus plain text) and the Drive route (Google Identity Services token → multipart upload that Drive converts to a Google Doc, then PATCH to update it). store.js : notes in IndexedDB (falling back to localStorage), settings, backup and restore. sfx.js : Nova Agent's sound effects. One listener works out what kind of thing was pressed and plays the matching sound; an element can choose its own with data-sfx . themes.js and backdrop.js : Nova Agent's colour themes and the star field, shared with Nova Calendar ."}],"news":[{"id":"what-s-new-0","title":"What's new","html":"<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>✦ <strong>Welcome guide</strong></td><td>The first time Nova Notes opens in a browser, a clickable guide shows once (no more &quot;Welcome to Nova Notes&quot; notes). Topics along the top jump to their part (Start, Writing, The look, Shared · Local, In and out, Shortcuts), and <strong>Try it</strong> buttons do the thing: a new note, find and replace, focus mode, the themes, Shared or Local, import, export, Google Docs, every shortcut. It&#39;s always in <strong>Help → Welcome guide</strong>.</td></tr><tr><td>👥 <strong>Shared and Local notes</strong></td><td><strong>Shared</strong> notes are the whole team&#39;s: everyone signed in with Nova Portal sees and edits them, on every device, and changes show up for the others within seconds. <strong>Local</strong> notes stay only on this device. Tap <strong>Local / Shared</strong> by &quot;Saved&quot; to move a note between the two (with Undo), and use <strong>All · Shared · Local</strong> above the list to pick what you see. New notes start Shared when you&#39;re signed in (Local when you&#39;re signed out or looking at Local). If two people change a shared note at the same time, both versions are kept (&quot;… (conflicted copy)&quot;).</td></tr><tr><td>🔔 <strong>Sound effects</strong></td><td>Soft cosmic sounds on every action. Switch them off or on in <strong>View → Sound effects</strong>.</td></tr><tr><td>🔒 <strong>All Nova Agent links</strong></td><td><strong>Help → 🔒 All Nova Agent links</strong> opens the password-protected page with every Nova Agent address, live and testing.</td></tr><tr><td>✦ <strong>Inside Nova Agent</strong></td><td>Nova Agent serves its own copy at <code>/notes/</code>, so privacy-minded browsers don&#39;t block it there. Nova Notes written there are kept on the VPS, where Nova Agent runs.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","text":"✦ Welcome guide The first time Nova Notes opens in a browser, a clickable guide shows once (no more \"Welcome to Nova Notes\" notes). Topics along the top jump to their part (Start, Writing, The look, Shared · Local, In and out, Shortcuts), and Try it buttons do the thing: a new note, find and replace, focus mode, the themes, Shared or Local, import, export, Google Docs, every shortcut. It's always in Help → Welcome guide . 👥 Shared and Local notes Shared notes are the whole team's: everyone signed in with Nova Portal sees and edits them, on every device, and changes show up for the others within seconds. Local notes stay only on this device. Tap Local / Shared by \"Saved\" to move a note between the two (with Undo), and use All · Shared · Local above the list to pick what you see. New notes start Shared when you're signed in (Local when you're signed out or looking at Local). If two people change a shared note at the same time, both versions are kept (\"… (conflicted copy)\"). 🔔 Sound effects Soft cosmic sounds on every action. Switch them off or on in View → Sound effects . 🔒 All Nova Agent links Help → 🔒 All Nova Agent links opens the password-protected page with every Nova Agent address, live and testing. ✦ Inside Nova Agent Nova Agent serves its own copy at /notes/ , so privacy-minded browsers don't block it there. Nova Notes written there are kept on the VPS, where Nova Agent runs."}],"history":{"total":57,"first":"2026-10-06T15:46:53+01:00","commits":[{"hash":"3e5e306","date":"2026-10-14T06:14:02+01:00","subject":"Manual and READMEs: Nova Agent runs on the VPS (day and night, every laptop off), not on the studio PC; Quests' options and the Fixer's wide view described","body":""},{"hash":"3a49323","date":"2026-10-14T02:54:08+01:00","subject":"Fit on screen in every panel: /shared/fit.js + fit.css keep menus, pop-ups, tooltips, non-modal dialogs and anything marked data-fit (or handed over with NovaFit.keep) inside the screen — nudged back in just far enough, capped and scrolling inside only when bigger than the screen, checked again on resize, turning round, a phone's keyboard and growing content; Agent's activity list and the planet card hooked in. scripts/check-fit-all.sh runs the whole fit check (throwaway server, 360×640, 768×1024, 1440×900, the Manual) and check-fit.mjs now also proves the fit layer is on every page and works after the window shrinks","body":""},{"hash":"8b1676e","date":"2026-10-14T01:23:54+01:00","subject":"All addresses: every web address in the suite in one list (Manual → All addresses; Portal → Settings → Addresses, and Apps and links), each with a plain line, Copy and Open; admins also see the ones other services use. Every link people see is https://nova.novacane.co.uk now (no studio-computer addresses in Portal, the Manual or the READMEs). scripts/check-addresses.mjs checks each one answers live","body":""},{"hash":"a23c9e9","date":"2026-10-13T22:54:11+01:00","subject":"Nova's own address in Nova Agent: nova.novacane.co.uk (the PC's link, links, the Manual); Computer talks about Nova's own computer","body":""},{"hash":"cf1ca77","date":"2026-10-13T10:45:15+01:00","subject":"WIP Board in Nova Agent's Apps (its icon and the phone bar); Notes opens one note from ?note=","body":""},{"hash":"321c19c","date":"2026-10-12T21:33:21+01:00","subject":"Google round two on the PC and in the panels: Tasks sync, Files in Drive, Agent's Drive/Docs/Tasks/YouTube tools, YouTube in Social, Meet in Calendar, today's calendar in Portal and what_now, Keep in Google Docs and Open a Google Doc in Notes, Google Contacts search in one-to-one emails","body":""},{"hash":"e6c2d32","date":"2026-10-12T20:21:21+01:00","subject":"Sizing: Portal's tabs never squash or cut off (the side menu only from 1024px; tab lanes below that whatever's chosen), Chats on narrow phones, Notes never left short of its frame, and a resize check","body":""},{"hash":"1d69ce2","date":"2026-10-12T20:19:55+01:00","subject":"Portal's Admin address is view=manage: ad blockers block any address with \"view=ad…\" (old admin links and remembered places are turned into the new one)","body":""},{"hash":"10334b3","date":"2026-10-12T19:17:54+01:00","subject":"Manual: Social, Money, the sorted inbox, one-to-one emails, Test stuff, the tab lanes, planet + chosen colour, Notes' Welcome guide, and Google (once connected)","body":""},{"hash":"2303434","date":"2026-10-12T18:52:49+01:00","subject":"Google: Portal → Admin → Google (set up one step at a time, what's kept in step), copies to Drive and nightly backups, Money's sheet, Notes to Docs in one tap, Agent's read-only Google tools","body":""},{"hash":"81e0b1e","date":"2026-10-12T12:42:39+01:00","subject":"Notes: a clickable Welcome guide instead of a Welcome note","body":"Notes no longer makes a 'Welcome to Notes' note (a new browser found no notes before the\nshared ones arrived, so copies piled up in Shared: 16 from the hourly checks). Instead:\n- the Welcome guide (Help → Welcome guide), shown once the first time: topics to jump to\n  and Try-it buttons (new note, list, outline, find, focus, themes, Shared/Local, import,\n  export, Google Docs, shortcuts); it stays on screen and only its contents scroll\n- a new browser waits for the shared notes; with none, one blank Local note\n- untouched copies of the old Welcome note are tidied away everywhere; edited ones stay"},{"hash":"1f748b5","date":"2026-10-11T12:11:55+01:00","subject":"Everything fits: nothing hangs off the screen in any panel; what doesn't fit scrolls inside its own box","body":"scripts/check-fit.mjs opens Nova Agent's home and every panel (on its own and inside Nova Agent) at\n7 sizes (incl. a phone with its keyboard up) with long sample content, opens every sheet, dialog and\npop-up, and reports anything past the screen or its clipping box. Fixes what it found:\n- Portal: the side-menu tab row started off its left edge (tabs unreachable); Booking tools' picked\n  day was wider than the screen; a chat's Enquiry pill was clamped away; Options buttons squashed\n  their icon; a busy day's dots spilled out; long words wrap in views\n- Calendar: long words break inside cards; day cards no longer squashed; narrow short events clamp\n  their title to their height; What to show scrolls inside on short screens\n- Notes: menus and pop-ups scroll inside (and stay on screen) on short screens; snippets wrap\n- Nova Agent: chat action chips, mission summaries and file titles wrap; Ho"},{"hash":"ccda75f","date":"2026-10-11T11:23:11+01:00","subject":"P0-4: chats, quests, missions and reminders tied to each person","body":"- Who's asking (src/person.ts): online, the staff member Nova Bot's relay\n  passes (marked on the request object itself, so it can't be forged); on\n  the PC, the person Nova Agent works for. Anything with no owner is theirs.\n- The Agent's system prompt names the person and their role; what its tools\n  make (missions, quests, blocked times, rhythm) is theirs; Index memory is\n  theirs.\n- Each person has their own Agent conversation (data/chats/<staff id>.json);\n  the PC person's old browser history is brought over once.\n- Missions, quests and blocks have an `owner`. Quests panels, Missions and\n  the Agent's tools show your own; admins and the PC can switch to\n  everyone's. Staff change only their own (and quests tied to a shared note).\n- Each person is planned in their own time: their own blocks, music time and\n  (optional) rhythm; one person's quests never take another's time.\n- Reminders"},{"hash":"bb1c08b","date":"2026-10-11T04:49:41+01:00","subject":"Centred text in Notes' list and Nova Agent's dialogs; days off wear the theme","body":"A note's name and its Shared / Local badge sit in the middle of its row; the daily rhythm's tick\nboxes, days off and buttons, and a mission's deadline row and buttons, gather in the middle. The\ndays-off chips use the theme's highlight instead of a fixed red."},{"hash":"6bb3462","date":"2026-10-11T04:28:58+01:00","subject":"Centred text reaches the last left-aligned corners","body":"The Manual (apps down the side, On this page, search, cards, results, next/previous), the Portal\nbadge's name and role, the Panels window's group headings (a line either side), Calendar's chosen\nday, Notes' menu bar and status bar, and Visualizer's header, buttons and part names. All follow\nCentre all text, so Left still works. Also: Visualizer is just \"Visualizer\" (not \"Nova\nVisualizer\"), Nova Bot spelt the usual way, and the Manual and badge say \"Nova Agent\" and\n\"panel\" rather than \"Nova app\"."},{"hash":"ce1ff1c","date":"2026-10-11T04:25:36+01:00","subject":"Dates and times written the British way, in London time, whatever the browser's language","body":"Calendar's mid-size day labels read \"19 Oct\" and \"19/10\" (not \"10month 19day\" and \"10 19\");\nthe status line's clock no longer follows the browser's language (\"So 5:04 am\"); Visualizer's\nstep times and every other date label say en-GB, Europe/London."},{"hash":"91d1fad","date":"2026-10-11T03:25:54+01:00","subject":"Plain app names again (only Nova Agent and Nova Bot keep Nova); titles on one surface; Portal's tabs wrap on tablets too","body":"Undoes the 'Nova <App>' renaming line by line (the ✦ marks, the tab bar and the scrollbars\nstay). Inside Nova Agent a shared rule kept Portal's tabs on one sliding row under 981px:\nfrom 761px they now wrap too, so every tab is on screen."},{"hash":"43e7562","date":"2026-10-11T03:18:54+01:00","subject":"Titles sit centred at the top of each open app (icon + name in the theme's gradient), Back and Reload tucked in the corners; Portal's tabs wrap so all stay on screen","body":""},{"hash":"d6d2213","date":"2026-10-11T02:57:49+01:00","subject":"Nova first in every app name (the bottom bars keep their short labels)","body":"Nova Portal, Nova Agent, Nova Calendar, Nova Notes, Nova Index, Nova Quests, Nova Missions,\nNova Lossless, Nova Visualizer, Nova Observatory, Nova Manual: titles, headers, the Panels\nwindow, the status line, the Manual, manifests, messages and alerts. Also: the Nova mark's CSS on\nthe panel icons (chat.html), Portal's tab labels and tabbar.js, and the scrollbars link in each page."},{"hash":"e2b63d9","date":"2026-10-11T02:57:49+01:00","subject":"Icons: the same small Nova sparkle in the corner of every app's icon","body":""},{"hash":"d805620","date":"2026-10-11T02:22:08+01:00","subject":"Merge branch 'themes-buttons'","body":""},{"hash":"95b9569","date":"2026-10-11T02:21:20+01:00","subject":"Themes: a colour spectrum with a Custom colour; one button look for every panel","body":"A spectrum of themes for all of Nova Agent (web/shared/spectrum.js): Crimson, Rose,\nCoral, Amber, Lime, Jade, Teal, Glacier, Indigo, Violet and Orchid join the old ones,\neach a hand-tuned set (deep sky, luminous accent, matching gradients and glows) whose\ntext reads at WCAG AA or better. Custom makes a whole theme from one hue and a\nvividness (OKLCH, so every hue is as readable as every other), remembered on the device\n(\"nova-look-custom\"). The pickers in the Panels window and Portal's and Index's Options\nshow every theme as an orb in rainbow order, then Custom with its two sliders; choosing\none, or moving a slider, recolours Nova Agent and every open panel straight away (look.js\nover storage events). Cosmic stays the default and looks the same; every old theme, id\nand the \"Each panel's own\" choice still work, and Portal's own theme can be any of them.\nOne button system (web/shared/butto"},{"hash":"4e34046","date":"2026-10-11T02:08:35+01:00","subject":"Notes: the page always fits the screen, and only its writing scrolls","body":"The page (sheet) used to be a 1056px-tall card that scrolled whole inside the\nwriting area, and a wide table pushed it sideways, so the page slid off screen.\nNow the page fills the space under the bars and stays put; the note scrolls\ninside it. Wide tables and code slide sideways in their own box, pictures stay\ninside. Find and replace sits over the page's corner. On phones the window\nfollows the visible screen (dvh, and js/fit.js with visualViewport, including\nNova Agent's around the frame) so the bars stay on top when the keyboard is up\nand the caret stays in view; the window itself never scrolls.\nscripts/check-notes-fit.mjs checks it at phone, tablet and desktop sizes, on\nits own and inside Nova Agent, with the side panels open."},{"hash":"7b816a8","date":"2026-10-10T15:52:31+01:00","subject":"Quests: pick which phones get the reminders; the whole quest wears its mode colour in Notes; Portal shows every quest; full note titles","body":"- A quest can pick its phones (📱 on the front page and in Notes; Agent can too); its pings\n  carry them, and Nova Bot sends them there (or to the studio owner's phones)\n- Notes: a quest's heading and everything under it are tinted in its mode's colour (drawn\n  live, never saved); the side panel's quest cards glow in it too\n- Portal gets every quest (open first, up to 400), shows quests not planned yet under Today,\n  and groups All quests by mode\n- Notes: Your Notes shows each note's whole title (long ones wrap)"},{"hash":"a4976f2","date":"2026-10-10T15:43:29+01:00","subject":"Quests in Notes, tied to Nova Quests; seven modes with colours that follow the theme","body":"- Notes: any heading with QUEST in it (TASK still counts) is a quest: + New quest, change its mode,\n  hand it to Agent, take it off Quests (the text stays). Each one is made in Nova Quests the moment\n  it appears, and kept in step: the heading is its title, the mode goes both ways\n- Nova Quests: every quest has a mode (Waiting, Soon, Working On It, Nearly Finished, Taking longer\n  than expected, Questions, Done), where it's from and what it's tied to; modes set the status\n  they mean (and Done / Start set the mode); Agent can set it; Portal's taps can too\n- Front page and Portal: a coloured mode chip on each quest, tap to change\n- /shared/quest-modes.css|js: the one set of mode colours (tinted toward the theme) and menu"},{"hash":"332bfcd","date":"2026-10-10T15:17:37+01:00","subject":"One gear for settings; admin things open in Portal → Admin","body":"- settings.js: the top-bar gear also opens the open panel's own settings (Portal's options,\n  or any panel's NovaPanelSettings): a button in the Panels window (desktop) and the gear's\n  sheet (phone)\n- All links (gear) and Notes' Google set-up and All links open Portal → Admin"},{"hash":"1f7ea3b","date":"2026-10-10T15:13:08+01:00","subject":"Portal first, Agent second; no 'Chat' left; Agent in Portal's side menu (the same conversation)","body":"- Taskbar and launcher: Portal, Agent, Calendar, Notes, Index\n- Notes' task button says Agent; Portal's website chats are Conversations\n- Portal's side menu (and More on phones) has Agent: inside Nova Agent the panel steps\n  aside for the one Agent conversation (NovaAgent.agent()); on its own it opens /agent/"},{"hash":"f0d6ad3","date":"2026-10-10T14:44:17+01:00","subject":"Files: Agent writes documents (Markdown, text, CSV, JSON, HTML) to preview, download or open in Notes; missions export as a document","body":"The owner's work on the studio PC, saved as it was (with their OK, 2026-10-10)."},{"hash":"b9569ef","date":"2026-10-10T13:34:21+01:00","subject":"Notes: pasted Markdown becomes formatting; TASK headings become a task list with statuses and chat","body":"Markdown on the clipboard (when it isn't already a formatted page) becomes headings, lists,\nchecklists, quotes, code, bold, links and tables. Every heading 3 with TASK in it is listed in the\nside panel's Tasks: jump to it, find it, set its status (Waiting, Soon, Working on it, Taking\nlonger than expected, Done; saved on the heading, shown beside it) and hand it to Agent to chat\nabout. A Markdown \"### TASK\" is always a heading 3. The outline never cuts a heading off."},{"hash":"7099c0b","date":"2026-10-10T13:27:59+01:00","subject":"Portal everywhere: no more Portal (names, code, phone app, Manual)","body":"The staff app is Portal in every word: notifications, the voice command, the old phone app's\nname and icon (installed from /app/), code names (portalsync, window.PortalApp), comments, docs\nand the Manual (old commit notes are told with the new name). Settings saved under the old names\n(theme, options, music, alerts seen, hands-free) carry over once, so nothing resets."},{"hash":"f741f8a","date":"2026-10-09T17:41:59+01:00","subject":"Notes: new notes start Shared when signed in (Local only when signed out or on the Local tab)","body":""},{"hash":"b9eb764","date":"2026-10-09T03:19:20+01:00","subject":"Every window size usable; the lower part of the window brings up the bar; Notes stays on screen","body":"Phone layout only below 481px tall (short computer windows keep the computer layout, tighter).\nNarrower computer windows: slimmer columns, a shorter New button, smaller tool buttons. Short\nones: slimmer header, one swipeable row of suggestions, smaller bars. Tablets: the bar in one\ncentred row. The column titles' grid applies on computers only (phones keep their own header).\nThe bottom 14% of the window brings the bar up. Notes inside Nova Agent: its toolbar wraps, the\npage starts as tall as the window, the outline's lines end with an ellipsis."},{"hash":"263cf4f","date":"2026-10-09T02:31:27+01:00","subject":"Cosmic icons, one theme for everything, planet colours, smart top bar, status line","body":"Icons: a cosmic set, each with its own colour (mixed with the theme), sky and shape; Talk to\nNova Agent, Quests and Missions have their own. look.js: one theme for every panel (or each its\nown), and colour everything from your planet. Typing hides the panels bar. The top bar: Auto,\nAlways shown or Always hidden. The status line under the bar: Panels button (the top one is\ngone), version and build, what changed lately for the part of the bar you point at, on and off\ntimes, recent activity and a 12-hour clock. Lossless audio's sounds come along."},{"hash":"8f8db84","date":"2026-10-08T23:34:26+01:00","subject":"Notes: Shared and Local notes","body":"Shared notes are the team's: kept by Nova Bot (/notes-api/), seen and edited by\neveryone signed in with Portal on every device, synced every 15 s and on focus,\nreadable offline with changes queued until the connection is back. Local notes\nstay on this device, as before. One tap by \"Saved\" moves a note between the two\n(with Undo); All · Shared · Local above the list, a badge on each note. Two\npeople changing a shared note at once keeps both (\"… (conflicted copy)\").\nOn the studio PC, Nova Agent passes /notes-api/ on with its sign-in.\nEvery existing Notes feature stays."},{"hash":"932c20c","date":"2026-10-08T16:59:59+01:00","subject":"Panels on phones: fit, lighter, less scrolling","body":"- Notes: one top bar (notes list, the note's name, Google Docs) and the menus;\n  the toolbar is one row you swipe, with the everyday tools (the rest stay in\n  the menus); 16px fields; no glass blur, grain or drifting background.\n- Observatory: a slim title, the numbers as a compact strip, each project as\n  one short row with a small drawn cover (no full-size screenshots on phones);\n  category chips in one row; no star map, no moving sky, no blur.\n- Calendar and Index: no glass blur or endless decorative motion on phones.\n- Lossless audio: snug margins, big buttons, 16px fields.\n- Visualizer: no error when the studio PC is off; fits a phone."},{"hash":"ed420d6","date":"2026-10-08T13:33:52+01:00","subject":"Portal is the one sign-in","body":"Signed out, the planet opens Portal's sign-in (in Nova Agent's viewer): no\nsign-in form of its own, and no Sign in with Google anywhere. Google is a\nconnection, not a way in: Portal's You page shows it (connected as whom), with\nSet up / Connect Google for admins (Admin → Google). Notes asks\n/auth/google-status for the studio's Google key."},{"hash":"4fabb4b","date":"2026-10-08T13:26:32+01:00","subject":"Sign in with Google, on the planet and in Portal; Notes uses the studio's Google","body":"- The planet's sign-in card and Portal's sign-in card get a Sign in with\n  Google button once an admin has set Google up (Admin → Google). Google's\n  page opens in a small window (full screen in the installed phone app) and\n  every panel follows when it's done.\n- On the studio PC, Nova Agent starts it (/auth/google): it makes up a\n  verifier, Nova Bot sends back a one-time code to /auth/google/done, and\n  Nova Agent swaps the two for its own sign-in (src/signin.ts).\n- Notes' Save to Google Docs uses the studio's Google key, with nothing to\n  set up; without it, a button opens Admin → Google."},{"hash":"0f31499","date":"2026-10-08T02:16:18+01:00","subject":"Merge branch 'live-fixes' into sign-in","body":""},{"hash":"8ac9531","date":"2026-10-08T02:04:26+01:00","subject":"Lossless audio and Observatory as panels everywhere; docs at the real addresses","body":"- Lossless audio is served by Nova Agent at /lossless/ and opens inside it like\n  the other panels. Signalling and the relay setup come from Nova Bot (which now\n  serves it online too), so the other device can be anywhere; invite links point\n  at the online address. /lossless/ice lets Nova Agent's own page ask.\n- Observatory online asks for a Portal sign-in before showing the projects\n  (Nova Bot keeps them for signed-in staff).\n- Calendar's and Notes' guides link to their addresses on Nova Bot, not the old\n  standalone sites."},{"hash":"53332dc","date":"2026-10-08T02:04:14+01:00","subject":"Panels fit inside Nova Agent's viewer","body":"- While a panel is open, the panels strip shrinks to one row of small\n  switchers (services and admin as icons) and the viewer bar slims down:\n  the panel gets about 80px more height (431 → 511 at 1280×720). Only in\n  the side-by-side layout; stacked on a phone it's unchanged.\n- /shared/inside.js marks <html class=\"embed\"> when a panel is shown in a\n  frame (as Calendar's own embed.js already did), for frame-only fixes.\n- Notes in a frame: a slimmer two-row header (no kicker, smaller mark,\n  icon-only Import/Export/Google Docs below 1500px so the menus aren't\n  cut off), a tighter toolbar, and no word count in short frames. The\n  writing area goes from 215px to 377px tall at 1280×720.\n- Observatory in a frame: a smaller title block. Its stat numbers size to\n  their card (container units), so \"142,408\" no longer breaks in two.\n- Index in a frame: a slimmer tab bar."},{"hash":"9e079ef","date":"2026-10-08T00:47:29+01:00","subject":"Notes and Calendar show the current version after an update","body":"Their offline helpers answered from the cache first and refreshed in the\nbackground, so after every change you saw the previous version once (old\nnames, old behaviour). Online they now fetch fresh first and use the cache\nonly when offline. Inside Nova Agent, where nothing needs to work offline,\ntheir helper clears what it kept, unregisters and reloads the page."},{"hash":"100fb09","date":"2026-10-08T00:43:48+01:00","subject":"Plain names: everything is Nova Agent, and its panels are Portal, Portal, Calendar…","body":"Undoes the made-up names. \"Studio\" is Portal again and \"Crew\" is Portal again\n(only where the earlier rename had changed them; real uses of the words are\nkept). Every panel and feature drops \"Nova\": Portal, Portal, Calendar, Notes,\nIndex, Observatory, Missions, Quests and the Manual. \"Nova\" stays for Nova\nAgent itself, Nova Bot and Nova Club.\nThe original addresses are back: Portal at /app/, Portal at /portal/ and\nIndex at /app/memory/ (the panels live in web/portal, web/portal, web/index).\nNova Agent's own icons move to /agent/ to make room. /studio/, /crew/ and\n/index/ redirect, for anything that picked them up yesterday."},{"hash":"9aa754c","date":"2026-10-07T23:40:50+01:00","subject":"README: Nova Agent is the studio's one app, with its panels","body":"The README starts with what Nova Agent is now (every former Nova app as a\npanel, on the studio PC and online for phones), a table of the panels with\ntheir addresses and code, how signing in works on the PC, and the new\nproject layout. Each panel's guide in docs/apps/ loses its old repo's\nbadges, clone and deploy steps and suite tables, says where the panel\nlives, and its pictures point at the right place (every link checked).\nStudio's GIFs move here from Nova Bot. The Nova Manual is rebuilt."},{"hash":"4b86f1f","date":"2026-10-07T23:33:47+01:00","subject":"Portal is Studio, Nova Portal is Crew, and the suite is Nova Agent","body":"- Renamed everywhere in Nova Agent: the code, its page, the panels, the\n  docs and the chat's instructions. On phones, notifications and the\n  installed app say Nova Agent.\n- Nova Agent's launcher lists its panels (Chat, Studio, Crew, Calendar,\n  Notes, Index, Observatory, Lossless audio), which all open inside it from\n  this computer, and Services and admin (Nova Bot, the Visualizer, Admin,\n  All links, the code).\n- On the studio PC, Studio's sign-in is your own account (the shared studio\n  password field is hidden there).\nChecked in a browser on a test copy: every panel opens inside Nova Agent,\nand signed out, Studio and Crew show their sign-in."},{"hash":"d3b02ec","date":"2026-10-07T23:29:25+01:00","subject":"One copy of what the panels share; Studio at /studio/, Crew at /crew/, Index at /index/","body":"- web/shared: the themes, sounds, the Portal badge and the Nova Manual,\n  once, instead of a copy in every app (4-5 copies each before). Nova\n  Agent serves it at /shared/ and no longer fetches the themes from Nova\n  Bot.\n- Studio (was Portal) lives at /studio/, Crew (was Nova Portal) at\n  /crew/ and Index (was at /app/memory/) at /index/; every link between\n  them follows. /app/memory/ redirects. The worker API paths (/app/api,\n  /auth, /staff) are unchanged.\n- Calendar's and Notes' offline helpers no longer list the shared files."},{"hash":"fef653e","date":"2026-10-07T23:27:20+01:00","subject":"Panels laid out: Studio (was Portal), Crew (was Nova Portal), Index…","body":"- web/studio: Portal's staff app, now Nova Agent's Studio panel\n- web/crew: Nova Portal's app (sign-in, me, crew, invites), now the Crew\n  panel, with the planet avatar generator beside it\n- web/index, web/calendar, web/notes, web/observatory: the panels\n- Each app's README and pictures move to docs/apps/<panel>\n- The manual and badge scripts move to scripts/, and the Observatory's\n  scanning tools to scripts/observatory (npm run observatory:scan,\n  :capture, :build), writing into web/observatory as before\n- Calendar's and Notes' own deploy configs (their separate workers.dev\n  sites) are dropped: they're panels now\nPaths inside the panels are fixed up next."},{"hash":"4ea0638","date":"2026-10-07T23:23:36+01:00","subject":"Nova Agent takes in Nova Notes (with its history), as web/notes","body":"git-subtree-dir: web/notes\ngit-subtree-mainline: 8d2427fdf1afc33e56967b85d00ad060811f104f\ngit-subtree-split: df4f557e8b3d79cc58b6de13712430abffef58e8"},{"hash":"df4f557","date":"2026-10-07T16:31:18+01:00","subject":"The Nova Manual: refreshed with today's changes","body":""},{"hash":"8a13755","date":"2026-10-07T16:30:13+01:00","subject":"The Nova Manual, beside the badge","body":"The book button next to the Portal badge opens the Nova Manual: every\nNova app's guide, how it's built, its history and what's new, with\nsearch. js/nova-manual.js and its pages are copies from Nova Portal;\nthe service worker caches them (v6)."},{"hash":"8f0d4f5","date":"2026-10-07T02:01:05+01:00","subject":"Nova Portal badge: Connect as me in Nova Agent","body":""},{"hash":"8573aa3","date":"2026-10-07T01:50:12+01:00","subject":"The Nova Portal badge in the top bar (Connect once in Nova Portal)","body":""},{"hash":"bc0b45e","date":"2026-10-07T01:34:22+01:00","subject":"README: new screenshots, a typing demo, sound effects and Nova Agent","body":"Fresh screenshots from a new browser with the welcome note and two\nmade-up notes, a GIF of the #, - and [] shortcuts writing a centred\nnote, and sections for View → Sound effects, Help → All Nova suite\nlinks and the copy Nova Agent serves at /notes/. The old MP4 demo\nis gone; the README shows the GIF only."},{"hash":"646698c","date":"2026-10-06T23:10:46+01:00","subject":"Sound effects, with a switch in the View menu","body":""},{"hash":"16aeab4","date":"2026-10-06T21:32:30+01:00","subject":"Help menu: a locked link to every Nova suite address","body":""},{"hash":"cc543e3","date":"2026-10-06T18:23:23+01:00","subject":"Nova Task is now Nova Calendar","body":"Update the name and links to the renamed repo\n(https://github.com/tuniveza/nova-calendar)."},{"hash":"519310e","date":"2026-10-06T16:02:32+01:00","subject":"Make Nova Notes an installable web app","body":"Add a manifest, offline service worker, the cosmic N app icon and\nlaunch screen, an Install button, a New note shortcut, share-to-note\nand opening files with the app, plus Cloudflare hosting with security\nheaders. Live at https://nova-notes.novacane-studio.workers.dev"},{"hash":"739d47a","date":"2026-10-06T15:46:53+01:00","subject":"Nova Notes: a cosmic note editor for the Nova suite","body":"Google Docs-style rich text editing in the Novacane look, centred by\ndefault, with six colour themes, Cosmic and Paper page styles, import\nfrom Word/HTML/Markdown/text, export to Google Docs, Word, HTML,\nMarkdown, text and PDF, and notes saved in the browser."}],"work":[],"workCount":0,"workStat":""}},{"id":"quests","name":"Quests","colour":"#FFC857","glyph":"✓","where":"A Nova Agent panel","links":[["Open Quests","https://nova.novacane.co.uk/quests/"]],"repo":"na","shared":"","tagline":"Every quest in one place. Write one the way you'd say it, tick it off, and choose how to see them: one thing at a time, a list, a board, or hour by hour. They're the same quests as Nova Agent's own (today's plan beside Nova Agent), Nova Notes and Nova Portal: a change in one shows in all of them.","intro":"<p>Every quest in one place. Write one the way you&#39;d say it, tick it off, and choose how to see them: one thing at a time, a list, a board, or hour by hour. They&#39;re the same quests as Nova Agent&#39;s own (today&#39;s plan beside Nova Agent), Nova Notes and Nova Portal: a change in one shows in all of them.</p>","guide":[{"id":"what-it-does-0","title":"What it does","html":"<ul><li><strong>Quick add.</strong> Type in the box at the top and press Enter: “tomorrow 3pm call Sam !high #studio 30m”. Under the box you see what was understood before you add it. It understands:</li><li class=\"sub\"><strong>when</strong>: today, tonight, tomorrow, monday… (or mon, tue, wed, thu, fri; “on sat”, “on sun”), next friday, in 3 days, in 20 min, 14/10, 14 oct, 3pm, 15:00, at 9, noon, morning / afternoon / evening;</li><li class=\"sub\"><strong>finish by</strong>: by friday, by 5pm, due tomorrow;</li><li class=\"sub\"><strong>how long</strong>: 30m, 45 min, 1h, 1h30, 2 hours;</li><li class=\"sub\"><strong>priority</strong>: !low, !high, !critical (! or !! is high, !!! critical);</li><li class=\"sub\"><strong>tags</strong>: #studio #mix;</li><li class=\"sub\"><strong>repeats</strong>: daily, weekdays, weekly, every monday, every 30 min, every 2 hours. A day with no time means some time that day; Nova plans it into free time. The button beside <strong>Add</strong> opens the details first.</li><li><strong>Focus.</strong> One quest, big: <strong>Done</strong>, <strong>Start it</strong> (or <strong>15 more minutes</strong>), <strong>Not now</strong> (the next one) and <strong>Details</strong>. Its steps tick off right there. Underneath: what&#39;s next.</li><li><strong>List.</strong> Everything in plain groups: Now, Overdue, Today, Coming up, Any time, and Done (folded). Tick the circle to finish one (tick again to undo). Drag the dots on the left to put them in your own order (or <strong>Alt</strong> + <strong>↑ ↓</strong> from the keyboard): your order stays.</li><li><strong>Board.</strong> A column for each “how it&#39;s going” (Waiting, Soon, Working on it, Nearly finished, Done; Taking longer and Questions when they have something). Drag a card to another column, or tap its chip.</li><li><strong>Today.</strong> Today and the next week, hour by hour, and what hasn&#39;t got a time yet (<strong>Plan them now</strong> fits them in).</li><li><strong>Details.</strong> Tap a quest: its name, when, finish by, how long, repeat, how it&#39;s going, priority, steps (tick, change, remove), tags, notes and where. <strong>Delete</strong> has <strong>Undo</strong> for a few seconds.</li><li><strong>Find.</strong> The magnifier (or <strong>/</strong>): words in names, notes and steps, or #tag. The tag chips under the box show only that tag.</li><li><strong>Calm.</strong> The moon (or <strong>C</strong>): fewer things on screen, less colour, nothing moving, at most five in a group and only today in Today. Remembered on the device.</li><li><strong>Little celebrations.</strong> A quiet word when you finish one (how many today, days in a row), and the days-in-a-row count at the top. Off in Options.</li><li><strong>Options</strong> (always on screen, in a row under the bar; it slides sideways if the screen is narrow): Everyone&#39;s quests (admins), Little celebrations, Reminders on my phone, Show what&#39;s done, <strong>Opens in</strong> (Today, Focus, List or Board; Today unless you change it), Re-plan from now, Keyboard shortcuts.</li></ul>","text":"Quick add. Type in the box at the top and press Enter: “tomorrow 3pm call Sam !high #studio 30m”. Under the box you see what was understood before you add it. It understands: when : today, tonight, tomorrow, monday… (or mon, tue, wed, thu, fri; “on sat”, “on sun”), next friday, in 3 days, in 20 min, 14/10, 14 oct, 3pm, 15:00, at 9, noon, morning / afternoon / evening; finish by : by friday, by 5pm, due tomorrow; how long : 30m, 45 min, 1h, 1h30, 2 hours; priority : !low, !high, !critical (! or !! is high, !!! critical); tags : #studio #mix; repeats : daily, weekdays, weekly, every monday, every 30 min, every 2 hours. A day with no time means some time that day; Nova plans it into free time. The button beside Add opens the details first. Focus. One quest, big: Done , Start it (or 15 more minutes ), Not now (the next one) and Details . Its steps tick off right there. Underneath: what's next. List. Everything in plain groups: Now, Overdue, Today, Coming up, Any time, and Done (folded). Tick the circle to finish one (tick again to undo). Drag the dots on the left to put them in your own order (or Alt + ↑ ↓ from the keyboard): your order stays. Board. A column for each “how it's going” (Waiting, Soon, Working on it, Nearly finished, Done; Taking longer and Questions when they have something). Drag a card to another column, or tap its chip. Today. Today and the next week, hour by hour, and what hasn't got a time yet ( Plan them now fits them in). Details. Tap a quest: its name, when, finish by, how long, repeat, how it's going, priority, steps (tick, change, remove), tags, notes and where. Delete has Undo for a few seconds. Find. The magnifier (or / ): words in names, notes and steps, or #tag. The tag chips under the box show only that tag. Calm. The moon (or C ): fewer things on screen, less colour, nothing moving, at most five in a group and only today in Today. Remembered on the device. Little celebrations. A quiet word when you finish one (how many today, days in a row), and the days-in-a-row count at the top. Off in Options. Options (always on screen, in a row under the bar; it slides sideways if the screen is narrow): Everyone's quests (admins), Little celebrations, Reminders on my phone, Show what's done, Opens in (Today, Focus, List or Board; Today unless you change it), Re-plan from now, Keyboard shortcuts."},{"id":"keyboard-1","title":"Keyboard","html":"<p><strong>N</strong> or <strong>Ctrl+K</strong> add · <strong>/</strong> find · <strong>1 2 3 4</strong> Focus, List, Board, Today · <strong>C</strong> Calm · <strong>J K</strong> (or ↓ ↑) move between quests · <strong>X</strong> or <strong>Space</strong> done · <strong>E</strong> or <strong>Enter</strong> details · <strong>Alt+↑ ↓</strong> move in the list · <strong>Delete</strong> delete (with Undo) · <strong>?</strong> all of these · <strong>Esc</strong> close.</p>","text":"N or Ctrl+K add · / find · 1 2 3 4 Focus, List, Board, Today · C Calm · J K (or ↓ ↑) move between quests · X or Space done · E or Enter details · Alt+↑ ↓ move in the list · Delete delete (with Undo) · ? all of these · Esc close."},{"id":"for-everyone-2","title":"For everyone","html":"<p>Big buttons and tick circles, every button named for screen readers, and what changed said out loud (done, added, moved). Less motion when the device asks for it (or Calm), stronger edges when it asks for more contrast, and the system&#39;s colours in high-contrast mode.</p>","text":"Big buttons and tick circles, every button named for screen readers, and what changed said out loud (done, added, moved). Less motion when the device asks for it (or Calm), stronger edges when it asks for more contrast, and the system's colours in high-contrast mode."}],"built":[{"id":"how-it-works-0","title":"How it works","html":"<p>The page is <code>web/quests/</code> (<code>js/parse.js</code> reads quick add, <code>js/sort.js</code> groups and sorts, <code>js/quests.js</code> draws it). Its quests come from Nova Agent: <code>GET /quests/state</code> and <code>/quests/events</code> (live), and <code>POST /actions/quests</code>, <code>/actions/quests/</code> and <code>/actions/quests/order</code> (drag and drop) in <code>src/visualizer/server.ts</code>; online the same addresses go through Nova Bot&#39;s link. A quest keeps <code>steps</code>, <code>tags</code> and <code>order</code> for this panel (<code>src/quests/store.ts</code>). Tests: <code>test/quests-panel.spec.ts</code>.</p>","text":"The page is web/quests/ ( js/parse.js reads quick add, js/sort.js groups and sorts, js/quests.js draws it). Its quests come from Nova Agent: GET /quests/state and /quests/events (live), and POST /actions/quests , /actions/quests/ and /actions/quests/order (drag and drop) in src/visualizer/server.ts ; online the same addresses go through Nova Bot's link. A quest keeps steps , tags and order for this panel ( src/quests/store.ts ). Tests: test/quests-panel.spec.ts ."}],"news":[{"id":"what-s-new-0","title":"What's new","html":"<ul><li><strong>Nova Quests opens in Today</strong> (hour by hour) unless you choose another: the options row under the bar → <strong>Opens in</strong> Today, Focus, List or Board. Remembered on the device. Today&#39;s plan is no longer a separate icon in Plans: it&#39;s this view.</li><li><strong>Nova Quests is a panel of its own</strong>, in Nova Agent&#39;s Plans (and on the phone&#39;s bar): quick add in everyday words, Focus, List, Board and Today, steps, tags, drag to reorder, Calm, and keyboard shortcuts. Today&#39;s plan beside Nova Agent is still there (<strong>Today</strong> on the bar).</li></ul>","text":"Nova Quests opens in Today (hour by hour) unless you choose another: the options row under the bar → Opens in Today, Focus, List or Board. Remembered on the device. Today's plan is no longer a separate icon in Plans: it's this view. Nova Quests is a panel of its own , in Nova Agent's Plans (and on the phone's bar): quick add in everyday words, Focus, List, Board and Today, steps, tags, drag to reorder, Calm, and keyboard shortcuts. Today's plan beside Nova Agent is still there ( Today on the bar)."}],"history":{"total":6,"first":"2026-10-14T02:48:29+01:00","commits":[{"hash":"c3dc189","date":"2026-10-14T06:03:27+01:00","subject":"No menus hiding things: every place stays on the phone's bar (two rows: Apps on top, Plans, Tools and Helpers below, each group as wide as its places; More is gone), and Quests' options sit on screen in a row under its bar (the ⋯ menu is gone; it wraps on a computer and slides sideways inside itself on a phone)","body":""},{"hash":"0e275ec","date":"2026-10-14T05:47:48+01:00","subject":"One screen everywhere: inside Nova Agent no panel's page (or its <main>) scrolls; only a box inside it does. Portal's open section scrolls inside itself under compact lanes, Today side by side (numbers | today's calendar + new enquiries); Quests' groups and days as columns; Lossless's four cards in a row; the Visualizer's columns (two by two or stacked on phones, each scrolling inside); the Fixer's open tab under its numbers and tabs; Index's open view; Observatory's decks; Calendar's week, day and list scroll inside their own box and the month shares the screen with the day's plan on phones and tablets. Panels and Portal's sections show at once (no fade in). check-fit.mjs fails a page or a <main> that scrolls inside Nova Agent","body":""},{"hash":"8c00669","date":"2026-10-14T03:59:33+01:00","subject":"Quests inside Nova Agent: its name isn't shown twice under the shared top bar (still there for screen readers)","body":""},{"hash":"8e178e2","date":"2026-10-14T03:25:49+01:00","subject":"Quests opens in Today (hour by hour) unless changed: Options → Opens in Today, Focus, List or Board (remembered on the device; ?view= still picks one); switching views no longer changes where it opens","body":""},{"hash":"2ae52a2","date":"2026-10-14T03:05:10+01:00","subject":"Quests: the fit layer too, and in the fit check","body":""},{"hash":"b2822b3","date":"2026-10-14T02:48:29+01:00","subject":"Quests: a panel of its own (/quests/). Quick add in everyday words with a preview of what was understood; Focus (one thing now), List (Now, Overdue, Today, Coming up, Any time, Done), Board (by how it's going, drag between columns) and Today (hour by hour); steps, tags, drag to reorder (and Alt+arrows), delete with Undo, Calm, little celebrations, search and #tag filters, keyboard shortcuts. Quests keep steps, tags and their own order (POST /actions/quests/order). In Nova Agent's Plans and on the phone's bar; today's plan beside Agent stays (Today)","body":""}],"work":[],"workCount":0,"workStat":""}},{"id":"board","name":"Board","colour":"#5FD8BD","glyph":"▦","where":"A Nova Agent panel","links":[["Open Board","https://nova.novacane.co.uk/board/"]],"repo":"na","shared":"","tagline":"A table to lay things out on. Bring notes, a stretch of the calendar, Nova Agent's answers, question cards, sticky notes, pictures, files and links onto it, and move them around with the mouse (or a finger), like papers on a real table. Pin the ones that should stay put.","intro":"<p>A table to lay things out on. Bring notes, a stretch of the calendar, Nova Agent&#39;s answers, question cards, sticky notes, pictures, files and links onto it, and move them around with the mouse (or a finger), like papers on a real table. Pin the ones that should stay put.</p>","guide":[{"id":"what-it-does-0","title":"What it does","html":"<ul><li><strong>The table.</strong> Drag empty table to move around. The wheel (or a pinch) zooms in and out where the pointer is; Shift and the wheel moves sideways. The buttons at the top zoom too: <strong>−</strong>, <strong>100%</strong> (back to the middle), <strong>+</strong> and <strong>Show every card</strong>. With the table selected, the arrow keys move around, <strong>+</strong> and <strong>−</strong> zoom and <strong>0</strong> goes back to 100%.</li><li><strong>Cards.</strong> Drag a card to move it, its bottom-right corner to make it bigger or smaller. A card you touch comes to the front. Each lies at a slight angle, like paper (straight if your device asks for less motion).</li><li><strong>Pin.</strong> The pin at the top of a card keeps it where it is: it can&#39;t be dragged or resized until you unpin it. A pinned card shows a little pin head.</li><li><strong>Remove and put back.</strong> The <strong>×</strong> on a card removes it, with <strong>Undo</strong> for a few seconds; removed cards wait in the bin (top right) for a week, with <strong>Put back</strong>.</li><li><strong>Boards.</strong> Keep as many boards as you like (up to 50): pick one at the top left, rename it, make a new one, or delete one (press delete twice).</li></ul>","text":"The table. Drag empty table to move around. The wheel (or a pinch) zooms in and out where the pointer is; Shift and the wheel moves sideways. The buttons at the top zoom too: − , 100% (back to the middle), + and Show every card . With the table selected, the arrow keys move around, + and − zoom and 0 goes back to 100%. Cards. Drag a card to move it, its bottom-right corner to make it bigger or smaller. A card you touch comes to the front. Each lies at a slight angle, like paper (straight if your device asks for less motion). Pin. The pin at the top of a card keeps it where it is: it can't be dragged or resized until you unpin it. A pinned card shows a little pin head. Remove and put back. The × on a card removes it, with Undo for a few seconds; removed cards wait in the bin (top right) for a week, with Put back . Boards. Keep as many boards as you like (up to 50): pick one at the top left, rename it, make a new one, or delete one (press delete twice)."},{"id":"adding-things-1","title":"Adding things","html":"<ul><li><strong>Add</strong> (top): a <strong>Question card</strong> (a question and room for the answer), <strong>Ask Nova Agent</strong>, a <strong>Sticky note</strong> (six colours), <strong>Text</strong>, a <strong>Link</strong>, a <strong>Picture or file</strong>, or the calendar: <strong>a day</strong>, <strong>a week</strong>, <strong>a month</strong> or <strong>a year</strong>.</li><li><strong>Nova Notes, calendar &amp; Nova Agent</strong> (top): a drawer with</li><li class=\"sub\"><strong>Nova Notes</strong>: your notes (the shared ones and this device&#39;s), newest first, with a search box. A note card shows its title, the start of what it says, and when it was made and last changed. Double-click it (or press its open button) to open it in Nova Notes.</li><li class=\"sub\"><strong>Nova Calendar</strong>: today, tomorrow, this week, next week, this month, next month and this year. A calendar card lists what&#39;s on, day by day (a year card counts each month), with arrows to go back and forward.</li><li class=\"sub\"><strong>Nova Agent</strong>: what you&#39;ve asked Nova Agent before, with the answers. Drag one onto the table, or press it to put it in the middle.</li><li><strong>Ask Nova Agent</strong> cards: type a question and press <strong>Ask</strong> (or Enter). The answer appears on the card (and in your Nova Agent conversation). <strong>Ask something else</strong> clears it for a new question.</li><li><strong>From outside Nova Agent</strong>: drop a picture, a file, a link or some text from the desktop or another browser tab onto the table, or paste one (Ctrl+V) with nothing else selected. Links show their page&#39;s title, a line about it and its little icon. Pictures (JPEG, PNG, WebP, GIF), PDFs, text files, audio (MP3, WAV, M4A, OGG) and videos (MP4, WebM, MOV) can go on a board: up to 500 MB each straight to Nova Agent, 95 MB through Nova Bot (just under what Nova Bot can take in one go). A big one shows how far along it is. Videos play right on the card.</li></ul>","text":"Add (top): a Question card (a question and room for the answer), Ask Nova Agent , a Sticky note (six colours), Text , a Link , a Picture or file , or the calendar: a day , a week , a month or a year . Nova Notes, calendar & Nova Agent (top): a drawer with Nova Notes : your notes (the shared ones and this device's), newest first, with a search box. A note card shows its title, the start of what it says, and when it was made and last changed. Double-click it (or press its open button) to open it in Nova Notes. Nova Calendar : today, tomorrow, this week, next week, this month, next month and this year. A calendar card lists what's on, day by day (a year card counts each month), with arrows to go back and forward. Nova Agent : what you've asked Nova Agent before, with the answers. Drag one onto the table, or press it to put it in the middle. Ask Nova Agent cards: type a question and press Ask (or Enter). The answer appears on the card (and in your Nova Agent conversation). Ask something else clears it for a new question. From outside Nova Agent : drop a picture, a file, a link or some text from the desktop or another browser tab onto the table, or paste one (Ctrl+V) with nothing else selected. Links show their page's title, a line about it and its little icon. Pictures (JPEG, PNG, WebP, GIF), PDFs, text files, audio (MP3, WAV, M4A, OGG) and videos (MP4, WebM, MOV) can go on a board: up to 500 MB each straight to Nova Agent, 95 MB through Nova Bot (just under what Nova Bot can take in one go). A big one shows how far along it is. Videos play right on the card."},{"id":"the-welcome-board-2","title":"The Welcome board","html":"<p>The first time each person opens Board, they get a Welcome board (once, ever): a calm showcase of everything a board can hold, laid out on the table, with a banner at the bottom. <strong>Clear it and start</strong> empties it (it becomes &quot;My board&quot;); <strong>Keep it, start a new board</strong> keeps it as &quot;Welcome&quot; and opens a fresh board; <strong>Keep as is</strong> just hides the banner. Its video, picture and sound come with Board (<code>web/board/assets/welcome/</code>, made by <code>scripts/make-board-welcome.py</code>, nothing borrowed).</p>","text":"The first time each person opens Board, they get a Welcome board (once, ever): a calm showcase of everything a board can hold, laid out on the table, with a banner at the bottom. Clear it and start empties it (it becomes \"My board\"); Keep it, start a new board keeps it as \"Welcome\" and opens a fresh board; Keep as is just hides the banner. Its video, picture and sound come with Board ( web/board/assets/welcome/ , made by scripts/make-board-welcome.py , nothing borrowed)."},{"id":"the-keyboard-3","title":"The keyboard","html":"<p>With a card selected: the arrow keys move it (Shift for bigger steps), <strong>P</strong> pins or unpins it, <strong>Delete</strong> removes it and <strong>Enter</strong> goes into its text. Tab moves from card to card.</p>","text":"With a card selected: the arrow keys move it (Shift for bigger steps), P pins or unpins it, Delete removes it and Enter goes into its text. Tab moves from card to card."},{"id":"where-it-s-kept-4","title":"Where it's kept","html":"<p>Each person&#39;s own boards, on the VPS (<code>data/boards/.json</code>), saved a moment after every change. Pictures and files are kept beside them (<code>data/board-files/</code>), under names Nova Agent makes up, written to disk as they arrive. When Google is connected, Nova Agent also uploads each one to Google Drive&#39;s <strong>Nova Agent/Board</strong> folder itself (straight from disk, any size; files dropped while Google was off follow within the hour), and online Board shows them from there: quick, and parts on request (Range), so videos start at once. Without a Drive copy they come from the VPS through Nova Bot, as before; a file cut off part-way now shows <strong>Try again</strong> instead of half a picture. Your browser keeps a copy too, so a board opens straight away; if Nova Agent is ever unreachable, changes wait in the browser and save when it&#39;s back. Online, Board reaches Nova Agent through Nova Bot, for signed-in staff only. An admin can look at everyone&#39;s boards (<code>/board-api/boards?who=everyone</code>); changing a board is for its owner.</p>","text":"Each person's own boards, on the VPS ( data/boards/.json ), saved a moment after every change. Pictures and files are kept beside them ( data/board-files/ ), under names Nova Agent makes up, written to disk as they arrive. When Google is connected, Nova Agent also uploads each one to Google Drive's Nova Agent/Board folder itself (straight from disk, any size; files dropped while Google was off follow within the hour), and online Board shows them from there: quick, and parts on request (Range), so videos start at once. Without a Drive copy they come from the VPS through Nova Bot, as before; a file cut off part-way now shows Try again instead of half a picture. Your browser keeps a copy too, so a board opens straight away; if Nova Agent is ever unreachable, changes wait in the browser and save when it's back. Online, Board reaches Nova Agent through Nova Bot, for signed-in staff only. An admin can look at everyone's boards ( /board-api/boards?who=everyone ); changing a board is for its owner."}],"built":[{"id":"how-it-works-0","title":"How it works","html":"<ul><li><code>web/board/</code>: the page (<code>index.html</code>), its look (<code>css/board.css</code>, in the theme&#39;s colours) and the table (<code>js/board.js</code>).</li><li><code>src/board.ts</code>: each person&#39;s boards, every card checked and trimmed before it&#39;s saved.</li><li><code>src/board-files.ts</code>: pictures and files, behind a <code>BoardFileStore</code> so a store on the studio&#39;s VPS can take over later.</li><li><code>src/board-link.ts</code>: a link&#39;s title and icon, only from public web pages (addresses on this computer or the studio&#39;s network are refused, each redirect checked again).</li><li><code>src/board-routes.ts</code>: the addresses (<code>/board-api/…</code>, <code>/actions/board…</code>, <code>/board-files/…</code>), relayed online (<code>src/relay.ts</code> here, <code>src/agent-relay.js</code> in Nova Bot).</li></ul>","text":"web/board/ : the page ( index.html ), its look ( css/board.css , in the theme's colours) and the table ( js/board.js ). src/board.ts : each person's boards, every card checked and trimmed before it's saved. src/board-files.ts : pictures and files, behind a BoardFileStore so a store on the studio's VPS can take over later. src/board-link.ts : a link's title and icon, only from public web pages (addresses on this computer or the studio's network are refused, each redirect checked again). src/board-routes.ts : the addresses ( /board-api/… , /actions/board… , /board-files/… ), relayed online ( src/relay.ts here, src/agent-relay.js in Nova Bot)."},{"id":"tests-1","title":"Tests","html":"<p><code>test/board.spec.ts</code>: the Welcome board (once, every kind of card, its choices), big files saved as they arrive and refused part-way when too big, parts on request (Range), the limits here and online, each person&#39;s own boards, an admin looking at everyone&#39;s, a stale page told about a newer save, saving only from Nova Agent&#39;s pages, what a card may hold, pictures and files (type checks, made-up names), links only to public pages, and the relay&#39;s list. <code>node scripts/check-fit.mjs --only board</code> checks it fits from phones to 4K; <code>node scripts/check-board-welcome.mjs</code> opens the Welcome board in a browser (video playing, picture and sound ready, each choice) and puts a 6 MB video on the table (kept whole, a part back on request). Nova Bot&#39;s tests cover a 3 MB answer coming through the link byte for byte, a cut-off answer being an error, and Board files from Drive (whole and Range, signed-in staff only).</p>","text":"test/board.spec.ts : the Welcome board (once, every kind of card, its choices), big files saved as they arrive and refused part-way when too big, parts on request (Range), the limits here and online, each person's own boards, an admin looking at everyone's, a stale page told about a newer save, saving only from Nova Agent's pages, what a card may hold, pictures and files (type checks, made-up names), links only to public pages, and the relay's list. node scripts/check-fit.mjs --only board checks it fits from phones to 4K; node scripts/check-board-welcome.mjs opens the Welcome board in a browser (video playing, picture and sound ready, each choice) and puts a 6 MB video on the table (kept whole, a part back on request). Nova Bot's tests cover a 3 MB answer coming through the link byte for byte, a cut-off answer being an error, and Board files from Drive (whole and Range, signed-in staff only)."}],"news":[{"id":"what-s-new-0","title":"What's new","html":"<ul><li><strong>A Welcome board</strong> the first time you open Board: a looping video, a picture, a sound, a link, a pinned card, a sticky note, a question card, an Nova Agent answer, a note and this week&#39;s calendar, with little labels saying what to try. Then choose: <strong>Clear it and start</strong>, <strong>Keep it, start a new board</strong>, or <strong>Keep as is</strong>.</li><li><strong>Pictures and videos show online</strong> (from their copy in Google Drive: quick, and videos start straight away and can skip), with a calm shimmer while they come and <strong>Try again</strong> if one doesn&#39;t.</li><li><strong>Bigger files</strong>: up to 500 MB inside Nova Agent on the VPS&#39;s own address, 95 MB through Nova Bot. WebM and MOV videos and OGG sound too.</li><li>Board joins Nova Agent&#39;s Apps: a table for notes (with their times), the calendar (a day, week, month or year), Nova Agent&#39;s questions and answers, question cards, sticky notes, text, links, pictures and files, moved around with the mouse and pinned in place.</li></ul>","text":"A Welcome board the first time you open Board: a looping video, a picture, a sound, a link, a pinned card, a sticky note, a question card, an Nova Agent answer, a note and this week's calendar, with little labels saying what to try. Then choose: Clear it and start , Keep it, start a new board , or Keep as is . Pictures and videos show online (from their copy in Google Drive: quick, and videos start straight away and can skip), with a calm shimmer while they come and Try again if one doesn't. Bigger files : up to 500 MB inside Nova Agent on the VPS's own address, 95 MB through Nova Bot. WebM and MOV videos and OGG sound too. Board joins Nova Agent's Apps: a table for notes (with their times), the calendar (a day, week, month or year), Nova Agent's questions and answers, question cards, sticky notes, text, links, pictures and files, moved around with the mouse and pinned in place."}],"history":{"total":14,"first":"2026-10-13T10:38:45+01:00","commits":[{"hash":"3e5e306","date":"2026-10-14T06:14:02+01:00","subject":"Manual and READMEs: Nova Agent runs on the VPS (day and night, every laptop off), not on the studio PC; Quests' options and the Fixer's wide view described","body":""},{"hash":"3a49323","date":"2026-10-14T02:54:08+01:00","subject":"Fit on screen in every panel: /shared/fit.js + fit.css keep menus, pop-ups, tooltips, non-modal dialogs and anything marked data-fit (or handed over with NovaFit.keep) inside the screen — nudged back in just far enough, capped and scrolling inside only when bigger than the screen, checked again on resize, turning round, a phone's keyboard and growing content; Agent's activity list and the planet card hooked in. scripts/check-fit-all.sh runs the whole fit check (throwaway server, 360×640, 768×1024, 1440×900, the Manual) and check-fit.mjs now also proves the fit layer is on every page and works after the window shrinks","body":""},{"hash":"03067f3","date":"2026-10-13T11:37:25+01:00","subject":"Board docs and Manual: the Welcome board, media from Drive, bigger files","body":""},{"hash":"fa34c0a","date":"2026-10-13T11:35:33+01:00","subject":"WIP Board welcome: everything fits above the banner, labels that fit, video and sound cards say what they are; a check script for the welcome board and big files","body":""},{"hash":"ecc8f34","date":"2026-10-13T11:33:29+01:00","subject":"WIP Board page: the Welcome banner (clear it, keep it and start a new one, keep as is), media with a calm loading shimmer and Try again, hint labels, uploads with progress and the new limits","body":""},{"hash":"3f91d85","date":"2026-10-13T11:32:17+01:00","subject":"WIP Board: the Welcome board, given once to each person (a showcase of every kind of card)","body":""},{"hash":"640482f","date":"2026-10-13T11:31:12+01:00","subject":"WIP Board welcome media: a looping nebula and planet video, a still of it, a calm chime (made here, nothing borrowed)","body":""},{"hash":"d3b256b","date":"2026-10-13T11:28:41+01:00","subject":"WIP Board files: saved as they arrive (500 MB here, 95 MB online), parts on request (Range) so videos start at once, a copy in Google Drive for online, webm/mov/ogg too","body":""},{"hash":"412e437","date":"2026-10-13T11:02:10+01:00","subject":"Board: a table in Nova Agent's Apps for notes, the calendar, Agent's answers, question cards, stickies, links, pictures and files, moved with the mouse and pinned in place","body":""},{"hash":"e2f0ff6","date":"2026-10-13T11:00:12+01:00","subject":"WIP Board: tests (ownership, saving, cards, files, links, relay), one save at a time per board","body":""},{"hash":"41bbcd0","date":"2026-10-13T10:58:22+01:00","subject":"WIP Board: new cards find a free spot, hidden boxes stay hidden, the open board remembered, Board in the fit check","body":""},{"hash":"ffccbbc","date":"2026-10-13T10:44:34+01:00","subject":"WIP Board: the table, cards, dragging, pinning, dropping, the drawer and saving","body":""},{"hash":"fd44479","date":"2026-10-13T10:41:14+01:00","subject":"WIP Board: the page and its look","body":""},{"hash":"3bb5c49","date":"2026-10-13T10:38:45+01:00","subject":"WIP Board: boards, files and link previews kept on the PC, their addresses and relay rules","body":""}],"work":[],"workCount":0,"workStat":""}},{"id":"index","name":"Index","colour":"#5CFFC0","glyph":"≡","where":"A Nova Agent panel","links":[["Open Index","https://nova.novacane.co.uk/app/memory/"]],"repo":"na","shared":"","tagline":"Everything Nova Agent remembers, in one place.","intro":"<blockquote><strong>A Nova Agent panel.</strong> Its code is in <code>web/index/</code> in Nova Agent&#39;s repo, and it opens inside Nova Agent at <code>/app/memory/</code>. Online, Nova Bot serves it at the same address.</blockquote>\n<p>Browse it, watch it grow, fix a line, and say yes or no to what&#39;s been learned about customers.</p>\n<p>Every Nova app hands its conversations to one shared memory. A tiny set of tagged, one-line facts comes out, kept in small files by subject. Before replying, each app reads back only the few files that matter for that turn. Nova Index is the window onto that memory.</p>\n<blockquote>The test for every fact: <strong>&quot;Would this still be true and useful in three months?&quot;</strong> If not, it isn&#39;t kept.</blockquote>\n<p>All the pictures here use made-up files and people.</p>\n<p>Open a file, add a fact, save; then approve a fact learned from a customer chat.</p>","guide":[{"id":"what-it-does-0","title":"What it does","html":"<ul><li><strong>All at once on a wide screen.</strong> Inside Nova Agent on a computer (1200px wide or more), Browse, Live and Approve show together: the numbers along the top, Browse on the left, Live and Approve on the right, each scrolling inside itself, and no tabs along the bottom. Narrower, the tabs are back. The page itself never scrolls; the open view does, inside its own box.</li></ul>\n<h4>Browse</h4>\n<p>Studio, staff and customer files as cards, grouped by who they&#39;re about, with counts at the top (tap one to jump to it). The <strong>scope chips</strong> (All, Studio, Staff, Customers) narrow it down, and <strong>search</strong> looks through names, aliases, owners and descriptions, and inside the facts themselves: a card shows the line that matched, with your words lit up. <strong>+ New file</strong> starts one by hand.</p>\n<p>Search finds facts, not just file names. An open file: each fact with its tag pill, ready to edit.</p>\n<h4>Edit, safely</h4>\n<p>Open a file to change, add or delete a fact (and its tag), its description (the line the apps use to decide whether to read it) or its aliases. <strong>Save</strong> only goes through if nobody else has saved the file since you opened it. If someone has, you see both versions side by side, with the differences lit up, and can put your edit on top of theirs in one tap, or keep theirs.</p>\n<h4>Live and Approve</h4>\n<p>Live: what the suite just learned, and which app learned it. Approve: nothing about a customer is kept until someone says yes.</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Live</strong> shows what the suite has just learned, and which app learned it (NovaBot, Nova Agent, Nova Portal, Nova Index). It checks every 20 seconds while it&#39;s on screen, and anything new glows as it arrives. Tap a row to open the file.</li><li><strong>Approve</strong> holds facts learned from customers. One tap approves, edits or rejects each one. Nothing about a customer is kept without a person saying yes.</li><li><strong>Options</strong>: the theme (shared with Nova Portal), sound effects, refresh everything, open Nova Portal and sign out. It installs as an app, with the suite&#39;s cosmic &quot;I&quot;.</li></ul>\n<h4>Smart extras</h4>\n<ul><li><strong>Search that forgives.</strong> Typos are fine (&quot;evnings&quot;, &quot;pricnig&quot;), and so are other forms of a word (&quot;evenings&quot; finds &quot;evening&quot;). When nothing matches, Nova Index offers <strong>Did you mean …?</strong> with the closest words it knows.</li><li><strong>Filters</strong>, under the search: what kind of file (the studio, public facts, profiles, people, topics, areas), when it last changed (today, this week, this month, or 6+ months old), and <strong>★ Pinned</strong>. It shows how many files are left, with <strong>Clear filters</strong>.</li><li><strong>Ask Nova Index.</strong> Type a question (&quot;when does Kai like to record?&quot;) and press Enter, or tap <strong>✦ Ask Nova Index</strong>. The answer comes only from what&#39;s remembered, with numbered sources: tap one to open its file. A small, cheap AI writes the answer, and asking the same thing again is free until memory changes. Without a match it says so and asks no AI. It only reads: nothing is sent or saved. Each person only gets answers from what they&#39;re allowed to see (Nova Agent&#39;s key never reads customers&#39;).</li><li><strong>Pinned and recent.</strong> <strong>☆ Pin</strong> a file (at the foot of an open file) to keep it at the top of Browse; the files you open most lately are listed under it. Kept in this browser only.</li><li><strong>Related.</strong> An open file lists the other files about the same people and things.</li><li><strong>Hints.</strong> Files that might be the same person or subject (&quot;Kai&quot; and &quot;Kai M&quot;), and files that haven&#39;t changed in 6 months (<strong>Show them</strong>). <strong>✕</strong> puts a hint away.</li><li><strong>Keys.</strong> <strong>Ctrl+K</strong> (or <strong>/</strong>) jumps to the search from anywhere; <strong>↓</strong> goes to the first file, <strong>↑ ↓ Home End</strong> move between files, <strong>Enter</strong> opens one and <strong>Esc</strong> closes it (or clears the search).</li><li><strong>Approve:</strong> a fact learned in a website chat has <strong>Open the chat</strong>, to see what was said in Nova Portal.</li></ul>\n<p>The logic is in <code>web/index/smart.js</code> (tested on its own: <code>test/index-smart.spec.ts</code>); Ask Nova Index&#39;s answers come from Nova Bot (<code>src/memory/ask.js</code>, <code>POST /app/api/memory/ask</code>).</p>","text":"All at once on a wide screen. Inside Nova Agent on a computer (1200px wide or more), Browse, Live and Approve show together: the numbers along the top, Browse on the left, Live and Approve on the right, each scrolling inside itself, and no tabs along the bottom. Narrower, the tabs are back. The page itself never scrolls; the open view does, inside its own box. Browse Studio, staff and customer files as cards, grouped by who they're about, with counts at the top (tap one to jump to it). The scope chips (All, Studio, Staff, Customers) narrow it down, and search looks through names, aliases, owners and descriptions, and inside the facts themselves: a card shows the line that matched, with your words lit up. + New file starts one by hand. Search finds facts, not just file names. An open file: each fact with its tag pill, ready to edit. Edit, safely Open a file to change, add or delete a fact (and its tag), its description (the line the apps use to decide whether to read it) or its aliases. Save only goes through if nobody else has saved the file since you opened it. If someone has, you see both versions side by side, with the differences lit up, and can put your edit on top of theirs in one tap, or keep theirs. Live and Approve Live: what the suite just learned, and which app learned it. Approve: nothing about a customer is kept until someone says yes. Live shows what the suite has just learned, and which app learned it (NovaBot, Nova Agent, Nova Portal, Nova Index). It checks every 20 seconds while it's on screen, and anything new glows as it arrives. Tap a row to open the file. Approve holds facts learned from customers. One tap approves, edits or rejects each one. Nothing about a customer is kept without a person saying yes. Options : the theme (shared with Nova Portal), sound effects, refresh everything, open Nova Portal and sign out. It installs as an app, with the suite's cosmic \"I\". Smart extras Search that forgives. Typos are fine (\"evnings\", \"pricnig\"), and so are other forms of a word (\"evenings\" finds \"evening\"). When nothing matches, Nova Index offers Did you mean …? with the closest words it knows. Filters , under the search: what kind of file (the studio, public facts, profiles, people, topics, areas), when it last changed (today, this week, this month, or 6+ months old), and ★ Pinned . It shows how many files are left, with Clear filters . Ask Nova Index. Type a question (\"when does Kai like to record?\") and press Enter, or tap ✦ Ask Nova Index . The answer comes only from what's remembered, with numbered sources: tap one to open its file. A small, cheap AI writes the answer, and asking the same thing again is free until memory changes. Without a match it says so and asks no AI. It only reads: nothing is sent or saved. Each person only gets answers from what they're allowed to see (Nova Agent's key never reads customers'). Pinned and recent. ☆ Pin a file (at the foot of an open file) to keep it at the top of Browse; the files you open most lately are listed under it. Kept in this browser only. Related. An open file lists the other files about the same people and things. Hints. Files that might be the same person or subject (\"Kai\" and \"Kai M\"), and files that haven't changed in 6 months ( Show them ). ✕ puts a hint away. Keys. Ctrl+K (or / ) jumps to the search from anywhere; ↓ goes to the first file, ↑ ↓ Home End move between files, Enter opens one and Esc closes it (or clears the search). Approve: a fact learned in a website chat has Open the chat , to see what was said in Nova Portal. The logic is in web/index/smart.js (tested on its own: test/index-smart.spec.ts ); Ask Nova Index's answers come from Nova Bot ( src/memory/ask.js , POST /app/api/memory/ask )."}],"built":[{"id":"how-the-memory-works-0","title":"How the memory works","html":"<pre><code>- [stated]   said directly          &quot;prefers evening sessions&quot;\n- [observed] seen in what happened  &quot;usually books the Live Room&quot;\n- [inferred] a clear pattern        &quot;books in the run-up to releases&quot;</code></pre>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Scopes</strong></td><td><code>studio</code> (shared, including <code>public</code>, which customers may be told), <code>staff</code> (one set per staff member), <code>customer</code> (one set per client: their email, or a website chat until it&#39;s known)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Paths</strong></td><td><code>studio</code>, <code>public</code>, <code>profile</code>, <code>people/</code>, <code>topics/</code>, <code>areas/</code></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Learning</strong></td><td>In the background, so no reply ever waits. A small model pulls out only durable facts; each file is then rewritten with them folded in, never just added to. Files past about 3 KB are condensed. Card, bank and ID numbers are never kept.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Reading</strong></td><td>Each turn loads the studio file and the person&#39;s profile, plus at most three other files whose description or aliases match, within a budget of about 800 tokens</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Saving</strong></td><td>Every write carries the version it was based on; a clash returns the current file instead of overwriting it</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><strong>Who sees what</strong> is decided by the server, never by the app asking:</p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Who</th><th>What they can see</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Nova Agent (its key)</td><td>The studio&#39;s memory and staff memory; never customers&#39;</td></tr><tr><td>The website&#39;s NovaBot</td><td>Only that customer&#39;s own file and the public studio facts</td></tr><tr><td>Nova Portal and Nova Index, signed in</td><td>Everything, including approvals</td></tr><tr><td>Staff signed in with <a href=\"https://github.com/tuniveza/nova-portal\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Nova Portal</a></td><td>Staff who aren&#39;t admins: the studio&#39;s memory and their own; admins: everything</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>Nova Index signs in with <strong>Nova Portal</strong>, the suite&#39;s one sign-in (&quot;✦ Sign in with Nova Portal&quot;), so each person sees what&#39;s theirs to see.</p>\n<p>The memory engine runs on Nova Bot&#39;s worker (<code>src/memory/</code> in <a href=\"https://github.com/tuniveza/nova-bot\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">nova-bot</a>): the store, extraction and the API. The memories live in its database, never in git. The full design is in docs/spec.md.</p>","text":"- [stated] said directly \"prefers evening sessions\" - [observed] seen in what happened \"usually books the Live Room\" - [inferred] a clear pattern \"books in the run-up to releases\" Scopes studio (shared, including public , which customers may be told), staff (one set per staff member), customer (one set per client: their email, or a website chat until it's known) Paths studio , public , profile , people/ , topics/ , areas/ Learning In the background, so no reply ever waits. A small model pulls out only durable facts; each file is then rewritten with them folded in, never just added to. Files past about 3 KB are condensed. Card, bank and ID numbers are never kept. Reading Each turn loads the studio file and the person's profile, plus at most three other files whose description or aliases match, within a budget of about 800 tokens Saving Every write carries the version it was based on; a clash returns the current file instead of overwriting it Who sees what is decided by the server, never by the app asking: Who What they can see Nova Agent (its key) The studio's memory and staff memory; never customers' The website's NovaBot Only that customer's own file and the public studio facts Nova Portal and Nova Index, signed in Everything, including approvals Staff signed in with Nova Portal Staff who aren't admins: the studio's memory and their own; admins: everything Nova Index signs in with Nova Portal , the suite's one sign-in (\"✦ Sign in with Nova Portal\"), so each person sees what's theirs to see. The memory engine runs on Nova Bot's worker ( src/memory/ in nova-bot ): the store, extraction and the API. The memories live in its database, never in git. The full design is in docs/spec.md."}],"news":[],"history":{"total":32,"first":"2026-10-07T00:22:46+01:00","commits":[{"hash":"7d684d4","date":"2026-10-14T05:56:03+01:00","subject":"Index on a wide screen: Browse, Live and Approve all at once (numbers along the top, Browse left, Live and Approve right, each scrolling inside itself; no tabs needed); Live keeps updating while it's on screen; narrower, the tabs are back","body":""},{"hash":"0e275ec","date":"2026-10-14T05:47:48+01:00","subject":"One screen everywhere: inside Nova Agent no panel's page (or its <main>) scrolls; only a box inside it does. Portal's open section scrolls inside itself under compact lanes, Today side by side (numbers | today's calendar + new enquiries); Quests' groups and days as columns; Lossless's four cards in a row; the Visualizer's columns (two by two or stacked on phones, each scrolling inside); the Fixer's open tab under its numbers and tabs; Index's open view; Observatory's decks; Calendar's week, day and list scroll inside their own box and the month shares the screen with the day's plan on phones and tablets. Panels and Portal's sections show at once (no fade in). check-fit.mjs fails a page or a <main> that scrolls inside Nova Agent","body":""},{"hash":"b14adcc","date":"2026-10-14T03:12:29+01:00","subject":"One top bar for Nova Agent and every open panel (web/shared/topbar.css: the same capsule, height, corners, mark and name, in the same place and width), on phones too; the panels bar floats over an open panel and only slides (0.18 s in, 0.15 s away), so the panel never resizes or jumps: no room taken and given back, no trail, no tile ripple, nothing measured per move, no endless frame polling; scrolling down hides it with a mouse too; typing on the home no longer shifts the page; the one-row bar (tablet, phone on its side) shares its width by places and name lengths, so nothing is squeezed or cut. scripts/check-bars.mjs measures it","body":""},{"hash":"3a49323","date":"2026-10-14T02:54:08+01:00","subject":"Fit on screen in every panel: /shared/fit.js + fit.css keep menus, pop-ups, tooltips, non-modal dialogs and anything marked data-fit (or handed over with NovaFit.keep) inside the screen — nudged back in just far enough, capped and scrolling inside only when bigger than the screen, checked again on resize, turning round, a phone's keyboard and growing content; Agent's activity list and the planet card hooked in. scripts/check-fit-all.sh runs the whole fit check (throwaway server, 360×640, 768×1024, 1440×900, the Manual) and check-fit.mjs now also proves the fit layer is on every page and works after the window shrinks","body":""},{"hash":"76c86ec","date":"2026-10-14T02:42:59+01:00","subject":"Index gets smarter: search that forgives typos with Did you mean, filters (kind, when it changed, pinned), Ask Index with sources, pinned and recent files, related files, look-alike and old-file hints, Ctrl+K and arrow keys, Open the chat on Approve (logic in web/index/smart.js)","body":""},{"hash":"a23c9e9","date":"2026-10-13T22:54:11+01:00","subject":"Nova's own address in Nova Agent: nova.novacane.co.uk (the PC's link, links, the Manual); Computer talks about Nova's own computer","body":""},{"hash":"7de0a7e","date":"2026-10-11T04:45:11+01:00","subject":"Centred text in Index's header, Lossless meters and Observatory's header; themed tick boxes","body":"Index's name sits under its kicker, Lossless' meter names sit with their levels, Observatory's\nname, buttons and line sit in the middle. The Panels window's tick boxes wear the theme instead of\nthe browser's blue."},{"hash":"9b6c6e5","date":"2026-10-11T04:28:57+01:00","subject":"Plain names: no more \"every Nova app\" (it's all Nova Agent now)","body":"Portal's sign-in, profile, crew and invite wording, and Index's empty states, speak of Nova Agent\n(and Nova Bot) instead of separate Nova apps."},{"hash":"ce1ff1c","date":"2026-10-11T04:25:36+01:00","subject":"Dates and times written the British way, in London time, whatever the browser's language","body":"Calendar's mid-size day labels read \"19 Oct\" and \"19/10\" (not \"10month 19day\" and \"10 19\");\nthe status line's clock no longer follows the browser's language (\"So 5:04 am\"); Visualizer's\nstep times and every other date label say en-GB, Europe/London."},{"hash":"91d1fad","date":"2026-10-11T03:25:54+01:00","subject":"Plain app names again (only Nova Agent and Nova Bot keep Nova); titles on one surface; Portal's tabs wrap on tablets too","body":"Undoes the 'Nova <App>' renaming line by line (the ✦ marks, the tab bar and the scrollbars\nstay). Inside Nova Agent a shared rule kept Portal's tabs on one sliding row under 981px:\nfrom 761px they now wrap too, so every tab is on screen."},{"hash":"d6d2213","date":"2026-10-11T02:57:49+01:00","subject":"Nova first in every app name (the bottom bars keep their short labels)","body":"Nova Portal, Nova Agent, Nova Calendar, Nova Notes, Nova Index, Nova Quests, Nova Missions,\nNova Lossless, Nova Visualizer, Nova Observatory, Nova Manual: titles, headers, the Panels\nwindow, the status line, the Manual, manifests, messages and alerts. Also: the Nova mark's CSS on\nthe panel icons (chat.html), Portal's tab labels and tabbar.js, and the scrollbars link in each page."},{"hash":"e2b63d9","date":"2026-10-11T02:57:49+01:00","subject":"Icons: the same small Nova sparkle in the corner of every app's icon","body":""},{"hash":"95b9569","date":"2026-10-11T02:21:20+01:00","subject":"Themes: a colour spectrum with a Custom colour; one button look for every panel","body":"A spectrum of themes for all of Nova Agent (web/shared/spectrum.js): Crimson, Rose,\nCoral, Amber, Lime, Jade, Teal, Glacier, Indigo, Violet and Orchid join the old ones,\neach a hand-tuned set (deep sky, luminous accent, matching gradients and glows) whose\ntext reads at WCAG AA or better. Custom makes a whole theme from one hue and a\nvividness (OKLCH, so every hue is as readable as every other), remembered on the device\n(\"nova-look-custom\"). The pickers in the Panels window and Portal's and Index's Options\nshow every theme as an orb in rainbow order, then Custom with its two sliders; choosing\none, or moving a slider, recolours Nova Agent and every open panel straight away (look.js\nover storage events). Cosmic stays the default and looks the same; every old theme, id\nand the \"Each panel's own\" choice still work, and Portal's own theme can be any of them.\nOne button system (web/shared/butto"},{"hash":"b41ad38","date":"2026-10-11T01:42:03+01:00","subject":"P0-5 Index cleanup: Tidy up for admins, permission-aware editing, a confirm per fact","body":"- Options > Tidy up (admins only): Check now shows what would be removed (counts, examples,\n  reasons, which copy stays); a second press, Remove them, sends exactly that report's ids.\n  The 30-day bin lists removed entries with Put back, and who ran each cleanup.\n- Files a person may not change (studio-wide memory for non-admins) open read-only with a\n  calm note; deleting a fact asks in its own line first; save toasts say why lines were left\n  out; deleting a file says it can come back from the bin. A new file needs its first fact.\n- On the studio PC without a Portal sign-in, the cleanup routes are refused."},{"hash":"7099c0b","date":"2026-10-10T13:27:59+01:00","subject":"Portal everywhere: no more Portal (names, code, phone app, Manual)","body":"The staff app is Portal in every word: notifications, the voice command, the old phone app's\nname and icon (installed from /app/), code names (portalsync, window.PortalApp), comments, docs\nand the Manual (old commit notes are told with the new name). Settings saved under the old names\n(theme, options, music, alerts seen, hands-free) carry over once, so nothing resets."},{"hash":"263cf4f","date":"2026-10-09T02:31:27+01:00","subject":"Cosmic icons, one theme for everything, planet colours, smart top bar, status line","body":"Icons: a cosmic set, each with its own colour (mixed with the theme), sky and shape; Talk to\nNova Agent, Quests and Missions have their own. look.js: one theme for every panel (or each its\nown), and colour everything from your planet. Typing hides the panels bar. The top bar: Auto,\nAlways shown or Always hidden. The status line under the bar: Panels button (the top one is\ngone), version and build, what changed lately for the part of the bar you point at, on and off\ntimes, recent activity and a 12-hour clock. Lossless audio's sounds come along."},{"hash":"932c20c","date":"2026-10-08T16:59:59+01:00","subject":"Panels on phones: fit, lighter, less scrolling","body":"- Notes: one top bar (notes list, the note's name, Google Docs) and the menus;\n  the toolbar is one row you swipe, with the everyday tools (the rest stay in\n  the menus); 16px fields; no glass blur, grain or drifting background.\n- Observatory: a slim title, the numbers as a compact strip, each project as\n  one short row with a small drawn cover (no full-size screenshots on phones);\n  category chips in one row; no star map, no moving sky, no blur.\n- Calendar and Index: no glass blur or endless decorative motion on phones.\n- Lossless audio: snug margins, big buttons, 16px fields.\n- Visualizer: no error when the studio PC is off; fits a phone."},{"hash":"3b87ce8","date":"2026-10-08T02:16:18+01:00","subject":"Merge branch 'portal-merge' into sign-in","body":""},{"hash":"37073d2","date":"2026-10-08T02:15:25+01:00","subject":"One Portal: one staff app at /portal/","body":"Portal is gone as a separate panel. Portal is the one staff app: one header,\none tab bar with Portal's work tabs (Enquiries, Chats, Calendar, Quests,\nAlerts, NovaBot) plus You (your planet and profile; admins reach the crew\nand the admin pages from there). Portal's sign-in, setup and invite cards\nreplace Portal's old sign-in screen.\n- web/portal's scripts and styles move into web/portal (app.js, app.css,\n  ambient.js, options.js, suite.js). portal.js runs the page (who's signed\n  in, the address, the You tab) and starts the work tabs (window.NovaHub);\n  the tabs hand sign-outs back (window.PortalPage). Tabs follow the\n  address: /portal/?view=enquiries|chats|calendar|quests|alerts|bot|me|crew,\n  #nova opens Alerts, no ?view opens the starting tab from Options (which\n  can now be You). Tells the badge when sign-in changes (NovaPortal.changed).\n- portal.css is scoped to Portal's own parts (.pv) with p"},{"hash":"53332dc","date":"2026-10-08T02:04:14+01:00","subject":"Panels fit inside Nova Agent's viewer","body":"- While a panel is open, the panels strip shrinks to one row of small\n  switchers (services and admin as icons) and the viewer bar slims down:\n  the panel gets about 80px more height (431 → 511 at 1280×720). Only in\n  the side-by-side layout; stacked on a phone it's unchanged.\n- /shared/inside.js marks <html class=\"embed\"> when a panel is shown in a\n  frame (as Calendar's own embed.js already did), for frame-only fixes.\n- Notes in a frame: a slimmer two-row header (no kicker, smaller mark,\n  icon-only Import/Export/Google Docs below 1500px so the menus aren't\n  cut off), a tighter toolbar, and no word count in short frames. The\n  writing area goes from 215px to 377px tall at 1280×720.\n- Observatory in a frame: a smaller title block. Its stat numbers size to\n  their card (container units), so \"142,408\" no longer breaks in two.\n- Index in a frame: a slimmer tab bar."},{"hash":"326ecf9","date":"2026-10-08T01:33:59+01:00","subject":"Portal and Index: Portal is the one sign-in","body":"The shared-password box is gone from Portal's and Index's sign-in screens:\nsigned out, there's one button, to Portal, which brings you back to\n/app/ or /app/memory/ (not the old /studio/ and /index/). The guides\nand the Manual say the same."},{"hash":"100fb09","date":"2026-10-08T00:43:48+01:00","subject":"Plain names: everything is Nova Agent, and its panels are Portal, Portal, Calendar…","body":"Undoes the made-up names. \"Studio\" is Portal again and \"Crew\" is Portal again\n(only where the earlier rename had changed them; real uses of the words are\nkept). Every panel and feature drops \"Nova\": Portal, Portal, Calendar, Notes,\nIndex, Observatory, Missions, Quests and the Manual. \"Nova\" stays for Nova\nAgent itself, Nova Bot and Nova Club.\nThe original addresses are back: Portal at /app/, Portal at /portal/ and\nIndex at /app/memory/ (the panels live in web/portal, web/portal, web/index).\nNova Agent's own icons move to /agent/ to make room. /studio/, /crew/ and\n/index/ redirect, for anything that picked them up yesterday."},{"hash":"9aa754c","date":"2026-10-07T23:40:50+01:00","subject":"README: Nova Agent is the studio's one app, with its panels","body":"The README starts with what Nova Agent is now (every former Nova app as a\npanel, on the studio PC and online for phones), a table of the panels with\ntheir addresses and code, how signing in works on the PC, and the new\nproject layout. Each panel's guide in docs/apps/ loses its old repo's\nbadges, clone and deploy steps and suite tables, says where the panel\nlives, and its pictures point at the right place (every link checked).\nStudio's GIFs move here from Nova Bot. The Nova Manual is rebuilt."},{"hash":"4b86f1f","date":"2026-10-07T23:33:47+01:00","subject":"Portal is Studio, Nova Portal is Crew, and the suite is Nova Agent","body":"- Renamed everywhere in Nova Agent: the code, its page, the panels, the\n  docs and the chat's instructions. On phones, notifications and the\n  installed app say Nova Agent.\n- Nova Agent's launcher lists its panels (Chat, Studio, Crew, Calendar,\n  Notes, Index, Observatory, Lossless audio), which all open inside it from\n  this computer, and Services and admin (Nova Bot, the Visualizer, Admin,\n  All links, the code).\n- On the studio PC, Studio's sign-in is your own account (the shared studio\n  password field is hidden there).\nChecked in a browser on a test copy: every panel opens inside Nova Agent,\nand signed out, Studio and Crew show their sign-in."},{"hash":"d3b02ec","date":"2026-10-07T23:29:25+01:00","subject":"One copy of what the panels share; Studio at /studio/, Crew at /crew/, Index at /index/","body":"- web/shared: the themes, sounds, the Portal badge and the Nova Manual,\n  once, instead of a copy in every app (4-5 copies each before). Nova\n  Agent serves it at /shared/ and no longer fetches the themes from Nova\n  Bot.\n- Studio (was Portal) lives at /studio/, Crew (was Nova Portal) at\n  /crew/ and Index (was at /app/memory/) at /index/; every link between\n  them follows. /app/memory/ redirects. The worker API paths (/app/api,\n  /auth, /staff) are unchanged.\n- Calendar's and Notes' offline helpers no longer list the shared files."},{"hash":"fef653e","date":"2026-10-07T23:27:20+01:00","subject":"Panels laid out: Studio (was Portal), Crew (was Nova Portal), Index…","body":"- web/studio: Portal's staff app, now Nova Agent's Studio panel\n- web/crew: Nova Portal's app (sign-in, me, crew, invites), now the Crew\n  panel, with the planet avatar generator beside it\n- web/index, web/calendar, web/notes, web/observatory: the panels\n- Each app's README and pictures move to docs/apps/<panel>\n- The manual and badge scripts move to scripts/, and the Observatory's\n  scanning tools to scripts/observatory (npm run observatory:scan,\n  :capture, :build), writing into web/observatory as before\n- Calendar's and Notes' own deploy configs (their separate workers.dev\n  sites) are dropped: they're panels now\nPaths inside the panels are fixed up next."},{"hash":"d7b8800","date":"2026-10-07T23:23:36+01:00","subject":"Nova Agent takes in Nova Index (with its history), as web/index","body":"git-subtree-dir: web/index\ngit-subtree-mainline: 4ea063844af5a5cd7e39524bb794b0fc061b39a8\ngit-subtree-split: 7127214aa027363c9e126bc99b7068a143217074"},{"hash":"7127214","date":"2026-10-07T16:30:11+01:00","subject":"The Nova Manual, beside the badge","body":""},{"hash":"c7f1806","date":"2026-10-07T01:50:06+01:00","subject":"The Nova Portal badge in the top bar","body":""},{"hash":"4317639","date":"2026-10-07T01:35:40+01:00","subject":"Sign in with Nova Portal, and open straight to a file","body":"- \"✦ Sign in with Nova Portal\" on the sign-in screen\n- ?scope=&owner= open Browse on one person's or one scope's files\n- README: Portal sign-in is live"},{"hash":"5591755","date":"2026-10-07T01:33:23+01:00","subject":"README: Nova Index with screenshots and a walkthrough","body":"- Browse with the scope chips, an open file with tag pills, search finding a\n  fact, the conflict panel, Live and Approve, all with made-up files\n- A GIF: open a file, add a fact, save, then approve a customer's fact\n- Who sees what, including Nova Portal sign-in (coming): staff who aren't\n  admins see the studio's memory and their own; admins see everything\n- The build step is scripts/sync-apps.mjs"},{"hash":"d2de367","date":"2026-10-07T00:22:46+01:00","subject":"Nova Index: the Nova suite's memory, browsable","body":"Browse, edit and approve everything the Nova suite remembers: studio, staff\nand customer facts as small files of one-line facts, a live feed of what's\njust been learned, and the approval queue for customers' facts. Served by\nNova Bot's worker at /app/memory/ (with Portal's sign-in) and by Nova Agent."}],"work":[],"workCount":0,"workStat":""}},{"id":"observatory","name":"Observatory","colour":"#FFB86B","glyph":"✧","where":"A Nova Agent panel","links":[["Open Observatory","https://nova.novacane.co.uk/observatory/"]],"repo":"na","shared":"","tagline":"Every project in one sky: a dashboard that measures your work on disk and shows it in screenshots and video.","intro":"<blockquote><strong>A Nova Agent panel.</strong> Its code is in <code>web/observatory/</code> in Nova Agent&#39;s repo, and it opens inside Nova Agent at <code>/observatory/</code>.</blockquote>\n<p>Always on inside Nova Agent at /observatory/ · or open index.html anywhere</p>\n<p>Nova Observatory is a dashboard of everything being worked on. It&#39;s kept true by scanning the disk rather than by hand: one script measures every project, another opens each one in headless Chromium and records screenshots and a short demo video, and a static page shows the lot as project decks and a star map.</p>\n<p>The screenshots here come from the studio&#39;s own catalogue: Nova Agent, plus games, tools and experiments. They show project names, sizes and folder trees, and nothing personal.</p>","guide":[{"id":"what-it-does-0","title":"What it does","html":"<p>Each project gets a <strong>deck</strong> showing:</p>\n<ul><li>where it lives in the folder tree</li><li>its goal and vision, and what it does</li><li>its size on disk, project files, lines of code and languages</li><li>git state and last activity</li><li>screenshots and a demo video (or a generated cosmic cover)</li></ul>\n<p>And across all of them:</p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Totals</strong></td><td>Lines of code, project files, size on disk, files, languages and last activity, with a language bar</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Search, filter and sort</strong></td><td>By name, goal, stack or path; by category; by recent activity and more</td></tr><tr><td><strong>A detailed view</strong></td><td>Each project&#39;s video, screenshots, folder tree, languages and facts</td></tr><tr><td><strong>A star map</strong></td><td>The whole folder structure, with every project as a star sized by its lines of code</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Six colour themes</strong></td><td>Shared with <a href=\"https://github.com/tuniveza/nova-calendar\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Nova Calendar</a> and <a href=\"https://github.com/tuniveza/nova-notes\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Nova Notes</a></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Sound effects</strong></td><td>The shared Nova Agent sounds, with a switch in the header</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","text":"Each project gets a deck showing: where it lives in the folder tree its goal and vision, and what it does its size on disk, project files, lines of code and languages git state and last activity screenshots and a demo video (or a generated cosmic cover) And across all of them: Totals Lines of code, project files, size on disk, files, languages and last activity, with a language bar Search, filter and sort By name, goal, stack or path; by category; by recent activity and more A detailed view Each project's video, screenshots, folder tree, languages and facts A star map The whole folder structure, with every project as a star sized by its lines of code Six colour themes Shared with Nova Calendar and Nova Notes Sound effects The shared Nova Agent sounds, with a switch in the header"},{"id":"inside-nova-agent-1","title":"Inside Nova Agent","html":"<p><a href=\"https://github.com/tuniveza/nova-agent\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Nova Agent</a> serves this folder at <strong><code>/observatory/</code></strong> () whenever it&#39;s running, so the Nova Observatory is always on there with the latest scan. Nova Agent looks for it next to itself, in <code>../no</code>.</p>","text":"Nova Agent serves this folder at /observatory/ () whenever it's running, so the Nova Observatory is always on there with the latest scan. Nova Agent looks for it next to itself, in ../no ."},{"id":"sound-effects-2","title":"Sound effects","html":"<p>Every press makes a soft cosmic sound, made live with the Web Audio API (no sound files) and kept quiet. The <strong>Sound on / Sound off</strong> switch beside <strong>🔒 All links</strong> turns them off and on, plays a little chime when it does, and is remembered on each device. The same <code>js/sfx.js</code> makes the sounds in Nova Notes and Nova Calendar.</p>","text":"Every press makes a soft cosmic sound, made live with the Web Audio API (no sound files) and kept quiet. The Sound on / Sound off switch beside 🔒 All links turns them off and on, plays a little chime when it does, and is remembered on each device. The same js/sfx.js makes the sounds in Nova Notes and Nova Calendar."}],"built":[{"id":"how-it-works-0","title":"How it works","html":"<pre><code>flowchart LR\n    CFG[projects.config.json&lt;br/&gt;the catalogue] --&gt; SCAN[scan.mjs]\n    CFG --&gt; CAP[capture.mjs]\n    DISK[(your projects&lt;br/&gt;on disk)] --&gt; SCAN\n    DISK --&gt; CAP\n    CAP --&gt;|Playwright + ffmpeg| MEDIA[media/&amp;lt;id&amp;gt;/&lt;br/&gt;shots + video]\n    MEDIA --&gt; SCAN\n    SCAN --&gt; DATA[data/projects.js&lt;br/&gt;data/projects.json]\n    DATA --&gt; PAGE[index.html&lt;br/&gt;js/observatory.js]\n    MEDIA --&gt; PAGE\n    PAGE -.-&gt;|served at /observatory/| AGENT[Nova Agent]</code></pre>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>File</th><th>Job</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>projects.config.json</code></td><td>Your catalogue. It holds what a scan can&#39;t know: each project&#39;s name, goal, vision, features, category, theme, and how to show it. <strong>Add a project here.</strong> Git ignores it; start from <code>projects.config.example.json</code>.</td></tr><tr><td><code>scan.mjs</code></td><td>Measures each project on disk. Writes <code>data/projects.json</code> and <code>data/projects.js</code>.</td></tr><tr><td><code>capture.mjs</code></td><td>Drives headless Chromium (Playwright) and ffmpeg. Writes into <code>media//</code>.</td></tr><tr><td><code>index.html</code>, <code>css/</code>, <code>js/observatory.js</code></td><td>The page.</td></tr><tr><td><code>js/themes.js</code>, <code>js/cosmos.js</code>, <code>js/backdrop.js</code></td><td>Shared with Nova Calendar: the colour themes, the generative space covers and the star backdrop.</td></tr><tr><td><code>js/sfx.js</code></td><td>The Nova Agent sound effects, shared with Nova Notes and Nova Calendar.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><strong>What counts as what in a scan:</strong></p>\n<ul><li><strong>On disk</strong> is everything, from <code>du</code>.</li><li><strong>Project files</strong> and <strong>lines of code</strong> leave out:</li><li class=\"sub\">dependencies and build output: <code>node_modules</code>, <code>build*</code>, <code>dist</code>, <code>.gradle</code>, <code>.godot</code> and so on</li><li class=\"sub\">vendored third-party code: <code>lib</code>, <code>deps</code>, <code>glad</code>, <code>Libs</code>, <code>vendor</code>, <code>thirdparty</code></li><li class=\"sub\">anything listed under <code>exclude</code> in the catalogue, such as copied-in SDL or cglm headers</li><li>Lines are counted only for code. Markdown, JSON, XML and config files don&#39;t count.</li></ul>\n<h4>Capture</h4>\n<p><strong>Capture modes</strong> (<code>capture.mode</code> in the catalogue):</p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Mode</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>page</code></td><td>Opens the project in Chromium and plays a short scripted demo, recording the screen. The project can be opened as a file, from a local static server (<code>serve</code>, with optional <code>mounts</code>), from the project&#39;s own Vite (<code>vite: true</code>) or from a <code>url</code>. The demo scripts are in <code>capture.mjs</code> under <code>SCRIPTS</code>.</td></tr><tr><td><code>images</code></td><td>Turns pictures already in the project into a Ken Burns slideshow video.</td></tr><tr><td><code>none</code></td><td>Shows a generated cosmic cover instead.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><strong>Safety:</strong> during capture, every request that leaves the machine is blocked, except Google Fonts, and every non-GET request is blocked too. A demo can type into a chat widget, but nothing can reach a live service.</p>\n<p><strong>Private projects:</strong> projects marked <code>&quot;private&quot;: true</code> are skipped unless you pass <code>--include-private</code>. Use it for anything whose pages can show personal data (Nova Agent&#39;s visualizer can show client names, so it&#39;s marked private in the example).</p>","text":"flowchart LR CFG[projects.config.json<br/>the catalogue] --> SCAN[scan.mjs] CFG --> CAP[capture.mjs] DISK[(your projects<br/>on disk)] --> SCAN DISK --> CAP CAP -->|Playwright + ffmpeg| MEDIA[media/<id>/<br/>shots + video] MEDIA --> SCAN SCAN --> DATA[data/projects.js<br/>data/projects.json] DATA --> PAGE[index.html<br/>js/observatory.js] MEDIA --> PAGE PAGE -.->|served at /observatory/| AGENT[Nova Agent] File Job projects.config.json Your catalogue. It holds what a scan can't know: each project's name, goal, vision, features, category, theme, and how to show it. Add a project here. Git ignores it; start from projects.config.example.json . scan.mjs Measures each project on disk. Writes data/projects.json and data/projects.js . capture.mjs Drives headless Chromium (Playwright) and ffmpeg. Writes into media// . index.html , css/ , js/observatory.js The page. js/themes.js , js/cosmos.js , js/backdrop.js Shared with Nova Calendar: the colour themes, the generative space covers and the star backdrop. js/sfx.js The Nova Agent sound effects, shared with Nova Notes and Nova Calendar. What counts as what in a scan: On disk is everything, from du . Project files and lines of code leave out: dependencies and build output: node_modules , build* , dist , .gradle , .godot and so on vendored third-party code: lib , deps , glad , Libs , vendor , thirdparty anything listed under exclude in the catalogue, such as copied-in SDL or cglm headers Lines are counted only for code. Markdown, JSON, XML and config files don't count. Capture Capture modes ( capture.mode in the catalogue): Mode What it does page Opens the project in Chromium and plays a short scripted demo, recording the screen. The project can be opened as a file, from a local static server ( serve , with optional mounts ), from the project's own Vite ( vite: true ) or from a url . The demo scripts are in capture.mjs under SCRIPTS . images Turns pictures already in the project into a Ken Burns slideshow video. none Shows a generated cosmic cover instead. Safety: during capture, every request that leaves the machine is blocked, except Google Fonts, and every non-GET request is blocked too. A demo can type into a chat widget, but nothing can reach a live service. Private projects: projects marked \"private\": true are skipped unless you pass --include-private . Use it for anything whose pages can show personal data (Nova Agent's visualizer can show client names, so it's marked private in the example)."}],"news":[{"id":"what-s-new-0","title":"What's new","html":"<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>🪟 <strong>Everything at once</strong></td><td>On a computer (and a tablet standing up) the whole Nova Observatory fits the window: the decks on the left, the star map on the right, nothing to scroll around. The star map closes in on the stars and keeps their names readable at any size. Only if there are more decks than fit does the deck column scroll, inside itself.</td></tr><tr><td>🔔 <strong>Sound switch</strong></td><td>Soft cosmic sound effects on every press. The <strong>Sound on / Sound off</strong> switch beside All links turns them off and on.</td></tr><tr><td>🔒 <strong>All links</strong></td><td>A pill in the header that opens the password-protected page with every Nova Agent address, live and testing.</td></tr><tr><td>✦ <strong>Served by Nova Agent</strong></td><td>Nova Agent serves it at <code>/observatory/</code>, so it&#39;s always on while Nova Agent is.</td></tr><tr><td>🧠 <strong>Nova Index</strong></td><td>The suite&#39;s shared memory now has its own deck. Nova Portal may join it later.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","text":"🪟 Everything at once On a computer (and a tablet standing up) the whole Nova Observatory fits the window: the decks on the left, the star map on the right, nothing to scroll around. The star map closes in on the stars and keeps their names readable at any size. Only if there are more decks than fit does the deck column scroll, inside itself. 🔔 Sound switch Soft cosmic sound effects on every press. The Sound on / Sound off switch beside All links turns them off and on. 🔒 All links A pill in the header that opens the password-protected page with every Nova Agent address, live and testing. ✦ Served by Nova Agent Nova Agent serves it at /observatory/ , so it's always on while Nova Agent is. 🧠 Nova Index The suite's shared memory now has its own deck. Nova Portal may join it later."}],"history":{"total":37,"first":"2026-10-06T15:57:57+01:00","commits":[{"hash":"0e275ec","date":"2026-10-14T05:47:48+01:00","subject":"One screen everywhere: inside Nova Agent no panel's page (or its <main>) scrolls; only a box inside it does. Portal's open section scrolls inside itself under compact lanes, Today side by side (numbers | today's calendar + new enquiries); Quests' groups and days as columns; Lossless's four cards in a row; the Visualizer's columns (two by two or stacked on phones, each scrolling inside); the Fixer's open tab under its numbers and tabs; Index's open view; Observatory's decks; Calendar's week, day and list scroll inside their own box and the month shares the screen with the day's plan on phones and tablets. Panels and Portal's sections show at once (no fade in). check-fit.mjs fails a page or a <main> that scrolls inside Nova Agent","body":""},{"hash":"3a49323","date":"2026-10-14T02:54:08+01:00","subject":"Fit on screen in every panel: /shared/fit.js + fit.css keep menus, pop-ups, tooltips, non-modal dialogs and anything marked data-fit (or handed over with NovaFit.keep) inside the screen — nudged back in just far enough, capped and scrolling inside only when bigger than the screen, checked again on resize, turning round, a phone's keyboard and growing content; Agent's activity list and the planet card hooked in. scripts/check-fit-all.sh runs the whole fit check (throwaway server, 360×640, 768×1024, 1440×900, the Manual) and check-fit.mjs now also proves the fit layer is on every page and works after the window shrinks","body":""},{"hash":"a96223c","date":"2026-10-14T02:52:57+01:00","subject":"Calendar: one modern line-icon set (2px, round), icons that say what they are (booking = ticked calendar, quest = target, note card, ghost/flame/party/suitcase/flower for day kinds), birthdays and anniversaries win over food, tooltips and names on every icon button. Observatory: everything at once on computers and standing tablets (decks left on their side, star map right, filling the window; the map closes in on the stars and keeps names readable), phones one row shorter","body":""},{"hash":"8b1676e","date":"2026-10-14T01:23:54+01:00","subject":"All addresses: every web address in the suite in one list (Manual → All addresses; Portal → Settings → Addresses, and Apps and links), each with a plain line, Copy and Open; admins also see the ones other services use. Every link people see is https://nova.novacane.co.uk now (no studio-computer addresses in Portal, the Manual or the READMEs). scripts/check-addresses.mjs checks each one answers live","body":""},{"hash":"a23c9e9","date":"2026-10-13T22:54:11+01:00","subject":"Nova's own address in Nova Agent: nova.novacane.co.uk (the PC's link, links, the Manual); Computer talks about Nova's own computer","body":""},{"hash":"1f748b5","date":"2026-10-11T12:11:55+01:00","subject":"Everything fits: nothing hangs off the screen in any panel; what doesn't fit scrolls inside its own box","body":"scripts/check-fit.mjs opens Nova Agent's home and every panel (on its own and inside Nova Agent) at\n7 sizes (incl. a phone with its keyboard up) with long sample content, opens every sheet, dialog and\npop-up, and reports anything past the screen or its clipping box. Fixes what it found:\n- Portal: the side-menu tab row started off its left edge (tabs unreachable); Booking tools' picked\n  day was wider than the screen; a chat's Enquiry pill was clamped away; Options buttons squashed\n  their icon; a busy day's dots spilled out; long words wrap in views\n- Calendar: long words break inside cards; day cards no longer squashed; narrow short events clamp\n  their title to their height; What to show scrolls inside on short screens\n- Notes: menus and pop-ups scroll inside (and stay on screen) on short screens; snippets wrap\n- Nova Agent: chat action chips, mission summaries and file titles wrap; Ho"},{"hash":"7de0a7e","date":"2026-10-11T04:45:11+01:00","subject":"Centred text in Index's header, Lossless meters and Observatory's header; themed tick boxes","body":"Index's name sits under its kicker, Lossless' meter names sit with their levels, Observatory's\nname, buttons and line sit in the middle. The Panels window's tick boxes wear the theme instead of\nthe browser's blue."},{"hash":"ce1ff1c","date":"2026-10-11T04:25:36+01:00","subject":"Dates and times written the British way, in London time, whatever the browser's language","body":"Calendar's mid-size day labels read \"19 Oct\" and \"19/10\" (not \"10month 19day\" and \"10 19\");\nthe status line's clock no longer follows the browser's language (\"So 5:04 am\"); Visualizer's\nstep times and every other date label say en-GB, Europe/London."},{"hash":"91d1fad","date":"2026-10-11T03:25:54+01:00","subject":"Plain app names again (only Nova Agent and Nova Bot keep Nova); titles on one surface; Portal's tabs wrap on tablets too","body":"Undoes the 'Nova <App>' renaming line by line (the ✦ marks, the tab bar and the scrollbars\nstay). Inside Nova Agent a shared rule kept Portal's tabs on one sliding row under 981px:\nfrom 761px they now wrap too, so every tab is on screen."},{"hash":"beb626e","date":"2026-10-11T03:05:16+01:00","subject":"Merge branch 'tools-manual'","body":"# Conflicts:\n#\tweb/agent/page.html\n#\tweb/shared/manual.js"},{"hash":"e46ce40","date":"2026-10-11T03:04:28+01:00","subject":"Tools in the Nova Agent family: Lossless audio, the Visualizer and Observatory","body":"- web/shared/tools.css: the tools' shared look, all theme tokens (deep sky, glass cards with the\n  soft gradient edge, display-font headings, mono small-caps labels, boxes, menus, sliders,\n  switches, chips, meters, tables, fold-outs, empty and loading states)\n- Lossless audio: off its own light/grey palette onto themes.css + tools.css; cards for Room,\n  Live, Sound devices and The connection (two columns when wide, one on a phone); every id,\n  button and line of help kept\n- Visualizer: the same; glass header with the live light, the four numbers as tiles, each part\n  of the agent coloured from the theme; the hidden screenshot no longer draws a stray line\n- Observatory: \"All links\" and the sound switch are the shared glass pills (no inline style),\n  the empty note spans the page, Star map's heading sits over its line, no empty map frame,\n  the search box gets its own row on phones, hard-"},{"hash":"d6d2213","date":"2026-10-11T02:57:49+01:00","subject":"Nova first in every app name (the bottom bars keep their short labels)","body":"Nova Portal, Nova Agent, Nova Calendar, Nova Notes, Nova Index, Nova Quests, Nova Missions,\nNova Lossless, Nova Visualizer, Nova Observatory, Nova Manual: titles, headers, the Panels\nwindow, the status line, the Manual, manifests, messages and alerts. Also: the Nova mark's CSS on\nthe panel icons (chat.html), Portal's tab labels and tabbar.js, and the scrollbars link in each page."},{"hash":"e2b63d9","date":"2026-10-11T02:57:49+01:00","subject":"Icons: the same small Nova sparkle in the corner of every app's icon","body":""},{"hash":"95b9569","date":"2026-10-11T02:21:20+01:00","subject":"Themes: a colour spectrum with a Custom colour; one button look for every panel","body":"A spectrum of themes for all of Nova Agent (web/shared/spectrum.js): Crimson, Rose,\nCoral, Amber, Lime, Jade, Teal, Glacier, Indigo, Violet and Orchid join the old ones,\neach a hand-tuned set (deep sky, luminous accent, matching gradients and glows) whose\ntext reads at WCAG AA or better. Custom makes a whole theme from one hue and a\nvividness (OKLCH, so every hue is as readable as every other), remembered on the device\n(\"nova-look-custom\"). The pickers in the Panels window and Portal's and Index's Options\nshow every theme as an orb in rainbow order, then Custom with its two sliders; choosing\none, or moving a slider, recolours Nova Agent and every open panel straight away (look.js\nover storage events). Cosmic stays the default and looks the same; every old theme, id\nand the \"Each panel's own\" choice still work, and Portal's own theme can be any of them.\nOne button system (web/shared/butto"},{"hash":"7099c0b","date":"2026-10-10T13:27:59+01:00","subject":"Portal everywhere: no more Portal (names, code, phone app, Manual)","body":"The staff app is Portal in every word: notifications, the voice command, the old phone app's\nname and icon (installed from /app/), code names (portalsync, window.PortalApp), comments, docs\nand the Manual (old commit notes are told with the new name). Settings saved under the old names\n(theme, options, music, alerts seen, hands-free) carry over once, so nothing resets."},{"hash":"28ebf5d","date":"2026-10-10T02:44:33+01:00","subject":"Observatory: only the categories that have projects show as filters","body":""},{"hash":"ae32409","date":"2026-10-10T01:26:38+01:00","subject":"Observatory: more on screen, in Nova Agent's glass; Agent: \"Give me a goal\" sits last, by the box","body":"Observatory: the title, the six numbers and the links share one slim header (the colours and\nthe languages the next line), the search, filters and sort stay at the top as one row, and the\ndecks are tighter with a glowing glass edge, so a full row of decks shows straight away. Short\nwindows drop the summary line and the goal (both in each deck's details); phones get one small\nblock above the projects, with the numbers sliding sideways. Nothing removed.\nAgent's welcome: the suggestions, Today in music, then the hello (\"Give me a goal…\") at the\nbottom, next to where you type."},{"hash":"263cf4f","date":"2026-10-09T02:31:27+01:00","subject":"Cosmic icons, one theme for everything, planet colours, smart top bar, status line","body":"Icons: a cosmic set, each with its own colour (mixed with the theme), sky and shape; Talk to\nNova Agent, Quests and Missions have their own. look.js: one theme for every panel (or each its\nown), and colour everything from your planet. Typing hides the panels bar. The top bar: Auto,\nAlways shown or Always hidden. The status line under the bar: Panels button (the top one is\ngone), version and build, what changed lately for the part of the bar you point at, on and off\ntimes, recent activity and a 12-hour clock. Lossless audio's sounds come along."},{"hash":"932c20c","date":"2026-10-08T16:59:59+01:00","subject":"Panels on phones: fit, lighter, less scrolling","body":"- Notes: one top bar (notes list, the note's name, Google Docs) and the menus;\n  the toolbar is one row you swipe, with the everyday tools (the rest stay in\n  the menus); 16px fields; no glass blur, grain or drifting background.\n- Observatory: a slim title, the numbers as a compact strip, each project as\n  one short row with a small drawn cover (no full-size screenshots on phones);\n  category chips in one row; no star map, no moving sky, no blur.\n- Calendar and Index: no glass blur or endless decorative motion on phones.\n- Lossless audio: snug margins, big buttons, 16px fields.\n- Visualizer: no error when the studio PC is off; fits a phone."},{"hash":"0f31499","date":"2026-10-08T02:16:18+01:00","subject":"Merge branch 'live-fixes' into sign-in","body":""},{"hash":"8ac9531","date":"2026-10-08T02:04:26+01:00","subject":"Lossless audio and Observatory as panels everywhere; docs at the real addresses","body":"- Lossless audio is served by Nova Agent at /lossless/ and opens inside it like\n  the other panels. Signalling and the relay setup come from Nova Bot (which now\n  serves it online too), so the other device can be anywhere; invite links point\n  at the online address. /lossless/ice lets Nova Agent's own page ask.\n- Observatory online asks for a Portal sign-in before showing the projects\n  (Nova Bot keeps them for signed-in staff).\n- Calendar's and Notes' guides link to their addresses on Nova Bot, not the old\n  standalone sites."},{"hash":"53332dc","date":"2026-10-08T02:04:14+01:00","subject":"Panels fit inside Nova Agent's viewer","body":"- While a panel is open, the panels strip shrinks to one row of small\n  switchers (services and admin as icons) and the viewer bar slims down:\n  the panel gets about 80px more height (431 → 511 at 1280×720). Only in\n  the side-by-side layout; stacked on a phone it's unchanged.\n- /shared/inside.js marks <html class=\"embed\"> when a panel is shown in a\n  frame (as Calendar's own embed.js already did), for frame-only fixes.\n- Notes in a frame: a slimmer two-row header (no kicker, smaller mark,\n  icon-only Import/Export/Google Docs below 1500px so the menus aren't\n  cut off), a tighter toolbar, and no word count in short frames. The\n  writing area goes from 215px to 377px tall at 1280×720.\n- Observatory in a frame: a smaller title block. Its stat numbers size to\n  their card (container units), so \"142,408\" no longer breaks in two.\n- Index in a frame: a slimmer tab bar."},{"hash":"100fb09","date":"2026-10-08T00:43:48+01:00","subject":"Plain names: everything is Nova Agent, and its panels are Portal, Portal, Calendar…","body":"Undoes the made-up names. \"Studio\" is Portal again and \"Crew\" is Portal again\n(only where the earlier rename had changed them; real uses of the words are\nkept). Every panel and feature drops \"Nova\": Portal, Portal, Calendar, Notes,\nIndex, Observatory, Missions, Quests and the Manual. \"Nova\" stays for Nova\nAgent itself, Nova Bot and Nova Club.\nThe original addresses are back: Portal at /app/, Portal at /portal/ and\nIndex at /app/memory/ (the panels live in web/portal, web/portal, web/index).\nNova Agent's own icons move to /agent/ to make room. /studio/, /crew/ and\n/index/ redirect, for anything that picked them up yesterday."},{"hash":"9aa754c","date":"2026-10-07T23:40:50+01:00","subject":"README: Nova Agent is the studio's one app, with its panels","body":"The README starts with what Nova Agent is now (every former Nova app as a\npanel, on the studio PC and online for phones), a table of the panels with\ntheir addresses and code, how signing in works on the PC, and the new\nproject layout. Each panel's guide in docs/apps/ loses its old repo's\nbadges, clone and deploy steps and suite tables, says where the panel\nlives, and its pictures point at the right place (every link checked).\nStudio's GIFs move here from Nova Bot. The Nova Manual is rebuilt."},{"hash":"4b86f1f","date":"2026-10-07T23:33:47+01:00","subject":"Portal is Studio, Nova Portal is Crew, and the suite is Nova Agent","body":"- Renamed everywhere in Nova Agent: the code, its page, the panels, the\n  docs and the chat's instructions. On phones, notifications and the\n  installed app say Nova Agent.\n- Nova Agent's launcher lists its panels (Chat, Studio, Crew, Calendar,\n  Notes, Index, Observatory, Lossless audio), which all open inside it from\n  this computer, and Services and admin (Nova Bot, the Visualizer, Admin,\n  All links, the code).\n- On the studio PC, Studio's sign-in is your own account (the shared studio\n  password field is hidden there).\nChecked in a browser on a test copy: every panel opens inside Nova Agent,\nand signed out, Studio and Crew show their sign-in."},{"hash":"d3b02ec","date":"2026-10-07T23:29:25+01:00","subject":"One copy of what the panels share; Studio at /studio/, Crew at /crew/, Index at /index/","body":"- web/shared: the themes, sounds, the Portal badge and the Nova Manual,\n  once, instead of a copy in every app (4-5 copies each before). Nova\n  Agent serves it at /shared/ and no longer fetches the themes from Nova\n  Bot.\n- Studio (was Portal) lives at /studio/, Crew (was Nova Portal) at\n  /crew/ and Index (was at /app/memory/) at /index/; every link between\n  them follows. /app/memory/ redirects. The worker API paths (/app/api,\n  /auth, /staff) are unchanged.\n- Calendar's and Notes' offline helpers no longer list the shared files."},{"hash":"fef653e","date":"2026-10-07T23:27:20+01:00","subject":"Panels laid out: Studio (was Portal), Crew (was Nova Portal), Index…","body":"- web/studio: Portal's staff app, now Nova Agent's Studio panel\n- web/crew: Nova Portal's app (sign-in, me, crew, invites), now the Crew\n  panel, with the planet avatar generator beside it\n- web/index, web/calendar, web/notes, web/observatory: the panels\n- Each app's README and pictures move to docs/apps/<panel>\n- The manual and badge scripts move to scripts/, and the Observatory's\n  scanning tools to scripts/observatory (npm run observatory:scan,\n  :capture, :build), writing into web/observatory as before\n- Calendar's and Notes' own deploy configs (their separate workers.dev\n  sites) are dropped: they're panels now\nPaths inside the panels are fixed up next."},{"hash":"1ec177b","date":"2026-10-07T23:23:37+01:00","subject":"Nova Agent takes in Nova Observatory (with its history), as web/observatory","body":"git-subtree-dir: web/observatory\ngit-subtree-mainline: d7b88000c2e0a7ba290b081327d3c9a8353d21c9\ngit-subtree-split: 1687028b1bfb772362f663103dd72b017826eaa5"},{"hash":"1687028","date":"2026-10-07T16:31:21+01:00","subject":"The Nova Manual: refreshed with today's changes","body":""},{"hash":"79e928f","date":"2026-10-07T16:30:16+01:00","subject":"The Nova Manual, beside the badge","body":"js/nova-manual.js and its pages are copies from Nova Portal\n(scripts/build-manual.mjs there)."},{"hash":"1f5052f","date":"2026-10-07T02:01:05+01:00","subject":"Nova Portal badge: Connect as me in Nova Agent","body":""},{"hash":"ae149c8","date":"2026-10-07T01:50:13+01:00","subject":"The Nova Portal badge in the header","body":""},{"hash":"b173664","date":"2026-10-07T01:34:40+01:00","subject":"README: new screenshots, a tour GIF, the Sound switch and Nova Agent","body":"Fresh overview, decks, project detail, folder tree and star map\nscreenshots from the current scan (now with Nova Index), a GIF that\nscrolls the overview and opens a project, and notes on the Sound\nswitch, the All links pill and Nova Agent serving it at /observatory/."},{"hash":"4b6ec2b","date":"2026-10-06T23:10:48+01:00","subject":"Sound effects, with a Sound switch beside All links","body":""},{"hash":"97aab97","date":"2026-10-06T21:32:33+01:00","subject":"A locked link to every Nova suite address","body":""},{"hash":"0412651","date":"2026-10-06T18:23:25+01:00","subject":"Nova Task is now Nova Calendar","body":"Update the name and links to the renamed repo\n(https://github.com/tuniveza/nova-calendar)."},{"hash":"7afacab","date":"2026-10-06T15:57:57+01:00","subject":"Nova Observatory: every project in one sky","body":""}],"work":[],"workCount":0,"workStat":""}},{"id":"fixer","name":"Fixer","colour":"#B3F26B","glyph":"✦","where":"A Nova Agent panel, for admins","links":[["Open the Fixer","https://nova.novacane.co.uk/fixer/"]],"repo":"na","shared":"","tagline":"Nothing goes live until an admin taps Approve","intro":"<p>Nova Agent&#39;s caretaker. It checks Nova Agent every hour, keeps a list of what it found, takes fixer quests from admins, and prepares fixes with Claude Code. <strong>Nothing goes live until an admin taps Approve</strong>: every change, trivial ones included, waits for a person.</p>","guide":[{"id":"what-it-does-0","title":"What it does","html":"<ul><li><strong>Hourly check</strong> (scripted, no AI, so it costs nothing): Nova Agent&#39;s and Nova Bot&#39;s tests, Nova Agent&#39;s typecheck, a sweep of every panel at phone (390) and desktop (1280) width (script errors, console errors, files that don&#39;t load, sideways scrolling, buttons off the screen), and health: Nova Agent&#39;s server, the online link, Nova Bot, restarts, disk space and the data files. Once a day it also measures the sound levels against the calm rules.</li><li><strong>Problems</strong> are kept once each and cleared when they&#39;re gone. The same problem seen on several panels or widths is one problem that says where it was seen. Nova Bot not answering for a moment (or a file failing because of it) is checked again a few times before it counts. The admins&#39; phones get one calm ping for a new serious problem, and one when a fix is ready to look at. Never repeated.</li><li><strong>Fixer quests</strong>: an admin adds a bug, a glitch or a change, with its details and priority.</li><li><strong>Suggested</strong>: quests (from Nova Agent and Nova Notes) that look like work on Nova Agent itself. Tap <strong>Adopt</strong> to make one a fixer quest; nothing starts by itself.</li><li><strong>Preparing a fix</strong>: for a problem or a fixer quest (by itself for new problems, if that&#39;s on in Settings). One at a time, at most 10 a day, 30 minutes each. Each fix is made in its own copy of the code, then tested, typechecked and swept there, with pictures before and after.</li><li><strong>Needs you</strong>: the approval card says what changed and why, in plain English, shows the files and every line, the before and after pictures, what it means for you, whether it&#39;s a good idea (with the risks), and a recommendation. A tiny change to looks or wording is labelled <strong>Trivial — safe to approve</strong>. Tap <strong>Approve</strong>, <strong>Reject</strong>, or <strong>Ask for a tweak</strong> (your note goes with it and it&#39;s prepared again).</li><li><strong>Approve</strong> merges it, puts it live and checks again. If things got worse, the Fixer undoes it by itself and tells you: the only thing it ever does without a tap.</li><li><strong>Done</strong> lists what went live (with <strong>Undo</strong>), what was rejected and what couldn&#39;t be prepared. <strong>Activity</strong> is its diary.</li><li><strong>Looks</strong> (in Health): when the looks check last ran, how many screens it saw, and a picture of each one that didn&#39;t look right, with what was wrong. Tap a picture to see it big.</li><li><strong>Settings</strong>: hourly checks on or off, preparing fixes by itself on or off, looks checks on or off, how many a day, and how long each may take.</li></ul>","text":"Hourly check (scripted, no AI, so it costs nothing): Nova Agent's and Nova Bot's tests, Nova Agent's typecheck, a sweep of every panel at phone (390) and desktop (1280) width (script errors, console errors, files that don't load, sideways scrolling, buttons off the screen), and health: Nova Agent's server, the online link, Nova Bot, restarts, disk space and the data files. Once a day it also measures the sound levels against the calm rules. Problems are kept once each and cleared when they're gone. The same problem seen on several panels or widths is one problem that says where it was seen. Nova Bot not answering for a moment (or a file failing because of it) is checked again a few times before it counts. The admins' phones get one calm ping for a new serious problem, and one when a fix is ready to look at. Never repeated. Fixer quests : an admin adds a bug, a glitch or a change, with its details and priority. Suggested : quests (from Nova Agent and Nova Notes) that look like work on Nova Agent itself. Tap Adopt to make one a fixer quest; nothing starts by itself. Preparing a fix : for a problem or a fixer quest (by itself for new problems, if that's on in Settings). One at a time, at most 10 a day, 30 minutes each. Each fix is made in its own copy of the code, then tested, typechecked and swept there, with pictures before and after. Needs you : the approval card says what changed and why, in plain English, shows the files and every line, the before and after pictures, what it means for you, whether it's a good idea (with the risks), and a recommendation. A tiny change to looks or wording is labelled Trivial — safe to approve . Tap Approve , Reject , or Ask for a tweak (your note goes with it and it's prepared again). Approve merges it, puts it live and checks again. If things got worse, the Fixer undoes it by itself and tells you: the only thing it ever does without a tap. Done lists what went live (with Undo ), what was rejected and what couldn't be prepared. Activity is its diary. Looks (in Health): when the looks check last ran, how many screens it saw, and a picture of each one that didn't look right, with what was wrong. Tap a picture to see it big. Settings : hourly checks on or off, preparing fixes by itself on or off, looks checks on or off, how many a day, and how long each may take."},{"id":"inside-nova-agent-1","title":"Inside Nova Agent","html":"<p>The Fixer is in the Panels window and on the bar, under Tools. It&#39;s for admins: sign in to Nova Portal as an admin. The Fixer runs on the VPS with Nova Agent, so it keeps checking with every laptop off.</p>","text":"The Fixer is in the Panels window and on the bar, under Tools. It's for admins: sign in to Nova Portal as an admin. The Fixer runs on the VPS with Nova Agent, so it keeps checking with every laptop off."}],"built":[{"id":"how-it-works-0","title":"How it works","html":"<ul><li>The sweep only looks: every request its browser makes to Nova Agent carries the <code>x-nova-fixer-sweep</code> header, and Nova Agent&#39;s server turns away anything that would change something (<code>src/fixer/sweep-guard.ts</code>).</li><li>The looks check: <code>src/fixer/looks.ts</code> measures each screen inside the page (where the content is, top to bottom; the bars; the panel&#39;s frame) and judges it with plain rules; <code>scripts/fixer-looks.ts</code> runs it as its own process, with low priority (<code>nice</code>), one browser and one page at a time. Its browser answers every write itself (&quot;the Fixer&#39;s check only looks&quot;), opens no WebSockets and runs no service worker. Signed in, it uses Nova Bot&#39;s looks account (<code>POST /nova-agent/looks-session</code>, Nova Agent&#39;s key; Nova Bot&#39;s <code>src/looks-account.js</code>): no password, a 45-minute session, deleted after the check, refused for anything but looking, and left out of the team list. The token goes to the check in its environment, never on a command line or in a log. After each update: the live pages&#39; <code>X-Nova-Build</code> changes, and a few minutes later the check runs.</li><li><code>src/fixer/fixer.ts</code> is the Fixer itself; <code>rules.ts</code> is its judgement (what&#39;s off limits, what&#39;s trivial, when to undo, what looks like Nova Agent work); <code>store.ts</code> keeps <code>data/fixer.json</code>; <code>sweep.ts</code> is the browser sweep; <code>health.ts</code> the health check; <code>claude.ts</code> how Claude Code is asked; <code>routes.ts</code> its addresses; <code>service.ts</code> the schedule.</li><li>Claude Code runs headless and confined: <code>claude -p --restricted --tools Read,Glob,Grep,Edit,Write,Bash --allowedTools Read Glob Grep Edit Write &quot;Bash(npx vitest run)&quot; &quot;Bash(npx vitest run:*)&quot; &quot;Bash(npx tsc --noEmit)&quot; --permission-mode acceptEdits --permission-prompts none --add-dir  --strict-mcp-config</code>, never with a skip-all-permissions flag, never with Nova Agent&#39;s keys. It doesn&#39;t run git: the Fixer commits its edits by name on the job&#39;s own branch, after checking nothing off limits was touched (secrets, migrations, data, payments, emails, Acuity, the deploy setup, the Fixer itself).</li><li>Going live is locked in code: only an Approve tap makes the approval that merging and deploying need.</li><li><code>FIXER_DRY=1</code> makes it inert (checks can run; nothing is prepared, merged or deployed). <code>FIXER_NA_DIR</code>, <code>FIXER_NB_DIR</code>, <code>FIXER_RELEASE_DIR</code>, <code>FIXER_JOBS_DIR</code> and <code>FIXER_CLAUDE</code> say where things are.</li></ul>","text":"The sweep only looks: every request its browser makes to Nova Agent carries the x-nova-fixer-sweep header, and Nova Agent's server turns away anything that would change something ( src/fixer/sweep-guard.ts ). The looks check: src/fixer/looks.ts measures each screen inside the page (where the content is, top to bottom; the bars; the panel's frame) and judges it with plain rules; scripts/fixer-looks.ts runs it as its own process, with low priority ( nice ), one browser and one page at a time. Its browser answers every write itself (\"the Fixer's check only looks\"), opens no WebSockets and runs no service worker. Signed in, it uses Nova Bot's looks account ( POST /nova-agent/looks-session , Nova Agent's key; Nova Bot's src/looks-account.js ): no password, a 45-minute session, deleted after the check, refused for anything but looking, and left out of the team list. The token goes to the check in its environment, never on a command line or in a log. After each update: the live pages' X-Nova-Build changes, and a few minutes later the check runs. src/fixer/fixer.ts is the Fixer itself; rules.ts is its judgement (what's off limits, what's trivial, when to undo, what looks like Nova Agent work); store.ts keeps data/fixer.json ; sweep.ts is the browser sweep; health.ts the health check; claude.ts how Claude Code is asked; routes.ts its addresses; service.ts the schedule. Claude Code runs headless and confined: claude -p --restricted --tools Read,Glob,Grep,Edit,Write,Bash --allowedTools Read Glob Grep Edit Write \"Bash(npx vitest run)\" \"Bash(npx vitest run:*)\" \"Bash(npx tsc --noEmit)\" --permission-mode acceptEdits --permission-prompts none --add-dir --strict-mcp-config , never with a skip-all-permissions flag, never with Nova Agent's keys. It doesn't run git: the Fixer commits its edits by name on the job's own branch, after checking nothing off limits was touched (secrets, migrations, data, payments, emails, Acuity, the deploy setup, the Fixer itself). Going live is locked in code: only an Approve tap makes the approval that merging and deploying need. FIXER_DRY=1 makes it inert (checks can run; nothing is prepared, merged or deployed). FIXER_NA_DIR , FIXER_NB_DIR , FIXER_RELEASE_DIR , FIXER_JOBS_DIR and FIXER_CLAUDE say where things are."},{"id":"tests-1","title":"Tests","html":"<p><code>test/fixer.spec.ts</code>: one problem wherever it&#39;s seen, closing fixes whose problem has gone, Nova Bot blips, nothing merges or deploys without Approve (every kind of change, trivial included), when it undoes by itself, the trivial label, suggestions, one job at a time and the daily cap, settings, admin-only addresses, and old or damaged <code>fixer.json</code> files. <code>test/fixer-sweep-guard.spec.ts</code>: a real sweep of a page that tries to save can&#39;t make shared notes, calendar items or quests. <code>test/fixer-looks.spec.ts</code>: real pages in a browser: the Nova Index gap of 14 October (an empty box on top, its header and numbers low) is caught, an ordinary empty state and a centred sign-in card aren&#39;t, blank panels, gaps, bars covering a panel, unused space, scrolling and cut-off pages, cut-off text; one problem per panel and kind. The looks part of <code>test/fixer.spec.ts</code>: problems with pictures, a ping, a fix looked at again where it was seen with before and after, and still nothing goes live without Approve. Nova Bot&#39;s <code>test/looks-account.spec.js</code>: only Nova Agent&#39;s key makes the account, it can only look, it isn&#39;t listed, and it&#39;s gone after.</p>","text":"test/fixer.spec.ts : one problem wherever it's seen, closing fixes whose problem has gone, Nova Bot blips, nothing merges or deploys without Approve (every kind of change, trivial included), when it undoes by itself, the trivial label, suggestions, one job at a time and the daily cap, settings, admin-only addresses, and old or damaged fixer.json files. test/fixer-sweep-guard.spec.ts : a real sweep of a page that tries to save can't make shared notes, calendar items or quests. test/fixer-looks.spec.ts : real pages in a browser: the Nova Index gap of 14 October (an empty box on top, its header and numbers low) is caught, an ordinary empty state and a centred sign-in card aren't, blank panels, gaps, bars covering a panel, unused space, scrolling and cut-off pages, cut-off text; one problem per panel and kind. The looks part of test/fixer.spec.ts : problems with pictures, a ping, a fix looked at again where it was seen with before and after, and still nothing goes live without Approve. Nova Bot's test/looks-account.spec.js : only Nova Agent's key makes the account, it can only look, it isn't listed, and it's gone after."}],"news":[{"id":"what-s-new-0","title":"What's new","html":"<ul><li><strong>Looks</strong>: the Fixer now checks how everything LOOKS, the way you see it. Every hour and a few minutes after each update, it opens Nova Agent and every panel inside it, signed in and signed out, at six sizes (360×740, 390×844, 1024×768, 1440×900, 1512×1500 and 2000×1130). It looks for big empty gaps, blank panels, a panel&#39;s header sitting low, the title panel or navigation panel covering a panel, more than one title panel, pages that scroll or are cut off at the bottom, buttons off the screen, cut-off text, errors and slow panels. Each problem comes with a picture and says every size it was seen at; a fix for it is looked at again at those sizes, with the before and after side by side. <strong>Check looks now</strong> is in Health; it can be switched off in Settings.</li><li>The looks check only looks: it signs in as a built-in test account that Nova Bot makes for that one check and deletes after. The account has no password and Nova Bot lets it do nothing but look (no emails, posts, bookings, approvals or saves), and the check&#39;s own browser stops anything that would change something before it leaves.</li><li>When Claude Code isn&#39;t signed in on the server, the Fixer says so at the top (&quot;Sign Claude Code in to let me prepare fixes&quot;); checks still run and report.</li><li>Everything at once on a wide screen: Needs you down the left, Health, Fixer quests and Suggested along the top, Done, Activity and Settings below, each scrolling inside itself. No tabs (on a phone the parts are still one at a time, behind the tabs).</li><li>One problem, wherever it&#39;s seen: a file that didn&#39;t load on Nova Notes, Nova Index and Nova Observatory is one problem (&quot;· on Nova Notes, Nova Index and Nova Observatory at 390px&quot;) with one fix, not three.</li><li>A fix whose problem has gone by itself (fixed another way) is closed, instead of sitting &quot;blocked&quot;.</li><li>No false alarms when Nova Bot blips: Nova Bot not answering, or a file failing with 502/503/504, is checked again (3 tries over about 2 minutes) before it counts, and never has a fix prepared.</li><li>The sweep only looks: its browser can&#39;t make notes, calendar items, quests or anything else (it once made 16 &quot;Welcome to Nova Notes&quot; notes).</li><li>The Fixer joins Nova Agent: hourly checks, fixer quests, suggestions from Nova Quests and Nova Notes, approval cards with before and after pictures, and Undo.</li></ul>","text":"Looks : the Fixer now checks how everything LOOKS, the way you see it. Every hour and a few minutes after each update, it opens Nova Agent and every panel inside it, signed in and signed out, at six sizes (360×740, 390×844, 1024×768, 1440×900, 1512×1500 and 2000×1130). It looks for big empty gaps, blank panels, a panel's header sitting low, the title panel or navigation panel covering a panel, more than one title panel, pages that scroll or are cut off at the bottom, buttons off the screen, cut-off text, errors and slow panels. Each problem comes with a picture and says every size it was seen at; a fix for it is looked at again at those sizes, with the before and after side by side. Check looks now is in Health; it can be switched off in Settings. The looks check only looks: it signs in as a built-in test account that Nova Bot makes for that one check and deletes after. The account has no password and Nova Bot lets it do nothing but look (no emails, posts, bookings, approvals or saves), and the check's own browser stops anything that would change something before it leaves. When Claude Code isn't signed in on the server, the Fixer says so at the top (\"Sign Claude Code in to let me prepare fixes\"); checks still run and report. Everything at once on a wide screen: Needs you down the left, Health, Fixer quests and Suggested along the top, Done, Activity and Settings below, each scrolling inside itself. No tabs (on a phone the parts are still one at a time, behind the tabs). One problem, wherever it's seen: a file that didn't load on Nova Notes, Nova Index and Nova Observatory is one problem (\"· on Nova Notes, Nova Index and Nova Observatory at 390px\") with one fix, not three. A fix whose problem has gone by itself (fixed another way) is closed, instead of sitting \"blocked\". No false alarms when Nova Bot blips: Nova Bot not answering, or a file failing with 502/503/504, is checked again (3 tries over about 2 minutes) before it counts, and never has a fix prepared. The sweep only looks: its browser can't make notes, calendar items, quests or anything else (it once made 16 \"Welcome to Nova Notes\" notes). The Fixer joins Nova Agent: hourly checks, fixer quests, suggestions from Nova Quests and Nova Notes, approval cards with before and after pictures, and Undo."}],"history":{"total":14,"first":"2026-10-11T11:50:32+01:00","commits":[{"hash":"97eddb3","date":"2026-10-14T12:48:01+01:00","subject":"Fixer looks: a problem seen only signed out is looked at signed out in the fix's copy too (no sample sign-in), so its before and after show the same screen","body":""},{"hash":"d1b4525","date":"2026-10-14T12:29:05+01:00","subject":"Fixer: the looks check. Every hour and after each update it opens Nova Agent and every panel inside it, signed in (Nova Bot's looks account, which can only look) and signed out, at six sizes, and finds big empty gaps, blank panels, low headers, bars covering a panel, extra title panels, scrolling or cut-off pages, cut-off text, errors and slow panels; each a problem with pictures, and a fix for one is looked at again where it was seen, before and after side by side (still waits for Approve). Check looks now in Health, a switch in Settings, and a note when Claude Code isn't signed in. The sweep's layout checks run again (esbuild's __name helper in the page)","body":""},{"hash":"400d081","date":"2026-10-14T07:17:56+01:00","subject":"Fixer's wide view: switch rows start at the left, so a long one never pokes out of its part","body":""},{"hash":"3e5e306","date":"2026-10-14T06:14:02+01:00","subject":"Manual and READMEs: Nova Agent runs on the VPS (day and night, every laptop off), not on the studio PC; Quests' options and the Fixer's wide view described","body":""},{"hash":"0f35d15","date":"2026-10-14T06:05:13+01:00","subject":"Fixer on a wide screen: all seven parts at once, no tabs (Needs you down the left; Health, Fixer quests and Suggested along the top; Done, Activity and Settings below; each scrolls inside itself); the numbers and Check now in one row; phones keep the tabs","body":""},{"hash":"0e275ec","date":"2026-10-14T05:47:48+01:00","subject":"One screen everywhere: inside Nova Agent no panel's page (or its <main>) scrolls; only a box inside it does. Portal's open section scrolls inside itself under compact lanes, Today side by side (numbers | today's calendar + new enquiries); Quests' groups and days as columns; Lossless's four cards in a row; the Visualizer's columns (two by two or stacked on phones, each scrolling inside); the Fixer's open tab under its numbers and tabs; Index's open view; Observatory's decks; Calendar's week, day and list scroll inside their own box and the month shares the screen with the day's plan on phones and tablets. Panels and Portal's sections show at once (no fade in). check-fit.mjs fails a page or a <main> that scrolls inside Nova Agent","body":""},{"hash":"3a49323","date":"2026-10-14T02:54:08+01:00","subject":"Fit on screen in every panel: /shared/fit.js + fit.css keep menus, pop-ups, tooltips, non-modal dialogs and anything marked data-fit (or handed over with NovaFit.keep) inside the screen — nudged back in just far enough, capped and scrolling inside only when bigger than the screen, checked again on resize, turning round, a phone's keyboard and growing content; Agent's activity list and the planet card hooked in. scripts/check-fit-all.sh runs the whole fit check (throwaway server, 360×640, 768×1024, 1440×900, the Manual) and check-fit.mjs now also proves the fit layer is on every page and works after the window shrinks","body":""},{"hash":"dc26b62","date":"2026-10-14T02:40:34+01:00","subject":"Fixer: scripted checks (no AI) with every hourly check and on their own (Health → Run the quick checks): every address, Nova Agent's pages and data, the status page's parts, bookings, the server's services, timed jobs, backup, memory, load and mail queue, SPF/DKIM/DMARC, the database, the Manual's links; grouped pass/fail with why; server fails are told, never prepared; the sweep also covers Board and Console. Online link: a watcher restarts a stuck attempt, and a hello/here check redoes a link Nova Bot lost","body":""},{"hash":"01bcb95","date":"2026-10-14T01:17:34+01:00","subject":"Campaigns sent by the studio's own mail server: Resend gone from Agent, Portal, the Fixer's rules and the docs","body":"Portal shows a campaign going out (Sending · n of m) and own-server results (sent, unsubscribed,\ndidn't go); Agent's campaign summaries say the same."},{"hash":"a98c163","date":"2026-10-13T23:51:38+01:00","subject":"Nova Agent on the server: NOVA_ON_SERVER mode, only one Nova Agent runs (link says where; PC stands down on 4002 and stays off by marker), Console + Shell is the server's shell (ssh tunnel), Fixer restarts nova-agent.service and checks Claude Code's sign-in, watchdog becomes a self-watch","body":""},{"hash":"d9f82f5","date":"2026-10-13T22:49:12+01:00","subject":"Fixer: put fixes live with vps/deploy-live.sh, wherever Nova Bot is live (a plain wrangler deploy would undo the switch-over)","body":""},{"hash":"731432a","date":"2026-10-12T19:16:25+01:00","subject":"Fixer: one problem wherever it's seen, fixes closed when their problem's gone, no alarms for Nova Bot blips, the sweep only looks","body":"- The same file/script/console problem on several panels or widths is one issue (and one fix) saying where it was seen; older per-place issues carry on as the grouped one\n- A queued, ready, failed or blocked fix whose problem has gone is closed\n- Nova Bot not answering / 502-504 / dropped connections are checked again (3 tries over ~2 minutes) before they count, and never get a fix prepared\n- The sweep's browser marks its requests (x-nova-fixer-sweep) and Nova Agent's server turns away its writes, so it can't make shared notes, calendar items or quests"},{"hash":"59b8b8a","date":"2026-10-11T12:32:24+01:00","subject":"Fit check covers the Fixer; its screenshot box keeps its ✕ inside","body":""},{"hash":"a756a95","date":"2026-10-11T11:50:32+01:00","subject":"The Fixer: hourly checks, fixer quests and suggestions, fixes prepared by Claude Code that wait for an admin's Approve","body":"- src/fixer: checks (tests, typecheck, a sweep of every panel at 390 and 1280, health; audio daily),\n  issues by fingerprint, one job at a time with a daily cap and time limit, each in its own worktree,\n  Claude Code headless and restricted, approval cards with before/after pictures\n- Nothing merges or deploys without Approve: only approve() mints the approval land() needs;\n  undoing a change that made things worse is the only thing it does by itself\n- Admin-only routes (PC page, or online admins through the relay); FIXER_DRY=1 makes it inert\n- web/fixer: the Fixer app; its tile in Tools and the Panels window; a Manual chapter"}],"work":[],"workCount":0,"workStat":""}},{"id":"console","name":"Console","colour":"#FF8CC6","glyph":"›","where":"A Nova Agent panel (Tools); terminals through a private connection","links":[["Open Console","https://nova.novacane.co.uk/console/"]],"repo":"na","shared":"","tagline":"Tools","intro":"<p>Console is in Nova Agent&#39;s <strong>Tools</strong>. Type commands for the whole of Nova Agent instead of clicking. On the computer Nova Agent runs on (the VPS), admins can also open a real terminal there, or one on another server.</p>","guide":[{"id":"the-nova-tab-0","title":"The Nova tab","html":"<p>Type a command and press Enter, or tap one in the row of commands above (Today, Now, Nova Quests, Nova Calendar, Nova Notes, Boards, Enquiries, Clients, Money, Social, Approvals, Google, Computer, Search…, Ask Nova Agent…, Help, Clear). <strong>Tab</strong> finishes a word, and <strong>↑ ↓</strong> go back through what you typed. Type <strong>help</strong> for every command in groups (Start here, Plans, Apps, Studio, Tools, Server, Admin, Console), each with what it does and an example, or <strong>help quests</strong> for one. A typo gets a &quot;Did you mean …?&quot;, and some other words work too (<code>inbox</code>, <code>tasks</code>, <code>cal</code>, <code>server</code>, <code>find</code>, <code>terminal</code>, <code>ssh</code>…).</p>\n<p>Everything is centred and easy to read: Console sits in a centred column, with bigger text, headings in the theme&#39;s colours, lined-up tables, and help with the command in pink and its example in green. On a phone, help stacks each command over what it does.</p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>What happens</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>today</code></td><td>Your day at a glance: now and next, quests, the calendar, new or open enquiries</td></tr><tr><td><code>status</code></td><td>How Nova Agent is doing: live or not, the online link, quests, and whether terminals can open here</td></tr><tr><td><code>search </code></td><td>Looks through quests, the calendar, boards, notes, Nova Index and enquiries at once</td></tr><tr><td><code>whoami</code> / <code>version</code></td><td>Who&#39;s signed in; which version of Nova Agent this is</td></tr><tr><td><code>now</code> (or <code>plans</code>)</td><td>What&#39;s on now and what&#39;s next</td></tr><tr><td><code>quests</code></td><td>Your quests. Also: <code>quests add &quot;Mix the EP&quot; --minutes 45</code>, then <code>quests start</code>, <code>done</code>, <code>skip</code> or <code>snooze </code>. The first 8 letters of an id are enough</td></tr><tr><td><code>missions</code></td><td>Your missions. Also: <code>missions new &quot;Release the EP by December&quot;</code> and <code>missions show </code></td></tr><tr><td><code>calendar today</code> / <code>calendar week</code></td><td>What&#39;s on the calendar. Also: <code>calendar add &quot;Engineer in&quot; 2026-10-20 14:00</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>notes</code></td><td>Your shared notes. Also: <code>notes open </code> and <code>notes new</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>board</code></td><td>Your boards. Also: <code>board open</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>enquiries</code>, <code>chats</code>, <code>clients</code>, <code>money</code>, <code>campaigns</code>, <code>outreach</code>, <code>social</code>, <code>approvals</code>, <code>alerts</code>, <code>tests</code></td><td>One of Nova Portal&#39;s sections (the same as <code>portal enquiries</code> and so on)</td></tr><tr><td><code>approve campaign 12</code></td><td>Approve something waiting (admins). It shows exactly what will go, then you type its number back to say yes. Anything else cancels. Also: <code>reject …</code>. Works for campaign, outreach, social, invoice, reminder and booking</td></tr><tr><td><code>google</code></td><td>Google&#39;s status. Also: <code>google sync contacts</code> (admins)</td></tr><tr><td><code>fixer</code></td><td>The Fixer (admins): <code>fixer check</code> and <code>fixer jobs</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>lossless</code></td><td>Opens Nova Lossless audio</td></tr><tr><td><code>music on</code> / <code>off</code> / <code>next</code> / <code>seed</code></td><td>The ambient music</td></tr><tr><td><code>theme list</code> / <code>theme pulsar</code> / <code>theme own</code></td><td>The look</td></tr><tr><td><code>open </code></td><td>Opens an app or panel: portal, calendar, notes, board, index, lossless, visualizer, observatory, fixer, agent, quests, missions, manual</td></tr><tr><td><code>agent &quot;what&#39;s on today?&quot;</code> (or <code>ask</code>)</td><td>Asks Nova Agent, and shows the answer here</td></tr><tr><td><code>computer</code> (or <code>desk</code>)</td><td>The VPS: Nova Bot and Nova Agent, versions, Nova Agent&#39;s link, VPS memory, disk, services, last data copy and backup, the timed jobs (admins)</td></tr><tr><td><code>deploy status</code></td><td>What&#39;s live where: Nova Bot and Nova Agent on the VPS</td></tr><tr><td><code>backup</code></td><td>Backs up the VPS&#39;s database now (admins; asks you to type yes first)</td></tr><tr><td><code>admin crew</code></td><td>Everyone on the crew (admins). Also: <code>admin invite</code> and <code>admin pages</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>index search </code></td><td>Searches what Nova knows</td></tr><tr><td><code>logs</code></td><td>Nova Agent&#39;s recent log (admins)</td></tr><tr><td><code>shell</code></td><td>A terminal on the computer Nova Agent runs on (admins, on that computer only)</td></tr><tr><td><code>vps</code></td><td>The VPSdime server (admins, on the computer Nova Agent runs on only): <code>vps set   [port]</code>, <code>vps setup-key</code>, <code>vps show</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>Every command does exactly what you could do with the mouse as yourself, and nothing more. Nothing is sent, posted, booked or approved without a person typing the item&#39;s number back. Nova Agent can&#39;t use Console.</p>","text":"Type a command and press Enter, or tap one in the row of commands above (Today, Now, Nova Quests, Nova Calendar, Nova Notes, Boards, Enquiries, Clients, Money, Social, Approvals, Google, Computer, Search…, Ask Nova Agent…, Help, Clear). Tab finishes a word, and ↑ ↓ go back through what you typed. Type help for every command in groups (Start here, Plans, Apps, Studio, Tools, Server, Admin, Console), each with what it does and an example, or help quests for one. A typo gets a \"Did you mean …?\", and some other words work too ( inbox , tasks , cal , server , find , terminal , ssh …). Everything is centred and easy to read: Console sits in a centred column, with bigger text, headings in the theme's colours, lined-up tables, and help with the command in pink and its example in green. On a phone, help stacks each command over what it does. Type What happens today Your day at a glance: now and next, quests, the calendar, new or open enquiries status How Nova Agent is doing: live or not, the online link, quests, and whether terminals can open here search Looks through quests, the calendar, boards, notes, Nova Index and enquiries at once whoami / version Who's signed in; which version of Nova Agent this is now (or plans ) What's on now and what's next quests Your quests. Also: quests add \"Mix the EP\" --minutes 45 , then quests start , done , skip or snooze . The first 8 letters of an id are enough missions Your missions. Also: missions new \"Release the EP by December\" and missions show calendar today / calendar week What's on the calendar. Also: calendar add \"Engineer in\" 2026-10-20 14:00 notes Your shared notes. Also: notes open and notes new board Your boards. Also: board open enquiries , chats , clients , money , campaigns , outreach , social , approvals , alerts , tests One of Nova Portal's sections (the same as portal enquiries and so on) approve campaign 12 Approve something waiting (admins). It shows exactly what will go, then you type its number back to say yes. Anything else cancels. Also: reject … . Works for campaign, outreach, social, invoice, reminder and booking google Google's status. Also: google sync contacts (admins) fixer The Fixer (admins): fixer check and fixer jobs lossless Opens Nova Lossless audio music on / off / next / seed The ambient music theme list / theme pulsar / theme own The look open Opens an app or panel: portal, calendar, notes, board, index, lossless, visualizer, observatory, fixer, agent, quests, missions, manual agent \"what's on today?\" (or ask ) Asks Nova Agent, and shows the answer here computer (or desk ) The VPS: Nova Bot and Nova Agent, versions, Nova Agent's link, VPS memory, disk, services, last data copy and backup, the timed jobs (admins) deploy status What's live where: Nova Bot and Nova Agent on the VPS backup Backs up the VPS's database now (admins; asks you to type yes first) admin crew Everyone on the crew (admins). Also: admin invite and admin pages index search Searches what Nova knows logs Nova Agent's recent log (admins) shell A terminal on the computer Nova Agent runs on (admins, on that computer only) vps The VPSdime server (admins, on the computer Nova Agent runs on only): vps set [port] , vps setup-key , vps show Every command does exactly what you could do with the mouse as yourself, and nothing more. Nothing is sent, posted, booked or approved without a person typing the item's number back. Nova Agent can't use Console."},{"id":"terminals-nova-agent-s-computer-and-another-server-1","title":"Terminals: Nova Agent's computer and another server","html":"<p><strong>+ Shell</strong> opens a terminal on the computer Nova Agent runs on (the VPS). <strong>+ VPS</strong> opens one on the VPSdime server, using ssh with the computer&#39;s own key (<code>~/.ssh/id_ed25519</code>). Each opens in its own tab. Copy, paste, scrolling back and resizing all work. If the page reloads, its terminals are still there.</p>\n<p>Terminals only open when all of these are true:</p>\n<ul><li>Console is opened on the computer Nova Agent runs on (at <code>localhost</code>).</li><li>You&#39;re an admin.</li><li>The request comes from Console&#39;s own page.</li></ul>\n<p>Online, through Nova Bot, they&#39;re always refused, and Nova Bot never passes them on. Only Nova commands work online. Instead, Console online shows an <strong>Open Console on this computer</strong> button: on the computer Nova Agent runs on it opens <code>http://localhost:4545/console/?here=1</code>, Console on its own page on the computer itself, where <strong>+ Shell</strong> and <strong>+ VPS</strong> work. (Nova Agent&#39;s pages normally move to Nova Agent online; this one address stays on the computer, for the terminals.)</p>\n<h4>The VPS</h4>\n<p>The VPS is already set: the studio&#39;s VPSdime server, <code>root@185.185.126.195</code> (port 22), and the laptop&#39;s key is already on it, so <strong>+ VPS</strong> connects straight away. To use another server: <code>vps set   [port]</code> (saved by Nova Agent in <code>data/console.json</code>; no password is ever saved), then <code>vps setup-key</code> once (it asks for that server&#39;s password inside the terminal and copies Nova Agent&#39;s computer&#39;s key there).</p>","text":"+ Shell opens a terminal on the computer Nova Agent runs on (the VPS). + VPS opens one on the VPSdime server, using ssh with the computer's own key ( ~/.ssh/id_ed25519 ). Each opens in its own tab. Copy, paste, scrolling back and resizing all work. If the page reloads, its terminals are still there. Terminals only open when all of these are true: Console is opened on the computer Nova Agent runs on (at localhost ). You're an admin. The request comes from Console's own page. Online, through Nova Bot, they're always refused, and Nova Bot never passes them on. Only Nova commands work online. Instead, Console online shows an Open Console on this computer button: on the computer Nova Agent runs on it opens http://localhost:4545/console/?here=1 , Console on its own page on the computer itself, where + Shell and + VPS work. (Nova Agent's pages normally move to Nova Agent online; this one address stays on the computer, for the terminals.) The VPS The VPS is already set: the studio's VPSdime server, root@185.185.126.195 (port 22), and the laptop's key is already on it, so + VPS connects straight away. To use another server: vps set [port] (saved by Nova Agent in data/console.json ; no password is ever saved), then vps setup-key once (it asks for that server's password inside the terminal and copies Nova Agent's computer's key there)."},{"id":"on-a-phone-2","title":"On a phone","html":"<p>A row of extra keys sits under the terminal: Tab, Ctrl, Esc, the arrows, <code>|</code>, <code>~</code> and <code>/</code>. Tap <strong>Ctrl</strong>, then a letter, for Ctrl+letter. <strong>A−</strong> and <strong>A+</strong> change the text size. Your choice is remembered on this device.</p>","text":"A row of extra keys sits under the terminal: Tab, Ctrl, Esc, the arrows, | , ~ and / . Tap Ctrl , then a letter, for Ctrl+letter. A− and A+ change the text size. Your choice is remembered on this device."},{"id":"how-it-s-built-3","title":"How it's built","html":"<ul><li><code>web/console/</code>: the page. It uses xterm.js 6 (copied into <code>web/console/vendor/</code>, nothing from the internet) with the theme&#39;s colours.</li><li class=\"sub\"><code>js/commands.js</code>: the command language.</li><li class=\"sub\"><code>js/console.js</code>: the tabs, the typing line and the terminals.</li><li><code>src/console.ts</code>: Nova Agent&#39;s side. Terminals run through node-pty, and their output comes back as server-sent events. Each terminal has a random token. One that nobody watches closes after 15 minutes. Nova Agent&#39;s own secret settings are left out of the terminal&#39;s environment.</li><li><code>src/relay.ts</code> and Nova Bot&#39;s <code>src/agent-relay.js</code> only pass on <code>GET /console-api/state</code> (everyone) and <code>/console-api/logs</code> (admins).</li><li>node-pty has a native part. After <code>npm install</code>, build it once with <code>npm install-scripts approve node-pty &amp;&amp; npm rebuild node-pty</code>, or <code>cd node_modules/node-pty &amp;&amp; npx node-gyp rebuild</code>. Without it, Nova commands still work and terminals say what&#39;s missing.</li><li>Checks:</li><li class=\"sub\"><code>test/console.spec.ts</code></li><li class=\"sub\"><code>node scripts/check-console.mjs http://localhost:4545</code>, a click-through</li><li class=\"sub\"><code>node scripts/check-fit.mjs … --only console</code></li></ul>","text":"web/console/ : the page. It uses xterm.js 6 (copied into web/console/vendor/ , nothing from the internet) with the theme's colours. js/commands.js : the command language. js/console.js : the tabs, the typing line and the terminals. src/console.ts : Nova Agent's side. Terminals run through node-pty, and their output comes back as server-sent events. Each terminal has a random token. One that nobody watches closes after 15 minutes. Nova Agent's own secret settings are left out of the terminal's environment. src/relay.ts and Nova Bot's src/agent-relay.js only pass on GET /console-api/state (everyone) and /console-api/logs (admins). node-pty has a native part. After npm install , build it once with npm install-scripts approve node-pty && npm rebuild node-pty , or cd node_modules/node-pty && npx node-gyp rebuild . Without it, Nova commands still work and terminals say what's missing. Checks: test/console.spec.ts node scripts/check-console.mjs http://localhost:4545 , a click-through node scripts/check-fit.mjs … --only console"}],"built":[],"news":[],"history":{"total":19,"first":"2026-10-13T11:33:36+01:00","commits":[{"hash":"3e5e306","date":"2026-10-14T06:14:02+01:00","subject":"Manual and READMEs: Nova Agent runs on the VPS (day and night, every laptop off), not on the studio PC; Quests' options and the Fixer's wide view described","body":""},{"hash":"3a49323","date":"2026-10-14T02:54:08+01:00","subject":"Fit on screen in every panel: /shared/fit.js + fit.css keep menus, pop-ups, tooltips, non-modal dialogs and anything marked data-fit (or handed over with NovaFit.keep) inside the screen — nudged back in just far enough, capped and scrolling inside only when bigger than the screen, checked again on resize, turning round, a phone's keyboard and growing content; Agent's activity list and the planet card hooked in. scripts/check-fit-all.sh runs the whole fit check (throwaway server, 360×640, 768×1024, 1440×900, the Manual) and check-fit.mjs now also proves the fit layer is on every page and works after the window shrinks","body":""},{"hash":"c27179b","date":"2026-10-14T02:12:02+01:00","subject":"Computer says the VPS inside: 'Your VPS', 'On the VPS', 'Move Nova Agent to the VPS'; Console names Nova Agent instead of the studio computer; Manual's Computer section describes the VPS (no Cloudflare)","body":""},{"hash":"2b2f304","date":"2026-10-14T01:12:16+01:00","subject":"Computer shows Nova's own computer (the VPS) only: where Nova Agent runs and how to move it, mail sender, backups kept, Restart Nova Agent; Console's computer/deploy without the old host","body":""},{"hash":"a98c163","date":"2026-10-13T23:51:38+01:00","subject":"Nova Agent on the server: NOVA_ON_SERVER mode, only one Nova Agent runs (link says where; PC stands down on 4002 and stays off by marker), Console + Shell is the server's shell (ssh tunnel), Fixer restarts nova-agent.service and checks Claude Code's sign-in, watchdog becomes a self-watch","body":""},{"hash":"3c6c6b5","date":"2026-10-13T22:43:26+01:00","subject":"Desk is called Computer now: Portal → Admin → Computer, Console's computer command (desk still works, and it says which side is live), view=computer, the status words","body":""},{"hash":"4463bcb","date":"2026-10-13T20:23:13+01:00","subject":"Console docs and Manual: tap-to-run commands, grouped help, today/search/desk/deploy/backup/shortcuts, Open Console on this computer, the VPS set","body":""},{"hash":"073c34b","date":"2026-10-13T20:17:09+01:00","subject":"Console tests: every command runs (answers stood in for), help covers every command, did-you-mean and other words","body":""},{"hash":"5c20f4d","date":"2026-10-13T20:16:33+01:00","subject":"WIP Console: centred and readable (a centred column, bigger text, headings, coloured lined-up help with examples, stacked on phones), commands to tap, an Open on this computer button online","body":""},{"hash":"eac261c","date":"2026-10-13T20:11:53+01:00","subject":"WIP Console: opens on the studio computer itself (/console/?here=1) for its terminals, the VPS set by default, the PC's person keeps their admin role until Nova Bot answers","body":""},{"hash":"d17994d","date":"2026-10-13T20:11:00+01:00","subject":"WIP Console: grouped help with examples, today, version, desk, deploy status, backup, search, ask, Portal shortcuts, aliases, did-you-mean","body":""},{"hash":"4da0c86","date":"2026-10-13T18:36:38+01:00","subject":"Console: the terminal sizes itself to an exact box (nothing past the edge at any size)","body":""},{"hash":"1b84562","date":"2026-10-13T18:34:42+01:00","subject":"Console: docs, the Manual and status words","body":""},{"hash":"3e3efd6","date":"2026-10-13T18:34:14+01:00","subject":"WIP Console: tests (commands, approvals typed back, terminals only on this computer for admins, VPS address, tokens), state and log through the link","body":""},{"hash":"5794b82","date":"2026-10-13T18:32:51+01:00","subject":"WIP Console: long lines that wrap redraw cleanly","body":""},{"hash":"482de5d","date":"2026-10-13T18:31:57+01:00","subject":"WIP Console: its own rows, left-aligned terminals, a shorter confirm line","body":""},{"hash":"f55b9b5","date":"2026-10-13T11:38:36+01:00","subject":"WIP Console: the page (Nova tab, terminal tabs, extra keys, theme colours)","body":""},{"hash":"c1b4c3d","date":"2026-10-13T11:36:18+01:00","subject":"WIP Console: the Nova commands","body":""},{"hash":"9d7ab79","date":"2026-10-13T11:33:36+01:00","subject":"WIP Console: terminals on the PC (admins, this computer only), the VPS's address, the log; xterm.js vendored","body":""}],"work":[],"workCount":0,"workStat":""}},{"id":"bot","name":"Nova Bot","colour":"#5CE1FF","glyph":"◎","where":"On the website and the studio's server: Nova Agent's back end","links":[["Admin pages","https://nova.novacane.co.uk/admin"]],"repo":"nb/novacane-worker","shared":"","tagline":"The front desk that never closes: a website assistant, a staff app and the engines behind Nova Agent, for Novacane Studios.","intro":"<p>Nova Bot runs on Cloudflare Workers for <a href=\"https://novacane.co.uk\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Novacane Studios</a>, a recording studio in London. One Worker does four jobs:</p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th></th><th>What it is</th><th>Where</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>✦ <strong>NovaBot</strong></td><td>The chat assistant on the studio&#39;s website. Answers questions with Claude and gets bookings ready, always with the deposit first</td><td><code>public/novabot.js</code>, <code>src/index.js</code></td></tr><tr><td>✦ <strong>Nova Portal</strong></td><td>The staff app: enquiries, chats, a smart calendar, quests, alerts, a staff chat with NovaBot, sign-in, everyone&#39;s planet and the team</td><td>Nova Agent&#39;s Nova Portal panel (copied into <code>public/portal/</code>), <code>src/app-page.js</code>, <code>src/portal/</code></td></tr><tr><td>✦ <strong>Admin pages</strong></td><td>Password-protected pages for referrals, enquiries, conversations, feedback, the booking system and the master list of links</td><td><code>src/admin.js</code></td></tr><tr><td>✦ <strong>Suite engines</strong></td><td>The memory behind <strong>Nova Index</strong> and the sign-in behind <strong>Nova Portal</strong>, shared by every Nova app</td><td><code>src/memory/</code>, <code>src/portal/</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>It comes with a <strong>sandbox</strong>, so you can run the whole thing on your own computer without any accounts.</p>\n<blockquote>Every screenshot and animation here was made with made-up data (Dana Hollis, Eric Mensah, Kai and friends, <code>example.com</code> addresses and <code>07700 900xxx</code> numbers). No real customers appear anywhere.</blockquote>","guide":[{"id":"novabot-on-the-website-0","title":"NovaBot, on the website","html":"<p>The chat widget on a page.   The booking card: session, day, free start times and details, all in the chat.</p>\n<ul><li><strong>It answers questions</strong> (<code>src/index.js</code>). Claude answers from the studio&#39;s own information: prices, policies and booking rules. Every link it gives is checked, and anything made up is replaced with a real one.</li><li><strong>Bookings always take the deposit.</strong> Nothing NovaBot does puts a session into Acuity unpaid (<code>src/book-session.js</code>). It works out the session, checks the time is still free and fills in the customer&#39;s details, then hands them Acuity&#39;s own booking page with everything ready. Paying the deposit there is what books it; the time isn&#39;t held until they pay. The same rule covers the staff chat and Nova Agent.</li><li><strong>The chat widget</strong> (<code>public/novabot.js</code>, <code>public/novabot.css</code>): opens after the page loads, keeps out of the way of buttons and forms, remembers the conversation across pages, and has a &quot;Keep chat closed&quot; switch. Optional voice: speak to it (Whisper on Workers AI) and hear replies (the browser&#39;s voice or MeloTTS).</li><li><strong>Booking links and free times</strong> (<code>src/booking.js</code>): reads session types and free start times from the studio&#39;s <em>public</em> Acuity booking page (no login, read-only).</li><li><strong>The booking card</strong> (<code>src/booking-form.js</code>): &quot;Book a session&quot; opens a card in the chat with the session, a strip of days, that day&#39;s free times and the visitor&#39;s details. The Worker checks the time again before anything happens.</li><li><strong>Enquiries</strong> (<code>src/enquiries.js</code>): NovaBot can take an enquiry, show the visitor a summary, and send it to the team once they confirm. It&#39;s saved for Nova Portal and the admin pages, and can be emailed (the studio&#39;s own mail server).</li><li><strong>Safety</strong>: per-visitor rate limits, only allowed websites can use the chat, spam limits on enquiries, and IP addresses stored only as a hash.</li></ul>","text":"The chat widget on a page. The booking card: session, day, free start times and details, all in the chat. It answers questions ( src/index.js ). Claude answers from the studio's own information: prices, policies and booking rules. Every link it gives is checked, and anything made up is replaced with a real one. Bookings always take the deposit. Nothing NovaBot does puts a session into Acuity unpaid ( src/book-session.js ). It works out the session, checks the time is still free and fills in the customer's details, then hands them Acuity's own booking page with everything ready. Paying the deposit there is what books it; the time isn't held until they pay. The same rule covers the staff chat and Nova Agent. The chat widget ( public/novabot.js , public/novabot.css ): opens after the page loads, keeps out of the way of buttons and forms, remembers the conversation across pages, and has a \"Keep chat closed\" switch. Optional voice: speak to it (Whisper on Workers AI) and hear replies (the browser's voice or MeloTTS). Booking links and free times ( src/booking.js ): reads session types and free start times from the studio's public Acuity booking page (no login, read-only). The booking card ( src/booking-form.js ): \"Book a session\" opens a card in the chat with the session, a strip of days, that day's free times and the visitor's details. The Worker checks the time again before anything happens. Enquiries ( src/enquiries.js ): NovaBot can take an enquiry, show the visitor a summary, and send it to the team once they confirm. It's saved for Nova Portal and the admin pages, and can be emailed (the studio's own mail server). Safety : per-visitor rate limits, only allowed websites can use the chat, spam limits on enquiries, and IP addresses stored only as a hash."},{"id":"portal-the-staff-app-1","title":"Nova Portal, the staff app","html":"<p>The staff app (enquiries, website chats, bookings, alerts, Ask NovaBot and push to the staff phones, plus sign-in, everyone&#39;s planet and the team) is Nova Agent&#39;s <strong>Nova Portal</strong> panel. Nova Portal is part of it now. Its pages live in Nova Agent&#39;s repo (<code>web/portal</code>) and are copied in at build time (see The build step). Online it&#39;s at <code>/portal/</code>; this Worker is its back end (<code>/app/api/*</code>, <code>src/app-page.js</code>, and <code>src/portal/</code> for sign-in and the team). Nova Portal&#39;s old address, <code>/app/</code>, redirects to Nova Portal, but phones that installed Nova Portal keep their push helper (<code>/app/sw.js</code>). Its guide and pictures are in Nova Agent&#39;s <code>docs/apps/portal</code>.</p>","text":"The staff app (enquiries, website chats, bookings, alerts, Ask NovaBot and push to the staff phones, plus sign-in, everyone's planet and the team) is Nova Agent's Nova Portal panel. Nova Portal is part of it now. Its pages live in Nova Agent's repo ( web/portal ) and are copied in at build time (see The build step). Online it's at /portal/ ; this Worker is its back end ( /app/api/* , src/app-page.js , and src/portal/ for sign-in and the team). Nova Portal's old address, /app/ , redirects to Nova Portal, but phones that installed Nova Portal keep their push helper ( /app/sw.js ). Its guide and pictures are in Nova Agent's docs/apps/portal ."},{"id":"the-admin-pages-2","title":"The admin pages","html":"<p><code>/admin</code>, in Nova Portal&#39;s look and themes. Sign in with Nova Portal as an admin; signed out, it sends you to Nova Portal and back.</p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Page</th><th>What&#39;s there</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Referrals</strong> (<code>/admin</code>)</td><td>Referral codes, the appointments they brought in, and a CSV report</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Enquiries</strong></td><td>Every enquiry, mark done, and a test email</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Conversations</strong></td><td>Recent chats (kept 90 days), one in full with <code>?chat=ID</code></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Feedback</strong></td><td>What visitors said about NovaBot, good and bad</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Booking system</strong> (<code>/admin/connections</code>)</td><td>The Acuity / Nova switch, plus Google and Stripe</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Links</strong> (<code>/admin/links</code>)</td><td>The master list: every address with a live check, <strong>What&#39;s changed</strong>, and <strong>everything the suite can do</strong>. Edited here as JSON</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>The Links page&#39;s changelog (sample entries).</p>\n<p>The master list is kept in the database (<code>settings</code>), never in the code, because the code is public. Nova Portal&#39;s Nova Agent sheet reads the same list from <code>/app/api/links</code> (<code>src/links.js</code>).</p>","text":"/admin , in Nova Portal's look and themes. Sign in with Nova Portal as an admin; signed out, it sends you to Nova Portal and back. Page What's there Referrals ( /admin ) Referral codes, the appointments they brought in, and a CSV report Enquiries Every enquiry, mark done, and a test email Conversations Recent chats (kept 90 days), one in full with ?chat=ID Feedback What visitors said about NovaBot, good and bad Booking system ( /admin/connections ) The Acuity / Nova switch, plus Google and Stripe Links ( /admin/links ) The master list: every address with a live check, What's changed , and everything the suite can do . Edited here as JSON The Links page's changelog (sample entries). The master list is kept in the database ( settings ), never in the code, because the code is public. Nova Portal's Nova Agent sheet reads the same list from /app/api/links ( src/links.js )."},{"id":"index-the-memory-engine-3","title":"Nova Index: the memory engine","html":"<p>Nova Index, browsing the suite&#39;s memory (sample data).</p>\n<p><code>src/memory/</code> is one shared memory for Nova Agent. Nova Agent&#39;s Nova Index panel (copied in at <code>/app/memory/</code>) is the window onto it; NovaBot, Nova Portal and Nova Agent read and add to it.</p>\n<p><strong>How it&#39;s kept.</strong> Small files of one-line facts, one file per subject, in D1 (never in git). Each line is tagged: <code>[stated]</code> said directly, <code>[observed]</code> seen in bookings or behaviour, <code>[inferred]</code> a pattern. Files stay small (about 3 KB; a condense pass tidies them), and at most about 800 tokens of memory go into any one prompt.</p>\n<p><strong>Scopes, and who sees what.</strong> The caller&#39;s role decides, never what it asks for.</p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Scope</th><th>Holds</th><th>Read by</th><th>Written by</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>studio</code></td><td>The studio&#39;s shared facts: people, topics, areas</td><td>Staff, Nova Agent, Nova Portal members</td><td>Staff, Nova Agent</td></tr><tr><td><code>staff</code></td><td>Each staff member&#39;s own partition</td><td>Staff, Nova Agent; a Nova Portal member sees only their own</td><td>Staff, Nova Agent, the member themself</td></tr><tr><td><code>customer</code></td><td>One file per client (their email, or the chat until it&#39;s known)</td><td>Staff; NovaBot on the website sees only <em>that</em> customer&#39;s file</td><td>Staff (website facts wait for approval)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><strong>What it learns, and when.</strong> Always in the background, never while someone waits:</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Nova Portal&#39;s staff chats</strong>: facts are saved straight away (staff are trusted).</li><li><strong>Website chats</strong>: the every-minute job reads a chat once it&#39;s been quiet for 10 minutes (or every 20 messages), two chats a run. Facts about clients go into an <strong>approval queue</strong> in Nova Index instead of being saved.</li><li><strong>Nova Agent</strong>: hands over conversation chunks with <code>POST /memory/extract</code>.</li></ul>\n<p>Each pass asks a small model for <strong>durable</strong> facts only (&quot;would this still be true and useful in three months?&quot;), and folds them into the file: a new line on the same subject replaces the old one rather than contradicting it. Writes carry a version token, so two apps can&#39;t overwrite each other.</p>\n<p><strong>Privacy.</strong> Card numbers, bank details, sort codes, National Insurance and passport numbers and passwords are refused at the door. Nothing is learned while a visitor waits. The website only ever sees the public studio file and that customer&#39;s own file, and client facts need a person to approve them.</p>\n<p>The API</p>\n<p>For Nova Agent (<code>Authorization: Bearer </code>):</p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Route</th><th>Does</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>GET /memory/context?scope=&amp;owner_id=&amp;q=</code></td><td>The files that matter for this turn, as text</td></tr><tr><td><code>GET /memory/file?scope=&amp;owner_id=&amp;path=</code></td><td>One file and its version token</td></tr><tr><td><code>PUT /memory/file</code></td><td>Write a file (<code>if_version: &quot;new&quot;</code> or the token; 409 with the current file on a clash)</td></tr><tr><td><code>POST /memory/extract</code></td><td>Hand over a conversation chunk; learned in the background (202)</td></tr><tr><td><code>GET /memory/index?scope=</code></td><td>The listing (no bodies)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>For Nova Portal and Nova Index (signed in), under <code>/app/api/memory/</code>: <code>index</code>, <code>file</code> (GET/PUT/DELETE), <code>pending</code>, <code>pending/:id</code> (approve or reject, optionally with an edited fact), and <code>stats</code>.</p>","text":"Nova Index, browsing the suite's memory (sample data). src/memory/ is one shared memory for Nova Agent. Nova Agent's Nova Index panel (copied in at /app/memory/ ) is the window onto it; NovaBot, Nova Portal and Nova Agent read and add to it. How it's kept. Small files of one-line facts, one file per subject, in D1 (never in git). Each line is tagged: [stated] said directly, [observed] seen in bookings or behaviour, [inferred] a pattern. Files stay small (about 3 KB; a condense pass tidies them), and at most about 800 tokens of memory go into any one prompt. Scopes, and who sees what. The caller's role decides, never what it asks for. Scope Holds Read by Written by studio The studio's shared facts: people, topics, areas Staff, Nova Agent, Nova Portal members Staff, Nova Agent staff Each staff member's own partition Staff, Nova Agent; a Nova Portal member sees only their own Staff, Nova Agent, the member themself customer One file per client (their email, or the chat until it's known) Staff; NovaBot on the website sees only that customer's file Staff (website facts wait for approval) What it learns, and when. Always in the background, never while someone waits: Nova Portal's staff chats : facts are saved straight away (staff are trusted). Website chats : the every-minute job reads a chat once it's been quiet for 10 minutes (or every 20 messages), two chats a run. Facts about clients go into an approval queue in Nova Index instead of being saved. Nova Agent : hands over conversation chunks with POST /memory/extract . Each pass asks a small model for durable facts only (\"would this still be true and useful in three months?\"), and folds them into the file: a new line on the same subject replaces the old one rather than contradicting it. Writes carry a version token, so two apps can't overwrite each other. Privacy. Card numbers, bank details, sort codes, National Insurance and passport numbers and passwords are refused at the door. Nothing is learned while a visitor waits. The website only ever sees the public studio file and that customer's own file, and client facts need a person to approve them. The API For Nova Agent ( Authorization: Bearer ): Route Does GET /memory/context?scope=&owner_id=&q= The files that matter for this turn, as text GET /memory/file?scope=&owner_id=&path= One file and its version token PUT /memory/file Write a file ( if_version: \"new\" or the token; 409 with the current file on a clash) POST /memory/extract Hand over a conversation chunk; learned in the background (202) GET /memory/index?scope= The listing (no bodies) For Nova Portal and Nova Index (signed in), under /app/api/memory/ : index , file (GET/PUT/DELETE), pending , pending/:id (approve or reject, optionally with an edited fact), and stats ."},{"id":"portal-one-sign-in-for-the-suite-4","title":"Nova Portal: one sign-in for the suite","html":"<p>Sign in once for every Nova app.  The crew, each with their own planet (sample people).</p>\n<p><code>src/portal/</code> signs people in once for Nova Portal, Nova Index and the admin pages. The pages are Nova Agent&#39;s Nova Portal panel (<code>web/portal</code> in Nova Agent&#39;s repo), copied in at build time (see the build step); this Worker serves them at <code>/portal/</code> and runs the API.</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Accounts.</strong> Everyone has their own (<code>staff</code> table): a readable id like <code>dana</code>, an email, a display name, a role and a status (active, invited or switched off). The first admin is set up with the studio&#39;s current password.</li><li><strong>Invites.</strong> An admin invites someone by email and gets a link that works once, for 7 days. Only a hash of its token is stored. The new person chooses a password and is signed in.</li><li><strong>Passwords.</strong> PBKDF2-SHA256 with 100,000 rounds and a random salt for each person; a few tries a minute at most per address.</li><li><strong>Sessions.</strong> A random token in an httpOnly, Secure cookie for 30 days (or an app token, <code>Authorization: Bearer nsess_…</code>, for native apps). Only its SHA-256 is stored, and signing out deletes it, so it stops working everywhere at once.</li><li><strong>Roles.</strong> <code>admin</code> (everything, including the crew and the admin pages) or <code>staff</code>. A staff member who isn&#39;t an admin sees the studio&#39;s memory and their own partition of Nova Index.</li><li><strong>Planets.</strong> Every person gets a planet, drawn fresh from their seed by the planet generator: <code>GET /staff/:id/planet.svg?size=&amp;animate=1</code>. It&#39;s their avatar across the suite.</li><li><strong>One sign-in.</strong> There&#39;s no shared password any more: Nova Portal, Nova Index, the admin pages and every other panel take a Nova Portal sign-in.</li></ul>\n<p>The API</p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Route</th><th>Does</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>POST /auth/login</code></td><td><code>{ email, password, client? }</code> → session cookie (or an app token)</td></tr><tr><td><code>POST /auth/logout</code></td><td>Ends this session everywhere</td></tr><tr><td><code>GET /auth/me</code></td><td>Who&#39;s signed in (every app starts with this)</td></tr><tr><td><code>GET /auth/status</code></td><td><code>{ setupNeeded }</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>POST /auth/setup</code></td><td>The first admin, proven with the studio&#39;s current password</td></tr><tr><td><code>GET /auth/invite?token=</code> / <code>POST /auth/invite/accept</code></td><td>Who an invite is for; choose a password</td></tr><tr><td><code>GET /staff</code>, <code>POST /staff</code></td><td>Admins: everyone; invite someone</td></tr><tr><td><code>POST /staff/:id/invite</code></td><td>Admins: a fresh invite link</td></tr><tr><td><code>GET /staff/:id</code>, <code>PATCH /staff/:id</code></td><td>A profile; change it (admins: role and status too)</td></tr><tr><td><code>GET /staff/:id/planet.svg</code></td><td>The planet badge</td></tr><tr><td><code>GET /staff/:id/index</code></td><td>That person&#39;s Nova Index view</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>Changes from a browser must come from this site (the Origin header).</p>","text":"Sign in once for every Nova app. The crew, each with their own planet (sample people). src/portal/ signs people in once for Nova Portal, Nova Index and the admin pages. The pages are Nova Agent's Nova Portal panel ( web/portal in Nova Agent's repo), copied in at build time (see the build step); this Worker serves them at /portal/ and runs the API. Accounts. Everyone has their own ( staff table): a readable id like dana , an email, a display name, a role and a status (active, invited or switched off). The first admin is set up with the studio's current password. Invites. An admin invites someone by email and gets a link that works once, for 7 days. Only a hash of its token is stored. The new person chooses a password and is signed in. Passwords. PBKDF2-SHA256 with 100,000 rounds and a random salt for each person; a few tries a minute at most per address. Sessions. A random token in an httpOnly, Secure cookie for 30 days (or an app token, Authorization: Bearer nsess_… , for native apps). Only its SHA-256 is stored, and signing out deletes it, so it stops working everywhere at once. Roles. admin (everything, including the crew and the admin pages) or staff . A staff member who isn't an admin sees the studio's memory and their own partition of Nova Index. Planets. Every person gets a planet, drawn fresh from their seed by the planet generator: GET /staff/:id/planet.svg?size=&animate=1 . It's their avatar across the suite. One sign-in. There's no shared password any more: Nova Portal, Nova Index, the admin pages and every other panel take a Nova Portal sign-in. The API Route Does POST /auth/login { email, password, client? } → session cookie (or an app token) POST /auth/logout Ends this session everywhere GET /auth/me Who's signed in (every app starts with this) GET /auth/status { setupNeeded } POST /auth/setup The first admin, proven with the studio's current password GET /auth/invite?token= / POST /auth/invite/accept Who an invite is for; choose a password GET /staff , POST /staff Admins: everyone; invite someone POST /staff/:id/invite Admins: a fresh invite link GET /staff/:id , PATCH /staff/:id A profile; change it (admins: role and status too) GET /staff/:id/planet.svg The planet badge GET /staff/:id/index That person's Nova Index view Changes from a browser must come from this site (the Origin header)."},{"id":"nova-bot-s-own-booking-system-behind-a-switch-5","title":"Nova Bot's own booking system (behind a switch)","html":"<p>Bookings go through <strong>Acuity</strong> by default. Alongside it, <code>src/nova/</code> holds Nova Bot&#39;s own booking system, switched <strong>off</strong> until you choose otherwise:</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Booking page</strong> at <code>/book</code>, with the studio&#39;s <strong>Google Nova Calendar</strong> as the diary, confirmation emails from the studio&#39;s <strong>Gmail</strong>, and deposits through <strong>Stripe</strong>.</li><li><strong>Customer pages</strong>: each customer gets a page to pay, move or cancel.</li><li><strong>Staff tools</strong> in Nova Portal: cancel, move, refund and send payment links.</li></ul>\n<p><strong>The switch</strong> is on <code>/admin/connections</code>, under &quot;Booking system&quot;. It&#39;s stored in the <code>settings</code> table as <code>booking_system</code> (<code>acuity</code> or <code>nova</code>), and falls back to the <code>BOOKING_SYSTEM</code> variable, then to Acuity (<code>src/mode.js</code>).</p>\n<ul><li>It takes effect straight away, with no redeploy.</li><li>Nova can only be switched on once Google and Stripe both work. Switching back to Acuity is always one click.</li><li>On Acuity, everything behaves exactly as before, and the original tests prove it.</li><li>Either way, a booking made with Nova keeps working (its page, payment links and Stripe&#39;s webhook), and Acuity&#39;s webhook is still listened to.</li></ul>\n<p>Setting it up</p>\n<ol><li><strong>Google:</strong> in Nova Agent, Admin → Google walks through it a step at a time (Google Cloud&#39;s pages open from buttons, with copy buttons for every address to paste), then takes the key and has a <strong>Connect Google</strong> button. The same key gives everyone <strong>Sign in with Google</strong> and Nova Notes&#39; Google Docs. (Setting <code>GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID</code> and <code>GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET</code> as secrets still works, and wins.)</li><li><strong>Stripe:</strong> <code>npx wrangler secret put STRIPE_SECRET_KEY</code> (use a <code>sk_test_…</code> key to try it). Add a webhook endpoint <code>https:///stripe/webhook</code> with the events <code>checkout.session.completed</code>, <code>checkout.session.async_payment_succeeded</code> and <code>checkout.session.expired</code>, and save its signing secret as <code>STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET</code>.</li><li><strong>Database:</strong> <code>npx wrangler d1 migrations apply novabot --remote</code>.</li><li><strong>Deploy,</strong> then on <code>/admin/connections</code>: press <strong>Send a test email</strong>, and flip the switch to try it.</li></ol>\n<p>Sessions, prices and rules (opening hours, 50% deposit, 48-hour cancellation) are in <code>src/nova/studio.js</code>.</p>","text":"Bookings go through Acuity by default. Alongside it, src/nova/ holds Nova Bot's own booking system, switched off until you choose otherwise: Booking page at /book , with the studio's Google Nova Calendar as the diary, confirmation emails from the studio's Gmail , and deposits through Stripe . Customer pages : each customer gets a page to pay, move or cancel. Staff tools in Nova Portal: cancel, move, refund and send payment links. The switch is on /admin/connections , under \"Booking system\". It's stored in the settings table as booking_system ( acuity or nova ), and falls back to the BOOKING_SYSTEM variable, then to Acuity ( src/mode.js ). It takes effect straight away, with no redeploy. Nova can only be switched on once Google and Stripe both work. Switching back to Acuity is always one click. On Acuity, everything behaves exactly as before, and the original tests prove it. Either way, a booking made with Nova keeps working (its page, payment links and Stripe's webhook), and Acuity's webhook is still listened to. Setting it up Google: in Nova Agent, Admin → Google walks through it a step at a time (Google Cloud's pages open from buttons, with copy buttons for every address to paste), then takes the key and has a Connect Google button. The same key gives everyone Sign in with Google and Nova Notes' Google Docs. (Setting GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID and GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET as secrets still works, and wins.) Stripe: npx wrangler secret put STRIPE_SECRET_KEY (use a sk_test_… key to try it). Add a webhook endpoint https:///stripe/webhook with the events checkout.session.completed , checkout.session.async_payment_succeeded and checkout.session.expired , and save its signing secret as STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET . Database: npx wrangler d1 migrations apply novabot --remote . Deploy, then on /admin/connections : press Send a test email , and flip the switch to try it. Sessions, prices and rules (opening hours, 50% deposit, 48-hour cancellation) are in src/nova/studio.js ."},{"id":"works-with-nova-agent-6","title":"Works with Nova Agent","html":"<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Project</th><th>What it is</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"https://github.com/tuniveza/nova-agent\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">nova-agent</a></td><td>The studio&#39;s one app: chat, Nova Missions and Nova Quests, and every panel (Nova Portal, Nova Calendar, Nova Notes, Nova Index, Nova Observatory, Nova Lossless audio). On the studio PC, and online from here for phones</td></tr><tr><td><strong><a href=\"https://github.com/tuniveza/nova-bot\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">nova-bot</a></strong></td><td>This repo: NovaBot on the website, and the back end behind Nova Agent (sign-in, push, bookings, the memory engine, jobs)</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://github.com/tuniveza/nova-club\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">nova-club</a></td><td>Members&#39; Android app that shows the studio&#39;s busy times</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","text":"Project What it is nova-agent The studio's one app: chat, Nova Missions and Nova Quests, and every panel (Nova Portal, Nova Calendar, Nova Notes, Nova Index, Nova Observatory, Nova Lossless audio). On the studio PC, and online from here for phones nova-bot This repo: NovaBot on the website, and the back end behind Nova Agent (sign-in, push, bookings, the memory engine, jobs) nova-club Members' Android app that shows the studio's busy times"}],"built":[{"id":"how-it-works-0","title":"How it works","html":"<pre><code>flowchart LR\n    V[Website visitor] --&gt;|chat widget| W\n    S[Staff · Portal&lt;br/&gt;Index] --&gt; W\n    C[Nova Club app] --&gt;|/club/busy| W\n    subgraph W[Nova Bot · Cloudflare Worker]\n      R[Routes · src/index.js] --&gt; CL[Claude]\n      R --&gt; DB[(D1 database)]\n      R --&gt; AI[Workers AI&lt;br/&gt;voice]\n      R --&gt; MEM[Memory engine&lt;br/&gt;src/memory]\n      R --&gt; PO[Sign-in&lt;br/&gt;src/portal]\n    end\n    W --&gt;|public booking page,&lt;br/&gt;API, calendar feed| A[Acuity Scheduling]\n    NA[Nova Agent&lt;br/&gt;studio PC] --&gt;|jobs, quests,&lt;br/&gt;memory| W\n    NA --&gt;|admin pages| A\n    W --&gt;|Web Push| S\n    W -.-&gt;|behind the switch| G[Google Calendar · Gmail · Stripe]</code></pre>\n<ul><li><strong>One Worker</strong> serves the widget, the chat API, Nova Portal, Nova Index, the admin pages, webhooks and a once-a-minute cron (booking pings, and reading website chats for memory).</li><li><strong>D1</strong> holds enquiries, chat logs (90 days), referral codes, notifications, settings, Nova Agent&#39;s job queue, the memory files, staff accounts and sessions and, when switched on, Nova Bot&#39;s own bookings (<code>migrations/</code>).</li><li><strong>Secrets</strong> live in Cloudflare (<code>wrangler secret put</code>), never in the code.</li></ul>","text":"flowchart LR V[Website visitor] -->|chat widget| W S[Staff · Nova Portal<br/>Nova Index] --> W C[Nova Club app] -->|/club/busy| W subgraph W[Nova Bot · Cloudflare Worker] R[Routes · src/index.js] --> CL[Claude] R --> DB[(D1 database)] R --> AI[Workers AI<br/>voice] R --> MEM[Memory engine<br/>src/memory] R --> PO[Sign-in<br/>src/portal] end W -->|public booking page,<br/>API, calendar feed| A[Acuity Scheduling] NA[Nova Agent<br/>studio PC] -->|jobs, quests,<br/>memory| W NA -->|admin pages| A W -->|Web Push| S W -.->|behind the switch| G[Google Nova Calendar · Gmail · Stripe] One Worker serves the widget, the chat API, Nova Portal, Nova Index, the admin pages, webhooks and a once-a-minute cron (booking pings, and reading website chats for memory). D1 holds enquiries, chat logs (90 days), referral codes, notifications, settings, Nova Agent's job queue, the memory files, staff accounts and sessions and, when switched on, Nova Bot's own bookings ( migrations/ ). Secrets live in Cloudflare ( wrangler secret put ), never in the code."},{"id":"run-it-locally-sandbox-1","title":"Run it locally (sandbox)","html":"<p>You need <a href=\"https://nodejs.org\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Node.js</a> 20 or newer. No Cloudflare, Claude or Acuity account is needed.</p>\n<pre><code>git clone https://github.com/tuniveza/nova-bot.git\ncd nova-bot\nnpm install\nnpm run sandbox:setup   # creates .dev.vars from the example, and a local database\nnpm run sandbox         # starts it at http://localhost:8787</code></pre>\n<p>Open : a pretend website with the chat widget on it.</p>\n<p>The sandbox: a pretend studio site, with clearly labelled stand-in replies when no AI key is set.</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Everything stays on your computer.</strong> The sandbox has its own local database and can&#39;t reach any live Nova Bot, database or calendar.</li><li><strong>Without an AI key</strong>, NovaBot gives clearly labelled stand-in replies, so you can try the widget, enquiries, Nova Portal and the admin pages for free.</li><li><strong>For real answers</strong>, put your own Claude API key (<a href=\"https://console.anthropic.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">console.anthropic.com</a>) in <code>.dev.vars</code> as <code>ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=...</code> and restart. That uses your own Anthropic account.</li><li><strong>Admin pages and Nova Portal</strong>:  and ; set up the first admin with the password in <code>.dev.vars</code> (<code>sandbox</code>).</li><li><strong>The booking card</strong> needs a booking system it can check times against. To try it offline, start the sandbox with Nova Bot&#39;s own system switched on: <code>npx wrangler dev --env sandbox --var BOOKING_SYSTEM:nova</code> (no Google key means the &quot;calendar&quot; is the local bookings table; no Stripe key means a local stand-in checkout).</li><li><strong>Voice</strong>: speech uses your browser&#39;s own voice; the microphone needs Workers AI, so it isn&#39;t available in the sandbox.</li></ul>\n<p><code>.dev.vars</code> is in <code>.gitignore</code>: your keys never get committed.</p>","text":"You need Node.js 20 or newer. No Cloudflare, Claude or Acuity account is needed. git clone https://github.com/tuniveza/nova-bot.git cd nova-bot npm install npm run sandbox:setup # creates .dev.vars from the example, and a local database npm run sandbox # starts it at http://localhost:8787 Open : a pretend website with the chat widget on it. The sandbox: a pretend studio site, with clearly labelled stand-in replies when no AI key is set. Everything stays on your computer. The sandbox has its own local database and can't reach any live Nova Bot, database or calendar. Without an AI key , NovaBot gives clearly labelled stand-in replies, so you can try the widget, enquiries, Nova Portal and the admin pages for free. For real answers , put your own Claude API key ( console.anthropic.com ) in .dev.vars as ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=... and restart. That uses your own Anthropic account. Admin pages and Nova Portal : and ; set up the first admin with the password in .dev.vars ( sandbox ). The booking card needs a booking system it can check times against. To try it offline, start the sandbox with Nova Bot's own system switched on: npx wrangler dev --env sandbox --var BOOKING_SYSTEM:nova (no Google key means the \"calendar\" is the local bookings table; no Stripe key means a local stand-in checkout). Voice : speech uses your browser's own voice; the microphone needs Workers AI, so it isn't available in the sandbox. .dev.vars is in .gitignore : your keys never get committed."},{"id":"the-build-step-2","title":"The build step","html":"<p>Nova Agent&#39;s panels (Nova Portal, Nova Index, Nova Calendar, Nova Notes, and what they share) live in Nova Agent&#39;s repo (<code>na/web</code>). They&#39;re served from here online, so they share this Worker&#39;s sign-in, so before every deploy or local run, wrangler&#39;s build step (<code>&quot;build&quot;: { &quot;command&quot;: &quot;node scripts/sync-apps.mjs&quot; }</code>) copies them in:</p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>From (Nova Agent)</th><th>To</th><th>What</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>web/portal/</code></td><td><code>public/portal/</code></td><td>Nova Portal</td></tr><tr><td><code>web/portal/old-app-address/</code></td><td><code>public/app/</code></td><td>What phones that installed Nova Portal from <code>/app/</code> still use: its push helper, manifest and icons</td></tr><tr><td><code>web/index/</code></td><td><code>public/app/memory/</code></td><td>Nova Index</td></tr><tr><td><code>web/calendar/</code>, <code>web/notes/</code></td><td><code>public/calendar/</code>, <code>public/notes/</code></td><td>Nova Calendar and Nova Notes (online, they save in the browser)</td></tr><tr><td><code>web/shared/</code></td><td><code>public/shared/</code></td><td>Themes, sounds, the badge and the Nova Manual</td></tr><tr><td><code>web/portal/planet/</code></td><td><code>src/portal/planet/</code></td><td>The planet generator (also draws <code>planet.svg</code>)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>Nova Agent is expected at <code>../../na</code>; <code>NOVA_AGENT_DIR</code> points elsewhere. The page copies are never saved in this repo (<code>.gitignore</code>). The planet generator copy is, so the project still builds and tests on its own.</p>\n<p><strong>Addresses</strong>: Nova Portal at <code>/portal/</code>, Nova Index at <code>/app/memory/</code>. Nova Portal&#39;s old pages (<code>/app/</code>, <code>/app/?view=alerts</code> and so on) redirect to Nova Portal (<code>src/index.js</code>, <code>movedPage</code>); its API (<code>/app/api/</code>) and the files in <code>public/app/</code> stay. The addresses the panels had for a day (<code>/studio/</code>, <code>/crew/</code>, <code>/index/</code>) redirect too.</p>","text":"Nova Agent's panels (Nova Portal, Nova Index, Nova Calendar, Nova Notes, and what they share) live in Nova Agent's repo ( na/web ). They're served from here online, so they share this Worker's sign-in, so before every deploy or local run, wrangler's build step ( \"build\": { \"command\": \"node scripts/sync-apps.mjs\" } ) copies them in: From (Nova Agent) To What web/portal/ public/portal/ Nova Portal web/portal/old-app-address/ public/app/ What phones that installed Nova Portal from /app/ still use: its push helper, manifest and icons web/index/ public/app/memory/ Nova Index web/calendar/ , web/notes/ public/calendar/ , public/notes/ Nova Calendar and Nova Notes (online, they save in the browser) web/shared/ public/shared/ Themes, sounds, the badge and the Nova Manual web/portal/planet/ src/portal/planet/ The planet generator (also draws planet.svg ) Nova Agent is expected at ../../na ; NOVA_AGENT_DIR points elsewhere. The page copies are never saved in this repo ( .gitignore ). The planet generator copy is, so the project still builds and tests on its own. Addresses : Nova Portal at /portal/ , Nova Index at /app/memory/ . Nova Portal's old pages ( /app/ , /app/?view=alerts and so on) redirect to Nova Portal ( src/index.js , movedPage ); its API ( /app/api/ ) and the files in public/app/ stay. The addresses the panels had for a day ( /studio/ , /crew/ , /index/ ) redirect too."},{"id":"configuration-3","title":"Configuration","html":"<p>Everything secret is a <strong>Wrangler secret</strong> (<code>npx wrangler secret put NAME</code>), or a line in <code>.dev.vars</code> for local runs. Names only; values never belong in the repository.</p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Needed for</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>ANTHROPIC_API_KEY</code></td><td>Claude answers and memory (required live)</td></tr><tr><td><code>ADMIN_PASSWORD</code></td><td>Only proves it&#39;s you when setting up the very first Nova Portal admin</td></tr><tr><td><code>ACUITY_USER_ID</code>, <code>ACUITY_API_KEY</code></td><td>Referral tracking, real-booking checks and managing bookings from Nova Portal (Acuity&#39;s Powerhouse plan)</td></tr><tr><td><code>ACUITY_WEBHOOK_KEY</code></td><td>Accepting Acuity&#39;s webhook (<code>/acuity/webhook?key=…</code>)</td></tr><tr><td><code>ACUITY_CALENDAR_URL</code></td><td>Acuity&#39;s private calendar feed: booking details, the Nova Calendar tab and Nova Club&#39;s busy times</td></tr><tr><td><code>ACUITY_EMAIL_KEY</code></td><td>The Google Apps Script that forwards Acuity&#39;s emails (<code>tools/acuity-email-forwarder.gs</code>)</td></tr><tr><td><code>AGENT_NOVA_KEY</code></td><td>Nova Agent&#39;s routes (<code>/nova-agent/*</code>; <code>/memory/*</code>), and its online link (<code>/nova-agent/link</code>, the AgentLink Durable Object in <code>src/agent-relay.js</code>: Nova Agent&#39;s chat, Nova Missions, Nova Quests, Nova Calendar and Nova Visualizer online, through the studio PC)</td></tr><tr><td><code>VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY</code>, <code>VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY</code></td><td>Phone notifications (Web Push)</td></tr><tr><td><code>MAIL_API_URL</code>, <code>MAIL_KEY</code>, <code>ENQUIRY_EMAIL_TO</code>, <code>ENQUIRY_EMAIL_FROM</code></td><td>Emailing (the studio&#39;s own mail server on the VPS; enquiries, replies, invoices, newsletters)</td></tr><tr><td><code>GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID</code>, <code>GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET</code></td><td>Optional: Admin → Google keeps the same key without them (Nova Notes&#39; Google Docs, Nova Calendar and Gmail for bookings; Google is never a way to sign in, Nova Portal is)</td></tr><tr><td><code>GOOGLE_REFRESH_TOKEN</code>, <code>GOOGLE_CALENDAR_ID</code>, <code>GOOGLE_ACCOUNT</code></td><td>Optional overrides; normally set by &quot;Connect Google&quot; on <code>/admin/connections</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>STRIPE_SECRET_KEY</code>, <code>STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET</code></td><td>Nova Bot&#39;s own booking system: deposits (optional)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>Plain variables (in <code>wrangler.jsonc</code> or <code>--var</code>): <code>BOOKING_SYSTEM</code> (<code>acuity</code> or <code>nova</code>, the fallback for the switch), <code>PUBLIC_URL</code>, <code>SANDBOX</code>, <code>BOOKING_DETAILS_WAIT_SECONDS</code>.</p>\n<p>Bindings in <code>wrangler.jsonc</code>: <code>DB</code> (D1), <code>AI</code> (Workers AI), <code>CHAT_LIMIT</code>, <code>VOICE_LIMIT</code> and <code>CLUB_LIMIT</code> (rate limits), static assets from <code>public/</code>, the build step, and a cron trigger every minute.</p>\n<p>More detail lives alongside this file: README-ENQUIRIES.md (enquiries, booking links, free times, chat log), README-REFERRALS.md (referral codes and Acuity&#39;s webhook), README-SQUARESPACE.md (adding the widget to a Squarespace site) and PRIVACY-POLICY-NOVABOT.md (privacy policy wording).</p>\n<p>Booking details from Acuity&#39;s confirmation page (optional back-up)</p>\n<p>Paste this into Acuity → Integrations → Custom conversion tracking, under anything already there, replacing <code>YOUR-WORKER</code> with your Worker&#39;s address:</p>\n<pre><code>&lt;!-- Portal: sends this booking&#39;s details to the staff notification --&gt;\n&lt;div id=&quot;nv-booked&quot; hidden&gt;&lt;i&gt;%type%&lt;/i&gt;&lt;i&gt;%id%&lt;/i&gt;&lt;i&gt;%appointmentType%&lt;/i&gt;&lt;i&gt;%clientDate%&lt;/i&gt;&lt;i&gt;%clientTime%&lt;/i&gt;&lt;i&gt;%price%&lt;/i&gt;&lt;i&gt;%email%&lt;/i&gt;&lt;i&gt;%calendar%&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;script&gt;\n(function () {\n  var names = [&quot;type&quot;, &quot;id&quot;, &quot;session&quot;, &quot;date&quot;, &quot;time&quot;, &quot;price&quot;, &quot;email&quot;, &quot;calendar&quot;];\n  var values = document.querySelectorAll(&quot;#nv-booked i&quot;);\n  var query = names.map(function (name, i) { return name + &quot;=&quot; + encodeURIComponent(values[i].textContent.trim()); }).join(&quot;&amp;&quot;);\n  new Image().src = &quot;https://YOUR-WORKER/acuity/booked?&quot; + query;\n})();\n&lt;/script&gt;</code></pre>\n<p>The main source of booking details is Acuity&#39;s private calendar feed (Acuity → Sync with Other Calendars → 1-way Nova Calendar Sync, saved as <code>ACUITY_CALENDAR_URL</code>), which works on every Acuity plan and for bookings staff add themselves. Acuity&#39;s own booking emails are a second back-up: <code>tools/acuity-email-forwarder.gs</code> runs in the mailbox Acuity emails and passes each one to <code>/acuity/email</code>. Once emails are coming through, notifications wait for them (up to 3 minutes, then the once-a-minute cron sends them anyway).</p>","text":"Everything secret is a Wrangler secret ( npx wrangler secret put NAME ), or a line in .dev.vars for local runs. Names only; values never belong in the repository. Name Needed for ANTHROPIC_API_KEY Claude answers and memory (required live) ADMIN_PASSWORD Only proves it's you when setting up the very first Nova Portal admin ACUITY_USER_ID , ACUITY_API_KEY Referral tracking, real-booking checks and managing bookings from Nova Portal (Acuity's Powerhouse plan) ACUITY_WEBHOOK_KEY Accepting Acuity's webhook ( /acuity/webhook?key=… ) ACUITY_CALENDAR_URL Acuity's private calendar feed: booking details, the Nova Calendar tab and Nova Club's busy times ACUITY_EMAIL_KEY The Google Apps Script that forwards Acuity's emails ( tools/acuity-email-forwarder.gs ) AGENT_NOVA_KEY Nova Agent's routes ( /nova-agent/* ; /memory/* ), and its online link ( /nova-agent/link , the AgentLink Durable Object in src/agent-relay.js : Nova Agent's chat, Nova Missions, Nova Quests, Nova Calendar and Nova Visualizer online, through the studio PC) VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY , VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY Phone notifications (Web Push) MAIL_API_URL , MAIL_KEY , ENQUIRY_EMAIL_TO , ENQUIRY_EMAIL_FROM Emailing (the studio's own mail server on the VPS; enquiries, replies, invoices, newsletters) GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID , GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET Optional: Admin → Google keeps the same key without them (Nova Notes' Google Docs, Nova Calendar and Gmail for bookings; Google is never a way to sign in, Nova Portal is) GOOGLE_REFRESH_TOKEN , GOOGLE_CALENDAR_ID , GOOGLE_ACCOUNT Optional overrides; normally set by \"Connect Google\" on /admin/connections STRIPE_SECRET_KEY , STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET Nova Bot's own booking system: deposits (optional) Plain variables (in wrangler.jsonc or --var ): BOOKING_SYSTEM ( acuity or nova , the fallback for the switch), PUBLIC_URL , SANDBOX , BOOKING_DETAILS_WAIT_SECONDS . Bindings in wrangler.jsonc : DB (D1), AI (Workers AI), CHAT_LIMIT , VOICE_LIMIT and CLUB_LIMIT (rate limits), static assets from public/ , the build step, and a cron trigger every minute. More detail lives alongside this file: README-ENQUIRIES.md (enquiries, booking links, free times, chat log), README-REFERRALS.md (referral codes and Acuity's webhook), README-SQUARESPACE.md (adding the widget to a Squarespace site) and PRIVACY-POLICY-NOVABOT.md (privacy policy wording). Booking details from Acuity's confirmation page (optional back-up) Paste this into Acuity → Integrations → Custom conversion tracking, under anything already there, replacing YOUR-WORKER with your Worker's address: <!-- Nova Portal: sends this booking's details to the staff notification --> <div id=\"nv-booked\" hidden><i>%type%</i><i>%id%</i><i>%appointmentType%</i><i>%clientDate%</i><i>%clientTime%</i><i>%price%</i><i>%email%</i><i>%calendar%</i></div> <script> (function () { var names = [\"type\", \"id\", \"session\", \"date\", \"time\", \"price\", \"email\", \"calendar\"]; var values = document.querySelectorAll(\"#nv-booked i\"); var query = names.map(function (name, i) { return name + \"=\" + encodeURIComponent(values[i].textContent.trim()); }).join(\"&\"); new Image().src = \"https://YOUR-WORKER/acuity/booked?\" + query; })(); </script> The main source of booking details is Acuity's private calendar feed (Acuity → Sync with Other Calendars → 1-way Nova Calendar Sync, saved as ACUITY_CALENDAR_URL ), which works on every Acuity plan and for bookings staff add themselves. Acuity's own booking emails are a second back-up: tools/acuity-email-forwarder.gs runs in the mailbox Acuity emails and passes each one to /acuity/email . Once emails are coming through, notifications wait for them (up to 3 minutes, then the once-a-minute cron sends them anyway)."},{"id":"tests-4","title":"Tests","html":"<pre><code>npm test            # watch mode\nnpx vitest run      # once</code></pre>\n<p>388 tests across 27 files, fully offline: they run inside the Workers runtime (<code>@cloudflare/vitest-plugin</code>) with a local database and fake versions of Claude, Acuity, Google, Stripe and the mail server (<code>test/fakes.js</code>). Every key in <code>vitest.config.mjs</code> is a test-only stand-in. The original Acuity tests run against the default; <code>test/*-nova.spec.js</code> run with the switch on Nova, and <code>test/switch.spec.js</code> tests the switch itself. The memory engine and Nova Portal have their own (<code>test/memory.spec.js</code>, <code>test/portal.spec.js</code>).</p>","text":"npm test # watch mode npx vitest run # once 388 tests across 27 files, fully offline: they run inside the Workers runtime ( @cloudflare/vitest-plugin ) with a local database and fake versions of Claude, Acuity, Google, Stripe and the mail server ( test/fakes.js ). Every key in vitest.config.mjs is a test-only stand-in. The original Acuity tests run against the default; test/*-nova.spec.js run with the switch on Nova, and test/switch.spec.js tests the switch itself. The memory engine and Nova Portal have their own ( test/memory.spec.js , test/portal.spec.js )."},{"id":"deploying-your-own-copy-5","title":"Deploying your own copy","html":"<ol><li>Log in to Cloudflare: <code>npx wrangler login</code>.</li><li>Create the database: <code>npx wrangler d1 create novabot</code>, put its <code>database_id</code> in <code>wrangler.jsonc</code>, then <code>npx wrangler d1 migrations apply novabot --remote</code>.</li><li>Add the secrets you need from Configuration, at least <code>ANTHROPIC_API_KEY</code> and <code>ADMIN_PASSWORD</code>.</li><li>Swap Novacane&#39;s details for your own:</li><li class=\"sub\"><code>src/index.js</code>: <code>BOOKING_LINK</code>, <code>ENQUIRY_LINK</code>, <code>WHATSAPP_NUMBER</code>, <code>WHATSAPP_LINK</code>, <code>ALLOWED_ORIGINS</code>, and the studio information in <code>STUDIO_INFO</code></li><li class=\"sub\"><code>src/booking.js</code>: <code>ACUITY_OWNER</code> (the number after <code>owner=</code> in your Acuity booking page&#39;s address)</li><li class=\"sub\"><code>src/nova/studio.js</code> and <code>src/nova/booking.js</code> (<code>LIVE_URL</code>) for the Nova system</li><li class=\"sub\"><code>public/novabot.js</code>: <code>LIVE_WORKER_URL</code>, <code>BOOKING_LINK</code>, <code>PRIVACY_LINK</code></li><li>Deploy with <code>npm run deploy</code> (the build step copies Nova Index and Nova Portal in), then add the widget to your website (see README-SQUARESPACE.md).</li><li>Open <code>/portal/</code> to set up the first admin with the studio password, then invite the team.</li></ol>","text":"Log in to Cloudflare: npx wrangler login . Create the database: npx wrangler d1 create novabot , put its database_id in wrangler.jsonc , then npx wrangler d1 migrations apply novabot --remote . Add the secrets you need from Configuration, at least ANTHROPIC_API_KEY and ADMIN_PASSWORD . Swap Novacane's details for your own: src/index.js : BOOKING_LINK , ENQUIRY_LINK , WHATSAPP_NUMBER , WHATSAPP_LINK , ALLOWED_ORIGINS , and the studio information in STUDIO_INFO src/booking.js : ACUITY_OWNER (the number after owner= in your Acuity booking page's address) src/nova/studio.js and src/nova/booking.js ( LIVE_URL ) for the Nova system public/novabot.js : LIVE_WORKER_URL , BOOKING_LINK , PRIVACY_LINK Deploy with npm run deploy (the build step copies Nova Index and Nova Portal in), then add the widget to your website (see README-SQUARESPACE.md). Open /portal/ to set up the first admin with the studio password, then invite the team."},{"id":"project-layout-6","title":"Project layout","html":"<pre><code>public/novabot.js, novabot.css   the chat widget (served by the Worker)\npublic/app, portal, calendar, … Nova Agent&#39;s panels, copied in at build time (not in this repo)\n  app.js, app.css                  the tabs, the smart calendar, alerts, voice, pings\n  suite.js                         Nova Agent sheet, All links, What&#39;s changed\n  options.js, themes.js/.css       Options and the six themes\n  ambient.js, sfx.js               ambient music and sound effects\n  sw.js                            notifications with the app closed\n  memory/                          Index (copied in at build time, not in git)\npublic/portal/                   Portal&#39;s pages (copied in at build time, not in git)\nsrc/index.js                     the Worker: chat, voice, routes, NovaBot&#39;s instructions\nsrc/app-page.js                  Portal&#39;s staff API (/app/api/*, from Portal&#39;s old address)\nsrc/portal-ask.js                Ask Nova: questions about bookings, enquiries and alerts\nsrc/admin.js                     the admin pages\nsrc/links.js                     the master list: links, features, changelog\nsrc/memory/                      the memory engine (store, extract, routes)\nsrc/portal/                      Portal: sign-in, sessions, staff, planets\nsrc/booking.js                   session types, booking links, free times (public Acuity page)\nsrc/booking-form.js              the booking card&#39;s API\nsrc/book-session.js              booking checks (deposit first)\nsrc/manage-bookings.js           staff finding, cancelling, moving and changing bookings\nsrc/agent-nova.js                jobs, quests and alerts for Nova Agent\nsrc/enquiries.js                 enquiries, enquiry emails, chat log\nsrc/push.js                      notifications, the Alerts tab, real-booking checks\nsrc/booking-calendar.js          booking details from Acuity&#39;s calendar feed\nsrc/booking-details.js           booking details from Acuity&#39;s confirmation page\nsrc/booking-emails.js            booking details from Acuity&#39;s emails\nsrc/booking-pings.js             when booking notifications go out\nsrc/club-calendar.js             busy times for Nova Club\nsrc/referrals.js                 referral tracking (Acuity API)\nsrc/feedback.js                  what visitors said about NovaBot\nsrc/health.js                    daily Acuity API check\nsrc/mode.js                      the booking-system switch\nsrc/nova/                        Nova Bot&#39;s own booking system (Google, Gmail, Stripe)\nsrc/fonts/                       Saira, Geist Mono and Source Code Pro (SIL OFL)\nmigrations/                      D1 tables\ntest/                            Vitest tests and fakes\ntools/acuity-email-forwarder.gs  Google Apps Script that forwards Acuity&#39;s emails\nscripts/sync-apps.mjs            the build step: copies Index and Portal in\nscripts/sandbox-setup.mjs        sandbox setup\ndocs/media/                      README images (all sample data)</code></pre>","text":"public/novabot.js, novabot.css the chat widget (served by the Worker) public/app, portal, calendar, … Nova Agent's panels, copied in at build time (not in this repo) app.js, app.css the tabs, the smart calendar, alerts, voice, pings suite.js Nova Agent sheet, All links, What's changed options.js, themes.js/.css Options and the six themes ambient.js, sfx.js ambient music and sound effects sw.js notifications with the app closed memory/ Nova Index (copied in at build time, not in git) public/portal/ Nova Portal's pages (copied in at build time, not in git) src/index.js the Worker: chat, voice, routes, NovaBot's instructions src/app-page.js Nova Portal's staff API (/app/api/*, from Nova Portal's old address) src/portal-ask.js Ask Nova: questions about bookings, enquiries and alerts src/admin.js the admin pages src/links.js the master list: links, features, changelog src/memory/ the memory engine (store, extract, routes) src/portal/ Nova Portal: sign-in, sessions, staff, planets src/booking.js session types, booking links, free times (public Acuity page) src/booking-form.js the booking card's API src/book-session.js booking checks (deposit first) src/manage-bookings.js staff finding, cancelling, moving and changing bookings src/agent-nova.js jobs, quests and alerts for Nova Agent src/enquiries.js enquiries, enquiry emails, chat log src/push.js notifications, the Alerts tab, real-booking checks src/booking-calendar.js booking details from Acuity's calendar feed src/booking-details.js booking details from Acuity's confirmation page src/booking-emails.js booking details from Acuity's emails src/booking-pings.js when booking notifications go out src/club-calendar.js busy times for Nova Club src/referrals.js referral tracking (Acuity API) src/feedback.js what visitors said about NovaBot src/health.js daily Acuity API check src/mode.js the booking-system switch src/nova/ Nova Bot's own booking system (Google, Gmail, Stripe) src/fonts/ Saira, Geist Mono and Source Code Pro (SIL OFL) migrations/ D1 tables test/ Vitest tests and fakes tools/acuity-email-forwarder.gs Google Apps Script that forwards Acuity's emails scripts/sync-apps.mjs the build step: copies Nova Index and Nova Portal in scripts/sandbox-setup.mjs sandbox setup docs/media/ README images (all sample data)"}],"news":[],"history":{"total":149,"first":"2026-10-06T15:46:34+01:00","commits":[{"hash":"6fabcf5","date":"2026-10-14T12:29:05+01:00","subject":"The Fixer's looks check account: Nova Agent makes it with its key for one check (POST /nova-agent/looks-session), no password, a 45-minute session, deleted after; it can only look (requireStaff refuses it for writes and WebSockets) and it's left out of the team list, the status count and the inbox's people","body":""},{"hash":"795f683","date":"2026-10-14T05:06:33+01:00","subject":"A page the browser already has (304) says its deploy too (X-Nova-Build)","body":""},{"hash":"f469c70","date":"2026-10-14T05:01:07+01:00","subject":"Nova's pages say which deploy's files they go with (X-Nova-Build, from public/nova-build.json) for Nova Agent's service worker","body":""},{"hash":"a9495a0","date":"2026-10-14T04:43:35+01:00","subject":"Faster Nova: sync-apps writes public/nova-build.json (every file of Nova's with a fingerprint, for Nova Agent's service worker to keep on devices); Portal's calendar shows Acuity's feed from a copy up to 10 minutes old at once and reads a fresh one behind it","body":""},{"hash":"29a0b2c","date":"2026-10-14T03:08:58+01:00","subject":"Quests: Nova Agent's new panel online (/quests/, /agent/quests opens it inside Nova Agent; copied in with the other panels). Board's, Console's and Quests' copies stay out of git","body":""},{"hash":"5320edd","date":"2026-10-14T02:42:59+01:00","subject":"Ask Index: a plain-English question answered only from the memory the asker may read (typos forgiven), with numbered sources; one small cheap model call, cached until memory changes, no model call without a match; POST /memory/ask and /app/api/memory/ask (per-minute limit); it only reads","body":""},{"hash":"00bf437","date":"2026-10-14T02:40:33+01:00","subject":"Link check: Nova Bot answers Nova Agent's hello (here, linked) so a link it has lost is redone; deploys only reinstall packages when package-lock changed, with Nova Bot (or Nova Agent) stopped first (npm ci under a running one crashed it: spawn ETXTBSY, and left the link half-open)","body":""},{"hash":"c973a15","date":"2026-10-14T01:24:25+01:00","subject":"Privacy page: Nova's data lives on the studio's own server (VPSdime), the AI is Anthropic's Claude, Google handles Google features, email goes from the studio's own mail server (Gmail as the backup); no Cloudflare. Google setup: one web address (the online one) and the return address, no studio-computer address. Caddy: redirects say https:// (the runtime's proxy said http://)","body":""},{"hash":"709c92e","date":"2026-10-14T01:20:34+01:00","subject":"Mail settings: only MAIL_API_URL and MAIL_KEY (the old Resend names are gone from the server)","body":""},{"hash":"bc9bf43","date":"2026-10-14T01:12:15+01:00","subject":"Computer: the VPS only — no old host or switch-over; Nova Agent on the server (its service, since when, restart-agent, its problems) and the commands to move it","body":""},{"hash":"913f6d7","date":"2026-10-14T01:10:22+01:00","subject":"Newsletters go through the studio's own mail server; Resend removed from Nova Bot","body":"Campaigns: approving makes the list of opted-in people and the every-minute cron sends a small\nbatch (CAMPAIGN_BATCH, 10; CAMPAIGN_GAP_MS, 3 s apart), re-checking everyone before each batch.\nEach email has its own signed unsubscribe link (/unsubscribe asks first; one-click POST works)\nand List-Unsubscribe + List-Unsubscribe-Post headers. Approval hash and admin-only approve\nunchanged. The Resend client (src/resend-marketing.js), segments, broadcasts and stats are gone.\nEvery email goes to MAIL_API_URL with MAIL_KEY (RESEND_API_URL / RESEND_API_KEY still read as a\nfallback until the VPS's settings are renamed). UI, docs, privacy policy and tests reworded."},{"hash":"2ea8737","date":"2026-10-14T00:17:27+01:00","subject":"Switching back only brings the server's data home when the server's Nova Agent ran on it (.ran-here); job branches fetched under the right name","body":""},{"hash":"4bc74e7","date":"2026-10-14T00:16:23+01:00","subject":"agent-switch.sh: the checks before the yes don't swallow it","body":""},{"hash":"a42a6c3","date":"2026-10-14T00:15:53+01:00","subject":"VPS README: Nova Agent on the server (setup, switch, switch back, full laptop-off test, code sync, Claude Code sign-in, Console tunnel)","body":""},{"hash":"4f408ca","date":"2026-10-14T00:06:49+01:00","subject":"agent-setup.sh: the server's public address in the Claude Code sign-in hint","body":""},{"hash":"47eecde","date":"2026-10-14T00:04:29+01:00","subject":"Laptop-off checks: the booking card as the studio's website; test person cleaned up on both sides","body":""},{"hash":"b844846","date":"2026-10-14T00:02:47+01:00","subject":"Nova Agent on the server: vps/agent-setup.sh, agent-sync.sh, agent-code-sync.sh, agent-switch.sh (--rehearse), agent-switch-back.sh, full-laptop-off-test.sh (PASS/FAIL per check); nova-agent.service, sudo rules, nova-deploy-here; deploy-live.sh deploys locally on the server and won't undo the server's Fixer changes","body":""},{"hash":"334de55","date":"2026-10-14T00:02:47+01:00","subject":"VPS: put the browser's Origin back to https (wrangler dev's proxy rewrites it to http), so every 'only from this site's own pages' check passes again — all POSTs on the VPS were answered 403","body":""},{"hash":"af5b89f","date":"2026-10-13T23:51:42+01:00","subject":"Only one Nova Agent: the server's link wins (a PC's gets 4002), link status says where; status row is now Nova Agent (on the server / on the studio PC)","body":""},{"hash":"3cdc1d4","date":"2026-10-13T23:07:38+01:00","subject":"Status page in the VPS README (outside watchdog sign-up, PC watchdog, laptop-off test); laptop-off test finds the right database file","body":""},{"hash":"b63bfe4","date":"2026-10-13T23:03:47+01:00","subject":"vps/laptop-off-test.sh: unplug the studio PC for ~2 minutes, check what should keep working, put the result on the status page","body":""},{"hash":"3f45a4d","date":"2026-10-13T23:02:42+01:00","subject":"Status page: /status (in a browser) and /status.json, public and nothing personal","body":"A light per part (website chat tested for real every 6 hours by the timed jobs, Portal, sign-in,\nemails from the VPS mail server, bookings feed, timed jobs heartbeat, backups, Google, the\nserver, the studio PC and what keeps working without it), the last laptop-off test, a\nrate-limited Test the chat now button and an If something's red card. 503 when red, for an\noutside watchdog. Nova Agent's own fetch('/status') still goes to the PC. desk-status now\nreports the mail sender (counts and times only)."},{"hash":"50f5ab6","date":"2026-10-13T22:58:27+01:00","subject":"Retiring the old address: it sends people on to nova.novacane.co.uk","body":"vps/retire-old-address.sh (asks yes, not run yet) puts MOVED_TO on the pass-through: every page\nand app call at the old address gets a 308 to the same page at the new one; only Acuity's webhook\nand the Google email script are still passed on with their old keys, so Acuity needs no change."},{"hash":"a06500b","date":"2026-10-13T22:53:37+01:00","subject":"Nova's own address: nova.novacane.co.uk (links, emails, the website chat script, Computer, deploys); the old address still works while it's moved over","body":""},{"hash":"346156c","date":"2026-10-13T22:48:55+01:00","subject":"vps/deploy-live.sh: deploy to wherever Nova Bot is live (the VPS after the switch-over, Cloudflare otherwise), so a deploy never undoes the switch","body":""},{"hash":"575aab7","date":"2026-10-13T22:44:19+01:00","subject":"Desk is called Computer now (what people see: messages, scripts' output, service names, the README); inside it's still desk","body":""},{"hash":"d43f742","date":"2026-10-13T22:34:09+01:00","subject":"switch-keys: writes only when something changed, and keeps the file's owner (Nova Bot reads it)","body":""},{"hash":"baaaa9a","date":"2026-10-13T22:32:33+01:00","subject":"vps/README: the switch-over, one command each way","body":""},{"hash":"63ad0f9","date":"2026-10-13T22:24:15+01:00","subject":"Switch-over: Desk says which side is live, the switch commands, and warns when newsletters can't send; tests for the pass-through and the VPS's front door","body":""},{"hash":"80bfc68","date":"2026-10-13T22:20:54+01:00","subject":"WIP switch-over: pass-through Worker, the VPS's front door (signed visitor and address), switch-keys, switch.sh and switch-back.sh","body":""},{"hash":"6de79dc","date":"2026-10-13T21:02:11+01:00","subject":"Desk mail: the DNS records (SPF keeping Google Workspace, DKIM nova key, mail A record) and the reverse DNS to set","body":""},{"hash":"19e0bea","date":"2026-10-13T21:01:33+01:00","subject":"WIP Desk mail: Nova Bot's single emails can go to the VPS's own mail service (RESEND_API_URL), VPS first with Gmail as the backup (MAIL_FIRST=vps)","body":""},{"hash":"9fad92e","date":"2026-10-13T19:50:21+01:00","subject":"Desk: the data copy loads with sqlite3 (big rows), builds the new copy beside the old one, and always starts Nova Bot again","body":""},{"hash":"f32bfbb","date":"2026-10-13T19:46:04+01:00","subject":"Desk: Caddy keeps the runtime's /__scheduled door closed from outside (handle block, so it runs before the catch-all)","body":""},{"hash":"a758f45","date":"2026-10-13T19:45:15+01:00","subject":"Desk: the VPS's README (what runs there, commands, secrets, the cutover plan and rollback)","body":""},{"hash":"a98df50","date":"2026-10-13T19:34:43+01:00","subject":"Desk: /app/api/desk — Nova Bot here and the VPS side by side (the VPS asked with a token from AGENT_NOVA_KEY), restart and back up for admins in a browser","body":""},{"hash":"cc473da","date":"2026-10-13T19:32:47+01:00","subject":"WIP Desk: the VPS's status service (token from AGENT_NOVA_KEY), behind Caddy at /desk-status/","body":""},{"hash":"39e19d1","date":"2026-10-13T19:29:40+01:00","subject":"WIP Desk: Nova Bot on the VPS (config, services, Caddy, deploy, data sync, backups, secrets)","body":""},{"hash":"0a2eda5","date":"2026-10-13T18:41:51+01:00","subject":"Website chat booking in lite mode: an even margin round the card, clear of the chat's rounded bottom corners","body":""},{"hash":"e3d30d9","date":"2026-10-13T18:37:27+01:00","subject":"Console online: its page copied in and opened inside Nova Agent; only its state and (admins) the log passed on to the PC, never a terminal","body":""},{"hash":"4e7cb2a","date":"2026-10-13T18:31:12+01:00","subject":"Website chat booking: the chat is as tall as the card (no big empty space under it), with an even margin round the card","body":""},{"hash":"53dd660","date":"2026-10-13T11:36:59+01:00","subject":"Board files online from Drive: tests (PC's own upload, linking only Board's own files, whole and Range), any Drive id shape","body":""},{"hash":"3f8c9df","date":"2026-10-13T11:25:53+01:00","subject":"WIP Board media: Board files from Drive first (Range works), big files uploaded by the PC straight to Drive, a cut-off answer is an error (not a shorter file), 95 MB online","body":""},{"hash":"062dc25","date":"2026-10-13T11:03:22+01:00","subject":"Board online: its page copied in and opened inside Nova Agent, its addresses passed on to the studio PC for signed-in staff","body":""},{"hash":"2c18e05","date":"2026-10-12T22:07:18+01:00","subject":"Google: YouTube left out of the main sign-in (Google refuses Drive and YouTube together); it gets its own sign-in","body":""},{"hash":"33fd1e5","date":"2026-10-12T22:02:40+01:00","subject":"Website chat booking: the title stays still, a slimmer header and the window's full height while booking, so the card fits with no scrolling","body":""},{"hash":"cba2d57","date":"2026-10-12T22:00:48+01:00","subject":"Shared notes carry \"Keep in Google Docs\" (gdocKeep) so Notes can show it","body":""},{"hash":"c086324","date":"2026-10-12T21:58:44+01:00","subject":"Website chat: the Book button stays still (no sweeping light, no stars sliding on hover), it just glows brighter","body":""},{"hash":"fd5845f","date":"2026-10-12T21:57:24+01:00","subject":"Website chat booking card: compact (no big gaps), as tall as its contents, and no corner drawing crossing its border","body":""},{"hash":"59e3cd0","date":"2026-10-12T21:49:21+01:00","subject":"Website chat booking card: its buttons in their own footer under the fields (never on top of each other), and clear of the chat's rounded corners so the whole border shows","body":""},{"hash":"ea47a0f","date":"2026-10-12T21:44:19+01:00","subject":"Website chat: the booking card fits the chat (fields scroll inside it, Book stays in sight); Send is the glowing pink of Book a session, not near-black","body":""},{"hash":"8e73b7a","date":"2026-10-12T21:07:51+01:00","subject":"Google round two, tested: the setup link switches on Tasks and YouTube; tests for the inbox, Meet, Today, Tasks, Docs, invoices, YouTube and search","body":""},{"hash":"64689ea","date":"2026-10-12T21:05:43+01:00","subject":"WIP Google round two: Gmail inbox, Meet, Tasks, Docs, invoices, YouTube","body":""},{"hash":"2c2a1b6","date":"2026-10-12T20:46:24+01:00","subject":"Google within the free Workers plan: small resumable steps, links read once and written together, holds when Google is busy, Connect again (with one ping a day) when the connection is turned down, Sync now in the background","body":""},{"hash":"3f5ef1f","date":"2026-10-12T20:35:18+01:00","subject":"Google Contacts: read the links once and skip contacts that aren't the studio's, so a big Google account doesn't time out","body":""},{"hash":"d91c481","date":"2026-10-12T20:25:19+01:00","subject":"Google key: checked with Google when it's saved, so a wrong or cut-short secret is caught at Save, not at Connect","body":""},{"hash":"20a997f","date":"2026-10-12T20:19:55+01:00","subject":"Admin pages open Portal at view=manage (ad blockers block \"view=ad…\" addresses)","body":""},{"hash":"51ff390","date":"2026-10-12T19:36:52+01:00","subject":"Connect Google: a one-time pass from Portal, so connecting works however the admin is signed in; Google's answer checked by its state cookie","body":""},{"hash":"8426430","date":"2026-10-12T19:28:07+01:00","subject":"Live chat: someone from the studio answers a website chat themselves (Take over, reply, Hand back); the visitor's chat shows them by first name","body":""},{"hash":"ec94208","date":"2026-10-12T18:52:45+01:00","subject":"Google everywhere: Calendar both ways, approved emails from Gmail and replies back into Enquiries, Contacts, Drive, the Money sheet, Docs, and Agent's read-only tools","body":""},{"hash":"5847548","date":"2026-10-12T17:25:30+01:00","subject":"Test stuff: things that look like tests or copies, with reasons, Delete (into a bin) and Not a test","body":"Admins see them in Portal → Test stuff; Nova Agent's key can only read the list."},{"hash":"3fae9af","date":"2026-10-12T16:31:50+01:00","subject":"Money: invoices with an admin's approval, payments, reminders and expenses","body":"New tables (migrations/0029_money.sql, new tables only). Invoices wait for an admin's Approve in\nPortal (a hash of exactly what was approved; the sender refuses anything that changed), then the\nclient is emailed a link to their invoice's page (/invoice/<token>: printable, pay by card\nthrough Stripe's checkout or by bank transfer). Stripe's webhook records invoice payments once.\nPayments keep the client list's invoiced and owed amounts in step. Reminders wait for an Approve\ntoo. Expenses from Nova Agent's key come in unconfirmed. The agent's key can't approve, send,\nremind, void, pay or change settings. Receipts' addresses are relayed to the PC for staff."},{"hash":"b72a1b1","date":"2026-10-12T16:21:21+01:00","subject":"Social (Quest 4): Facebook and Instagram posts, only after an admin approves them","body":"- migrations/0027_social.sql: social_posts, social_post_log, social_comments, social_followers\n  (new tables only)\n- src/social.js: drafts from Agent or staff; an admin's Approve (cookie) stores a hash of exactly\n  what was approved; Meta's Graph API posts it now or at its time (Instagram containers carried on\n  by the minute's cron), each platform once; without Meta, it waits to be posted by hand. Hourly\n  results, followers and comments; replies wait for approval too\n- /social/media/<post>/<file>?t=…: signed addresses Meta fetches the files from, only while that\n  approval is being posted; the files come from the studio computer over its link (askPC), or\n  SOCIAL_MEDIA_BASE later\n- Portal's /app/api/social…, Agent's /nova-agent/social… (no approve or post), Services entry"},{"hash":"916c371","date":"2026-10-12T16:14:34+01:00","subject":"Inbox: enquiries sorted like tickets, a Spam folder, saved replies, chats marked","body":"- Enquiries move between New, Open, Waiting on them (replied), Done and Spam in one\n  press; who's on it, a label, search; the badge counts New and Open.\n- A plain spam filter on arrival (links, throwaway addresses, spam phrases, mashing,\n  a busy visitor), with the reasons kept. Spam doesn't ping or email anyone; nothing\n  is deleted; Not spam moves it back. Spam stays out of clients and Ask Nova.\n- Saved replies for routine questions; they only fill the reply box.\n- Website chats can be marked needs-a-person or done.\n- Agent's key can sort enquiries and read saved replies; it can't send anything.\n- migrations/0030_inbox.sql only adds columns and two tables."},{"hash":"5ee6ba3","date":"2026-10-12T16:05:44+01:00","subject":"One-to-one emails (outreach): approved by an admin, only to people the studio may email","body":"A personal email to one business, client or someone who wrote in. Agent and staff write them;\nonly an admin in a browser approves, rejects or test-sends. Approval stores a hash of exactly\nwhat was approved and the sender takes it once. UK GDPR / PECR checks: never anyone who opted\nout, business only at a work address, a client only about their booking unless they consented,\na reply only to someone who wrote in. Every email has a footer with /no-thanks (a Confirm\nbutton records the opt-out). New tables only: migrations/0028_outreach.sql."},{"hash":"edb55d2","date":"2026-10-12T15:25:38+01:00","subject":"Fixer: Nova Agent at 1280px: still loading after 20 seconds","body":"I couldn't load the page in a browser here, but the most likely cause is the pictures on Nova Agent's \"Today in music\" front page. They come from Wikipedia and Apple through Nova Bot, and some had no time limit while others could wait twice in a row. Now each picture gets one 8-second limit in total. If that runs out, the picture quietly doesn't show and the page finishes loading. All 727 Nova Bot tests pass, including 3 new ones.\nPrepared by the Fixer with Claude Code; waits for an admin's approval."},{"hash":"c72d477","date":"2026-10-12T01:39:49+01:00","subject":"Fixer: Nova Agent at 390px: a file didn't load: /music-world/photo/Nina_Simo…","body":"The musician photo beside the quote on Nova Agent's music front page (and the other small pictures there) could show up as a failed file, an error 502. Nova Bot now stops waiting on Wikipedia after 8 seconds and answers \"no photo\". If Nova Agent can't reach Nova Bot at all, it now gives that same quiet \"no photo\" for these pictures instead of an error. One step was blocked: my first try at the Nova Bot edit was a small script, and it needed approval that nobody here could give. I made the same change with the normal file editor instead. New tests check both cases and pass, and the type check …\nPrepared by the Fixer with Claude Code; waits for an admin's approval."},{"hash":"3f29fb8","date":"2026-10-11T11:50:32+01:00","subject":"The Fixer online: its addresses relayed to the PC for admins only, its pings to admins' phones, its page copied in","body":""},{"hash":"b76a17e","date":"2026-10-11T11:20:42+01:00","subject":"P0-4: quests, missions and reminders are each person's own","body":"- Quest and mission reminders go to the quest's owner's phones (Nova Agent\n  sends `owner`), unless phones were picked; without an owner, the studio\n  owner's as before. Never another person's phone.\n- Portal's Quests: your own by default; admins can switch to everyone's\n  (?who=everyone). Quests from before owners are the studio owner's.\n- Portal taps say who tapped, so Nova Agent keeps staff to their own.\n- The relay passes each person's Agent chat history (/chat/history,\n  /actions/chat/clear, /actions/chat/adopt) to the PC as them.\nNo database changes."},{"hash":"171ea91","date":"2026-10-11T01:43:33+01:00","subject":"Index: saving a file never drops lines already in it (only the cleanup's report, with the bin, removes old ones)","body":""},{"hash":"a6cf777","date":"2026-10-11T01:42:03+01:00","subject":"P0-5 Index cleanup: checks and repeats on every write, a dry-run cleanup, a 30-day bin","body":"- Every memory write (Index/Portal edits, Agent- and AI-learned facts, website facts waiting\n  for approval, approvals) refuses empty, placeholder, punctuation-only, too-short, too-long\n  and cut-off facts and repeats in the same file, normalising spaces; each refusal says why.\n  An empty file isn't saved.\n- Admin-only cleanup: POST /app/api/memory/cleanup/check saves and returns a report of what\n  WOULD go (empty/junk files, junk and repeated lines, junk and repeated waiting facts; the\n  first/oldest copy stays). POST cleanup/apply takes that report's id and ids, re-checks each\n  and removes only those. Recorded in memory_cleanups; removed entries (and files deleted in\n  Index) go to memory_removed and can be put back for 30 days.\n- The listing says which files each person may change (editable) and whether they're an admin.\n- migrations/0026_memory_cleanup.sql only adds two tables."},{"hash":"7681a20","date":"2026-10-11T01:22:27+01:00","subject":"Approval rule everywhere; booking-form marketing tick; plain Powerhouse message","body":"- Nova's own booking system: the staff chat can check and summarise a change but never carry\n  it out (confirmed true is refused; staff do it by hand until an approval step exists).\n  carryOutNovaChange() keeps the changes for that step and the tests; no AI can call it.\n- Client list: a tick in a 'send me studio news' question on Acuity's booking form records a\n  marketing yes (from the customer, with the question as the source), only for clients with\n  nothing recorded yet, so an unsubscribe or a staff no is never undone.\n- Test booking: without Acuity's Powerhouse plan the Acuity test says so plainly, and how to\n  check bookings by hand meanwhile."},{"hash":"77239ed","date":"2026-10-11T00:37:15+01:00","subject":"Campaigns: fan sign-up confirms with a button (an email scanner opening the link can't sign anyone up); preview page with its own rules for Portal","body":""},{"hash":"650fa4b","date":"2026-10-11T00:35:29+01:00","subject":"Email campaigns (Quest 3): newsletters on Resend, sent only after an admin approves them","body":"- migrations/0025: fans (double opt-in), email_campaigns, email_campaign_log\n- src/campaigns.js: drafts from Nova Agent's AI or staff wait as pending_approval (admins'\n  phones get a quiet ping); only an admin with Portal's browser cookie can approve, reject or\n  test-send. Approval stores a hash of subject, body, audience and send time; any edit clears it\n  (a scheduled send is cancelled in Resend) and the sender refuses a mismatch. Approve is one\n  guarded UPDATE, so two presses send once.\n- Sync to Resend: segments \"Nova · Fans / Studio clients / Everyone\"; only confirmed fans and\n  clients with marketing consent go in (everyone else out); each contact gets a `why` property\n  for the footer. Unsubscribes come back hourly: fan -> unsubscribed, client -> consent no with a\n  consent-log entry by 'customer'. Stats (sent, delivered, opened, clicked, bounced,\n  unsubscribed, complained) ref"},{"hash":"f107ac0","date":"2026-10-11T00:20:11+01:00","subject":"Client list (Quest 2): clients from Acuity's calendar feed, its webhook, enquiries and CSV imports; bookings from the feed for Nova Agent","body":"- migrations/0024_clients.sql: clients, client_sessions, client_consent_log (marketing consent NO by default)\n- src/clients.js: matching (email any case, else mobile, else exact name), syncs that change nothing when run twice\n  and never overwrite staff edits, the webhook hook (never throws), CSV import (appointments and clients, UK times\n  to UTC), the list and its filters, staff edits with a consent log\n- Portal: /app/api/clients… (import and sync for admins only); Nova Agent: /nova-agent/clients/… (read-only)\n  and /nova-agent/bookings-feed\n- The every-minute cron syncs every 30 minutes"},{"hash":"6801f9f","date":"2026-10-10T23:56:04+01:00","subject":"Acuity API: a refusal (401/403, e.g. the plan doesn't include the API) says 'Acuity refused' with Acuity's reason, not 'unreachable'","body":""},{"hash":"ee463e4","date":"2026-10-10T23:53:48+01:00","subject":"Booking actions: an admin's edits can be just what changed (merged over the saved proposal)","body":""},{"hash":"41f7ad5","date":"2026-10-10T23:43:15+01:00","subject":"Booking actions: session type/price/paid changes need approval too; a change cut off part-way shows as failed","body":"change_booking_extras now proposes an 'extras' action; only once an admin approves does\nNova Agent get the job. An approved change that never finished (Nova Bot stopped part-way)\nshows as failed after 5 minutes, telling the admin to check Acuity."},{"hash":"6cc28c2","date":"2026-10-10T23:40:34+01:00","subject":"Acuity API with approved booking actions (Nova Bot half of Quest 1)","body":"- src/acuity/api.js: one Acuity API client (Basic auth, 10 s timeout, 429 retries\n  with Retry-After, one retry on 5xx/network except POST) and read helpers with UTC\n  times; UK wall clock <-> Europe/London offset helpers.\n- src/booking-actions.js + migrations/0023_booking_actions.sql: AI-proposed booking\n  changes (create, reschedule, cancel, update, block_add, block_remove), saved as\n  pending with a summary Nova Bot writes from Acuity's data; admins pinged. Only an\n  admin with a Portal cookie session can edit / approve / reject; approve is one\n  guarded UPDATE and execution is claimed once, so a double press runs it once.\n- Nova Agent routes: /nova-agent/acuity/* (read-only), /nova-agent/booking-actions\n  (list) and /propose; /next reports bookingsChanged and wakes early on news.\n- Portal routes: /app/api/booking-actions (+ approve, edit, reject).\n- Acuity's webhook records bookings_"},{"hash":"b14f132","date":"2026-10-10T23:14:25+01:00","subject":"Test booking: an Acuity test that checks what customers actually use","body":"Portal → Admin → Test booking now runs a real booking in Acuity as staff (admin=true,\nnoEmail=true: no payment, nobody emailed), named 'Nova TEST booking', then checks Acuity's\nwebhook reached Nova Bot, the staff alert (only to the admin's own phones, if asked; never\nAlerts), and Acuity's calendar feed (Portal's Calendar), and cancels it in Acuity by itself.\nThe minute timer cancels any test still booked after 15 minutes. Tests are skipped by\nreferral tracking. One at a time. No database change (kept in settings).\nNova's own system's test is folded below; it now says Google isn't connected and greys out\nRun instead of showing 'Something went wrong (502)'."},{"hash":"0e74740","date":"2026-10-10T19:18:04+01:00","subject":"Enquiries: WhatsApp, calls and texts from your own phone, recorded in the conversation; How it works list","body":"Portal opens WhatsApp, Messages or the dialler with the customer's full international\nnumber and the message filled in, then records what happened (POST /enquiries/logged).\nNova sends nothing itself. GET /services lists what each part runs on (Resend, Claude,\nStripe, Cloudflare...) and whether it's set up, never a key; Send me a test email goes\nto the person who pressed it, once a minute at most."},{"hash":"689cab8","date":"2026-10-10T16:57:24+01:00","subject":"Enquiries: reply from Portal and Agent; Agent only drafts, a person approves","body":"- One conversation per enquiry (migration 0022: enquiry_messages, consent, don't contact)\n- Staff Send / notes / edit, Approve & send, discard drafts, Retry (browser cookie only)\n- Nova Agent's key can list, read and draft; nothing it can call approves or sends\n- Each reply goes once (guarded updates, press keys, Resend idempotency keys), to the\n  enquiry's address only, with the UK GDPR footer and a stop link (/enquiry/stop)\n- Quiet staff ping when a draft is waiting"},{"hash":"554b8ce","date":"2026-10-10T16:34:25+01:00","subject":"NovaBot: nothing goes to the studio for a reply without a name, an email and a mobile number","body":"- send_enquiry needs all three (checked in code); the mobile must look like one (UK 07 / +44 7,\n  or a number from abroad with its country code); it's kept as they wrote it\n- NovaBot asks for whichever are missing whenever someone wants the studio to get back to them\n- The chat page's 'use the booking card' rule leaves those questions alone"},{"hash":"bc9ba72","date":"2026-10-10T16:08:03+01:00","subject":"Test booking for admins: run the booking flow end to end without real money","body":"Portal → Admin → Test booking (/admin/test-booking, admins only, Origin-checked)\nruns one pretend booking through Nova Bot's own booking engine and ticks off\neach step: slot found, booking created, payment (skipped, or faked in Stripe\nTEST mode only; simulated with no Stripe call when only a live key is set),\nconfirmation email (preview; sent only to the admin if asked), calendar event\n(read back), alerts (preview; only the admin's own phones if asked).\nTest bookings are flagged (bookings.test, migration 0021) and shown as TEST;\nthey use made-up details, never email or alert anyone else, never take a real\npayment or refund, don't block customers' times unless the admin chooses, stay\nout of Nova Club's busy times, reminders, referrals and NovaBot's tools and\ncounts. \"Remove all test bookings\" removes them with their calendar events, and\nthe every-minute cron removes any older than 24 hour"},{"hash":"0cd1ee1","date":"2026-10-10T15:52:31+01:00","subject":"Quest and mission reminders go to the quest's phones, or the studio owner's (not every phone)","body":""},{"hash":"355e29b","date":"2026-10-10T15:43:29+01:00","subject":"Portal can change a quest's mode (queued for Nova Agent like every quest tap)","body":""},{"hash":"89d20de","date":"2026-10-10T15:14:26+01:00","subject":"node_modules is never part of the repo (not even as a link)","body":""},{"hash":"525e752","date":"2026-10-10T15:04:13+01:00","subject":"Portal: emails and passwords change only when signed in, from Portal","body":"- PATCH /staff/:id { email }: yourself (staff confirm with their password) or anyone (admins)\n- POST /staff/:id/password: an admin sets someone else's password; they're signed out\n  (someone still invited is let in)"},{"hash":"98b5535","date":"2026-10-10T14:58:13+01:00","subject":"Calendar reminders: sent only once a phone takes them, tried again, flagged if they never arrive; pick which phone gets each","body":"- A reminder counts as sent only when a phone took it; otherwise it's tried each minute for\n  15 minutes, then marked failed and Portal's Alerts says it didn't arrive\n- Phones remember who turned them on and what they are; GET /app/api/push/phones lists them\n- An event's reminders go to the phones it picked, else the studio owner's phones\n  (phones from before owners count as the owner's)\n- Edits made to the latest version save even when the device's clock is behind (base)\n- Migration 0020_reminder_delivery.sql"},{"hash":"f1d0a0f","date":"2026-10-10T14:34:16+01:00","subject":"Every deploy has a version (/app-version) the apps check to refresh themselves","body":""},{"hash":"872bcff","date":"2026-10-10T13:59:59+01:00","subject":"Portal can be its own phone app again: its pages decide whether to open in Nova Agent","body":""},{"hash":"42a8399","date":"2026-10-10T13:27:14+01:00","subject":"Portal everywhere: no more Portal (names, addresses, code, docs)","body":"The staff app is Portal in every word: notifications, the Ask feature (portal-ask.js), Index's\nmemory scope, the admin link, comments, tests and docs. Nova Agent's routes are /nova-agent/* only\n(the older addresses are gone; the PC has used the new ones since 2026-10-08). Migration 0019\nrenames stored text (remembered facts' source, facts, alert history) that still used the old\nname. The one-off link-fixing tool, already run, is removed."},{"hash":"ca5d1d9","date":"2026-10-09T16:41:51+01:00","subject":"/music-world/img: an exact Apple Music cover, served from here","body":""},{"hash":"29d0176","date":"2026-10-09T16:38:37+01:00","subject":"/music-world/file/<name>: one exact Commons photo, served from here","body":""},{"hash":"a2e835d","date":"2026-10-09T16:33:46+01:00","subject":"/music-world photos and art served from here (not redirects): nothing in the browser blocks them","body":""},{"hash":"d996840","date":"2026-10-09T04:27:42+01:00","subject":"/music-world: a fresh cache (forgets the early misses)","body":""},{"hash":"34b4431","date":"2026-10-09T04:25:38+01:00","subject":"/music-world: Apple's current chart address with a browser identity, Wikipedia's new picture host, album art lookup","body":""},{"hash":"416c43a","date":"2026-10-09T04:13:55+01:00","subject":"Nova Agent's front page music bits: /music-world (live Top 10 across 12 markets) and musicians' photos","body":""},{"hash":"4310d50","date":"2026-10-09T02:31:26+01:00","subject":"Sign-in details carry the planet's colours (for Nova Agent's planet colouring)","body":""},{"hash":"48897b9","date":"2026-10-08T23:34:26+01:00","subject":"Shared notes: /notes-api/ for the team's notes","body":"Migration 0018 (shared_notes), staff-only API with conflict-safe saves\n(a clash keeps both: the second becomes a conflicted copy), refused stale\ndeletes, change paging by rev, size and rate limits."},{"hash":"46482fa","date":"2026-10-08T17:45:50+01:00","subject":"Merge branch 'main' into calendar-pro","body":""},{"hash":"0402fe8","date":"2026-10-08T17:45:50+01:00","subject":"WIP calendar-pro","body":""},{"hash":"738a7ee","date":"2026-10-08T17:44:17+01:00","subject":"Admin addresses open Portal's Admin section","body":""},{"hash":"8e0a8e3","date":"2026-10-08T16:59:59+01:00","subject":"Admin pages on phones: rows as cards, swipeable tabs","body":"Each table row becomes a small card with every value named after its column;\nname-value tables stack; the tabs are one row you swipe; number tiles in one\ncompact row; 16px fields; no blur."},{"hash":"e37085c","date":"2026-10-08T14:01:04+01:00","subject":"tools/add-admin.mjs: make an admin straight away (no invite)","body":"Asks for a name, an email and a hidden password, then adds them to the live\ndatabase as an active admin."},{"hash":"881c629","date":"2026-10-08T13:48:41+01:00","subject":"Any password the person likes (not empty, not over 200 characters)","body":"Guessing is still held back by the sign-in rate limit."},{"hash":"6dc17c0","date":"2026-10-08T13:44:08+01:00","subject":"Portal: POST /auth/password to choose a new password","body":"Admins needn't give the old one; staff confirm it. Other sign-ins end."},{"hash":"4b2ff2d","date":"2026-10-08T13:33:58+01:00","subject":"Portal is the one sign-in: no Sign in with Google","body":"Sign in with Google is gone (its routes, the PC hand-off, the per-person\nGoogle email links and its redirect address in Admin → Google). Google stays a\nconnection for Docs, Calendar and Gmail. /auth/google-status tells signed-in\nstaff whether Google is set up and as whom (Portal's You page, Notes)."},{"hash":"082d92b","date":"2026-10-08T13:28:18+01:00","subject":"Merge branch 'google' into relay","body":""},{"hash":"7bb7999","date":"2026-10-08T13:27:09+01:00","subject":"The PC link: Nova Agent online, through the studio PC","body":"AgentLink (a Durable Object) holds the socket the studio PC opens to\n/nova-agent/link with AGENT_NOVA_KEY. Nova Agent's own addresses are passed\nto it for signed-in staff (the Visualizer's feeds for admins), streamed, with\npath tricks refused and changes only from this site; PC off answers 503\n{ pcOffline } straight away. Calendar's page online gets calendar-sync.js\n(copied in at build) so it uses Nova Agent's calendar."},{"hash":"ac5fd6e","date":"2026-10-08T13:26:26+01:00","subject":"Google, set up from inside Nova Agent; Sign in with Google","body":"- Admin → Google: a step-at-a-time setup (buttons to the right Google\n  Cloud pages, copy buttons for every address), then paste the key and\n  press Connect Google. The client ID is kept in settings, the secret and\n  the refresh token encrypted (AES-GCM, key from AGENT_NOVA_KEY via HKDF).\n  Cloudflare secrets, if set, still win. Every Google feature reads the\n  key through one place (nova/google-keys.js).\n- Connect Google runs in a small window and comes back (Google won't show\n  inside Nova Agent).\n- Sign in with Google (/auth/google/*): openid + email only, state and\n  PKCE; matches the verified Google email to a Portal account (or a Google\n  email an admin linked). The studio PC gets a two-minute, single-use code\n  bound to a verifier only it has, and swaps it for its own sign-in.\n- /auth/google/available tells the buttons (and Notes) when it's set up."},{"hash":"780350e","date":"2026-10-08T13:15:37+01:00","subject":"Merge branch 'main' into relay","body":"# Conflicts:\n#\twrangler.jsonc"},{"hash":"84c681a","date":"2026-10-08T13:15:28+01:00","subject":"WIP: the PC link (from the earlier attempt)","body":""},{"hash":"364e6ca","date":"2026-10-08T12:33:36+01:00","subject":"Old Lossless preview site: redirect into Nova Agent too","body":""},{"hash":"019afe7","date":"2026-10-08T12:03:07+01:00","subject":"Privacy policy: the staff app is Nova Agent","body":""},{"hash":"f4ab37a","date":"2026-10-08T12:00:35+01:00","subject":"/agent/ is the only address","body":"Any page opened in a browser that isn't Nova Agent goes to /agent/ (a panel's\naddress, an old one or /agent/<panel> opens that panel). Files, the website\nchat's customer pages (/book, /referral, /privacy) and connecting Google stay.\nThe old Notes, Calendar and Lossless sites send people into Nova Agent, and\ntools/only-agent-links.mjs brings Admin → Links down to the one address."},{"hash":"bc5d96d","date":"2026-10-08T11:50:33+01:00","subject":"Links: drop Nova Agent's old main-address links now it's at /agent/","body":""},{"hash":"76f2409","date":"2026-10-08T11:48:07+01:00","subject":"Nova Agent at /agent/; the main address is Nova Bot's again","body":"A browser opening / goes on to /agent/; the website chat still POSTs to /.\n/agent/<panel> opens Nova Agent with that panel, and panels opened on their\nown go to /agent/?open=<panel>. The links list points at /agent/."},{"hash":"df52ab7","date":"2026-10-08T11:38:31+01:00","subject":"Nova Agent at the main address; the panels open only inside it","body":"- GET / is Nova Agent's page (web/agent/chat.html, copied to\n  public/index.html at build time, with its icons, manifest and /sw.js).\n  The website chat still POSTs to /; the sandbox keeps its demo page.\n- A panel's page opened on its own (Sec-Fetch-Dest: document) goes to\n  /?open=<its address>; inside Nova Agent's viewer (iframe) it loads as\n  itself. Not pages: Lossless audio's signalling, connecting Google (it\n  leaves Nova Agent: Google won't show inside a frame), files, the API.\n  run_worker_first sends / and the panels' pages through the Worker.\n- Portal, Index and the admin pages may be shown inside Nova Agent (same\n  site only: SAMEORIGIN, frame-ancestors 'self'); Nova Agent itself isn't\n  shown inside other pages. The admin pages fit the Admin panel.\n- tools/fix-links.mjs: for the studio team, just Nova Agent online and on\n  the studio computer (the panels are inside it); the d"},{"hash":"3104217","date":"2026-10-08T02:16:39+01:00","subject":"Merge branch 'portal-merge' into sign-in","body":"# Conflicts:\n#\tsrc/index.js"}],"work":[],"workCount":0,"workStat":""}}],"addresses":[{"title":"The apps","note":"Nova Agent and its panels. Open Nova Agent and every panel is inside it.","items":[{"name":"Nova Agent","path":"/agent/","what":"The app for everyone: Agent, quests and every panel. Add it to your phone's home screen.","url":"https://nova.novacane.co.uk/agent/"},{"name":"Portal","path":"/portal/","what":"Enquiries, bookings, clients, campaigns, money and settings.","url":"https://nova.novacane.co.uk/portal/"},{"name":"Calendar","path":"/calendar/","what":"Note cards and day cards, with your quests on them.","url":"https://nova.novacane.co.uk/calendar/"},{"name":"Notes","path":"/notes/","what":"Notes and documents, shared with the team.","url":"https://nova.novacane.co.uk/notes/"},{"name":"Quests","path":"/quests/","what":"Every quest: add one in your own words, Focus, List, Board and Today.","url":"https://nova.novacane.co.uk/quests/"},{"name":"Board","path":"/board/","what":"Boards of cards for plans, files, pictures and video.","url":"https://nova.novacane.co.uk/board/"},{"name":"Index","path":"/app/memory/","what":"Nova Agent's memory: everything it knows, searchable.","url":"https://nova.novacane.co.uk/app/memory/"},{"name":"Console","path":"/console/","what":"Nova commands, typed. (Terminals only open through a private connection.)","url":"https://nova.novacane.co.uk/console/"},{"name":"Observatory","path":"/observatory/","what":"Every project, its code and the star map.","url":"https://nova.novacane.co.uk/observatory/"},{"name":"Lossless","path":"/lossless/","what":"Lossless audio rooms: listen together at full quality.","url":"https://nova.novacane.co.uk/lossless/"}]},{"title":"For everyone","note":"Pages clients, fans and anyone else can open.","items":[{"name":"Status","path":"/status","what":"Is everything working? All green means yes.","url":"https://nova.novacane.co.uk/status"},{"name":"Book a session","path":"/book","what":"Goes to the studio's booking page.","url":"https://nova.novacane.co.uk/book"},{"name":"Studio news","path":"/join","what":"Fans sign up for the studio's news here.","url":"https://nova.novacane.co.uk/join"},{"name":"Were you referred?","path":"/referral","what":"Clients say who sent them.","url":"https://nova.novacane.co.uk/referral"},{"name":"Privacy","path":"/privacy","what":"How Nova looks after people's details.","url":"https://nova.novacane.co.uk/privacy"}]},{"title":"Website chat","note":"The chat on novacane.co.uk. These two lines go in Squarespace: search Code Injection in the dashboard, then Footer.","items":[{"name":"Chat script","path":"/novabot.js","what":"The chat itself.","url":"https://nova.novacane.co.uk/novabot.js"},{"name":"Chat look","path":"/novabot.css","what":"How the chat looks.","url":"https://nova.novacane.co.uk/novabot.css"},{"name":"The two lines for Squarespace","code":"<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://nova.novacane.co.uk/novabot.css\">\n<script src=\"https://nova.novacane.co.uk/novabot.js\" defer></script>","what":"Copy both lines into Squarespace's Code Injection (Footer).","url":""}]}]};
